          "textEn": "67\n\nDestroyed by the aversion of the unhappy, always by the service of the Bhagavata.\nIn the supreme Bhagavata verse, devotion is established. 18>. Shabdartham\nNasht-- finished; Prayeshu-- often; Abhadreshu-- from all misfortunes; Fem-regularly; Bhagwat-Shrimadbhagwat\nOr of a pure devotee; Sevaya- by service; Bhagavati- in God; Uttam- Divine; Shlokes- Praises; Bhakti: devotion, love;\nSeva- service; Bhavati- occurs; Nisthiki- steadfast, unwavering..\n\nBy regularly attending Bhagwat's classes and serving pure devotees, all the sorrows of the heart\nare almost completely destroyed, and unwavering\nlove and devotion are established in those virtuous souls, whose praises are sung in divine songs. Meaning: Here, a treatment is given to remove those inauspicious things from the heart,\nwhich are obstacles on the path of self-realization. This treatment is to associate with the Bhagavata. Bhagavata are of two types, one is Granth-Bhagavata and the other is Bhakta-Bhagavata.\nThese both\nare effective medicines of Bhagwat and out of these one or both are removing the obstructions. Bhakta-Bhagavat is similar to the Granth-Bhagavat, because according to the Bhakta-Bhagavat Granth-Bhagavat,\none who lives his life and the Granth-Bhagavat is full of the knowledge of God and his pure devotees, that is, the Bhagavatas. The Bhagavata text and the Bhagavata person are inseparable. The devotee is the direct representative of God. Therefore, by pleasing the devotee-Bhagwat,\nthe benefit of the Granth Bhagwat Granth can be taken. Human logic does not understand in what\nway a devotee-Bhagwat or by serving the Granth-Bhagwat, one progresses on the path of devotion. But these are the facts, the explanation of which has been given by Srila Naradadeva, who was a son of a maid in his previous birth. The maid used to stroll with the sages, and in this way, she also came into contact with them. Only by their association and by eating their leftovers, this maidservant-son, a great devotee named Srila Naradadeva,\nand a great personality could become.\nThe miraculous effects of the Bhagavata's company are such that ¶. In\nTo understand these effects practically, it is necessary to pay attention to the fact that Bhagavatam"
