          "textEn": "89\nSometimes they incarnate themselves, and sometimes they make a suitable being their representative\nand empower it, but in every case, the purpose remains the same--God wants that\nthe suffering being should return to them, that is, the abode of God. All beings, after which happiness\nare crazy, that is not attainable in countless universes and in any corner of any physical planet.\nIt is not attainable. The eternal happiness that a living being desires is only available in the abode of God.\nHowever, the forgetful living being, being subject to the qualities of nature, does not know anything about the abode of God. Therefore, God himself\ndescends to spread the message of his abode, or comes as an authentic representative of the son of God. Such an incarnation\nor son of God, does not only propagate the message of going to the abode of God in human society,\nbut their work is in all societies, It also continues among the gods and other beings besides humans.\nThus, under the first canto of Srimad Bhagavatam, \"Divinity and Divine Service\" named\nThe Bhakti Vedanta meaning of the second chapter is completed."
