          "textEn": "97\nAre parts, are the supreme beings of the creatures of the world, and they are the caretakers of the universe or the one who resides in the ocean, Vishnu\nare called. Thus, three forms of the original man are known. Within this universe, all the\nincarnations that are, they originate from this Kshirodakshayi Vishnu. In different eras, there are countless different incarnations, but some of them are very prominent--such as Matsya, Kurma, Varaha, Rama, Nrusimha, Vamana, and many other incarnations. These are Avatar Leelas.\nThey are called Avatars. There are also multiple avatars – such as Brahma, Vishnu and Shiva (or Rudra) who are responsible for different qualities of nature. Lord Vishnu is one of the principal deities in Hinduism. Shivji is in the middle position between God and living beings.\nAnd Brahma is always the element of living beings. The supreme virtuous soul or devotee of God, by God\nis given the power to create, and he is called Brahma.\nTheir power is like the sun,\nwhich keeps reflecting through gems and jewels. When there is no being worthy of taking Brahma's place,\nthen God himself, becoming Brahma, takes on this responsibility. Lord Shiva is not an ordinary being. They are the qui of God, but due to living in direct contact with the material nature, they do not attain a divine place like Vishnu. Among them, milk and yogurt\nhave a difference. Although it is yogurt and milk, it cannot be used in place of milk. Then the incarnations of Manu will come. In one day of Brahma's life (according to our solar year calculation) there are fourteen Manus.\nThus, in one Brahma's\nmonth, there are 420 Manus, and in one year of Brahma, there are 5,04,000 Manus. Brahma's age is 100 years,\ntherefore, in Brahma's life, there are 5,04,000 Manus. The number of universes\nis countless, and each of them contains one Brahma, and all these are created and destroyed in the time it takes for a man to breathe in and\nexhale. Therefore, it can be 