          "textEn": "23\nAnd by the seer, the seen, the seer, the seen, the seer. 31. Meaning of the word\nAs-- in the manner; Nabhasi-- in the sky; Megha-oghah-- a group of clouds; Renuh-- dust; Va-- and; Parthiva:--\nDirt, fog; Anile-- in the air; Evam-- thus; Drashtari- to the seer; Drishatvamu-- for seeing;\nAropitam-- is attributed; Abuddhibhih-- by the few; L\n\nClouds and dust are carried away by the wind, but the few say that the sky\nis covered with clouds and the air is dusty. Similarly, those people also attribute to the soul\nthe perceptions of the physical body. Meaning: Here, further confirmation has been given that we cannot see those Gods with our physical eyes\nand senses, who are completely the soul. Even we are unable to recognize the spiritual spark present in the physical bodies of living beings. We search for the external\ncovering of the body or the subtle mind of the living being, but we cannot see the\nspiritual spark within the body.\nTherefore, due to the presence of the gross body of the living being,\nthe presence of the living being has to be accepted. Similarly, those who want to see God with their current\nphysical eyes or with physical senses, they are advised to meditate on the cosmic form.\nFor example, when a person sits in his car and goes somewhere, which\ncan be easily seen, then the identity of that car is lost from the person sitting in it. When\nthe President sits in his special car and goes somewhere, we say, '* There he is, the President.'\" At that\ntime, we identify the car with the President. Similarly, those ignorant people who\nwant to have a direct vision of God without necessary qualifications, they are shown that\nthe gigantic physical universe is the form of God, although God is everywhere, inside and out. In this context, the example of clouds in the sky and the blue sky can be taken.\nAlthough,\nthe blue of the sky and the sky are different, but we consider the color of the sky to be blue. But this is only a general perception of the alpannam."
