          "textEn": "28\nIs, therefore every task is easily accomplished by them as if it has been accomplished by itself. Fact.\nSo, it is that the complete, supreme God's concealment and disappearance, and their various actions, all of these\nare also supremely mysterious for Vedic literature. Even then, all these are displayed by God to show mercy on living beings. We should benefit from the narratives (Leelas) of God's actions,\nbecause these are the most easy and interesting means of meditating on Brahma.\nSa va idam vishwam amoghaleelah\nSrijatyavatyatti na sajate'smim.\nThe inner self, hidden in the beings,\nThe sixfold, the destroyer of the sixfold, the lord of the sixfold. 36). Meaning of the word:\nSah--God; Va--Or; Idam--This; Vishwam--The universe; Amogh-leelah--Those who are free from blemishes;\nSrijati--They create; Avati-atti- They nurture and destroy; Na--Not; Sajate--They are influenced by; Asmin--In them;\nBhuteshu--In all beings; Cha--And; Antarhitah--Staying within; Atma-tanrah--Self-controlled; Shad-vargikam--Endowed with six qualities; Jighniti--Like fragrance, attached superficially; Shat-guna-Ishah--Endowed with six qualities-- The master of the six senses.\n\nThose whose actions are always pure, they are God, the master of the six senses, and all six\nare all-powerful with opulence. They create the universes, they sustain them.\nAnd without being affected even a bit, they destroy them. They reside within all beings,\nand are always independent.\nMeaning: The main difference between God and living beings is that God is the creator and living beings\nare created. Here, they are called Amogh Lila:, which indicates that in their creation,\nthere is nothing that is worthy of sorrow. Those who create disturbances in their creation, they themselves get disturbed. They are beyond all material anxieties, because they are endowed with all six opulences, namely wealth, power, fame,\nbeauty, knowledge, and sacrifice--. Thus, they are the masters of the