          "textEn": "30\nJust as children are deceived by the magic tricks of magicians, the non-devotees always\nremain in ignorance, even if they are very skilled in desire-driven actions and arguments. Through such limited knowledge, they are unable to enter the mysterious realm of spirituality. Logical seekers are slightly better than workers, but even they, living in the clutches of attachment, assume that\nany object that has form, name, and action, is produced by physical power. For such people,\nGod is formless, nameless, and devoid of action. And because such a knower (Gnani) equates the divine name and form of God with worldly names and forms, therefore they are truly ignorant. With so little\nknowledge, one cannot reach the true nature of the Supreme Being. As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, God is always, even while living within the physical world, in a divine state\n.\nBut ignorant people consider God to be a great manifestation of the universe, and in this way, they remain deluded by Maya. The Veda is the root of the word, the end of the word,\nThe chariot's axle is the end of the chariot. By the constant practice of devotion,\nI worship the lotus feet of the universe. 38). Meaning of the word:\nSah-He; Veda-- can know; Dhatu-- of the metal; Padi-Mahima-- glory; Parasya-- of the spiritual; Durantah-Viryasya-- of the mighty; Ratha-Adg-Paneah-- of Lord Krishna, who holds the wheel of the chariot in his hand; Yah-Who;\nAmayaya-Without any hesitation; Sanataya-Continuously; Anuvrittiya-By following; Bhajet-Serves; Tat-That-\nPad-Of their feet; Saroj-Gandham-The fragrance of the lotus..\n\nHe who, without hesitation, unobstructedly holds the wheel of the chariot in his hands,\nwho serves the lotus feet of God in a favorable manner, only he can understand the complete\nglory, power, and divinity of the creator of this world.\nMeaning: Only pure devotees are able to understand the divine name, form, and their divine plays, as a reason for being freed from t