          "textEn": "32\nThey are able to know within a proper limit, no one else knows, therefore all the devotees\nare fully known through spiritual knowledge. The ultimate reality is none other than God. The formless Brahman and the indwelling Supreme Soul are included in the knowledge of God. Therefore, one who knows God,\nknows about Himself, about His various powers and His parts, automatically\nknows everything. Therefore, the devotees are called the most fortunate (successful). Of God,\nA hundred percent devotee remains indifferent to the terrible physical heat of the cycle of birth and death. Idam bhagavatam naam puranam brahmasammatam.\nThe best verse and character is uttered by the divine sage.\nFor the welfare of the world, it is a blessed and auspicious beginning. 40. Shabdartham\nIdam-- This; Bhagavatam-- The book containing the stories of Lord and his pure devotees; Naam-- Named; Puranam-- Complement of Vedas; Brahma-Sammetam-- The incarnation of Lord Krishna; Uttam-Shloka-- The best verse of the Lord; Charitam-- The activity of the Lord; Chakar-Compiled; Bhagavan-- The incarnation of the Lord; Rishi-Shri Vyasadeva; Nishreyasaya-For the welfare of all; Lokasya-Of the people; Dhanyam-Blessed, fully successful, blessed; Swasti-Ayanam-All bliss; Maham-Complete..\n\nThis is the literary incarnation of Shrimad Bhagwat Bhagwan, which was compiled by the incarnation of Bhagwan, Ved Vyas. This is for the ultimate welfare of all people, and it is in every way\nsuccessful, joyful, and complete. Meaning: Lord Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu has declared that Shrimad Bhagavat is the pure voice of all Vedic\nknowledge and history.\nIn this, the chosen characters of some great devotees who live in the association of God\nare given. Shrimad Bhagavat is the literary incarnation of Lord Krishna, therefore this\nis inseparable from them. We should worship Shrimad Bhagwat with the same respect as we\ndo to God. We can receive the supreme blessings of God through its sincere and patient study. Just as God is complete in full light, full bliss, and completely complete,\nso is this Shripadbhagwat. By reciting Shrimad Bhagavat, we can attain all the divine light of the Supreme Brahman, Shri Krishna,\nprovided that we receive it through a transparent guru. In Puri"
