          "textEn": "33\nTo the extent that people used to come for the darshan of Bhagavan Chaitanya, Srila Swaroop, the personal secretary of Mahaprabhu,\nDamodar Goswami used to say that one should study Bhagwat only from a devotee-Bhagavat.\nShould be. Devotees are the authentic gurus who are the embodiment of Bhagwat, and to attain the desired fruit, one should receive the teachings of Bhagwat from them. All those benefits can be obtained from the study of Bhagwat,\nwhich are from the direct presence of God. This is the one who bestows all the blessings of Lord Krishna,\nwhich can be obtained through direct contact with God. Tadidam grahyamas sutamatmavatam varam.\nThe essence of all the histories is contained in this. 419). Shabdartham\nTat--That; Idam--This; Grahyam--To be accepted; Sutam--To their son; Atmavatam--To the self-realized;\nVaram--Extremely respectable; Sarva- all; Veda--Vedic literature (knowledge scripture); Itihaasanam--All histories;\nSaram--Summary, conclusion; Saram Saram; Samuddhrutam--Extracted.\n\nAmong the self-realized, the most highly respected Shri Vyasadeva extracted the essence of all Vedic literature and\nthe history of the universe, and presented it to his son. Meaning: The ignorant people consider the history of the world only from the time of Buddha, that is, from 600 BC,\nand they consider all the histories mentioned in the scriptures before this period as mere fictional stories.\nThey consider it. This is not the fact. All the stories described in the Puranas and Mahabharata etc. are real\nhistory, which is not only related to this world but also to millions of other worlds in this universe.\nare related.\nSuch people sometimes find the history of other worlds beyond this world unbelievable. But perhaps they do not know that different planets are not uniform in every way, therefore,\nsome historical facts of other planets do not match the facts of this planet. Of different people\nUpon considering different situations and times and circumstances, in the stories of the Puranas, neither\nwill there be any strangeness, nor will they seem imaginary. We should always remember this saying.\nThat a person's food can become someone else's meal. ©. Therefore, we"
