          "textEn": "85\n\nHaving abandoned the lotus feet of your own dharma,\nIf one is not devoted to the Lord,\nWhere does evil arise from?\nWhoever is not devoted to their own dharma,\nIs not devoted to their own dharma. 97. Meaning of the word:\nAbandon, renounce; one's own duty; lotus feet; Hari (God);\nDuring devotion; unripe, immature; Ath (for) - for; Pateet (falls) - falls; Tath (therefore) - from that place; Yad (if) - if; Yatra (where) - where; Kri (how) - how; Va (or) - or (irony); Abhadram (unfavorable) - adverse; Abhut (will be) - will be; Amushya (of no one) - of no one;\nKim (what) - nothing; Kah (who) - who; Arthah (profit) - what is the benefit; Aptah (received) - received; Abhajatam (not deviated) - deviated from; Swa-dharmatha (by one's own duty) - by one's own duty;\nBy being engaged in one's own duty; while engaged..\n\nHe who has renounced his material senses to engage in the devotional service of God,\neven if he sometimes falls down in a raw state, there is no danger of him\nfailing. On the contrary, a non-devotee, even if fully engaged in his duties,\ndoes not get any benefit.\nMeaning: As far as the duties of mankind are concerned, there are countless of them. Every\nperson is not only bound by their parents, family, society, country, humanity, other beings, and gods,\nbut also towards great philosophers, poets, and scientists. The scriptures say that a man can renounce all such duties and take refuge in God. Therefore, if\nsomeone does this way and if they succeed in devotional service to God, then\nit is auspicious. But sometimes it happens that a person, in a moment of emotional fervor,\nbecomes dedicated to the service of God, but until the end, due to some reason or another, due to bad association,\nthey deviate from the path of service. There are many examples of this in history. Bharat Maharaj\nBecause of being attached to a deer, he had to assume the body of a deer. When they were dying,\nthey were thinking about the deer.\nTherefore, in the next birth, he became a deer, but he did not forget the events of his previous birth. Similarly, due to committing an offense against the feet of Shivaji, Chitraketu\nalso met his downfall. But, even so, the stress here is on taking refuge in the lotus feet of the Lord"
