          "textEn": "20]\n\nMeaning: In the physical world, ignorance is compared to darkness, and in all Vedic\nliterature, God is compared to the sun. Wherever there is light, there darkness cannot remain. Listening to the divine plays of God is the divine association of God himself, because God\nand there is no difference in his plays. The meaning of attaining the company of the supreme light will be\nto drive away all ignorance. Only out of ignorance, a bound soul falsely thinks that it and\nGod are both born from material nature. But in reality, God and the living being are both divine.\nAnd they have nothing to do with physical nature. When ignorance is removed and this\nis experienced that without God, nothing exists, then ignorance\ndisappears. Because the gross and subtle bodies are emanated from God, therefore, as soon as one gains the knowledge of light,\nthese two bodies can be engaged in the service of God.\nThe gross body should be engaged in serving God (as in bringing water, sweeping the temple, or in prostrations, etc.). In Archana, that is, in the temple, in worshiping God, this gross body is used to serve God. Similarly, the subtle mind should be engaged in listening to the divine plays of God, in their\ncontemplation, in the chanting of the name of God, etc. All such works are divine. In addition to these, one should not engage the gross or subtle senses in any other work. Divine\nSuch a realization of actions is attained by staying in devotion for many years and serving,\nBut the way love arose towards God in Narad Muni through hearing, that\nis extremely effective. Thus, the autumn rain covers,\nThe sun shines, and the world is filled with fame.\nThe glory is praised by the sages and great souls,\nDevotion is engaged, and the darkness of ego is dispelled. 28 ”."
