          "textEn": "249\nChapter seven\nDrona's son is punished\nShaunaka said\nNarada's son, the sage, Lord Vadarayan. Having heard what was intended, what did he do? 1>. Meaning of the word:\nShounak said-- Shounak said; Nirgatte-- after leaving; Narade-- of Narad Muni; Soot-- O Soot; Bhagwan-- divine form;\nFrom; Vadarayanah-- Vedavyasa; Shrutvan-- heard; Td-- his; Abhipretam-- desired; Mana ki-- by; Manovancha-- desire;\nTatah-- after that; Kim-- what; Akarot- did; Vibhuh- the great..\nRishi Shaunak asked: Hey Suta, the great and divinely powerful Vyasadeva, having heard everything from Shri\nNarad Muni, what did Vyasadeva do after Narad left? Meaning: This chapter indicates that the description of Srimad Bhagavat is being given,\nbecause Maharaj Parikshit was miraculously saved in his mother's womb.\nThis\nincident happened because of Acharya Drona's son, Droni (Ashwatthama), who killed Draupadi's five sons\nwhile they were sleeping, and for which Arjuna punished him. Before starting this Mahapurana\nSrimad Bhagavat, Shri Vyasadeva attained the realization of all truths through Samadhi. Suta said:\nIn the Brahmanadya, on the western bank of the Saraswati, there is an hermitage.\nIt is called Shamyapras, and it is the assembly of the sages. 2>. Meaning of the word:\nSuta said:\nOn the banks of the river Brahmanadya, which is closely associated with Brahmins, saints, and God,\nOn the banks of the river,\nOn the banks of the Saraswati,\nAshrama: a hut for meditation; Paschima: west; Tate: on the bank; Shamyaprasah:"
