          "textEn": "273\n\nBecause his life was in danger, therefore he touched water to purify himself,\nand concentrated his attention in the mantra chanting to fire the Brahmastra, although\nhe did not know the method of bringing this weapon back. Meaning: The subtle forms of physical activities are more subtle than the grosser methods of physical work. Such subtle forms of physical activities are obtained through the purification of sound. Here, this method has been adopted to activate the Brahmatra through chanting. Then, the radiant, fierce, and all-directed light emerged.\nTaking refuge in the life force, Vishnu, Jishnu, spoke thus. 21). Meaning of the word:\nTatah-- After that; Pradushkritam-- spread out; Tejah-- Shine; Prachandam-- terrible; Sarvatom-- all around; Disham--\nDirections; Prana-apadam-- affecting life; Abhiprashya-looking: Vishnum-- from God; Jishnu-Arjuna\nSaid.\n.\nAfter that, intense light failed in all directions. This was so fierce that Arjuna\nfelt compelled to address Lord Krishna\nbecause of his life's crisis. Arjuna said,\nKrishna, Krishna, the mighty-armed one, the fearful to devotees. You are the destroyer of those who are destroying themselves. 22). Meaning:\nArjuna said--Arjuna said; Krishna--Oh Lord Krishna; Krishna--Oh Lord Krishna; Maha-baho--Almighty;\nBhaktanam--Of the devotees; Abhayadtar--One who drives away fear; Tvam--You; Teh:—Only; Dahyamanam--To be burned;\nOf those who are burning; Apavargah--Path to salvation; Asi--Be; Samsrutih--Amidst the sufferings..\nArjuna said: O Lord Krishna, You are the Lord of all. Your diverse\npowers have no bounds. Therefore, only you are the one who has fearlessness in the hearts of your devotees"
