          "textEn": "297\nTo the wife; Priyamu--pleasure; Cha--and; Bhimsenasya--of Shri Bhimsen; Panchalyaah--of Draupadi; Mahyam--my also; Ev--\nCertainly; Cha--and.,\n\nLord Shri Krishna said: One should not kill a Brahmin, but if he\nis an intruder, then he must be killed. All these orders are in the scriptures, and you should act according to them.\nAccording to these, you should act. You also have to fulfill the promises made to your wife, and you have to\nwork for the satisfaction of Bhimsen and me as well. Meaning: Arjun was in a dilemma because according to the evidence given by different persons from different scriptures,\nAshwatthama was to be killed and he was also to be granted life. Brahmabandhu\nOr, as the unworthy son of a Brahmin, Ashwatthama was not a killer, but at the same time, he was also an aggressor. According to the opinion prescribed by Manu, an aggressor, even if he is a Brahmin, (what to say of a Brahmin's\nineligible son) is condemned.\nDronacharya undoubtedly was a real Brahmin, but he\nwas afraid in the battlefield, so he was killed. But Ashwatthama, even after being an aggressor, without any reason,\nwas standing. The rule is such that if a terrorist is unarmed or without a chariot, then he should not be killed.\nShould not be killed. Certainly, all these were Arjuna's confusions. In addition to this, Arjun had to\nfulfill that promise of his, which he had given while consoling Draupadi. And to him,\nBheem and Krishna also had to be satisfied, who advised the killing of Ashwatthama. This\nwas a dilemma before Arjun, and Krishna found a solution for it.\nSoot said,\nArjuna suddenly, with his mind, with his head, with his head.\nHe removed the gem from his head, the head of the Brahmin. 55>. Meaning of the word.\nSuta said - Suta Goswami said; Arjuna:--Arjuna; Sahasa--At that very moment; Aanjaya--Knowing; Hareh--Of the Lord;\nKe; Hardam- desired; Ath--In this way; Asina--With the sword; Manim- the gem; Jahara- separated; Murdhanyam-\nO