          "textEn": "307.\nAfter mourning for them and having offered sufficient Ganges water, all of them\nbathing in the Ganges, the water of which has become sacred because of mixing with the dust of the lotus feet of God. There, with the king, Dhritarashtra, and his younger brother,\nGandhari, grieving for her son, and Krishna and Madhava. 3). Shabdartham\nTatra- there; Asinam-- sitting; Kuru-patim-- king of the Kurus; Dhritarashtram-- to Dhritarashtra; Saha- with; Anujam-- younger brother; Putra- son; Shoka- grief; Artam- suffering; Pritham- to; Kunti- to; Krishnam- Krishna; Draupadi- Draupadi; Cha- also; Madhavah- Lord Krishna.,\n\nThere, King Yudhishthira of the Kuru dynasty, along with his younger brothers, Dhritarashtra, Gandhari, Kunti,\nand Draupadi, sat down. They were all overwhelmed with grief. Oh Lord Krishna was also there.\nMeaning: Since the Kurukshetra war was between family members, therefore, those who were\naffected by it were all family members--namely, Maharaj Yudhishthira and his brothers,\nKunti, Draupadi, Subhadra, Dhritarashtra, Gandhari, and their daughters-in-law, etc. All the dead were somehow\nrelated, therefore, the family mourning was joint. Lord Krishna also\nwas the maternal uncle's brother of the Pandavas and the nephew of Kunti and the brother of Subhadra. Therefore, God had equal sympathy towards all of them. Therefore, they began to give solace to all of them in accordance with the times.\nHe who, with compassion, shows the path of time to the deluded and the bound,\nIn the beings, shows the way to the passage of time, and also shows the reaction. 4>. Meaning of the word:\nSanvatayam as--with the help of; munibhih--with the sages present; hata-bandhun- those who were killed; mareyten- those who were killed; shucharpitan- all those who were pushed; bhuteshu- on the living beings; kalasya- of the almighty; gati- reaction; darshayan- shown; na- not; pratirakshan- treatment."
