          "textEn": "306\nThey did not deviate even a bit from the practices of the ashram. God, for a purpose, completed these social\ntraditions, so that in the future, other people would continue to follow them.\nGanthanu kritamatirbrahyan dwarakam rathamasthitah.\nUpalebhyam abhidhavantimuttaram bhayavihalam. 8 ”. Meaning of the word:\nTo go. Kritamatiha--with resolve; Brahman--Oh Brahmin; Dwarkam--towards Dwarka; Ratham--chariot; Para--over; Asthitah--arrived; Upalebhe--seen; Abhidhavantim--approaching quickly; Uttara--to Uttara; Bhaya-vihlalam--frightened.\nFearful L.\n\nAs soon as they mounted the chariot to depart for Dwarka, they saw Uttara\napproaching them quickly. Meaning: All the members of the Pandava clan were dependent on God for their protection, therefore,\nGod protected them in all circumstances. Well, God protects everyone,\nBut those who depend on Him completely, He protects them especially.\nThe father remains especially vigilant towards his\nyoung son, because he is completely dependent on the father. Uttaro vacha\nPahi Pahi Mahayogin Devdev Jagatpati. I see no other fear than yours, where death is mutual. 9>. Meaning of the word.\nUttara said--Uttara said; Padi Padi--Protect, protect; Maha-Yogi--Supreme Yogi; Dev-Dev--Even of the worshiped\nWorshipful; Jagat-Pate-He, the lord of the universe; Na-No; Anyam-Other; Tvat-Beyond you; Abhayam-Fearless\nThe feeling of being; Pashye-I see; Yatra-Where; Mrityu-Death; Parasparam-In the duality in the world..\n\nUttara said: Oh, God of Gods, Oh, Lord of the Universe, you are the greatest Yogi of all. Please\nprotect me, because in this duality-filled world, there is no one other than you to save me from the noose of death."
