          "textEn": "320\nThe intense attention of those who are constantly engaged should be drawn towards that. Meditative people worship a tangible form within their minds, therefore God is compassionate even to women, Shudras, and Brahmin relatives,\nprovided that they accept to go to temples made in various forms. Those who go to temples\nare not idol worshippers, as some ignorant people say. Great teachers,\nWhile bestowing grace upon the ignorant, established such worship temples everywhere. In reality, a Shudra or\na woman or someone living in a lower class than them should not pretend that\nhe has crossed the stage of temple worship. A person should, in order to have a vision of God,\nstart from his lotus feet and gradually reach his thighs, waist, chest, and face. Without practicing seeing the lotus feet of God,\none should not try to see the face of God.\nBecause she is the aunt of God, Mrs. Kunti did not start seeing God with her lotus feet, because God would be ashamed of this. Therefore, to escape from this situation,\nto avoid it, he slowly rose upwards from the waist, towards the upper part of the lotus feet of God,\nand then saw the lotus feet. In the cycle, each object\nbecomes in the appropriate order. As the gods were destroyed by Kamsa,\nI was also released by you, O Lord, with your own self-born son.\nI was freed by you, O Lord, from the multitude of enemies. 22). Shabdartham\nYatha--as; Hrishikesha Indriyo ke swami; Khalen--by the one who is greedy; Devaki--Devaki (mother of Shri Krishna); Kansa--by King Kansa; Rudhira--captured; Ati-chiram--for a long time; Sucha-arpita- sorrowful; Vimochita- liberated; Muccita- released;\nAham cha--I also; Saha-atma-ja--with one's children; Vibho--Oh great one; Tvaya eva--by you alone;\nNathen--as a protector; Muhuh--constantly; Vipat-ganat- from a group of calamities."
