          "textEn": "33]  No one really cares about maintaining relationships. Although the door to God's grace remains open for him,\nhe avoids it. This is the only difference between a pure devotee and a mixed devotee. Those who are completely against serving God are considered to be living in inferior darkness.\nThose who pray to God in times of need are partial recipients of grace, and those who\nare constantly engaged in serving God are fully worthy of God's grace. In attaining God's grace, such bias is relative to the recipient, not because of the bias of the supremely merciful God.\nReason.\n\nWhen God descends into this world through His complete merciful power, He plays like a human. Therefore, it seems that they favor their devotees,\nbut this is not the fact. Despite such bias, their grace remains equally distributed.\nIn the battlefield of Kurukshetra, all the people who died in the war before God, all of them\nwere liberated without considering their worthiness, because by dying before God,\nthe dying being becomes pure from all the fruits of karma, and the dying person gets a place in the supreme abode\nsomewhere. If a person sits in front of the sun's rays, then he definitely\ngets the benefit of heat and ultraviolet rays. The conclusion that emerges is that God never\ndoes not discriminate. It is wrong for a common man to think that they discriminate.\nBirth, action, and the self are all the same; the self is not the doer of actions. Firey yaad: tadatatavidambanam. 30. Meaning of the word:\nBirth--birth; Kamam--action; Cha--therefore; Vishch-atman--of the soul; Ajasya--of the unborn; Akartuh--of the uncreated;\nAtmanah--of the life force; Tiryak--of the animal; Nu--of the human; Rishishu--of the sages; Yadahsu--in the water; Tat--that; Atyanth--excessive;\nReal, excessive; Vidambanam--deceptive, deceptive;\n.\n\nOh, the soul of the universe, it is truly a surprising thing (irony) that you, while being inactive, perform actions, and being in the form 