          "textEn": "344\n\nJust as the body's name and fame end as soon as the soul becomes invisible,\nin the same way, if you do not have mercy on us, then our fame and activities, including the Pandavas and the Yadus,\nwill be destroyed immediately. Meaning: Kunti Devi is fully aware that the existence of the Pandavas is due to the one and only Shri Krishna.\nReason. Undoubtedly, the Pandavas were completely established in their name and fame, and the righteous\nMaharaj Yudhishthira was guiding them; the Yadus were friends, but without the guidance of Shri Krishna,\nall of them had no existence, just as all the senses of the body remain in vain without consciousness. No one should be proud of their prestige, power, and glory without receiving guidance through God's grace. The living being is always dependent and the ultimate refuge is God himself.\nTherefore, even if we gather all the material resources, no matter how regressive,\nwithout the guidance of God, all such inventions, whether they are\nhowever strong and reactive, become futile.\nWhat is to be achieved there, just as it is now, is like a mace. They are distinguished by their own nature, as they are marked by their own characteristics. 39 |\nMeaning of the word\nNa- not; Iyam-- this is our kingdom; Shanjobhishyate-- it will look beautiful; Tatra-- then; Yatha-- as it is now, in this form; Idanim--\nhow; Gadadhar-- O Krishna; Tvat-- yours; Padaih-- by your feet; Ankita-- marked; Bhati-- is shining; Swa-\nLakshan-- from your consciousness; Vilakshitaih-- from the signs;\n\nO Gadadhar (Krishna), at this time, the mark of your footsteps has been imprinted in our kingdom,\nand because of this, it looks beautiful, but when you leave, it will not remain like this\n. Meaning: There are certain signs of the Lord's feet, because of which they are different from others.\nThe fag of Lord's feet (Fd) is made up of various objects like the flag, Vajra, goad, umbrella, lotus, chakra etc. Wherever Gods walk, there the footprints of the gods are marked on the soft ground."
