          "textEn": "384\nIt should be reached through the medium. Humans should not establish direct contact with them, but\nreach them through a medium that is transparent and capable of leading them on the right path. By devotion, in which the mind is engaged, and by speech, in which one's name is chanted.\nWhen the body is abandoned, the Yogi is freed from the fruits of action. 23). Meaning of the word:\nWith devotion; with thought; with mind; in which; with words; that which is of Krishna;\nName: holy name; while chanting; while renouncing; Kalevaram: this physical body;\nYogi: devotee) is liberated; from desire and action;\nThose supreme beings who appear in the minds of devotees through concentration, devotion, and contemplation,\nand through the chanting of the holy name, They free those devotees from the bondage of desire-driven actions while leaving their physical bodies.\nOh!\n\nMeaning: The meaning of yoga is to remove the mind from all other subjects and to focus it\nSuch concentration is or is a samadhi, a perfected state of meditation. He who concentrates his mind in this way, is called a Yogi. Such a Yogi of God,\nA devotee, spends 24 hours every day in the service of God. As a result, all his attention\nremains engaged in the contemplation of God in Navadha Bhakti. In Navadha Bhakti, there is listening, chanting, remembrance, worship,\nPraise, devotion, obedience, friendship, or dedication. From such practices of yoga,\nthat is, by serving God, by connecting with Him, recognition is given by God, as the supreme state of Samadhi\nWhile describing, God himself explains in the Bhagavad Gita. God such\nis called the best among the yogis. By the grace of God, such a complete Yogi concentrates his mind with full consciousness\nin God, and in this way, before leaving the body, by chanting His name,\nHe is immediately sent to such a world by the inner power of God, where physical life\nAnd the question of the causes related to it does not arise. In physical