          "textEn": "399\n\nDetachment from all sense-activities is called the state (yoga-dharana) of yoga. Closing all the doors of the senses and establishing the mind in the heart and the life air in the upper part of the head,\nby establishing oneself in yoga, O man. 13. Being situated in this yoga and uttering the ultimate combination of letters, the 'U' sound,\nIf any complete Supreme Personality of Godhead contemplates and renounces his body, then he\ncertainly goes to the abode of the Lord.\n\n14. O son of Pritha, he who constantly remembers me with undivided devotion, I am easily accessible to him,\nbecause he constantly remains engaged in my devotion. 15. Great men, who are devoted, after attaining me, never return to this world full of sorrows, because they have attained supreme perfection. Shri Bhishmadev had attained the accomplishment of voluntarily giving up his body, and at the time of death, he was blessed to have found his desired Shri Krishna in front of him.\nTherefore, he placed his open eyes on them. They wanted to see Shri Krishna for a long time because of their intense love. Because\nthey were pure devotees, therefore they did not need the detailed practices of yoga. For accomplishment,\nsimple devotion is sufficient. Therefore, Bhishmadev's heartfelt desire was to see Lord Krishna in person.\nIt was to take Shri Bhishmadev's last breath with the grace of God. This\nopportunity was obtained. Purely by holding, auspicious and inauspicious,\nBy steadfastness, the inauspicious, the auspicious, and the end of the long life. Nivruttasarvendriyavruttivibhrama-\nStushtavajanyam visrujjannadanam. 31. Shabdartham\nVishuddhaya--pure; Dharanaya--with attention; Hata-ashubha--one who has reduced the inauspicious qualities of material existence;\nTat--that; Ikshaya--by seeing; Eva--only; Ashu--immediately; Gata--having gone; Yudha--with arrows; Shramah--tiredness;"
