          "textEn": "44\nIt constantly compels to serve, and is never satisfied. Such satisfaction of desires\nThere is no end to such trades, and without the hope of being freed, one remains entangled in such service.\nIs. Salvation is only attained when one is in the company of pure devotees. Through such association, he slowly\ngradually rises towards his divine consciousness. In this way, he can know that his eternal\nposition is to serve God, not for the fulfillment of desires like lust, anger, and the desire to assert dominance over others, etc.\nPhysical society, friendship, and love, various states of lust,\nare the reasons for bondage in the physical world, where three types of heat are created. By associating with pure devotees and with humble feelings,\nby listening to them, attachment to material pleasures decreases, and there is a predominance of attraction towards listening to the divine activities of God. Once attraction is generated,\nit continues without stopping, like the fire of gunpowder. It has been said that\nShri Hari is so divinely attractive that those who are content with themselves through self-realization\nAnd have truly been freed from all worldly bonds, they too become devotees of God. In such a\nsituation, it can be well understood what the state of the Pandavas would have been, who\nwere the eternal companions of God? They could not even imagine the separation of Shri Krishna, because\nDue to constant personal contact, their attraction was extremely TE.\nEven for a pure devotee,\nthe remembrance of their form, qualities, name, fame, activities, etc., is so attractive that he forgets all the forms, qualities, names, fame, and activities of the world,\nand because of the mature association of pure devotees,\nhe does not get away from the contact of God even for a moment. All those who are without desire, with a mind agitated by incessant thoughts,\nSeeing with affection, with delight, here and there. 13."
