          "textEn": "457\n\nThen God, out of his part, with the desire to give names and forms to the living beings,\nput them under the guidance of material nature. He has been authorized to recreate the physical nature with his own power. Meaning: All beings are part of God. They are of two types-- eternally liberated and eternally ag)\nEternally liberated beings are eternally liberated and they remain eternally immersed in the exchange of divine love-filled service in the divine abode of God, which is beyond the visible world. But eternally bound, that is, perpetually,\nthe responsibility of bound beings lies on the external power, Maya, that it should improve their\nrebellious attitude towards the Supreme Father. Eternally bound, they always forget that their relationship with God is in the form of their part. They remain attached to the products of matter through Maya, and\nIn this way, they keep making various kinds of plans in the material world to become happy.\nThey happily carry forward these\nplans, but those who make plans according to God's will, and\ntheir plans are destroyed after some time--as has been said before. This is testified by the Bhagavad Gita (9.7),* O son of Kunti! At the end of the eon, all beings\nbecome absorbed in my nature, and when the time comes to create again, I begin creation with my\nexternal energy.\"\n\nThe word 'bhayu' is indicative of 'again and again', meaning that the creation, sustenance, and destruction\nactions continue incessantly from the external power of God. They are the reasons for everything. But\nall beings, who are naturally part of God and remain forgetful of the sweet relationship, are\ngiven another opportunity to escape the clutches of external power. And to re-awaken the consciousness of the living being,\nthe creation of scriptures is also done by God.\nFor the bound soul, the Vedic\nliterature is the one who guides, so that they can be freed from the repetition of the creation and destruction of the physical world and the physical body."
