en a certificate of honor. In these addresses,\nKrishna used to be. Krishna means Krishna and his eternal devotees, just as Raja means king, Raja\nand his Vishchaspatra Darwari-gan. Krishna and his unique devotees cannot be separated. Therefore, the meaning of the devotee's praise of God\nis, the praise of God, and the meaning of the praise of God is the praise of the devotee. Maharaj,\nParikshit would not have been so pleased to hear the praises of his ancestors, Maharaj Yudhishthir, and Arjun,\nif they were not all connected to the activities of Lord Krishna. God to save his devotees"
