          "textEn": "272\nare, although there is no such desire in the mind of the devotee. The divine service of God, for the devotee, within oneself,\nis the divine benefit, therefore the devotee has no expectation of anything from God. Vedic proverb,\nBased on the all-pervading rays of God's radiance, which is called Brahmajyoti,\nare pervading within or outside every object, like the all-pervading physical sky, and thus\nthey are omniscient as well. As far as the beauty of God is concerned, some specific characteristics are found in them, by which they are different from all other\nliving beings, but apart from these, some of their specific beautiful characteristics are very attractive,\nby which even the mind of Radharani, the most beautiful creation of God, is attracted.\nTherefore, they are called Madanmohan,\nThat is, they are those who are capable of attracting even the mind of Kamadeva. Srila Jiva Goswami Prabhu has\nanalyzed other divine qualities of God and he confirms that God\nis Shri Krishna, the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead (Parabrahma). They are omnipotent because of their inconceivable powers,\nTherefore, they are Yogeshwar, meaning they are the supreme lords of all yogic powers. Because of being Yogedhar, their\neternal form is spiritual--it is a mixture of eternity, knowledge, and bliss. Devotees cannot understand the\ndynamic nature of their knowledge, because they become satisfied by reaching the eternal form of their knowledge. All great men desire to become as knowledgeable as them. This means that\nall other knowledge is always incomplete, delicate, and measurable, But the knowledge of God is always stable and\nincomprehensible.\nSrila Suta Goswami has confirmed in the Bhagavat that although the residents of Dwarka daily\nused to see God, they were still eager to see him again and again. We can appreciate the qualities of God\nas the ultimate goal, but we can never equal them. This physical world is a product of the great element, which is the dream state of Yoganidra in the ocean of God's cause; yet, all this creation appears to originate from Him. This means that\nGod's dream state is also a real expression. Therefore, they can bring every object under their divine control. They appear in their full form whenever and wherever they appear."
