          "textEn": "3\n\nSuta said,\nThen, after requesting, he gave him places to stay.\nThe gambling, drinking, and gambling, where there are four kinds of unrighteousness. 38>. Meaning of the word:\nSuta said:—Suta Goswami said; Abhyarthita:--Requested; Tada--At that time; Tasme--SH; Sthanaani places;\nKo; Kalaye--To Kali; Dadau--Given permission; Dyutam--Gambling; Panam--Intoxicated woman:--Illegal relations with women;\nSuna--Slaughter of animals; Yatra-wherever; Adharma--Sinful act; Chatuh--Four types of..\n\nSut Goswami said: Upon being asked in this way by Kaliyuga, Maharaj Parikshit\nallowed him to live in places where gambling, drinking alcohol, prostitution, and\nslaughter of animals take place.\n\nMeaning: The root characteristics of unrighteousness, namely ego, prostitution, intoxicating substances, and false speech,\nare contrary to the four principles of righteousness-- penance, purity, compassion, and truth.\nThe four places in which Kali was specially permitted to live by the king are: the place of gambling, the brothel,\nthe tavern, and the butcher shop.\n\nSrila Jeeva Goswami instructs that against the principles of the scriptures, drinking alcohol, such as Sautramani Yagya,\nthe association of women without marriage, and animal slaughter against the orders of the scriptures, are unrighteous acts. In the Vedas,\nfor those who are engaged in material pleasures, and for those who are free from worldly bondage,\nthere are two different types of commands. For the Gita, the Vedic command is that they gradually regulate their actions\ntowards the path of liberation. Therefore, those who are completely ignorant and are addicted to alcohol, women, and meat,\nby performing Sautramani Yagya, to consume alcohol, to marry, to have intercourse with a prostitute, and through Yajna,\nto eat meat, permission is sometimes granted. Vedic literature, such recommendations are for a class,\nare for a special group, not for the general public.\nBut since these are Ved