          "textEn": "372\nMade. When their father Vasudev was taking the child Krishna across the Yamuna and taking him from Mathura to Gokul,\nthen God fell into this river, and upon touching the dust of the lotus feet of God, she\nbecame immediately pure. Here, there is a special mention that Maharaj Parikshit took refuge in that special river\nwhich was flowing beautifully and was mixing with the lotus feet of God\ntaking dust off. Tulsi leaves are always placed on the lotus feet of Lord Krishna, therefore as soon as\ntheir lotus feet touch the water of the Ganges and Yamuna rivers, the rivers become sacred. But God touched Yamuna more than Ganga. According to the Varaha Purana, as\nSrila Jiva Goswami has quoted, there is no difference in the water of the Ganga and Yamuna rivers, but\nthe water of Jan Gaga becomes a hundred times pure, then it is called Yamuna.\nSimilarly, in the scriptures,\nit is said that one thousand names of Vishnu are equal to one name of Ram, and three names of Ram are equal to one name of Krishna.\nof. Thus, having distinguished, these Pandavas:\nApproaching Vishnu's feet,\nHe offered Mukundaarda, the supreme, the unparalleled.\nThe ascetic, free from all attachments, was freed. 7/. Shabdartham\nIti--Thus; Vyavachchidya nishchay karine; Saha-King; Pandaveyah-worthy descendants of the Pandavas; Praya-Upavesham-for fasting; Prati-towards; Vishnupadiyam-at the bank of the Ganges river ( descending from the feet of Lord Vishnu ); Dadhau-\nsacrificed; Mukunda-angahri-at the lotus feet of Lord Krishna; Ananya-detached; Bhavah-soul, Bhavah; Muni-Tratha-taking of a sage; Mukta-liberated; Samasta-all kinds of; Sangah-with association.\n.\n\nThus, the king, a worthy descendant of the Pandavas, firmly resolved to fast until death\nand to dedicate himself to the lotus feet of Lord Krishna, he sat on the banks of the Ganges\nriver, because only Krishna is capable of delivering liberation. In this way, he\nFreed himself from all attachments and possessions and accepted the vow of a sage. Meaning: The water of the Ganges purifies the three worlds, including the gods, because it comes from the lotus feet of Lord Vishnu. Lord Krishna is the source of Vishnu's essence, therefore his lotus feet"
