          "textEn": "397\nThey were considering it sacred, because the presence of such a saint transforms any place into a pilgrimage site.\n. By the remembrance of the Lord, the houses are immediately purified. That by the sight of the feet, the cleansing of the body, and the act of sitting. 33). Shabdartham\nYesham- Of whom; Sansmaranat- From memory; Punasam- Of a man; Sadyah- Immediately; Shuddhayanti- Become pure; Vai- Certainly;\nGrihaah- All houses; Kim- What; Punah- Again; Darshan- Meeting; Sp- Touching; Pada Pavam- Feet; Shauch Dhoone- Washing; Asan- etc. - Seat\nBy merely remembering you, our houses become immediately pure. So, to see you, to touch you,\nTo wash your holy feet and to provide you with a seat in your house, what more can I say? Meaning: The importance of holy pilgrimage sites is due to the presence of great sages and saints.\nIt is said that sinful people go to holy places and leave their sins there, so that they\nare accumulated there. But with the presence of great saints, that place becomes free from the pollution of accumulated sins\nand in this way, by the grace of the devotees and saints present there, that holy place remains holy. If such saints appear in the homes of worldly people, then surely the accumulated sins of worldly devotees\nbegin to be pacified. Therefore, the householders of the holy saints have no selfishness; their only\npurpose is to purify the homes of householders. Therefore, when such saints and great souls come to the door, then householders\nshould be grateful to them. The householder who disregards such sacred commands is a great offender.\nTherefore, it is an order that the householder who does not bow his head upon seeing the saint, should fast on that day\nto neutralize his great sin. By the presence of the great yogis, even the great ones are destroyed.\nThey are immediately destroyed, like Vishnu and other gods. 34)."
