          "textEn": "398\n\nMeaning of the word:\nSatnidhyat-- due to presence; Te-- yours; Maha-yogin-- these great yogis; Patakani- all sins; Mahanti- impenetrable;\nApi- despite; Sadyah- immediately; Nashanti- get destroyed; Vai- certainly; Pumsa- person; Vishnu- God's\npresence; Iva- like; Sur- others besides; Devas- deities..\n\nJust as an atheist cannot stand in the presence of God, similarly, O saint, O great one,\neven the invincible sins of a man are immediately destroyed in your presence, O.\n\nMeaning: There are two categories of humans -- atheists and devotees of God. Because a devotee of God\nmanifests divine qualities, he is called a deity, while an atheist is called an Asura (demon).\nIn the presence of Lord Vishnu, an Asura (demon) cannot stand.\nThe demons are always engaged in destroying God,\nbut the fact is that as soon as God appears through his name, form, qualities, pastimes, attire, or diversity,\nthe demon is immediately destroyed. It is said that as soon as the name of God\nis chanted, the ghost runs away. Great saints and devotees are included in the list of God's belongings.\nAnd as soon as a saint-like devotee appears, all the sin-like ghosts\nare immediately destroyed. This is the decision of all the Vedic texts.\nTherefore, for a human, it is only recommended to associate with saints and devotees,\nso that worldly demons and ghosts cannot cast their evil influence.\nEven if God is pleased, Krishna is dear to the sons of Pandu.\nFor the sake of pleasing the father, those relatives of that lineage. 35). Meaning of the word:\nApi- certainly; Me-to me; Bhagavan-- God; Preetah-- pleased; Krishnah-- God; Pandu-Sut-- son of King Pandu;\nFora: - dear; Pitru-- related to father; Swaseya-- son of sister; Preeti- satisfaction; Artham- regarding; Tat-- theirs;\nGotrasya- descendants; Atta- accepted; Bandhavah- as a friend;\nLord Krishna, who is very dear to the sons of King Pandu, has accepted me also as a relative to please his great brothers. Meaning: A pure, unique devotee of God serves his family, in false family matters,\nmore than out of interest, with a better intention. Generally, people are attached to family matters"
