कृत गुरु थे, अतएव",
          "textEn": "399\nremains and the entire economic force of human society is driven by family affection. Such deluded people do not have enough information that they can serve their family better by becoming devotees of God. God provides special protection to the family members and descendants of his devotee,\neven if these members themselves are non-devotees! Maharaj Prahlad was a great devotee of God,\nBut his father Hiranyakashipu was a terrible atheist and openly declared himself an enemy of God. But even with so much,\nEven after all this, Hiranyakashipu was granted salvation because he was the father of Maharaj Prahlad. God is so merciful that he provides all the protection to the family members of his devotee, so that the devotee\ndoes not need to worry about his family, to the extent that even if devotion\nto do, he may even leave such members.\nMaharaj Yudhishthir and his brother were the sons of Kunti, and\nKunti was Krishna's aunt. Maharaj Parikshit, being the only grandson of the great Pandavas, accepts the protection of God\nKrishna.\nOtherwise, how can we not see the unseen?\nThe other beloved ones are the accomplished ones of the forest. 36). Meaning of the word:\nOtherwise, otherwise; T— yours; Avyakta-gatih— without being visible; Darshanam-meeting, encounter; Nah-- for us;\nKatham-how; Nram-of the people; Nitaram-especially; Priyamananam-of the beloved; Sansiddhasthah-of the perfect;\nVanijasah-by their own will.\n\nOtherwise (without the inspiration of Lord Krishna), how is it possible that you voluntarily here\nappeared, while you wander away from ordinary people and are not visible to us, the dying\nones?\nMeaning: Certainly, Maharishi Shukdev Goswami, inspired by Lord Krishna, a great devotee of God,\nrevealed himself willingly before Maharaj Parikshit, so that he could impart the teachings of Shrimad Bhagwat. A human being can attain the essence of devotion to God only through the grace of his guru and God. Guru\nare the expressed representatives of God, helping him to achieve ultimate success. One who is not given the authority of God,\ncannot become a guru. Srila Shukadeva Goswami was the authorized guru, therefore"
