है, अपितु उन लोगों के लिए भी है जिन्होंने\nकर्मी, दार्शनिक या भगवद्भक्त के रूप में पहले ही सफलता प्राप्त कर ली है।",
          "textEn": "6. There are various types of people who are eager to achieve success in various kinds of tasks.\nGenerally, these people are materialistic, who want to enjoy material satisfaction the most. After them comes the number of spiritualists who have attained complete knowledge about the nature of material enjoyment\nand in this way they stay away from the deceptive style of life. By little or much, they remain satisfied in themselves through self-realization. There are even greater devotees of God, who neither desire to enjoy the material world,\nnor wish to get rid of it. They remain engaged in pleasing Lord Krishna. In other words, a bhagavatam guide never makes any requests for himself. If God's\nwill is there, then devotees accept all material comforts, and if God does not want it,\nthen devotees can put all kinds of comforts, even salvation, on the shelf.\nThey are not.\nThey are self-content (Atmaram) because they desire only the pleasure of God. In this verse,\nSrisukadeva Goswami praises the divine Kirtan of the Lord. By the innocent feeling of the holy name of God,\nthrough chanting and listening, a person first becomes acquainted with the divine form of God, then with the\nqualities of God, and then with the divine nature of His divine plays, etc. Here, it is mentioned that after hearing the name of God from the authorities, one should continuously chant it. Its meaning is that listening to the authorities is the first condition. By constantly listening to the holy name,\ngradually a person attains the state of listening about the form, qualities, pastimes, etc., of God,\nand in this way, there is a need for continuously chanting His glory. This method is not\nonly prescribed for the successful completion of devotion, but also for those who\nare physically attached.\nAccording to Srishukdev Goswami, this is a well-established\nmethod for achieving success, which has been established not only by him but by all other predecessor Acharyas. Therefore, there is no need to provide further evidence. This method is not only for idealists,\nbut also for those who have already achieved success as workers, philosophers, or devotees of God."
