          "textEn": "29\nIt does and in this way it prevents a person from attaining 100% self-realization. Therefore,\nShukdev Goswami says to adopt a trustworthy policy, and this is to steady the mind in the service of God.\nTo stabilize. The Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Krishna, also recommends this direct method in the Bhagavad Gita (6.47). In this way, when the mind is spiritually cleansed, a person should immediately engage in hearing, chanting, etc., and through devotional activities, in the divine love of God. If under the right guidance,\nif this is done, then even a distracted mind can definitely progress.\nMeditate on that one being, with the mind united without separation.\n\nHaving concentrated the mind on that pure abode, do not remember anything else.\n\nThat supreme abode of the mind is Vishnu, where it is pleased. 19. Meaning of the word:\nThere- after that; one-- one by one; Avayavam-- body parts; Dhyayet-- meditate; Avyuchhinneen-- from complete form;\nVitarita- without being distracted; Chetasa-- from the mind; Manah- mind; Nirvishayam- without being contaminated by objects; Yuktva- by joining; Tat- that; Paramam- supreme; Vishnu- of Vishnu;\nManah- mind; Yatra- where; Prasidati- is pleased, is delighted;\nTatpashchit, without removing the conception of the complete body of Shri Vishnu, One by one, Vishnu,\nshould meditate on the parts of the body. In this way, the mind becomes free from all objects of the senses. Then,\nno other object should remain for contemplation. Because Lord Vishnu is the ultimate truth,\ntherefore, the mind is completely absorbed in only him.\nMeaning: Being fascinated by the external power of Vishnu, foolish people do not realize that the ultimate goal of continuous search for happiness is to attain the presence of Lord Vishnu. The Vishnu Tattva is the infinite expansion of the various divine forms of God, and the supreme or original form of Vishnu Tattva is Govinda or\nKrishna, who is the cause of all causes. Therefore, contemplation of Vishnu or the divine form of Vishnu, especially of Krishna, is the ultimate limit of meditation. This meditation can be started from the lotus feet of God. But a human should not forget the complete form of God. In this way, he should\npractice contemplating each and every part of his divine body. In this verse,\nIt has been definitely assured that the Supreme Brahman is not without attributes. They are individuals, but their"
