          "textEn": "30\nThe body is different from the living beings like us. Otherwise, for the attainment of complete spiritual perfection, Shukdev,\nGoswami, did not recommend the meditation of every limb of Vishnu's embodied form, starting from the Pranava (Na-kara).\nIn the grand temples of India, the worship of Shri Vishnu idols is not idol worship, as some oe\npeople misunderstand, but these temples are spiritual centers for meditating on the divine limbs of Shri Vishnu. In the temples of Shri Vishnu, due to the inconceivable power of God, the venerable idol of God\nis inseparable from God. As Srishukdev Goswami, who is a great officer, has recommended, that\nfor those who cannot meditate on the Pranava (Omkar) or the limbs of Vishnu while sitting in one place,\nfor them, in the temple, meditating on the divine limbs of Vishnu according to the branch method, is a\neasy opportunity for meditation.\nThe common man, instead of expecting 3kar made from the divine combination of these three letters,\ncan gain more benefit by meditating on the form of Vishnu in the temple. Although there is no difference between the ukar and the forms of Vishnu,\nthose who are not aware of the science of the ultimate truth, they try to create differences by pointing out the difference between the forms of Vishnu and the Omkar. Here it is indicated\nthat the form of Vishnu itself is the ultimate goal of meditation. Therefore, it is better to concentrate the mind on the forms of Vishnu, rather than on the formless Omkara. Of these, the first method is also more difficult than the second.\nThe mind, which is restrained, is confused, and is controlled by the self.\nThe wise destroy the impurities that are created by the act of holding back. 20>. Shabdartham.\nTS: — Rajoguna; Tamobhyam-- through Tamoguna; Ashchittham-- uprooted; Vimoodham-- deluded; Manah-- mind; Atmanah-- self;\nYachhet-- to improve; Dharanaya-- by holding; Dheerah-- patient; Hanti-- destroys; Ya-- they all; Tatkritam-- done by them;\nMalam-- dirty things..\nThe human mind is always distracted by the quality of Rajas and deluded by the quality of Tamas. But man can correct such beliefs by relating them to Lord Vishnu, and thus\ncan become calm by cleaning the dirty things produced by them. Meaning: Those who are generally driven by Rajo and Tamo Gunas are not authentic vessels for attaining divine realization. The person driven by the quality of goodness is the ultimate truth"
