त कर सकता है।",
          "textEn": "3\nCan acquire knowledge. The influence of Rajo and Tamo Guna appears excessive towards Kanchan and Kamini.\nDue to excessive desire. And those who are after Kanchan and Kamini, they can improve their\nattitudes by constantly remembering the powerful, formless form of Lord Vishnu.\nCan. Generally, the Nirvisheshvadi or Advaitavadi is influenced by Rajo and Tamoguna. Such\nNirvisheshvadis consider themselves liberated souls, but they know nothing about the divine, tangible form of the ultimate truth. In reality, due to their lack of knowledge about the concrete form of Brahman, their\ninner self remains impure. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that after hundreds of births, a non-different thinker\ntakes refuge in God. To attain the ability to realize the embodied form of God,\nto get initiated, the novice non-differentialist is given the opportunity to realize the relationship of God with every object through the philosophy of Brahmavada.\nIn its higher state, Brahman does not allow any seeker to form a non-different perception of the ultimate truth,\nbut rather it extends this perception of the ultimate truth to the realm of so-called physical power. All objects created by physical power can be connected with Brahma through service, which is an essential part of life force. A pure devotee of God, through his service, every\nobject becomes aware of the art of transforming into spiritual power, and through this devotional method,\ncan fully provide the principle of Brahmanism.\nYasyam sandharyamanayam yogino bhakti-lakshanah.\nAashu sampadyaate yog ashrayam bhadramikshatah. 21). Meaning of the word\nYasyam- from this well-planned remembrance; Sandharyamanayam- by being stable in such practice; Yoginah- the yogis; Bhakti-\nLakshanah- by practicing Bhakti-Yoga; Ashu- quickly; Samyadayate- achieves success; Yogah- the relation of Bhakti-Yoga;\nAshrayam- under shelter; Bhadram- welfare; Ikshatah- seeing GUL\nOh king, by this method of remembrance and 