          "textEn": "47\nThere is mention of offering to many deities by various names, but in this verse, it\nsuggests that all those deities are inherent in the form of God. They are only a part of the whole. In the same way,\nthe various castes of human society--such as Brahmins (the enlightened caste), Kshatriyas (the administrators), Vaishyas (the merchant\ncastes), and Shudras (the laborer caste)--are contained within the body of God. Therefore, these are recommended to be offered to God with available\nobjects, to perform Yagya (sacrificial ritual). Generally, ghee and\nfood are offered, but with the progress of time, human society has transformed the material nature of God\ninto various kinds of goods, producing many things. Therefore,\nhuman society should not only learn to offer to Shiva; but also to spread the glory of God,\none should offer to other prepared goods as well. This will bring completeness to human society.\nFor such yagyas,\nthe intelligent caste people, that is, Brahmins, can advise and give instructions by consulting the predecessor Acharyas. The administrative class can provide all the facilities for such yagyas to be completed, the Vaishya class or\nthe commercial caste, which produces such goods that can be offered in the yagya, and the Shudra class can provide\nphysical labor to successfully complete such a yagya. Thus, with the cooperation of all the classes of mankind,\nthe yagya that is prescribed in this era is that of the holy name of God, which can be completed throughout the world\nfor the welfare of mankind. Iyansavi Shwar-vigrahasya\nYaha Sannivesha Krito Maya Te.\nBeing engaged in this body, firmly established,\nWith mind, with self-intellect, whatever is there. 38. Meaning of the word\nIyaan- all these; Asau-- that; Ishwar- of God; Vigrahasya- of form; Yah- that which; Sannivesha- in the way they are situated;\nKathitah- said; Maya- by me; Te- to you; Sandharyate- can concentrate; Asmin- in this; Vapushi- in the body; Manah-