ऊपर-ऊपर उठते हुए उनके मुसकाते मुख तक आना चाहिए।",
          "textEn": "7]\nWhen one becomes free from the intoxication of lust through the refinement of intellect, then one should proceed to meditate.\nThat is, in other words, the meditation on the various parts of God's divine body should be increased in proportion to the purity of the heart. The conclusion is that those who are still engrossed in lust\nand are trapped, should never focus on the parts above the feet of God, therefore they\nshould limit themselves to reciting only the first two cantos of Shrimad Bhagavat. Man should first complete the process of purification by assimilating the subject matter of the first nine skandhas.\nShould want. Then he must be allowed to enter the Dasham Skandha of Shrimad Bhagavat.\nOne should contemplate the essence of each of these.\nOne should hold the feet of those who are covered by the mud of the gada (mace).\nOne should hold the place of victory, avoiding defeat.\nOne purifies the supreme, the supreme, as the wise understand. 93. Meaning of the word\nOne-one-one-one-one, or one after another; ignorant--organs; meditative--with attention; Anubhavayet--to meditate;\nPad-adi--feet etc.; Yavat--until; Hasitam--smiling; Gadabhrutah--God; Jitam Jitam--slowly the mind\nControlling; Sthanam--place; Apohya- leaving; Dharayet- to meditate; Param Param- higher than higher; Shuddhayati-\nbecomes pure; Dhih- intellect; Yatha Yatha- as much as;\nStarting the process of meditation from the lotus feet of God, bring it to his smiling face. In this way, first focus the attention on the lotus feet, then on the calves, then\non the thighs, and gradually rise upwards. The more the mind is fixed on each and every part of God,\nthe more refined the intellect will be.\nMeaning: The method of meditation that has been prescribed in Shri Bhagavat is not for any particular object or\nto fix the mind on nothingness. Attention should be focused on God, whether it is\ntheir immense form, that is, the immense universal form, or the true form of their blissful embodiment described in the scriptures. There are authentic descriptions of Vishnu's forms and authentic replicas of the archaic icons in temples. In this way, a person can begin to meditate on the idol, in which he should concentrate his mind on the lotus feet of God,\nand gradually rise upwards, reaching the smiling face of the Lord."
