निर्विशेषवादी तथा शून्यवादी अपने आध्यात्मिक कार्य-कलापों में पर्याप्त शुद्ध नहीं होते, अतएव",
          "textEn": "72\nAccording to Bhagavata-Vedanta, the rasanritya of the Lord is the rasamudra of the Lord. Because\nIn this verse, the conclusion is given that man, while meditating on the lotus feet of God, smiling,\nrises up gradually to the face, therefore we should not leap to understand the pastimes of God in Rasanritya.\nFor that, we should not jump. It would be better if we practice concentrating our attention by offering flowers and basil leaves on the lotus feet of God. In this way, slowly, we become pure through the method of worship. We dress God, we bathe him, etcetera, etcetera, all the\nall the divine activities happen. They help us in making our life pure.\nWhen we reach the higher level of purity,\nand if we see the beautiful face of God or hear the THA of God,\nthen we can taste the essence of his activities. That is why\nin Shrimad Bhagavat, Rasleela is quoted in the tenth canto (chapters 29-34).\nThe more a person concentrates his mind on the divine form of God, whether it is on the lotus feet,\nor on the palms, or on the thighs, or on the chest, the purer he becomes. In this verse,\nit is clearly stated that, “The more refined the intellect will be, \" which means that man\nthe more he becomes detached from sensual pleasure, the more refined the intellect will be. In the present bound\nstate, our intellect is impure, because it remains busy in sense gratification. Of God,\nThe fruit of meditating on the divine form will manifest through the detachment from the senses of man, therefore the ultimate purpose of meditation\nis the purification (refinement) of one's intellect.\nThose people who live in excessive indulgence, they should not be allowed to participate in worship or touch the divine form of Radha-Krishna\nor Vishnu Archa-Vigraha. For them,\nIt would be more appropriate that they meditate on the immense form of God, as it is said in the next verse. Therefore, the nirvishishtavadis and shunyavadis are advised to meditate on the immense form of God,\nbut devotees are encouraged to meditate on the archa-vigraha in the temple. Because\nThe nihilists and the voidists are not sufficiently pure in their spiritual activities, therefore"
