          "textEn": "76\nThe ultimate consequence is in the search for nuclear particles. ©. But when the mind works under spiritual emotion,\nit works in a surprising way to go back to its home, that is, the abode of God, for complete joy and eternity in life.\nTherefore, the mind should be well-organized through excellent and pure intellect. The perfect intellect is meant to serve God. A human being\nshould understand this much that a living being is a slave to all circumstances. Every living being\nserves according to the commands of desire, anger, lust, delusion, madness, and envy, and all of these\nare influenced by materialism.\nBut to follow the orders of all these senses, he constantly\nremains sad. When he truly experiences it and uses his intellect to search for it from the right sources,\nhe realizes the divine love and devotion to God. Then the intellect, body,\ndoes not serve the materiality of the above-mentioned rasas (emotions), but is freed from the painful illusion of a materialistic mentality,\nand thus the mind, with pure intellect, engages in the service of God. O Lord,\nand their service is inseparable because it is on the supreme plane.\nTherefore, the unmixed intellect and mind become one with God.\nIn this way, the individual soul no longer remains a seer; rather, the visible becomes through the divine qualities of God.\nWhen the individual is directly seen by God, He commands the individual according to His will.\nAnd when the individual begins to fully obey His commands, the individual ceases to perform other tasks for their\ndelusive gratification. The individual, in their pure state, experiences complete bliss,\nand becomes free from all material desires. Where is the timeless, all-seeing Lord?\nWhere are the gods for the world?\nWhere there is neither goodness nor evil,\nNeither change nor greatness is predominant. 17). Meaning of the word\nNa- not; Yatra- where; Kalah- destructive time; Animisham- of the gods; Parah- superior; Prabhuh-