          "textEn": "97\n\n(6) If sufficient care is not taken, then irrigation will only increase weeds,\nA healthy vine will remain stunted, due to which the fruit of divine love will not be able to grow in it.\n\n(7) Therefore, the devotee should completely destroy various weeds at the beginning itself. Then,\nthe main vine can have healthy growth and it will not remain stunted.\n\n(8) By doing this, the devotee gets to taste the fruit of divine love, and he can live with Lord Krishna in his own\nlife and can have darshan (sight) of God at every step.\n\nThe highest achievement in life is to continuously enjoy the eternal happiness of life in constant association with God, and\nwhoever has tasted it, does not desire any momentary pleasure of the material world in any other way. Tenatmanatmanamupeti shantah\nManandamanandamayo avasane.\nHe who has gone to this path, the glorious one,\nThat one is not known by the poison of attachment. 31st. Meaning of the word\n\nTen--that pure; Atmana--by the soul; Atmanam--to the Supreme Soul; Upaiti--obtains; Shantam--peace; Anandam--\nhappiness; Anandamayah--being naturally so; Avasane--being free from all material impurities; Etam-Esa;\nGatim--to reach; Bhagavatim--devoted; Gatah--reached; Yah--who; Sah-He; He; Vai-Certainly; Punah-Again; Na--Never; Iha-In this world; Vishajanate--attracted; Anga-Oh, Maharaj Parikshit..\n\nOnly the pure soul can attain the completeness of the company of God in its natural state, complete.\nWith joy and satisfaction. Whoever is able to awaken such devotional completeness again,\nis not attracted to this material world again, and\nnever returns to it. Note: The verse describes the movement of Bhagavati.\nBy the Brahmavadi-Nirvishishtavadi, the desired Parabrahma, the God, is not fully attained by the rays of the Bhagavati. The devotees of the Bhagavata never\nwant to be absorbed in the unique rays of God. They always aspire to be in the spiritual sky, in some\none Vaikuntha world, in the company of God. The entire spiritual sky"
