he complete being.\nUdar-dhi: means broad-sighted or broad-minded. Those who desire material pleasures,\nthey worship small deities. In the Bhagavad Gita (7.20), such intellect is called 'hrutgya,' meaning such\na person's intellect that has become HIE, is condemned. Any person of God"
