          "textEn": "35. When the donkey is tempted for intercourse, the donkey gets angry, yet the donkey for intercourse\nstays behind it. Therefore, a wife's slave is compared to a donkey. The common people,\nIn this Kali Yuga, especially, work very hard. He remains engaged in the work of a donkey, he carries heavy\nburdens and pulls I and rickshaws. The so-called development of human civilization has kept man engaged in the work of donkeys. Even in large factories and workshops, laborers are engaged in heavy work,\nand after working hard all day, the poor laborer is not only at home for\npleasure but also for many household chores, his wife is addicted to it. Therefore, it is not an exaggeration to say that a common man, without spiritual light, is placed in the category of pigs, porkers, camels,\nor donkeys. Even if the leaders of such an ignorant group of people\nare proud to be worshiped by all pigs, but this is no respect.\nBhagwat is open.\nIt declares that even if a person is a leader of humans in the guise of such cookers and pigs, but if\nhe is not interested in being aware of Krishna's science, then such a person is nothing but an animal. He can be called a powerful, strong animal or a huge animal, but according to the Shrimad Bhagwat,\nhe can never be placed in the category of man due to his atheistic nature. Or in other words, the godless leaders of individuals like cookers -pigs -are greater than even animals,\nin which the ratio of brutal qualities is greater.\nThose who do not listen to the stories of the kings,\nThey do not listen to the stories of the kings.\nThey do not listen to the stories of the kings,\nThey do not listen to the stories of the kings. 20>. Meaning of the word\nBille--snake's hole; Bat--sight; Urukram--God who performs wondrous deeds; Vikramanu--Bravery; Ye- all these; Na--never; Shrunvat--hearing; Karnam--in the ear; Kharanam--in the ear; Jihna--tongue; Asti--never; Dardurika--of frogs\nof; Iva--like; Soot--Oh Soot Goswami; Na