रीष ने। अतएव\nभगवद्‌भक्त न केवल भगवान्‌ से अधिक शक्तिशाली होता है, अपितु भक्त की पूजा भी भगवान्‌ की\nप्रत्यक्ष पूजा से अधिक प्रभावशाली मानी जाती है ( मद्भक्तपूजाध्यधिका) |",
          "textEn": "64\nThey originate from Him, yet they remain complete as they were (Purnamaday Purnamayavashishyate).\nTherefore, the material concept of God created by the wise has no validity. In this way, they\n(God) always remain a mystery to the worldly scholar, even if he is very\npious in Vedic literature. Therefore, God is completely beyond the perceptions of worldly scholars,\nphilosophers, or scientists. They are easily accessible by pure devotees, because\nIn Bhagavad Gita (18.54), God declares that when someone transcends the state of knowledge\nand becomes absorbed in devotion to God, only then can they understand the true nature of God.\nUntil one is engaged in devotion to God, one cannot have a clear understanding of God or His holy name, form,\ncharacteristics, pastimes, etc. This statement of the Bhagavad Gita that\nfirst man should be freed from all other engagements and surrender to God, it indicates that\nman should be a pure, liberated devotee of God. Only then can he know them through the power of devotion. ©\n\nIn the previous verse, Maharaj Parikshit admitted that even for the scholars greater than the great,\nGod is incomprehensible. So why do they request Shukdev Goswami to clarify his incomplete knowledge?\nWhy? The reason is obvious. Shukdev Goswami was not only a profound scholar in Vedic literature, but he\nwas also a great, self-realized person and a devotee of God with power.\nBy the grace of God, a powerful devotee of God is greater than God himself. Lord Shriramchandra, after building a bridge over the Indian Ocean,\nwas trying to reach the island of Lanka, but his unique devotee, Shri Hanumanji, jumped and crossed that\nocean. God is so merciful to his devotees that he presents his beloved devotees\nMore than himself. God had expressed his inability to protect Durvasa Muni\nGiven, although Durvasa Muni was so powerful that he directly reached God in physical forms. But Durvasa Muni was protected by a devotee of God, that is, King Ambarisha. Therefore,\nA devotee is not only more powerful than God, but the worship of the devotee is also considered more effective than the direct worship of God."
