          "textEn": "93\nWhether it is life or spiritual touch. Therefore, the hidden God is of all truths, not a gross substance,\nAs a delusion, the materialist thinks. From Vedic literature, we come to know that first\nGod entered the void of the physical universe and then all the things developed one by one.\nSimilarly, God is present in every creature's home as the Supreme Soul, therefore, by them\nall tasks are accomplished well. Sixteen major creative elements, whose names are Earth, Water,\nFire, Air, Sky, and eleven senses, were developed from God himself and then went to the beings. In this way, the creation of physical elements was done for the enjoyment of living beings. Therefore, the beautiful arrangement behind all physical\nexpressions is possible by the power of God, and every\nbeing can only pray to God to understand it properly. Because God is supreme consciousness,\nand is different from Shukadeva Goswami, therefore his prayer should be known.\nGod, of the material creation,\nhelps the living being in enjoying, but they remain separate from such false enjoyment. Shukdev Goswami\nprays to God to bestow grace so that he himself may find help in presenting the truth,\nas well as help those whom he is about to narrate. Salutations to Lord Vasudeva, the auspicious one. Pampuranamayam Saumyayanmukham Bumruhasavam. 24). Meaning of the word:\nNamah--My salutations; Tasmai--To Him; Bhagavate--To the Lord; Vasudevaya--To Vasudeva or his incarnations; Vedase--Compilers of Vedic texts;\nPapuha--Drinker; Gnanam--Knowledge; Ayam--This Vedic knowledge; Saumyah--Devotees, especially Lord Krishna's\nlovers; Yat--Of whom; Mukha-Amburuh--Like a lotus face; Asavam--Nectar.\nI respectfully bow to Srila Vyasadeva, the incarnation of Vasudeva, who\ncompiled the Vedic scriptures. Pure devotees, falling from the lotus-like face of God,\ndrink the nectar-like divine knowledge, O.\nMeaning: While explaining the word 'Vedase', Srila Sridhar Swami has commented that by this 