          "textEn": "95\nInformation can be obtained © | That is why Brahmaji was full of perfect knowledge, so that he could be able to create\n. Therefore, Brahmaji was aware of the complete details of creation, because Lord Hari had made him aware of it. When Narad asked Brahma a question, he told Narad exactly as\nhe had heard from God himself. Narad told Vyas exactly this and Vyas also narrated to Shukdev\nGoswami in the same way that he had heard from Narad. Shukdev Goswami, those very things\nWere going to narrate to whom he had heard from Vyasa. This is the only way to understand Vedic knowledge. Only through the aforementioned tradition can the language of the Vedas be understood, otherwise not.\n\nThere is no benefit from theories. Knowledge should be real. There are many such things,\nthat are complex and no one understands them until they are told by a knower.\nIt is also difficult to know Vedic knowledge.\nHe should learn from the above system, otherwise he does not understand. Therefore, Shukdev Goswami prayed to God to have mercy, so that he could repeat the message directly spoken by him to Brahma, or what Brahma said to Narada. Therefore,\nthe creation-related statements described by Shukdev Goswami are not theoretical, as some worldly people say,\nbut are completely true. He who listens to these messages (stories) and tries to assimilate them,\nreceives complete information about the material creation. Thus, under the second canto of Srimad Bhagavat, the \"Suti process\" of the fourth chapter of the hero,\nthe Bhakti Vedanta meaning is completed."
