          "textEn": "24\nFrom the spots that sometimes appear in the infinite expanse of the rays of God's Brahmajyoti,\nremain unaffected. The cause-effect-action-knowledge-action-abode:\nThey bind the eternal, liberated, free, and unmanifest, the Supreme Being. 99. Meaning of word\n\nEffect of action, result; cause-- cause; in the sense of doer-- in the works; substance-- substance; knowledge-- knowledge; action-dependent-- dependent; eternal-- eternal; liberated-- divine; influenced by material power-- influenced by material power; the individual-- to the living being;\nQualities-- physical qualities \\\n\nThese three qualities of physical nature, later on, manifest as matter, knowledge, and actions,\nand by becoming such, they put the divine being under the bondage of cause and effect, and for such actions,\nthey make him responsible.\nMeaning: Since the eternal conscious being is situated between the inner and outer powers, therefore they\nare called the stationary power of God. In reality, the living being is not bound by physical power,\nbut due to the false feeling of dominating physical power, they become subject to such power\nand thus become bound by the three qualities. This external power of God, it veils the pure knowledge of that being,\nwhich is eternally with God. This covering is so permanent\nthat the bound soul appears eternally ignorant. The influence of Maya or external energy is so amazing\nas if it has originated from ghosts. Due to the enveloping strength of physical energy, the physicist\ncannot see beyond physical causes, but in reality, behind physical manifestations, there are super-bodily, spiritual\nand divine actions, which the Tamoguni bound soul cannot see.\nUnder the superimposed expression,\nincluding old age and disease, there is a repetition of birth and death; in spiritual expression, the soul is bound.\nAnd the superimposed expression is a regulatory system. These are the physical manifestations of responsibility in causal and