मित्त मात्र बन जाये तो ऐसा कर सकता है । इन्द्रियों को कभी उनके व्यापारो से रोकना नहीं चाहिए",
          "textEn": "225\n\nThey come. Meaning: Vaikarika is the indifferent state of creation, and Tejas is the beginning of creation, while Tamas\nunder the ignorance, this physical creation is the complete display. In factories and workshops, the creation of the necessities of life\nis the most important in Kali Yuga, and this creation is the highest\nstate of ignorance. Human society is enriched with such constructive industries in the quality of darkness, because in reality\nthere is no need for manufactured materials. Human society is fundamentally in need of food for its sustenance,\nshelter for sleeping, protection for protection, and desire for objects for sensual gratification. The senses are practical signs of life, as will be explained in the next verse. Human civilization is for the purification of the senses and the fulfillment of the objects of sensual gratification\nshould only be according to need, not to provoke artificial sensory needs\nfor.\nFood, shelter, security, and sense gratification are the necessities of physical life. Otherwise, in the pure, original state of life, the living being does not need these. Therefore,\nthe needs are artificial, and such needs do not arise in the pure state of life. This\nincreasing artificial needs, as if it has become the standard of material civilization, or of human society,\nto do economic development is, in a way, to wander in darkness without knowledge. From such busyness,\nthe power of man is destroyed, because human power is to purify the senses, so that they\ncan be used to satisfy the senses of God. God is the master of all senses, Hashikesh,\nbecause he is the possessor of spiritual senses. Hashik means senses and Ish means\nLord. Lord is not a slave to the senses, in other words, he does not act on the direction of the senses. Yes,\nBound beings or living beings are slaves to special senses.\nThey follow the signals of the senses, that's why this\nPhysical civilization is, in a way, merely a distraction from the satisfaction of the senses. The standard of human civilization should be the treatment of the disease of satisfaction of the senses,\nand if someone becomes merely an instrument for satisfying the spiritual senses of God,\nthen they can do so. The senses should never be stopped from their functions"
