          "textEn": "24]\nFor the enemies of the war, whatever sacrifices are offered.\nHair, nails, and other things, along with stone, iron, and lightning.5>. Meaning of the word\nRomani--the hair of the body; Udadhi--vegetation; Jatinam--of species; Yaih- by which; Va--or; Yagya--sacrifice; Tu--but;\nSambhrithah-- especially served; Kesha--hair; Amshru-mri; Nakhani--nails; Asya- his; Shila-stone; Loha-iron\nAyaskan; ANY--cloud; Vidyutam- lightning.\nTheir body hair is due to all kinds of vegetation, especially those trees,\nwhich serve as material (parts) of the Yagya (sacrificial fire). Their head and face hair are the abode of clouds,\nand their nails are the origin of lightning, stones, and iron ores.\nMeaning: The shiny nails of God generate lightning, and all the clouds are on the hair of his head.\nThey stay on the hair.\nTherefore, all kinds of essential things for life can be gathered from the body of God.\nThat is why the Vedas confirm that God is the cause of all created things.\nGod is the supreme cause of all causes.\nBahvo lokapalanam prayashchit karmanam. 6>. Meaning of the word\nBahav:--Arms; Lokapalanam--Lords of the worlds or of the gods; Prayashah Prayashah; Kshem-Karmanam--Of the people--Common\nOf the leaders and protectors..\nThe arms of God are the origin of other heroes who protect great gods and the common people. Meaning: This important verse of Shrimad Bhagavatam is explained in the Bhagavad Gita (10.41-42) as follows--\nThat which is the essence of all glories, that which is the truth, is indeed the best of all. That alone you have come to me, that alone is the source of my light. Or by many, or by going, then Arjuna. I am the one who is present in everything, in every particle of the world. All powerful kings, leaders, scientists, artists, sculptors, explorers, archaeologists, industrialists,"
