          "textEn": "250\nSah--He; Amrutasya--Of immortality; Abhayasya--Of fearlessness; Ishah Niyanta; Martyamu-Damarshi; Annam-Sakam\nKarma; Yat-Which; Atyagat-Crossed; Mahima-Glory; Eshah-His; Tatah-Therefore; Brahman-Oh Brahmin Narada;\nPurushasya-Of man; Duratyaya-Beyond\n\nThe complete Supreme Being, the Lord, is the controller of immortality and fearlessness, and He is beyond the desires of death and the material\nworld. Hey Narad, Hey Brahmin, therefore, it is difficult to estimate the glory of the Supreme Being. Meaning: The divine seventy-five percent of the inner power of God is the glory of God, which\nis described in Padma Purana (Uttar Khanda). It is said in it that the spiritual sky is the seventy-five percent of the inner power of God,\nin which the situated worlds are structured from the outer power of God,\nare much larger than the worlds of the entire universe. In Chaitanya-Charitagata, God's outer power\nhas compared the entire universe to a bucket full of mustard seeds.\nEach mustard seed within itself is like a universe. In one of these universes, in which we are living now, the ability to count the number of worlds\nis beyond the power of a human, so how can we think about all those universes\nwhich are like a bucket full of mustard seeds? Not only this, in the spiritual sky, the number of worlds\nis at least three times greater than the physical sky. Such people, being spiritual,\nare beyond physical qualities, therefore they are only made of pure Satoguna. In these worlds,\nthe dominance of divine bliss remains. Each of these is eternal, imperishable, and free from all kinds of madness experienced in the physical world. Each of these worlds is self-illuminated, and\nis far more dazzling than the light of millions of physical suns (if we can imagine it). The inhabitants of those worlds are free from birth, death, old age, and disease, and they have complete knowledge of everything.\nThey are all endowed with Bhagavad-bhava and devoid of material thirsts. They have to do nothing more than the divine loving service of that God\nNarayan, who is the chief Shrivigraha of such Vaikuntha Loka. They are ever busy in singing the songs of Samaveda (Veda.\nSangapadakrayopanishadgavinti ya samagaha). They are all direct quotes from all five Upanishads. Trirupad Vibhuti,\nWhich is 75 percent of the inner power of God, that abode of God is, which is from the physical sky"
