          "textEn": "252\nThere is no need to try to get it. Happiness is the nature of the soul, as it is said in the Vedanta Sutra--Anandamayod dhyasat--the soul is inherently full of bliss. This happiness of the soul always keeps increasing.\nThere is no question of this joy diminishing. Such unique spiritual bliss\nis not attainable anywhere in the periphery of the physical universe, not even in the world or in the great world or\neven in the realm of truth, because Brahmaji is also bound by desire-driven actions and the laws of birth and death. Therefore,\nIt is said here, 'Duratyayah' or in other words, the spiritual happiness of the divine abode cannot be imagined by even the greatest\ngreat celibate or renunciant, who are worthy of attaining realms beyond heaven. Or\nGod is so great that even great celibates or monks cannot imagine His greatness,\nbut by the grace of God, the unique devotees of God truly attain this happiness.\n\nIn the feet, all beings know the state of being in the position of men.\nAmritam kshemam bhayam trimurdho adhayi murdhasu. 19. Meaning:\nIn the feet, one-fourth; all--all; beings--living beings; the Supreme Being; the abode of all material opulence;\nKnow this--You know; immortal--Immortal; safety--Free from worry about happiness, old age, disease, etc.; fearless--Fearless; frst--\nBeyond the three higher realms; existing--Existing; beyond the material coverings--\nThe Supreme Being, the complete Supreme Being, is known as the supreme abode of all material opulence, in which all living beings are residing. The abode of God, which is three higher\nworlds and beyond material coverings, in that immortality, fearlessness, and freedom from old age and disease\nare eternally residing. Meaning: One-fourth of the total expression of the divine's power is manifested in the physical world,\nand three-fourths in the spiritual world. There are three parts of the power of God-- Santhini,\nSavit and Hladini.\nIn other words, they are completely o