          "textEn": "279\nAs Shri Krishna, he is separate from the created universe. The Nirvisheshvadi emphasize the Nirvishesh form of God,\nand do not believe in the original personality of God, but the Vaishnavas accept the original form of God,\nwhose Nirvishesh form is only one among many forms. The concrete and\nformless concepts of God are found together, and in the Bhagavad Gita and Srimad Bhagavatam, and in other\nVedic scriptures, this fact has been clearly described. This idea is unimaginable for human intellect,\ntherefore it should be accepted on the basis of the evidence of the scriptures. Its practical experience\nis only possible when there is progress in devotion, not based on any mental contemplation or dry reasoning. The non-specialists mostly depend on dry reasoning, therefore they remain in darkness regarding the original Lord Shri Krishna.\nTheir concept of Krishna is not clear, although it is clearly found in all\nVedic scriptures.\nFrom limited knowledge, the existence of the original, formless form of God cannot be understood, because God is pervasive in all things. This imperfection is due to this physical\nperception that the object that gets distributed into its parts, it cannot remain in its original (root) form.\nIt cannot remain existing. The first God (Adi) Govinda, as the incarnation of Mahavishnu, expands himself and rests in the Karanaravana created by him. In Brahma-Sahita (5.47), its confirmation is this--\n\nHe who worships the ocean of causality in the water of causality,\n\nThe one who is the support of the universe, the ocean, the lotus, and the cave,\n\nRelying on the power of support, the supreme form,\n\nThe first lord, Govinda, I am TH. In the Brahma Samhita, Brahmaji says, \"I worship the complete Lord Govinda, who is in the form of Mahavishnu, lying in Karanaravana, and from whose divine body's every pore, all\nthe universes are created, and who remains in eternal Yoganidra.\"''"
