          "textEn": "374. Therefore, all the land of the universe came to Bali Maharaj, and he began to generously give donations to the Brahmins. As a result, God disguised himself as a Brahmin mendicant and asked Bali Maharaj for three paces of land. God is the master of all things, therefore, if he wanted, he could have taken all the land of Bali Maharaj, but he did not do so, because Bali had obtained all this land according to the rights of the king. When God asked Bali Maharaj for such a trivial donation, then Bali's\nguru Shukracharya opposed this proposal, because he knew that Vaman, as a beggar,\nwas Vishnu himself. When Bali Maharaj came to know that the beggar is indeed Vishnu, he, without caring for his guru's\norders, immediately accepted to donate the land that had gone to waste. According to this agreement,\nBhagwan Vaman measured all the land of the universe in the first two steps, and from Bali Maharaj,\nhe asked for land to place his third step.\nBali Maharaj placed his third foot on his forehead.\nHe expressed pleasure in going. In this way, whatever he had, Bali Maharaj did not lose it, but rather\nHe received blessings from God that he would remain with him as his constant companion and doorkeeper. Therefore, by dedicating everything to God, a person does not lose anything, but gains everything,\nWhose otherwise he has no hope.\n\nNartho Balerayamurkram-Pad-Shauch-\nMaapaha Shikha-Dhrutavato Vibudhaadhipatyam.\nYo Ve Pratishrutamrute Na Chikaukshadanya-\nDatmanamangka Manasa Haraye Abhimane. 98 Meaning of the word\nN-- Never; Artha-- Importance in comparison; Baleh-- Power; Ayam-- This; Urukram-Pada-Shaucham-- Shri Bhagavan\nObtained from the washing of the feet of Shri Bhagavan; Aapah-- Water; Shikha-Dhritavatah-- Of the one who holds it above the head; Vibudha-Adhipatyam- Of the gods\nPrimacy over the empire; Yah- Who; Vai- Certainly; Pratishrutam- Given word; Rite Na- Besides that; Chikirshat-\nAn effort was made; others--some others; Atmanam--one's own body; Adbh--Oh Narad; Manasa--from the mind; Haraye--to Hari;\nAbhimene--dedicated,\nBali Maharaj, who holds the lotus-footed water cleansed on his head,\nEven after being forbidden by his guru, he did not hold anything else in his mind besides his word. The King offered his body to complete the thirtieth step of the great journey to the Divine."
