          "textEn": "39\nBy doing one, fourteen Manus change ©. In this way, in one month of Brahma, there are 420 Manus, and in one year,\nthere are 5,040 Manus. According to his calculation, Brahmaji lives for Loo years, therefore one Brahma\nhas 504,000 Manu in his lifetime. There are countless such Brahmas, and they live for the duration of a desire of Mahavishnu. In this way, we can imagine that in all the worlds, those who are equal to the fourth power of God, how do the incarnations of God work?\n\nManvantara Avatar Chakradhari, the complete Supreme God, punishes the wicked rulers of various worlds with the same power. Manvantara Avatars spread the divine glories of God. Dhanvantari, the Lord himself, is the fame-\nnamed, of the men, the great-born, quickly destroying.\nThose who are immersed in the nectar of the journey,\nAnd are taught by the Vedas of life, are in this world. 29>. Meaning of the word\n\nDhanvantari - the incarnation named Dhanvantari; cha-- and; Bhagavan-- Shri Bhagavan; Swayam eva- by himself; Kortiha- directly; Kirtiha- fame;\nNamna-- by name; Nriṁnaḥ- of the people; Rujaha- disease; Ashu- immediately; Hanti- kills; Yagye- in the Yagya; cha-- also; Bhagam- part, share; Amrutam- nectar; Ayuha- life; Aviya- from; Avardhne- obtains; Ayushya- life; Vedam- knowledge; Anushasti- instructs; Avatiya- taking incarnation; Loke- in the world; Brahmaṇḍa- in the universe; Avi- from; Avarunde- obtains; Ayu- life; Ayu- life; Ayu- life; Ayu- life; Ayu- life; Ayu- life In his Dhanvantari incarnation, God, through his direct glory, immediately cures the diseases of the living beings who are constantly suffering.\nAnd it is because of them that all the gods attain longevity.\nIn this way, God becomes ever glorified. He took out a part from the Yagyas as well.\nAnd he only initiated the science of medicine (Ayurveda) in the world.\nMeaning: As it has been said in the beginning of Shrimad Bhagwat, every object is originated from the form of Shri Bhagwan.\nTherefore, this verse conveys that Shri Bhagwan in his Dhanvantari\nincarnation also initiated Ayurveda, and in this way, this knowledge is described in the Vedas. The Vedas are the source of all knowledge, therefore all the information about how to completely cure the diseases of living beings is also described in them. The embodied souls are diseased because of the structure of the body. This body is a symbol of disease. Diseases\ncan be of various types, but they remain in the body in the same way as birth and death with each."
