लाते हैं जिसका अर्थ है कि वे परम सत्य के मार्ग का विरोध कर रहे",
          "textEn": "320\nTherefore, by the grace of God, not only do the diseases of the body and mind get cured, but the soul also constantly\ngets freedom from wandering. ©. One name of God is Dhvāśādhi, which means a source of protection from worldly diseases.\n\nKshatram kshayaya vidhinopabhrutam mahatma\nBrahma-dharugjhit-patham narakarti-lipsu.\nUddhantyasavanikantakamugra-virya-\nStrih-sapta-katvam urudhar- parashvadhena. 22). Meaning of the word\n\nKshatram--Kshatra dynasty; Kshaya--to diminish; Vidhina--by fate; Upabhrutam-- divided; Mahatma--the supreme saint, in the form of Parashurama;\nLord; Brahma-Shukka--the supreme truth of Brahma; Ujjit-Patham--one who has abandoned the supreme truth path; Naraka-Arti-Lipsu--\nOne who desires the torment of hell; Uddanti--compelled; Asau--all of them; Avanikantakam--the edge of the world; Ugra-Virya--\nThe great valiant; Tri-Sapti--twenty-one times; Krityah--completed; Urudhar--extremely sharp; Parashchadhena--with a huge axe.\n.\n\nWhen the ruling class, who were known as Kshatriyas, became corrupt from the path of the ultimate truth, and\nbecame desirous of suffering hell, then God, taking the incarnation of Parashurama Muni, destroyed those unwanted\nkings who were thorns to the earth. In this way, he eradicated the SER of the Kshatriyas through his sharp\nWH. Meaning: In any part of the universe, whether it is in this world or in other worlds, the Kshatriyas who rule are actually representatives of the almighty God, and they are instrumental in leading the people\ntowards devotion to God. Of every state and its administrator,\nwhatever the administration may be-monarchy, dictatorship, democracy, etc.-the main duty is to lead the people\ntowards realization of God. This is mandatory for all human beings, and it is the duty of the father, guru,\nand ultimately the state to lead the people in this direction.\nThe creation of the physical world happened with this\npurpose that those fallen souls can get an opportunity who, against the wishes of God,\nhave become bound by nature by acting. The power of physical nature slowly leads man to eternal sorrows and\nsufferings, or to a hellish state. Those who act against the prescribed rules of bound life,\nare called Brahmajnit-path, which means that they are opposing the path of the ultimate truth"
