          "textEn": "340\nBut in the end, unrighteousness remains, and Shiva and the angry atheists, etc., remain. All these\nAll of them live as various representatives of the power of God, who is the supreme power. Meaning: This physical world is created by the power of God, whose manifestation at the beginning of creation\nis through the penance of the primal being Brahma. Then comes the nine Prajapatis, called Maharishi. When\nthe state of sustaining creation comes, then the devotion to Lord Vishnu or the true religion, various deities and\nkings of different realms appear, who nourish the world. When this creation is about to end,\nthen first, unrighteousness manifests, then along with the angry atheists, Shiva resides. But these are nothing but different forms of God. Therefore, Brahma, Vishnu, and\nMahadev (Shiva) are different incarnations of the various qualities of nature. Vishnu is of Satoguna, Brahma is of Rajoguna,\nand Shiva is the lord of Tamoguna.\nThus, this physical creation is nothing but a transient existence.\nAnd its purpose is to provide the opportunity for liberation to those bound souls who are trapped in this physical world.\nAnd in this, the man who attains the quality of goodness under the protection of Lord Vishnu,\ndue to following the Vaishnava rules, gets the greatest opportunity to be liberated and to go to the abode of God,\nfrom where there is never to return again in this sorrowful world. Who among the heroes is worthy of being counted among the heroes?\nEven the best of kings, I am not equal to him, O poet, who is like a mountain of dust.\nHe who is like a swan, whose throat is like a flute, with three hoods,\nHe who makes the three-fold sound of the earth tremble. 40>. Meaning of the word\n\nVishnoha--of Lord Vishnu; Nu--but; Virya--valor; Gananam--in counting; Katamah--who is that; Ahathi--to do this; Iha-in this world; Yah-who; Parthivani-atomic; Api-also; Kavih-great scientist; Vimame-must have counted;\nRajansi-to the partic