          "textEn": "357\nChapter 36\nQuestions asked by King Parikshit.\nKing said,\n\"O Brahman, it is spoken by Brahman, of the virtues and demerits of the virtuous.\"\nTo whom, to whom, as Narada said, the divine vision. 1>. Meaning of the word.\n\nKing--by the king; Uvacha--said; Brahmana--by Brahmaji; Choditah--being ordered; Brahman-He is a learned Brahmin (Shukadeva Goswami); Guna-Akane-in the description of divine qualities; Agunasya--devoid of qualities, of God; Cha--and; Yasmai Yasmai-therefore; Tatha-as much; Praah-being told; Narada--Narada Muni; Deva-darshanah-He, whose listener is as excellent as a god..\n\nKing Parikshit asked Shukdev Goswami that Narad Muni, whose listeners are the fortunate listeners who were\nadvised by Shri Brahma, how did he describe the divine qualities of the attributeless God, and\nin whose presence did he speak? Meaning: Devarshi Narada was directly given the Upadesha by Brahmaji.\nBrahma was also given the sermon by God himself; therefore, the sermons given by Narada to various disciples are equivalent to the sermons given by God himself. This is the only way to understand Vedic wisdom. This, having received from God through the disciple-tradition,\nspreads throughout all the universe in descending order. But there is no opportunity to gain Vedic knowledge from a mental thinker. Therefore, wherever Narad Muni goes, he represents God, and\nhis absence is as good as God's presence. Similarly, the disciple tradition that strictly follows divine teachings\nis the most authentic, and the test of these authentic gurus is that\nin the beginning, the teachings that God gave to his devotees, and now the teachings that are given in the disciple tradition,\nthere should be no difference in them. Narad Muni, in the manner in which he distributed the divine knowledge of God,\nits description will be done in the later sections.\nIt may also seem that even before the physical creation, there was the existence of God; therefore, their\ndivine name, qualities, etc., are not indicative of any physical quality. Therefore, whenever God"
