          "textEn": "36.\nEntering: --Entering in this way; Karna-randhena--from the holes of the ear; Swanam--according to one's free state; Bhavah--\nNatural relations; Sarah-ruham--lotus flower; Dhunoti--purifies; Shamalam--qualities like lust, anger, jealousy, and pride; Krishna: --Lord Krishna; Salilasya--of the reservoir; Yatha--as; Sharath--autumn;\nThe word incarnation (that is, Srimad Bhagavatam) of the Supreme Lord Krishna,\nenters the heart of the devotee, and he sits on the lotus-flower of his emotional relationship,\nand thus washes away the dust of material associations like lust, anger, and greed. Thus it acts as a reservoir of autumnal rains in the water bodies of Gandala. Meaning: It is said that a single pure devotee of God can uplift all the fallen in the world.\nCan.\nTherefore, one who has the faith of a pure devotee like Narad or Shukdev Goswami, and who receives power from his\nguru, just as Narad received from Brahmaji, not only liberates himself from the clutches of Maya,\nbut also with the power of his pure and powerful devotion, he can uplift the entire world. Giving an analogy to the Sharadiya rain falling in muddy reservoirs is very appropriate. In the rainy season,\nthe water of all the rivers becomes muddy, but in the autumn season, when there is light rain, So, in the whole world,\nthe water of rivers becomes clean. With a small amount of a chemical, like a city water reservoir, the water of a small reservoir can be purified, but with such a small effort, the water of rivers cannot be purified. But a pure devotee of God, empowered by his power, not only can save himself,\nbut also saves many others through his association.\nIn other words, one's own impure heart can be cleansed by other methods (such as the path of knowledge or yoga), but devotion to God is so powerful that it can cleanse the hearts of all people through the devotion of a purely powerful devotee. Narad, Shukadeva Goswami, Bhagwan\nChaitanya, all the Goswamis, and after them, Srila Bhaktivinod Thakur and Srimad Bhaktisiddhanta Saraswati\nThakur, etc., like the real representatives of God, through their powerful devotion, can redeem all people.\n\nBy making sincere efforts to listen to Shrimad Bhagavat, a person becomes aware of their natural relationship with God, as a servant, friend, affection, or sweet love, and in this way"
