को जानने के इच्छुक हैं । वे ब्रह्माण्ड के आन्तरिक तथा बाहरी अवकाश के विषय में",
          "textEn": "370\nBhutalat-kakubvyom-grah-nakshatra-bhubhrutam.\nSaritasamudra-dwipanaam sambhavashraitadokasam. 95 Meaning of the word\nBhoo-patal--under the earth; Kaku- all four directions of heaven; Vyom--sky; Graha--planet, world, planet; Nakshatra- stars; Bhoo-bhrutam--of the earth;\nSaritu--river; Samudra--sea; Dwipa-an-islands; Sambhavah--origin; Cha--also; Etat--their; Okasam-of the inhabitants..\nOh, best of Brahmins, please also tell us how the spheres of the universe, the four directions of heaven,\nthe sky, planets, stars, mountains, rivers, seas, and islands, and all the various types of inhabitants of these\noriginate? Meaning: Residents of different types of terrains etc. are situated differently and they are not uniform in all\ncases. The inhabitants of the site are different from the inhabitants of water or sky. In the same way, the inhabitants of different planets and constellations of the sky are also different from each other.\nAccording to the divine law,\nno place is vacant, but the inhabitants of one place are different from another. Even to the extent that\neven in human society, the inhabitants of forests or deserts are different from the inhabitants of villages and cities. They are made according to the different properties of nature. This confluence of the laws of nature is not blindly\ndoing. Behind this system, a huge event takes place. Maharaj Parikshit, in all these matters,\nprays to know from the authentic Mahamuni Srila Shukdev Goswami. From the external and internal differences of the Pramanamanda-kosha,\nAnd also from the greatness and the rules of the Varna and Ashrama. 16). Meaning of the word\nPramanam-- expansion and measurement; Andakoshasya-- of the universe; Bahya-- outer space; Abhyantara-- inner space;\nBhedat-- in the division; Mahatam-- of great men; Cha-- also; Anucharitam-- character and actions; Varna-- castes; Ashrama-- life\nof the four ashrams; Vinischayah-- specifically describe.\n.\nAlso, please describe the external and internal specific departments of the universe, the characters of great men,\nand the works, and also describe the classification of various castes and the four ashramas of life. Meaning: Maharaj Parikshit is a unique devotee of Lord Shri Krishna, therefore he is eager to know the complete importance of God's creation. They are about the inner and outer space of the universe"
