          "textEn": "373\n\nMeaning: Of all categories of humans, whether they are one or something, the common religion is devotional service.\nIs. Even animals can be included in devotion to God, and its best example\nis presented by Bajrangbali or Hanuman Ji, a devotee of Lord Shri Ram. We have already said\nThat if the true devotee of God receives guidance, then the tribals and man-eating people\ncan also engage in devotion to God. In the Skanda Purana, there is a story of how a rogue became a devotee of God due to the influence of Shri Narad Muni.\nHow? Therefore, devotion to God is equally accessible to every living being. In different countries, in different cultural circumstances, the religious attachment that exists is clearly not the common religion of man, but rather the fundamental principle is devotional service. If any religion does not accept the supremacy of God,\neven then, it is necessary to follow the disciplinary rules prescribed by a particular leader.\nA leader of a religious sect is never the best, because such a leader comes to his position\nthrough some penance. But to become a leader, God does not have to do such disciplinary work\nas we see in the activities of Lord Krishna.\n\nBased on the duties, livelihoods, and rules of society's castes and ashrams, devotion\nalso depends on principles. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that a person can attain the ultimate perfection of life merely by offering the fruits of his actions\nin devotion to God. One who worships God\ndoes not suffer any hardship, therefore there is no question of disaster. As\nThe supreme authority, Srila Shukadeva Goswami, will explain in this book, besides devotion to God, there is no\nother religion, even if it does not appear in various forms.\nThe characteristic of enumeration of elements is the characteristic of cause.\nOf the spiritual method of worshiping the Supreme Being. 99. Meaning of word\n\nOf the elements that create the creation of elements; Parisadhyanam-- of