          "textEn": "377\n\nThere are many things for that, and one should learn them from a trustworthy great man like Shukdev Goswami. The appropriate situation for performing devotional service is that the service to God should be done with great enthusiasm.\nGod, in the form of his Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu, has wished that in every corner of the world,\nthe propagation of the Bhakti sect should be done; therefore, it is the supreme duty of a pure devotee that as far as possible,\nhe should fulfill this order. Every devotee should not only be enthusiastic about daily devotional practices,\nbut also should peacefully propagate the sect by following the footsteps of Lord Chaitanya. If he does not get success in this superficially, then he should not be averse to his duty.\nShould not be. For a pure devotee, success and failure have no meaning, because he\nis like a soldier on the battlefield. The propagation of the ideology of devotional service is somewhat similar to\ndeclaring war against material life.\nMaterialists are of many types--such as\ndesirous workers, knowledgeable, miraculous yogis, etc. etc. All of them are against the existence of God. They\ndeclare themselves as God, even if they are dependent on God's grace for every task step by step.\nWhy not be dependent? Therefore, a pure devotee should not support these groups of atheists. God\nThe strong devotee of the ungodly is never misled by such atheistic propaganda, but a newly initiated\ndevotee should be very careful of these. A devotee should properly practice devotion in the guidance of an authentic guru,\nand should not cling to mere formalities. In the direction of an authentic guru,\none should see how much devotional service is being performed, not just in relation to rituals.\nA devotee should not run after any object, but should be content with whatever is attained by the will of God.\nOne should desire.\nThis should be the principle of a devotional life. All such principles can be easily learned under the guidance of a guru like Shukdev Goswami. ©.\nMaharaj Parikshit asked Shukdev Ji correctly and\nMan should imitate his example. Maharaj Parikshit asked about the procedure for performing sacred rituals described in Vedic texts, such as the origin, preservation, and destruction of the world, as well as the Puranas,\nand the Mahabharata, regarding the procedure for performing sacred tasks. As before"
