          "textEn": "\nOne of these was the sixteenth, and the other the twenty-first, the touching letter. These two together\nBecame the treasure of detached life. Note: In Sanskrit, consonants are classified into two categories--sparsha varna and talabya varna. From 'ka' to\n'ma' the letters are called 'sparshan varg' (touching letters) and the sixteenth letter of this group is 'ta', while\nthe twenty-first letter is 'pa'. So when they come together, the word Tapasya, that is, Tapasya becomes Daivam. This penance\nis the beauty and wealth of Brahmins and ascetics. According to Bhagwat Darshan, every human being is made for penance,\nand not for any other purpose, because through only penance can one attain self-realization. Human\nlife's purpose is not sensual gratification, but self-realization. This penance has been going on since the beginning of creation.\nIt has been coming and was first accepted by the supreme guru Brahmaji. Through penance, a human can attain the benefit of human\nlife, not from the superficial civilization of animal life.\nAnimals eat, drink, and\nenjoy, but know nothing beyond the sense gratification, but man's birth is for doing penance\nto return to the abode of God."
