ि से बताएं । आप मकड़ी के समान खेल",
          "textEn": "49\nAnd also--still; Nathmanasya--of the beggar; Nath--Oh Lord; Nathay--give; Nathitam--desired; Par-Avare--\nIn worldly and divine matters; Yatha--as; Rupa--in form; Janiyam--to know; Te--yours; Tu- but;\nArupinah--without form..\n\nHowever, O Lord, my prayer to you is to fulfill my wish. Please tell me that\neven though you are of divine form, how do you assume a worldly form, although you have no such\nform. As the self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers,\nHaving abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned, having abandoned,\nThat self-illusion-yoga, adorned with various powers, 27). Meaning of the word\nAs--in the manner; Atma-swa--self; Maya--power; Yogena--by association; Nana--various; Shakti--power; Upavritham--by accumulation;\nVilumpan--for destruction; Visrujan--for creation; Grihanan--for acceptance; Bibhrat--for following; Atmanam--your own\nself; Atmana--by oneself \\.\nAnd please also tell me how you can differentiate between different combinations\nThey reveal the various powers of destruction, creation, acceptance, and nurturing. Meaning: This entire world is God's various powers--inner, outer, and deen--\nGod is directly manifest through the expansion of powers, just as the light of the sun is the manifestation of the power of the solar world. Such power is one with God and also different, just as sunlight remains different even after being inseparable from the solar world. These powers act on the signal of God through various combinations, and\nrepresentative doers like Brahma, Vishnu, and Shiva are also various incarnations of God. In other words, God\nIs nothing besides, yet He is separate from such manifest actions.\nHow does this happen?\nIts explanation will be given later.\nKridasyamodh-sankalpa urdhnabhiyathorunnete.\nAnd in that matter, meditate on me, O wise one, O Madhava. 28>. Meaning of the word:\nKridasi-- in the manner of playing; Amogh-- accurate; Sankalp-- determination; Oornanabhih-- spider; Yatha-- in the manner;\nOornute-- covers; Tatha-- in the same way; Tatvam-- about them; Dhehi-- tell me; Manisham-- by philosophical method;\nMayi-- to me; Madhav-- the lord of all powers..\nHey Madhav, tell me about all of them in philosophical terms. You are a game like a spider"
