          "textEn": "420\n\nThose who are going to do, who cover themselves with their own power. Your resolve is strong. Meaning: By the unimaginable power of God, each element has its own powers, which are called\nelemental power, knowledge power, and the power of cause and effect. By the combination of such powers of God,\nthe manifestation of creation, sustenance, and destruction occurs at the right time, whose various doers are Brahma, Vishnu, and Maheshwar. Brahma is the creator, Vishnu is the sustainer, and Shiva is the destroyer. But all these doers and powers\nare only in accordance with God, therefore there is nothing other than God, or various\ndifferent diversities are the same supreme source. The correct example of this is a spider and its web. This\nis woven by a spider, it is protected by it, and when the spider's desire\nis, then it encloses it within itself. The spider remains hidden inside the web.\nIf a trivial\nspider has so much power to act according to its will, then why can't God, with His supreme will,\nperform the work of creation, sustenance, and destruction of worldly manifestation? Only by the grace of God, Brahma,\nLike any devotee or any other devotee from the same disciple lineage, can one understand the omnipotent God,\nWho is constantly engaged in his divine plays through various powers. I am enlightened by the divine, and I am overjoyed.\nI am pleased with the creation of the people, by whose grace. 29>. Meaning of the word:\n\nBhagavat-- by God; Shikshitam-- educated; Aham-- me; Karvani-- by action; Hi- certainly; Atandrithaḥ--\nCausal; Na-- never; Iha- here; Aham- I; Yadya- although; Karyakarita- while doing; Praja- creation; Om- origin; Baddheya- to be bound;\nYat- from which; Anugrahata- by grace.\nPlease tell me so that according to your will, I can receive education on this subject\nand without being bound by such actions, I can continue to perform the task of mechanically producing souls. Meaning: Brahmaji does not want them