          "textEn": "423\n\nWe should get education from Brahmaji. In reality, Brahmaji does not create souls. They were given this right at the beginning of creation,\nthat they should provide bodies to souls according to the deeds done in the previous kalpa. Of Brahmaji,\nthe task is to awaken these souls from sleep and put them in their appropriate tasks. Brahmaji\ndoes not create souls arbitrarily, but rather entrusts them with the task of providing them with various types of bodies\nso that they can perform actions accordingly. Even after this, Brahmaji remains aware of this.\nIt remains that they are merely instruments, so that they do not consider themselves God. Devotees remain engaged in the tasks assigned by God, and such tasks continue uninterrupted, because\nthe order that is received from God. The credit for success goes not to individuals but to God. But,\nthose who are ignorant consider themselves the cause of success and do not give any credit to God.\nThis is\nthe characteristic of devout men. Shri Bhagavan said:\nKnowledge is the most secret, that which is unknowingly combined.\nThe mystery is that which is hidden, and that which is spoken by me. 39). Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Bhagavan said-- Shri Bhagavan said; Gyanam-- attained knowledge; Param-- exceeding; Guhayam-- confidential; Me- mine; Yat- that;\nVinchana- understanding; Samanvitam- combined; Sa- mystery; Bhakti- with devotion; Tat- that; Adgham- difficult; Cha- difficult; Grihan- to accept;\nTake the effort to accept; Gaditam- explained; Maya- by me;\nBy the coordination of devotion, the knowledge related to me, described in the scriptures, can be attained. The explanation of the materials required for this method\nhas already been done by me.\nYou take this carefully.\n\nMeaning: Brahmaji is the supreme devotee of God in this universe, therefore God has answered his four questions\nin the form of four important statements, which are known as Chatushloki Mool Bhagwat.\nBrahmaji's questions were as follows-(1) What are the forms of God in matter and in spirituality? (2) How do the different powers of God work? (3) God, with his powers, which"
