angible form and appear directly to the inhabitants of Vaikuntha Loka.\nTherefore, they remain formless in physical terms, like that of the executive chairman of the state, who does not remain formless in the palace. Similarly, God also does not remain formless in his abode; his abode is Nirasta-Krukram, as it is said in the beginning of the Bhagavata. Therefore, as revealed by the scriptures, the manifest and"
