          "textEn": "444\n\n(18.61) It is clearly mentioned--\n\nGod: He who is pleased with all beings. THIF YI Yanterudhati Mayaya. God, in the form of the Supreme Soul, is situated in the hearts of all beings, and through his external power,\nHe keeps all the creatures of the world under control. Therefore, it is a clear mention that God is the supreme controller,\nand the souls are controlled by God. In the same Bhagavad Gita (18.65), God commands\nthat-\n\nWhatever you desire, I will grant you; do not grieve over my devotion. I know you are true to me, O beloved. It is clear from this that it is God's command that man should be Bhagwato-mukhi, a devotee of God, only of Him\nShould be a worshiper and should bow down only to Lord Shri Krishna. By doing this, the devotee\nwill undoubtedly attain the abode of God. Indirectly, it is said that the entire Vedic structure of human society is formed in such a way that every individual functions as a part of the entire body of God.\nWise men\nThat is, Brahmins are situated on the face of God, the ruling class, that is, Kshatriyas, on their arms the merchant class\nThat is, Vaishyas are situated on the waist of God and the working class or Shudras are situated on the feet of God. Therefore,\nthe entire social structure is the body of God, and the various parts of the body--such as Brahmin, Kshatriya, Vaishya,\nand Shudra--all together are meant to serve the entire body of God; otherwise, these parts would not remain worthy of being integrated into the supreme consciousness. By coordinating all those associated with Shri Bhagwan,\nworld consciousness can be attained, therefore even the greatest scientists, great philosophers, thinkers,\npoliticians, industrialists, social reformers, etc., cannot provide any relief to the restless society of this world,\nbecause they do not know the secret of success described in this verse of Bhagwat, that is, the secret of Bhakti Yoga. The Bhagavad Gita (7.15) also says:"
