          "textEn": "445\n\nThose who are ignorant of the difficulties, the foolish men, the wicked men,\n\nare deluded by me, and are attached to the demonic emotion. Because the so-called great leaders of human society remain unaware of this great knowledge of devotion,\nand being fascinated by the external power of God, they are always engaged in inferior acts of sensual gratification,\ntherefore, they are staunch opponents of the supremacy of God, and they never accept going to the refuge of God,\nbecause they are fools, rogues, and vile men. Such a faithless atheist, no matter how much higher education they may have\nIn reality, they are the biggest fools in the world, because due to the influence of external nature, all their knowledge becomes useless. Therefore, all modern advanced knowledge is spent fighting among themselves for sensory gratification like dogs and cats. And science, philosophy, art, nationalism,\nEconomic development, all the knowledge acquired regarding religion, and all the great works are wasted in the same way, just like a garment used for a corpse.\nCovering the corpse with various types of clothes, fools,\nThere is no benefit in looting false praise from the public. Therefore, Shrimad Bhagwat repeatedly says that without attaining the position of devotion, all the activities of human society become fruitless. It is said--\n\nParadhvastavadbodhajato\n\nYavatatvagyasatvam.\n\nYavatkriyastavadidam manau ve\n\nKamamthimikena yena shareerbandhah. (Bhagwat 5.5.5)\n\nUntil a person neglects self-realization and curiosity, even the greatest material\nactivities are in the form of defeat, because the purpose of human life is not fulfilled by such unwanted and futile actions. The function of the human body is to be free from worldly bondage, but as long as someone remains engrossed in material\nactivities, their mind will keep revolving in the vortex of material things, and they will remain trapped in the bondage of body after birth."
