          "textEn": "458\nShowing his divine form (Atmano Roopam), he was preaching the essence of Srimad Bhagavatam in four verses.\nWas preaching. He is the Janaka, meaning the Supreme Being, among all men. All souls are separate-separate\nIndividuals, and among such individuals, Lord Hari is the best, as is confirmed by this Shruti mantra--\nTitiyo nityanam chetanashchaitanam. Therefore, in the divine world, there is no place for a formless form, just as\nin the physical world, there is no formless form. Whenever there is consciousness (of the knower), the manifested (of the knower) follows. In the spiritual world, every object is full of knowledge, therefore every object of the divine world, place,\nwater, tree, mountain, river, human, animal, bird, is full of this quality, that is, consciousness, therefore every object there\nis individual and concrete.\nWe get this information from the best Vedic literature, Shrimad Bhagavat, and\nShri Bhagavan gave this information to Brahmaji so that, being the leader of the souls, he could spread this\nmessage throughout the world and impart the supreme knowledge-filled teaching of devotion. Brahmaji\ngave this message of Shrimad Bhagavat to his beloved son Narad. Narad gave it to Vyasadeva,\nand he gave it to Shukadeva Goswami. By the courtesy of Shukadeva Swami and the grace of Maharaj Parikshit,\nwe have received this Shrimad Bhagavat, from which we can permanently learn the science of the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, Shri Krishna.\nFor the sake of the hidden meaning, the hands offered to Hari (Lord Vishnu) are the same as before. 39). Meaning of the word\nIncluded -- upon being included; Indriya-Arthaya -- for the sake of all senses, for Shri Bhagavan; Haraye -- for God; Vidhita --\nAnjaliha -- with folded hands; Sarva-Bhuta -- all living beings; Om-- --From complete; the universe; created; this--\nThis; he--He (Brahmaji); like before--\nDevotees, the complete Supreme Lord Hari, who bestows divine bliss to t