          "textEn": "459\nInstead of worshiping their senses, they begin.\n\nIn Haribhakti Sudhodhya (13.2), the following verse has come--\n\nSET: Kalam ETE Hi\n\nTanoh Phalam AEE |\n\nJihlafalam Tadashkirtanam Hi\n\nGeet Bhagwat Hi Loke. “Oh devotee of God! Your eyes become successful by seeing you, and by the touch of your body, the touch is fulfilled, oh. The tongue is for singing the praises of your virtues, because in this world, a pure devotee of God\nis extremely rare to find.In the beginning, the senses were provided to the souls for this purpose that they may serve God\nor their devotees with love, but the bound soul, coming into the delusion of external power,\nbecame fascinated by inner pleasures. Therefore, the entire process of divine consciousness is to bring the bound actions of the senses to the right path and then to put them back into the service of God.\nTherefore, Brahmaji again created the universe\nto work in it, creating bound souls again and again, and engaged his senses in the direct service of God. Thus, this universe is created and destroyed by the will of God. Its creation\nis done to provide opportunities to bound beings, so that they can work in the direction of returning to the abode of God,\nand Brahmaji, Naradji, Vyasji, and their group engage in the work of God with this objective. This is the task of liberating beings bound by the sphere of sensory gratification and bringing the senses back to the normal state of being engaged in the service of God. But the nihilists, instead of doing this, keep making bound souls and God also unconscious. This is an abuse with bound souls.\nThe dry state of the senses can be cured by the treatment of the defect, not by the\nextirpation of the senses. If there is any disease in the eyes, then treatment should be done to see properly.\nRemoving the eyes did not cure it. Similarly, all diseases are based on sensory gratification"
