          "textEn": "470\nSthitirvakuntha-vijayah, nourishment, that grace.\nManvantaras, good righteousness, desires of action. 4>. Meaning of the word:\n\nSthiti:--Appropriate state; Vaikuntha-Vijayah--Victory of the lord of Vaikuntha; Poshanam--Nurturing: Tat--Grace:--Unselfish grace;\nManvantaras:--The reign of the Manus; Sat--Righteousness:--Complete righteousness; Uttayah--Inspiration to act; Karma--Desire:--Of desire\nAspiration:--\n\nFor the soul, it is appropriate that it follows the rules of God and completely\nachieves complete mental peace in the protection of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. All the Manus and their\nrules are to provide the right direction to life. The inspiration to work is the desire for the fruits of action.\nIt is the aspiration. Meaning: This physical world is created, exists for some time, and is destroyed again by the will of God.\nThe creation of the elements and the creator Brahma is originated by Lord Vishnu in his\nfirst and second incarnations. The first person incarnation is Mahavishnu, and the second person incarnation\nis Garbhodakshayi Vishnu, from whom Brahma was born. The third person incarnation is Kshirodakshayi Vishnu, who\nremains in the form of the Supreme Soul in every object of the universe and\nobserves the creation created by Brahma. Among the many sons of Brahma, Shiva is also one whose work is the destruction of this creation. Therefore,\nVishnu is the original creator of the universe, and he is also the protector of the beings created by his unconditional grace. In this\nway, all bound souls should accept the supremacy of God and, becoming his pure devotees, should live peacefully in this\nsuffering and crisis-filled world.\nTo this world, for the satisfaction of one's senses,\nto consider it suitable, and in this way, due to being deluded by the external power of Vishnu, the bound soul\nhas to live in order to experience again the natural laws of creation and destruction. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that from the highest realm of the universe to the lowest realm,\nall the realms up to the netherworld are perishable, and bound souls can travel in space through their good or bad deeds, or through modern\nspacecraft, but their death is certain anywhere. Yes,\nIn different people, their ages are different. But the only way to attain eternal life is"
