          "textEn": "472) Should be done. Avataranucharitam Harishchasyanuvartinam. Punasamisha-kathaa: Proktôna nánakhyônopavrithaha. 5>. Meaning of the word\nAvatar-- incarnation of God; Anucharitam-- activities; Hareh-- of God; Cha-- also; Ashyah-- his; Anuvartinam-- following;\nFollowers; Pumsam-- of humans; Isha-kathaah-- the science of God, the divine essence; Prokthah-- said; Nana-- various; Akhyan--\nStories; Upavahitaha - described.\nIsha-katha (God's story) describes the various incarnations of Lord Shri Bhagavan, his pastimes, and also\nthe activities of his devotees. Meaning: In the existence of this universe, a sequence of history is formed, in which the accounts of the actions of the souls\nare recorded. Generally, people have a tendency to know the history and narratives of various individuals and times,\nbut due to the lack of knowledge about the subject of divine science (Isha Katha),\nthey are not able to study the history of the incarnations of God.\nIt should always be remembered that this creation is made for the salvation of living beings. God\nDue to his benevolence, descending into the various realms of this material world, works for the salvation of bound souls. This makes history and narratives readable. In Shrimad Bhagavatam,\nthere are many divine stories about God and his devotees. Therefore, devotees and God\nshould listen to the stories with respect. By restraint, the self, with its powers, is established in the other form. 6>. Meaning of the word\nNirodhah - the dissolution of the world; Asya-- His; Anushayanam-- the yogic sleep of the incarnate Mahavishnu; Atmanah-- of the individual soul; Saha- with; Shaktibhih-- with powers; Muktih-- liberation; Hitva- by abandoning; Anyatha- otherwise; Roopam- - form; Swa- in one's own form; Vyavasthitih- permanent position.\n.\nWhile the soul sleeps with the life-related tendencies of its bound state,\nBeing absorbed in Mahavishnu is called the culmination of the manifest universe. Changeable, gross, and"
