          "textEn": "48\nNot God A | Generally, they consider the molecules and infinite forms of God, because they\ncannot be themselves molecules or infinite, but they should understand that this molecule and infinite form\nis not the supreme glory of God. Their most amazing display of power happens when the infinite\nGod appears among us, just like us. Even then, their divine plays are different from ordinary humans. To lift Govardhan Parvat at the age of seven, and to marry sixteen thousand\nwives in his youth--these are some examples of his immense power, but foolish people, seeing or hearing these, reject them by calling them imaginary and consider God to be equal to themselves. They do not understand that even though they are in human form by their own power, they are still God and are imbued with the power of the supreme\nregulator.\nBut when such foolish people, by the disciple-tradition, receive the messages of God given in the Shrimad Bhagavad Gita or Shrimad Bhagavat,\nthen they too, by the grace of pure devotees, become devotees. Therefore, for the benefit of such ignorant people, the worldly pastimes of God\nare depicted in the Bhagavad Gita, in the Srimad Bhagavatam. Tasvavatsit swa srishtasu sahasraparivatsaran |\nTena Narayano naam yadapah purushoddhavaah. 11). Meaning of the word\nAG - in that; Avatisit - residing; Swa - own; Srishtasu - in creation; Sahasram - a thousand; Parivatsaran - year; Tena - by that\nbecause; Narayanah - Narayanah; Naam - name; Yat - because; Aapah - water; Purusha-udbhavaah - born from the supreme being..\nThe supreme being is not formless, therefore, they are clearly male or male. That is why this supreme male by\nThe divine water produced is called Nar.\nBecause they sleep in this water, therefore Narayan is called.\nDravya, karma, and time are all nature, and the soul is also.\nWhat is there by grace, what is not by expectation. 12). Lexicon"
