          "textEn": "482\nDravyamu--matter; Bhauti--force; Karma--action; Cha--and; Kaal--time; Cha--also; Swa-bhaavah--self-feeling; Jiva--soul; Eva--certainly;\nCha--also; Yat--whose; Anugrahitah--by grace; Santi--are, are situated; Na--not; Santi-sthitah--are situated; Yat--without expectation--out of expectation..\n\nMan should understand very well that all material elements, actions, time, and\nqualities, and all these enjoying souls are present only by the grace of God. Neglected by them,\nAs soon as they are neglected, all these things become non-existent. Meaning: Souls want to assert their dominance over nature, therefore they are the enjoyers of material elements, time,\nqualities, etc. God is the ultimate enjoyer, and the souls are to be helpful in His enjoyment and\nThus, to be included in the divine enjoyment of each one. In enjoyment, both the enjoyer and the enjoyable take part.\nBut, being controlled by Maya, the souls want to become enjoyers themselves, like God,\nthough they are not the cause of it.\nIn the Bhagavad Gita, living beings, that is, the souls, are said to be the supreme nature of God. Vishnu Purana also has a similar mention. Therefore, the souls are never men or real enjoyers.\nTherefore, in this world, the desire for pleasure by the soul is false. In the spiritual world,\nsouls are purified, therefore they are the ones who extend their hands in the happiness of God. In the physical world,\nthrough one's actions, the feeling of the soul's enjoyment of pleasures gradually diminishes due to natural laws,\nand the illusion keeps filling the ears of bound souls, so that they may become one with God. This is Maya's\nLast trap. When this final trap is also removed by the grace of God, then the soul attains its\noriginal state and thus becomes truly liberated. God creates this world only to give freedom from the bondage of existence, nurtures it for some time (according to his calculation, for one\nthousand years, as it has come in the previous verse), and then destroys it according to his own will\nand gives.\nTherefore, souls remain completely dependent on the grace of God, and that is why when God wants,\nscientists mix the so-called pleasures produced by development into the soil. From the yoga-tapas, he arose, with various forms.\nThe heroic, golden God was created by Maya in three forms. 13. Shabdharam"
