          "textEn": "484\nIn an unmanifest state, the living powers remain liberated within God, and when in the world\nrestraint is released, they are subject to the qualities of nature, according to different desires, in different\nways they are manifested. Such unequal manifestations of living forces are indicative of the bound state of living beings.\nAre. But in their eternal manifestation, the liberated souls are surrendered in an inert form, therefore they\ndo not come under the creation and destruction. In this way, in yogic sleep, while lying on one's bed, the creation of this universe happens through the contemplation of God. And in this way, all the universes and the lord of the universe, Brahma,\nrepeatedly appear and disappear.\nThe Supreme Being is the cause of the material and the cause of the spiritual.\nThen, the one-sided strength is divided into three; listen to that. 14>. Meaning of the word\nAdhidaivam--Controller of beings; Ath--Now; Adhyatmamu--Controlled being; Adhibhutam--Physical body; Iti--Thus; Prabhuh--Lord; Ath--Thus; Ekam--Only one; Paurusham--To the man, of the Lord; Viryam--Power; Tridha--In three parts;\nAbhidyata--Divided; Tat--That; Shrunu--Listen;\nListen from me how the Lord divides his one power into three parts named Adhidaivam, Adhyatma, and\nAdhibhuta, which has already been mentioned above. From the inner body, from the sky, from the consciousness of the being,\nFrom vigor and strength, from birth, then the life force is greatly increased. 95 Meaning of the word\nAntah sharee--inside the body; Akashaat--from the sky; Purushasya--of the male; Vichesthitah--while performing; Ojah--sense organs;\nBalah--strength; Sahah--mental strength; Balam--physical strength; Jajne-utyan karita; el: -thereafter; Praanah--life, vital energy; Mahan--great;\nAsuh--the emanation of each life.\n.\nInside the divine body of Mahavishnu, from the sky, sensory strength, mental strength, and\nphysical strength are produced. With these, the complete l