ै । चूँकि वे समस्त मुखों की समष्टि हैं, अत: अलग-अलग\nजीवात्माओं में मुख होता है। इसी प्रकार से अन्य सारी इन्द्रियाँ तथा उनके अंग भी होते हैं। यहाँ पर",
          "textEn": "485\nMeaning of the word\n\nAnuprananti--following the characteristics of life; Yamu--which; Prana:--organs; Pranantamu--action; Sarva-janitushu--in all living beings; Apaanantamu--on stopping the action; Apaananti--all others stop; Nara-devamu--king; Iva--like; Anugaah--followers;\nFollowers..\n\nJust as the followers of a king follow their master, similarly, when the entire power\nbecomes dynamic, all other living beings move (behave). And when the entire power\nbecomes inactive, the sensory activity of all other living beings ceases. Meaning: Individual souls are completely dependent on the Supreme Soul's supreme power. No one's independent\nexistence remains, just as there is no independent light in an electric bulb.\nEvery machine of electricity\nis completely dependent on the power plant, this power plant depends on the reservoir for electricity generation\ndepends on the reservoir, the reservoir depends on the clouds, the clouds depend on the sun and the sun depends on creation and this creation is completely\ndependent on the effort or motion of the Supreme Lord. Thus, God is the cause of all causes.\nHe is the cause of cause.\n\nPranenaakshipata kshuttrantara jayate vibho.\nPipasato jakshatashcha prangamam nirabidhat. 97. Meaning of the word\n\nPranen-- from the life force; akshipata-- being distracted; kshut- hunger; trit- thirst; antara-- from within; jayate-- rises; vibhoh-- of God; pipasatah-- desiring to quench thirst; jakshatah-- desiring to eat; cha- tatha; pra- before;\nMukham- mouth; nirabhidyatah-- appeared \\.\n\nWhen the life force (prana) was disturbed by the Virat Purusha, hunger and thirst\nwere generated, and when the Virat Purusha desired to drink and eat, the mouth opened.\nMeaning: Just as the organs and sensory experiences of living beings develop in the mother's womb,\nin the same way, it seems that the development of the cosmic, universal being from all living beings also occurs, therefore,\nthe ultimate cause of all creation work is not without attributes or inactive. Even in God, all kinds of senses\nexperiences of the organs of action and the organs of knowledge remain, and in this way they occur in every individual. This desire or effort is the nature of the Supreme Soul. Because they are the aggregate of all faces, therefore, in different\nliving beings, there is a face. Similarly, all other senses and their parts also exist. Here"
