          "textEn": "486\nThe face is the symbol of all the senses, because the same rules apply to others as well. From the mouth, the indivisible tongue is born.\nThen various juices are born, and one who attains them through the tongue. 98 Meaning of the word\nFrom the mouth-- from the mouth; palate-- palate; indistinct-- originated; tongue-- tongue; there-- there; from there; arises-- appears; then-- then;\nVarious tastes-- various tastes; known-- appeared; from the tongue-- from the tongue; He-- who; Are tasted-- are tasted..\nThe palate appeared from the mouth, and then the tongue also originated. After all this, various tastes\nwere created so that the tongue could taste them.\nMeaning: This sequential process of evolution presents a description of the regulating gods (adhidaiva),\nbecause the regulating god of tastes is Varuna. Therefore, the mouth becomes the abode of the tongue, which\ntastes various juices, whose regulator is the god Varuna. It seems that along with the tongue,\nVaruna was also created.\nThe tongue and palate are merely caused by the form of the underlying or substance,\nwhereas the working deity is the supreme deity, who is the soul, and the man on whom the action is performed,\nthat is spiritual. Thus, after the opening of the mouth of the great man, the explanation of the birth of the three categories\nhappens. In the presented verse, four principles are given, from which the three main elements mentioned earlier are explained:\nAdhyatma (spiritual), Adhidaiva (divine), and Adhibhutam (elemental).\nVivakshormukhato bhumno vadhrvaag vyatatam tayor.\nJale cha itasya suchiram nirodhaha samajayata. 19. Meaning of the word\nVivakshooh- when there is a need to speak; Mukhat- from the mouth; Bhoomanah- of God; Vadhi- fire or fire god; Vak- speech;\nShabda- word; Vyahatam- speech; Tayooh- by both; Jale- in water; Cha- still; Etasya- of all these; Suchiram- for a long time;\nNirodhah- obstruction; Samajayat- remained;\nJanmaayat- was born; Nirh