          "textEn": "503\nDivision of beings:--Inanimate and animate beings; Division of beings:--Born, egg, germ, and produced from seed, four types of beings; These are--Others;\nOthers-All; Water--Water; Land--Land; Sky--Sky;--Birds; Skillful--Happy; Unskillful--Sad; Mixed--Happy-Sad\nBoth; Karmas--According to one's past actions; Gotaya--Motion, result; Tu--But; Ima--They, we,\nO King, know from me that all living beings are produced by God according to their deeds. In this, Brahma and his sons like Daksha, Vaivasvata Manu like Samayik,\nPradhan, Indra, Chandra and Varun like deities, Bhrigu, Vyas, Vasistha like Maharishis, residents of Pitruloka and\nresidents of Siddhaloka, Charan, Gandharva, Vidyadhar, Asura, Yaksha, Kinnaras and Devdutas, Nagas, Bandar like\nKimpurushas, humans, residents of Matrukul, Asuras, Pishachas, ghosts, spirits, unconscious, auspicious-inauspicious constellations,\nVinayak, wild animals, birds, domestic animals, reptiles, mountains, inert and conscious beings, Janavajj,\nAndaja, Swedaja and Udbhija beings and all other happy, unhappy of water, land or sky\nOr mixed happy –sad creatures are included. All these, according to their past deeds, are created by God.\nOkay. Note: This list describes various types of souls. From the highest realm to\nAll the beings in the lowest realm of the universe have been created by the omnipotent father Vishnu.\nHave been produced. Therefore, no being is independent of the Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, God has called all souls as his progeny in the following verse in the Bhagavad Gita--\n\nFrom all beings, O son of Kunti, are born all beings.\n\nThose are Brahma, \"EEE, the father who gives seed.\" Nature's comparison to mother has gone. Although every living being is seen to be born from its mother,\nBut the truth is that the real reason for such birth is not the mother. The real reason for birth\nis the father. A mother cannot give birth to a child without the father's sperm.\nTherefore,