          "textEn": "504\nThe physical nature is one of the powers of God (Bhagavad Gita 7.4). Physical nature is lower than the supreme nature.\nThat is, it is inferior to the soul. God, by the combination of the above and below nature, reveals all worldly affairs.\nSome souls are happily expecting, while some live in sorrowful situations. But in reality, none of these are happy in physical life. No one remains happy in prison life, even if\nhe is a first-class prisoner or a third-class prisoner. An intelligent person should try to be free from prison itself, rather than being elevated from a third-class prison life to a first-class prison life. Someone can be promoted to the first class prisoner, but in the next period,\nhe may have to go back to the third class. Man should try to be free from imprisonment and\ngo to the abode of God.\nThis is the real destination for all kinds of beings.\nSattva, Rajas, Tamas, these are the three kinds of beings. There, each king is different, and they are divided into three.\nEach one is different from the other, and their own nature is revealed. 49). Meaning of the word\nSatvamu--Satva Guna; Rajah--Rajoguna; Tamah--Tamoguna, thus; Tisrah--Three; Surah--Gods; Nru--Humans; Narakah--\nIn the state of Narakas; Tatapi--there also; Ekankshah--one each; Rajah--Hey Rajah; Bhidante-- are divided into; Gatayah--\nCourses; Tridha- three; Yada--At that time, when; Ekantarah-- one to another; Anyabhyam-- from others; Swabhāvah-- nature,\nHabit; Upahanyate obtains..\nAccording to the various qualities of nature, Satogun, Rajogun, and Tamogun -- different types of\nanimals are born, who are called gods, humans, and hellish beings. Oh king, not only this, when\none quality combines with two other qualities, it is divided into three, and in this way, each\nanimal is influenced by other qualities and acquires its habits.\nMeaning: Different creatures are driven by a particular quality, but along with this,\nother two qualities can also affect them. Generally, all bound beings are influenced by the\nquality of passion, because every living being wants to assert its dominance over nature for its own\ngratification. But even when there is a quality of passion separately, by being in contact with other qualities, by them"
