          "textEn": "505\nThe possibility of being affected always remains. If someone maintains good company, then he can become virtuous.\nAnd if he maintains bad company, then he can become dark-complexioned. But nothing happens in the same way.\nIt does not decrease. A person can change their nature with good or bad company, therefore, to be able to differentiate between good and bad, it is necessary to be intelligent. The best company is the service of God's devotees,\nand through that company, a person can become the most worthy by the grace of God's pure devotees. As we have seen in the life of Srila Narada Muni, he could become the most worthy only by associating with pure devotees of God. He was the son of a maidservant since birth, he did not even know his father\nand he did not have even the minimum educational qualification.\nBut only by associating with devotees and eating their leftover food, they gradually developed divine qualities of devotees. Because of such association,\nthe tendency to listen to and sing the divine glory of God emerged in them, and because God's\nglory is inseparable from God, therefore Due to the utterance of words (kirtan), he was able to attain the direct presence of God. Similarly, Ajamila's life is also like that (in the sixth canto), who was the son of a Brahmin\nand who was given proper education in the performance of the duties of a Brahmin, but even then, the prostitute's\nFUT brought him to the most despicable state of a Chandal, that is, of the human race. Therefore, the gateway of liberation,\nto open it, the Bhagavata always teaches the lesson of great harmony. Associating with such men who want to assert their authority over this\nphysical world is like entering the terribly dark part of hell. A person should seek the company of great people to uplift themselves. That is the way to life-success.\nThus, the creator of the universe, the Lord, is the embodiment of righteousness.\n\nHe establishes the universe, turning 