कार मछली या मनुष्य",
          "textEn": "506\n\nMeaning: The complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Vishnu, incarnates in various societies of living beings to liberate them from the clutches of Maya.\nAnd such activities of God are not limited to human society alone. They incarnate in the form of a fish, a pig, a tree, and many other forms, but the ignorant\nmen, due to not knowing God, mock Him, even if they are in human form in human society.\nWhy not? Therefore, the Lord says in the Bhagavad Gita (9.11)—\n\nThose who are ignorant of the Supreme Being, who have taken refuge in the body of a human being,\n\nand do not know the Supreme Being, even though they are great,\nare deluded. As we have stated in the previous verses, the conclusion is that God never\nis the origin of the physical creation. His divine state remains unchanged forever. They are the eternal forms of knowledge and\nbliss, and through their various powers, they fulfill their omnipotent will. ©.\nThus, they do not experience the fruits of any of their actions. They are beyond all such determinations of cause and effect.\nEven if they appear in the world, this display is only of STR powers, because they\nare above the good and bad concepts of this physical world. In this world, a fish or a pig can be considered lower than a human,\nbut when God appears in the form of a fish or a pig, then they are not even one of these from a physical\npoint of view. It is their unintentional grace that they appear in every society and species,\nbut they can never be considered one of them. The concepts of the physical world\nsuch as good and bad, low and high, important and negligible, such perceptions are estimates of physical power\nand God is beyond all such concepts.\nThe supreme emotion, that is, divine nature,\ncan never be compared to material perception. Man should not forget that God's\npowers always remain the same, never diminish, because God constantly assumes the form of lower animals\nand continues to incarnate. 