          "textEn": "8\n\nThe Kshatriyas used to fight with the kings of various states and, after defeating them, would abduct their beautiful princesses.\nThey would kidnap them. This system was commendable because the marriage of Kshatriyas and princesses\nwas based on the bravery of the victorious Kshatriya. All the princes of the Yadu dynasty, by the strength of bravery,\nIn the same way, they married the daughters of other kings. In this way, they were the conquerors of all the kings of the world. Vidur wanted to instill in his brother's mind that fighting the Pandavas is full of many\ndangers, because Shri Krishna was helping them, who had defeated demons like Kansa\nand Jarasandha in his childhood, and gods like Brahma and Indra. Therefore, the complete power of the world was with the Pandavas.\nThis is the fault, the two men are divided.\nEntering the house, the son of Yama,\nYou are prosperous, Krishna, with a crooked face, gone,\nForsaking the art of family. 92 Meaning of the word\n\n|: — He; TH: — This; Dosha: - Crime; Purusha-dvit: Shrikrishna's wife]; Asthe- existing; Grihan- in the house;\nPravishthah- entered; Yam- to whom; Apatya- thinking of one's own son; Pushnasi- are nurturing; Krishnat- from Krishna;\nVimukhah- against; Gata- Shree: -- Without every auspicious object: renounce-- Abandon; Aashu-- quickly; Ashcham-- inauspicious;\nKul-- family; Kaushalay-- for the sake of; \\.\n\nYou are directly nurturing Duryodhana, who is a form of sin, as your unyielding son,\nBut he is asking from Lord Krishna. Because you are following Krishna's devotee in this way,\ntherefore, you are devoid of all auspicious qualities. Get rid of this misfortune as soon as possible,\nand bring well-being to the entire family. Meaning: A good son is said to be a 'apat' (child), that is, he does not let his father fall.\nAfter the father's\ndeath, to please Lord Vishnu, the son, by performing a Yagya, can protect the soul of his father.\nThis tradition is still prevalent in India. After the death of his father, the son goes to Lord Vishnu's lotus feet to perform a Yagya (ritual), and in this way, if the father is separated from the path,\nhe redeems the father's soul. But if the son is already an enemy of Vishnu, then how can such an enemy\nin emotion, perform a Yagya at the lotus feet of Lord Vishnu? Lord Krishna, the direct Lord Vishnu"
