          "textEn": "4\nHe should be eager to meet those great souls who are already engaged in the service of God there.\nIn every pilgrimage site, God remains present in his various divine forms. These forms are called Archayati--that is, those forms of God whom an ordinary person can easily\nunderstand. God is inaccessible to our worldly senses. They cannot be seen by our present eyes,\nNor can they be heard by our present ears. We, in that measure, as much as we\nhave entered into the service of God, or in that proportion, as much as our lives remain free from sins,\nwe can experience God. But even though we are not free from sins, God is so merciful\nthat he provides us with the facility to give us his darshan in the temple in the form of his uncreated forms. God\nis omnipotent, therefore He can accept our services by presenting His form.\nTherefore, no one should be foolish to think that the form of the temple is a statue.\nSuch an archayoti is not a statue, but the Lord himself, and whoever is freed from sins in whatever proportion,\ncan understand the importance of that archamurti accordingly. Therefore, to get guidance,\nthe need for a pure devotee always remains. In India, across the country, millions of pilgrimage sites are spread out, and according to tradition, the common person travels to these holy places throughout the year.\nIn all seasons, he travels to these sacred places. The mention of some of the archa forms located in various pilgrimage sites is as follows: In Mathura (the birthplace of Krishna), as Adikeshava, in Puri\n(Odisha), as Lord Jagannath (also known as Purushottama), in Allahabad (Prayag), as Bindu-Madhava,\nin Mandarachal, as Madhusudan, in Anandaranya, as Vasudev, Padmanabha, and Janardan,\nin Vishnukanchi, as Vishnu, and in Mayapur, as Hari, they are present.\nThroughout the universe, there are millions of such idols of God. The summary of all these archa-murvi is given as follows in Chaitanya-Charitamrita--\n\nEverywhere light, the wandering, the giver of happiness. The world destroys unrighteousness and establishes righteousness. *' God has spread himself throughout the universe in such a way that devotees get joy,"
