          "textEn": "7\n\nMeaning: More than five thousand years ago, when Saint Vidur was traveling the earth as a pilgrim,\n*India' was known by the name Bharatvarsham, as it is even today. The history of the past cannot give a systematic account of more than three thousand years, but before that, the whole world\nwas under the flag and military power of Maharaj Yudhishthir, and he was the emperor (Chakravarti Raja) of the world. In today's time, hundreds of thousands of flags are hoisted in the United Nations, but in the time of Vidur, Lord Krishna,\nthat is, by the grace of Ajit Kau, there was only one flag.\nAll the nations of the world are eagerly waiting for one power under one flag, but for this they will have to receive the grace of Lord Krishna, because\nOnly he can be helpful in creating a universal nation.\nTatratha shushrāva suhṛdhvinashtim\nVanam yatha venujavahidhisamshrayam.\nSamspradhaya dagdhamathanushocan\nSarasvatim pratyagiyaay tushnim. 29). Meaning of the word\n\nTatra- there; Atha- after; Shushrāva- to hear; Suhṭ- dear; Vinashtam- dead; Vanam- forest; Yatha- as; Venuj-\nVahvi- fire caused by bamboo; Sansrayam- from each other; Sanspardhaya- by intense desire; Dagdham- burnt; Atha-\nThus; Anushochan- thinking; Saraswatim- to Saraswati river; Pratyak- towards the west; Iyaay- gone; Trushnim- silent\nHTL\n\nIn Prabhas Tirtha, they found out that all their relatives were killed in the same way due to the intense fervor\nLike the friction of bamboos The fire that is produced burns the entire forest.\nAfter this, they proceeded towards the west, where the Saraswati river flows. Note: Both Kauravas and Yadavas were relatives of Vidura. Vidur heard the news of their destruction as a result of the fratricidal war. It is appropriate to compare the friction of wild bamboos with the charged (vishvabhukta)\nhuman society. The whole world has been compared to a jungle. Due to friction in the jungle,\na fire can break out at any moment. No one goes to set fire in the forest, but from the struggle between the bamboos,\nfire is produced, which burns the entire forest. Similarly,\nIn the worldly, my-thirteen-formed, greater forest, due to the fierce aggression of bound souls, deluded by Maya,\nA fire of war-like form ignites. Such worldly fire was extinguished only by the water of the clouds, the grace of the saints"
