          "textEn": "8\nCan go, just as a forest fire can only be extinguished by rain falling from the clouds.\nSimilarly, the three kinds of suffering, the mind,\nThe earth, fire, and air.\nThe sacred water of Sudas, the cow, and the secret.\nThat which is the offering to the Lord of the gods. 22). Shabdarmam.\nTasyaam- on the banks of the Saraswati River; Tritasya- a pilgrimage place named Trit; Ushanasah:--Ushna named pilgrimage site; Manoah ch-- Manu named\nPilgrimage site also; Prithoh-- of Prithu; Ath-- after that; Agnih-- of fire; Asitasya-- of Asita; Vayoh-- of wind; Tirtham--\nPilgrimage site; Sudasasya-- of Sudas name; Gavam-- of cow; Guhasya-- of Guha; Yat-- after that; Shradhdevasya-- of Shradhdev\nKa; Sahas-- Vidur did; Asisheve- properly saw and performed rituals \\\nOn the banks of the Saraswati River, there were eleven pilgrimage sites whose names are (9) Trit (2) Ushana\n(3) Manu (4) Prithu (5) Agni (6) Asit (7) Vayu (8) Sudas (9) Go (10) Guha and\n(11) The Shraddha-deva. Vidura went among all of them and performed the rituals properly. Others are the gods of the twice-born,\nCreated by Vishnu in various abodes.\nThose who are chiefly attached to the objects of their sight,\nare remembered by the sight of the dark one. 23 ज़a. Meaning of the word\nAnanyi--other; Cha--and; Iha--here; Dwija-deva--by the great sages; Devaai:--by the gods; Kritani--established; Nana--various; Ayatnani--various forms; Vishnuha--of Lord Vishnu; Prati-each; Adgam--limb; Mukhyam--main; Adhit--marked;\nMandirani--temple; Yat-whose; Darshanat-from seeing; Krishnam--to Lord Krishna; Anusmaranti--they constantly remember;\nThey make..\nThere were also many other temples, full of various forms, of Lord Vishnu, established by sages and gods. These temples were inscribed with the main symbols of God,\nand were always reminders of Lord Shri Krishna.\nMeaning: Human society is divided into four social castes and four spiritual Prayags, which each\napplies to man. This system is called Varnaashram Dharma, and in this great book, in many places,\nits explanation has been given. Saints or those individuals who were fully engaged in the spiritual upliftment of the entire human society were called Dwija Dev, meaning the best among the twice-born. Above the lunar sphere"
