          "textEn": "27\nThe god, in the image of the mother of the gods, was conceived in her womb. Is she (Devaki) alright? Meaning: All the Vedas are full of divine knowledge and spiritual values. In this way, Lord Krishna's\nmother Devaki, in the form of the direct meaning of the Vedas, held God in her womb. There is no difference between the Vedas and\nGod. The purpose of the Vedas is to understand God, and God is the direct Veda.\nDevaki is compared to meaningful Vedas, and God is compared to their purpose. Apisvidante Bhagavansukham vo\nYah saatatam kamadughaaniruddhah.\nThey know that I am in the word-born.\nThe mind-made, the essence of the three qualities. 34). Meaning of the word\n\nApi-- also; Swit-- what; Aaste-- is; Bhagavan-- God; Sukham-- all happiness; Vah-- yours; Yah- who; Sattvatam-- of the devotees; Kama-dughah-- the source of all desires; Aniruddah-- self-existent; Yam- to whom; Aamananti- accept;\nSm-- from ancient times; Hi- certainly; Shabd-born; Ruveved- the cause; Manah- of the mind; Sthit- fixed; Satv- divine;\nTurya- the fourth expansion; Tatvamu- the essence, the principle;\n\nCan I ask if Aniruddha is skillfully present? He is the one who fulfills all the desires of pure devotees,\nand from ancient times, he has been considered the cause of the Rigveda, the creator of the mind, and Vishnu's\nfourth share. Meaning: The first four arms (Vyuha) are of Baladeva, the first part of Vasudeva, Sankarshana, Pradyumna and Aniruddha. They are all Vishnu Tattva. In the incarnation of Shri Ram, all of these aspects manifested for specific divine plays.\nHappened.\nLord Rama, etc., Vasudeva, and Sankarshana, Pradyumna and Aniruddha were his brothers. Aniruddha\nis also the reason for Mahavishnu, from whose breath the Rigveda was manifested. In the Markandeya Purana, it is beautifully explained.\nIn the incarnation of Lord Krishna, Aniruddha was born as his son. In Dwarka, God\nKrishna is a part of the Vasudeva of the Adi Vyuha. The original Lord Krishna never leaves Golok Vrindavan. All\nThe essence is one Vishnu Tattva, and there is no difference in their power. Apisvidnye cha nijatmadaeva-"
