          "textEn": "28\nThose who are engaged in contemplation and are devoted to the mind,\nAnd those who are truthful, the sons of truth,\nAnd those who are like Gada, they prosper in prosperity. 25. Meaning of the word\nApi--also; Swit--what; Anye--other; Cha-tatha; Nija-atma--own; Daivam--Shri Krishna; Ananya-purna-rpe; Vrtya--\nFaith; Samanutratah--followers; Ye--those who; Hadi-k--Hadi; Satya-atmaja--Satyabhama's son; Charudesna--Charudesna;\nGad--Gad; Aadi-h--etc. Swasti-kushalata-paksha; Charanti-time they spend; Saumya--Oh, gentleman..\nOh, noble men, other people, as per the tradition, Charudeshna, Gad, and the son of Satyabhama, who consider Shri Krishna\nas their own soul and follow his path without any deviation,\nare they right? Even with his own strength and the strength of his victories,\nHe built a bridge of righteousness.\nDuryodhana, burning with anger,\nIn that assembly, with the victory of the empire's glory. 26). Meaning of the word: Api-- also; Swa-dorbhyam-- own arms; Vijay-- Arjuna; Achyutabhyam-- including Shri Krishna; Dharmena-- through Dharma; Dharma:--king\nYudhishthira; Paripati--Nurturing; Setum--Respect of Dharma; Duryodhana--Duryodhana; Atapyata--Got jealousy; Yat--Of;\nWhose; Sabhayam--Royal court; Samrajya--Royal; Lakshya-Eshraya; Vijaya-Anuvrittiya--By service to Arjuna..\nNow I would like to ask that Maharaj Yudhishthir, according to religious principles and the path of Dharma,\nis being nurtured by the state with respect? Earlier, Duryodhana used to burn with jealousy.\nBecause Yudhishthira was protected by two arms in the form of Krishna and Arjuna, as if they\nwere his own arms. Meaning: Maharaj Yudhishthir was the symbol of dharma. When they, with the help of Lord Krishna and Arjuna,\nwere ruling their empire, the glory of their empire had surpassed even the imaginations of all the gods in heaven. His real arms were those of Lord Krishna and Arjuna. In this way, they were far ahead of everyone.\nDuryodhana was jealous of th