          "textEn": "35\nThe crimes of the Kurus were forgiven. On Earth, there were many kings who were proud due to three types of\nwealth--money, education, and followers--and they were constantly disturbing the Earth with military\nactivities. God was in this box that all of them of Kurukshetra\nIn the battlefield, so that all of them could be wiped out together, so that their killing\nThe purpose could be fulfilled in a short time. When the rulers or heads of states, or states, become proud of wealth, education, and population growth,\nthey display military force and cause suffering to the innocent. When\nLord Krishna himself was present, there were many such kings in the world, therefore, Lord prepared a plan for the Kurukshetra war. In the manifestation of his universal form, God has expressed his intention to kill in this way,\n\"I have descended on this earth in a cruel form to reduce the unwanted population\nwillingly.\"\nI will eliminate all the people gathered here, in addition to you Pandavas.\nI will put them down. This slaughter will not wait for your participation. It is pre-planned. All the people\nWill be killed by me. If you want to become famous like a hero in the battlefield and in the war,\nIf you want to enjoy the looted property, then O Savyasachi! You immediately become the cause of this killing,\nand receive its credit. Drona, Bhishma, Jayadratha, Karna, and other great warriors have already been killed by me. Don't worry. Fight the war and become famous as a great warrior. ( Bhagavad Gita 11.32-34)\n\nGod always wants that his devotee becomes the hero of any anecdote performed by him. They wanted to see their devotee and friend Arjun as a hero of the Kurukshetra war,\nThat is why they waited for all the wicked people of the world to gather. This is the reason for their waiting,\nAnd there is no other reason.\nFor the destruction of the obstacles to unbornness,\nFor the sake of performing actions, for the sake of attaining the objects of action,\nOtherwise, what does one attain? The body, the yoga,\nAnd the other qualities, the system of actions. 44)."
