          "textEn": "44\nThey take the form of self-realization. These various stages of gradual development lead to the supreme state of divine love.\nEven in this supreme state, other characteristics like affection, anger, and attachment\nare found. Slowly, in special circumstances, they attain this state of Mahabhav, which is not generally possible in living beings. All of these manifestations of God's love were revealed in Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu. In the Dhakti-rasasuta-sindhu composed by Shri Roop Goswami, the chief disciple of Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu, these divine\nsequences of characteristics have been systematically described, which are demonstrated by pure devotees like Uddhava. We also\npresented a study titled 'The Nectar of Decoction' as a summary of Bhakti-Rasamrita-Chindhu.\nHave. This book can be seen for more information on Bhakti Science.\nShanakarbhagavalokanrulokam punaragatam.\nVimrjya netre viduram preetyahodhava utsmayan. 6>. Meaning of the word:\n\nShanakayah - slowly; Bhagavat - God; Lokat - from the abode; Nri-lokam - human world; Agatah - having come again;\nVimrijya - having wiped; Netre - eyes; Viduram - from Vidura; Preetya - with affection; Aah - said; Uddhava: - Uddhava; Utasmyan - through those\nmemories..\n\nMahabhagavat Uddhav immediately descended from the abode of God to the human level and wiping his eyes, he awakened his old memories and he spoke to Vidur with a pleasant face. Meaning: When Uddhav was absorbed in the divine emotion of love for God, he forgot everything about the external world. A pure devotee constantly resides in the abode of God, even in the present body, which is related to this world. A pure devotee does not remain completely on the physical level, because he remains immersed in the divine thoughts of God.\nBecause now Uddhav wanted to talk to Vidur, therefore Uddhav, from the abode of God, Dwarka,\ndescended and came to the physical level of humans. Although a pure devotee remains present in this mortal world,\nit is only because God is engaged in divine love that he lives here, not due to any other\nphysical reason. A being can either live on a physical level according to the state of their existence\nor in the divine abode of God. The explanation of the ecological changes occurring in the living being is given by Lord Shri\nChaitanya in the teachings given to Srila Rupa Goswami in Chaitanya Charitamrita, Kaun Gai Hey, \"All...\""
