          "textEn": "56\n\nAlways, especially, they remain merciful. Kurshiya, wise men, and yogis have special tendencies in the qualities of their nature, therefore they are called others or\ndevotees. These others, in whom yogis are also included, sometimes torment the devotees of God. The great sage Durvasa Muni, therefore, tormented Maharaj Ambarisha, because he was a great devotee of the Lord. The great worker and wise Hiranyakashipu tormented his own Vaishnava son, YER Maharaj. By others,\nThere are many examples of being aware of the peaceful devotion of the Lord. When such a conflict occurs,\nGod, out of great grace towards his pure devotees, appears in a tangible form with his associates who control the great essence. God is everywhere, in both the physical and spiritual worlds, and when a conflict arises between his devotees and non-devotees,\nHe appears for his devotees.\nJust as electricity is generated anywhere due to the friction of matter,\nin the same way, because God is omnipresent, due to the conflict of devotees and non-devotees,\nthey are generated anywhere. When Lord Krishna appears for a purpose (mission),\nall his senses are with him. When they appeared as the son of Vasudeva, there was a difference of opinion regarding their incarnation. Some said ^“He is the perfect being, the Supreme Personality of Godhead”.” Some said ^“He is an avatar of Narayan.' ' Others said, \"They are incarnations of Kshirodakshayi Vishnu,\" but in reality, they are the original complete\nParamatma, Lord. †— Krishna is the Lord himself, and Narayana is the same. All men and other incarnations,\ncome with them to perform various parts of their divine plays. The sign of greatness being filled with\nindication that men live with them, who create the great element. This is confirmed by this Vedic hymn\nMahantam Vibharamatyanam.\nWhen there was a clash between Kansa and Vasudeva and Ugrasen, Lord Krishna appeared like lightning. Vasudeva and Ugrasen were devotees of God,