 वह उन अभक्तं के लिए शोक\nकरता है, जो भगवान्‌ के परम यशों को न जानते हुए उन्हें इसलिए काल्पनिक सोचते हैं क्योकि शास्त्रों",
          "textEn": "57\nIn this way, leaving all the objects in darkness, they disappeared, as Uddhava described.\nMother, why is this birth of his?\nA mockery in the house of Vasudeva.\nHe himself, dwelling in the forest, is afraid of the arrogant.\nHe is the one who is born from the beginning, and he is the one who is endless in strength. RE Il\nMeaning of the word\n\nMam--To me; Khedayati-- Causes pain; Etat-- This; Ajasya-- Of the unborn; Janma-- Birth; Vidambanam-- To deceive;\nYat-- Which; Vasudeva-gehe- In Vasudeva's house; Vrije-- In Vrindavan; Cha-- Also; Vasah- Vasah; Bhiyat-- From fear;\nIva-- Like; Swayam- Self; Purat- From Mathura; Vyavatisit- Went away; Yat- Which are; Anant- Virya- Immensely powerful. When I think about Lord Krishna, how he, being unborn, was born in Vasudeva's\nFETE, how he went to Vraja under the protection of his father, and how he remained hidden there from the fear of enemies,\nand how, despite being immensely powerful, he fearfully fled from Mathura,\nthese confusing events cause me pain.\nMeaning: Since Shri Krishna is the original being from whom all things and all living beings originated ​​— Aham\nSarvasya Prabhavah (Bhagavad Gita 10.8), Janmadyasya Yatah (Vedanta Sutra 1.1.2) Therefore, equal to him or\nThere can be no object greater than him. God is supremely complete, and whenever he performs his divine play as a son, a relative, or\nan enemy, he plays his role so perfectly that even pure devotees like Uddhava become deluded. For example, Uddhava knew very well that Shri Krishna is always present,\nremains, and they can never die or disappear forever, yet they were grieving for Krishna. All these events are like complete arrangements to fully grant their ultimate glory.\nare. It is all for the sake of joy. When a father plays with his young son, and he lies down on the ground,\nas if he has been defeated by his son, then this is only to provide joy to that young son,\nand nothing else.\nBecause God is omnipotent, therefore He can reconcile the contradictions like birth and non-birth, power and defeat, fear and fearlessness. A pure devotee knows very well that\nhow it is possible to reconcile contradictions for God, but he grieves for those who, without knowing the supreme glories of God, consider them imaginary because the scriptures"
