          "textEn": "62\nSo, they were friends, not enemies, but because of appreciating the beauty of God's face, they were somewhat in love with God, they were immediately sent to Vaikuntha. The private abode of God is called Golok Vrindavan.\nAnd that abode, where his descendants reside, is called Vaikuntha Loka, where Lord Narayana remains in the form of\nexisting. In every living being, the Team remains dormant, and the entire method of devotion to God is to\nawaken the dormant eternal devotion to God. But such divine awakenings happen in crores.\nThey happen. Those in whom the divine love is fully awakened, they go to the spiritual sky, Golok Vrindavan.\nBut those in whom, by coincidence or through association, the divine love is properly awakened,\nthey are sent to Vaikuntha Loka.\nFrom a philosophical point of view, there is no difference between Golok and Vaikuntha,\nbut in Vaikuntha, the service of God is done with immense devotion, while in Golok, his service\nis done with natural affection.\n\nThis divine love is awakened by the association of pure devotees of God. Here, the word 'Parthak-pu:' is important. Those who had seen the beautiful face of God in the battlefield of Kurukshetra, they were first\nArjun had purified with the strike of his arrows. With the intention of lightening the burden of the world,\nArjun had appeared, and Arjun was helping them by fighting on their behalf. Arjun had personally\nrefused to fight, and the entire teaching of the Bhagavad Gita was given to Arjun to put him in the war. As a pure devotee of God, Arjun, giving it priority before his decision,\naccepted to fight. In this way, Arjun fought to help God in reducing the burden of the world.\nIn this aim, he fought to be helpful.\nAll the works are accomplished by pure devotees on behalf of God,\nbecause the pure devotee of God has nothing personal to do. The destruction by Arjuna was equivalent to the destruction caused by God himself. As soon as Arjun shoots an arrow at 