          "textEn": "86\nKi--what; Bhu--on earth; Ayam--this; Kshipta--having been; Ur--very; Bharah--burden; Yat--that;\nDrona--Drona; Bhishma--Bhishma; Arjuna--Arjuna; Bhima--Bhima; Mulayah--with support; Athashat--eighteen; Akshauhini--army;\nVyuha-vinyoga (see Bhagavad 1.16.34); Mat-anshai: -with my descendants; Asthe--are still; Balam--great power;\nDurvishaham--unbearable; Yadunamu--of the Yadu dynasty..\n\n[ At the end of the Kurukshetra war, the Lord said] Now, with the help of Drona, Bhishma, Arjuna, and Bhima,\nthe heavy burden of the earth on the eighteen Akshauhini armies has been reduced. But what is this? Even now, the vast power of the Yadu dynasty, which was born from me, remains, which can become even more unbearable burden. Meaning: This is a false theory that the world becomes overburdened by population growth, and\nthat is why wars and other destructive processes occur. The Earth is never overburdened.\nOn Earth,\nin the greatest mountains and seas, more creatures live than humans, but they are never\noverburdened. If the entire population of creatures living on the surface of the earth is counted, then it\nwill definitely be found that the population of humans is not even five percent of the number of creatures. If the birth rate of humans is increasing, then in the same proportion, the birth rate of other creatures is also increasing.\nIs. The lower animals-mammals, reptiles, aquatic organisms-have far better birthrates than humans. By the order of God, there is sufficient provision of food for all the creatures of the earth, and if there is unequal growth among the creatures,\nthen they can arrange for more.\nTherefore, the question of increasing burden due to population growth does not arise. The earth has become overburdened due to irregular adherence to God's will. God appeared on earth to stop the increase of the wicked,\nnot due to the increase in population, as false statements are made by worldly economists. When Lord Krishna appeared, 