          "textEn": "87\n\nTherefore, even if there is a great increase in population on Earth, if people properly follow the divine nectar of devotion and are not wicked, then this burden of the Earth is a source of joy for them. Load.\nThere are two types--animal load and love load. The burden of animals is unbearable, but the burden of love is the source of joy. Srila Viswanath Chakravarthy has given a very practical description of love-burden. They say\nthat the burden of a young wife on her husband, the burden of a child in the mother's lap, and the burden of property on a merchant, these\nalthough in reality are burdens from the point of view of gravity, but these are sources of joy, and in the absence of such burdensome things,\nthe burden of separation can be experienced, which is heavier to bear than the real burden of love. When Lord Krishna spoke of the burden of the Yadava dynasty on Earth, he\nbrought up the topic of something different from the burden of animals.\nThe number of family members born from Krishna was in the millions.\nAnd this was indeed a great increase in the population of the earth, but they were all parts of their divine descendants.\nTherefore, for the earth, they were a great source of joy. When God mentioned them in relation to the weight of the earth, then in his mind, there was a feeling of their imminent disappearance from the earth. All the members of Lord Krishna's family were incarnations of various deities, and they were to be extinct from the earth along with God. When he mentioned the unbearable burden of the earth regarding the Yaduvansh,\nhe was indicating their separation burden. Srila Jeeva Goswami has confirmed this conclusion.\nThose who are deluded by falsehood,\nare the eyes of the wise.\nHe is the means of their destruction, yet he himself is not destroyed. 95 Meaning of the word\n\nMithah-- mutual; Yada-- when; Esham-- theirs; Bhavita-- will be; Vivadah-- quarrel; Madhu-amad-- intoxication caused by drinking alco