          "textEn": "88\n\nWill decrease. Meaning: God and his attendants appear and disappear at the will of God. On them,\nthe laws of physical nature do not apply. No one was able to kill the family of God,\nnor was there any possibility of their natural death by the laws of nature. Therefore, the only way to eliminate them was that they should wage war against each other, as if they were becoming intoxicated by drinking alcohol. This so-called\nwar could have happened by the will of God, otherwise there was no reason for all of them to fight. The way\nArjun was fascinated by family affection, and then the Bhagavad Gita was told to him,\nIn the same way, the Yaduvansh was made into a drunkard by the will of God. Nothing more concrete than that. Devotees of God and fellow seekers are fully surrendered souls. Therefore, they are divine instruments in the hands of God,\nand they can be used as God wishes.\nEven pure devotees enjoy such pastimes of God,\nbecause they want to see God pleased. The devotees of God never emphasize independent\npersonality; instead, they use their individuality to fulfill God's wishes. This association of devotees with God perfects the divine plays of God. And establishing in the kingdom of the Lord, the unborn, the righteous.\nHe showed the path to the good, the virtuous. 16 Il\n\nMeaning of the word\n\nEvam--in this way; Saschintya--thinking in one's mind; Bhagavan--God; Swa-rajye--in one's own kingdom; Sthapya- established; Dharmajam--to Maharaj Yudhishthira; Nandayam- made happy; Suhridah- friends; Sadhunam- of saints; Varm- path;\nDarshayan- showing.\n.\n\nThinking in this way, Lord Krishna, to demonstrate the ideal of administration in the path of virtue,\nestablished Maharaj Yudhishthira on the position of the supreme controller of the world.\nUttarayam Dhrutah Purovashah Sadhvabhimanyuna.\nSa Vai Dronastrasamplushtah Punarbhagavata Dhrutah. 17). Shabdartham.\n\nUttarayam--of Uttara; Yel--established; Piroh--of Pruh; Vanshah--heir;