          "textEn": "89\n\nThe embryo of the descendant of Puru, established in the womb of his wife Uttara by the great warrior Abhimanyu,\nwas burnt by the weapon of Drona's son, but later God protected him again. Meaning: When Parikshit's body, after being conceived by Uttara from the great warrior Abhimanyu,\nwas in the embryonic stage, it was burnt by Ashwatthama's Brahma, but God provided another body inside the womb. In this way, the descendants of Puru were saved. This event is its direct\nproof that the body and the soul, that is, the spiritual spark, are different. When the sperm of a man enters\nand the life takes shelter in the womb of a woman, then there is a mixture of the secretions of the male and female, which creates a body of pea-\nsized, which gradually grows and develops into a complete body, hey. But if\nsomehow this fetus is destroyed, then the creature has to take shelter in another body or in the womb of another woman.\nIt has to take shelter.\nThat specific being, whom Maharaj was chosen to be the descendant of Puru or Pandavas,\nwas no ordinary being, and by the great will of God, he was to be the successor of Maharaj Yudhishthira.\nTherefore, when Ashwatthama destroyed the embryo of Maharaj Parikshit, then God, through his\ninner power, entered the womb of Uttara, to give darshan to the future and hybrid Maharaj Parikshit. Within the womb, God encouraged the infant with his grace, and\nWith his omnipotence, he provided complete protection to him in the new body. With the power of his omnipresence,\nHe was present within and outside the other members of the Uttara and Pandava families.\nAyajayadharmasutamaschamedhastaribhirvibhuh.\nSoapi kshmaanuja rakshatreme krishnamanuvratah. 18>. Meaning of the word:\n\nAyajayat-- Having made prosperous; Dharma-Sutam-- Son of Dharma (Maharaj Yudhishthir); Aschamedhah-- By Yagya; Tribhih-- By three; Vibhuh-- The Supreme Being; Saha- Maharaj Yudhishthir; Api-- Also; Kshamam- To the earth; Anujaih- Along 