          "textEn": "9]\nDid not violate the Vedic commands, because these are guides for human life ©.\nAccording to the Vedic principles based on the knowledge system called Sankhya\nPhilosophy, regular human life is the real path to enjoying the necessities of life. In the absence of such knowledge of detachment and worldly affairs, the so-called human civilization is equivalent to an animal society that eats, drinks, and indulges. God was acting independently according to His will; yet He gave the teaching to live such a life through His practical example\nthat it would not be against the principles of detachment and knowledge. Knowledge and\nThe attainment of detachment is the real completeness of life, as has been elaborately propounded in Sankhya philosophy. The meaning of knowledge is to know that the purpose of human life is to end all the sufferings of the world.\nAnd despite regularly fulfilling physical needs, man's such\nis to be detached from such a brutal life.\nTo fulfill the demands of the body is animalistic life, and to fulfill the purpose of the soul is human purpose. With a smiling face, with a beautiful speech,\nWith a character that is never false, with a beautiful form, and with a self. 20>. Meaning of the word:\n\nSnigdh--gentle; Smit--smiling; Chitvan--with a gentle gaze; Vacha--with words; Piyush-kalpayan--like nectar;\nCharitrena--with character; Anavadya-nen--without fault; Shri--Lakshmi; Niketen--abode; Cha--and; Atmana--from one's divine body..\n\nThey were there, in the abode of Goddess Lakshmi, in their divine body, as always, with their gentle and\nsweet smiling face, with their nectarous words, and with their unblemished character. Meaning: It is said in the previous verse that Lord Krishna, situated in the truths of Sankhya philosophy,\nis detached from all kinds of subjects. In the presented verse, it is said that they are the abode of Lakshmi Devi. Neither of these facts is inconsistent with each other.\nLord Krishna is detached