          "textEn": "95\nMeaning of the word\nPuryamu--in Dwarka Puri; Kad- once; Kridadhi:--by sports; Yadu--of the Yadava dynasty; Bhoj--descendants of Bhoja;\nKumarakaih--by the princes; Kopitah--became angry; Munayah--by the sages; Shepu--cursed; Bhagwat--of God; Mat--desire;\nKovida:--knower..\nOnce, the great sages became angry with the games of the Yaduvanshi and Bhojavanshi princes, so\nthey cursed those princes according to the will of God. Meaning: Those companions of God who were playing the roles of the princes of the Yadu and Bhoj dynasties\nwere not ordinary beings. It is not possible that they insult any saintly man or sage, or the group of sages,\nwho were pure devotees of God, of the princes born in the holy Yadu or Bhoj dynasties, of any kind\nof play, FG would be, because God himself had incarnated as the descendant of them. By the sages\nBeing cursed by the princes was a divine play of God for anger display.\nTo the princes,\nTherefore, they were cursed so that people could know that those descendants of God could also be the objects of the wrath of the great devotees of God,\nWho could never be destroyed by any action of nature. Therefore, a person should exercise great caution that he does not commit any offense at the feet of a devotee of God.\nDo not commit any offense. Then, some months, the Vrishnis, the guests, and the followers,\nWere joyful, shining brightly, and the gods were deluded in the chariot. 25. Meaning of the word\nTatha--thereafter; Katipaya--some; Masaih--after spending time; Vrishni--descendants of Vrishni; Bhoj--descendants of Bhoj; Andhaka-\nAdayah-descendants of Andhaka, etc.; Yayu-went; Prabhasam-a pilgrimage place named Prabhas; Sahashtaah-with great joy; Ratheh-\nOn their respective chariots; Dev-by Krishna; Vimohitaah-attracted..\nA few months passed, then all the Vrishni, Bhoja, and Andhaka dynasties, who were enchanted by Krishna,\nwho were incarnations of gods, went to Prabhas. But those who were eternally devoted 