          "textEn": "96\nThere-- there; after bathing; to the ancestors; to the gods; to the sages; also-- also; this-- this;\nCertainly; that-- that; from water; after bathing; then-- thereafter; to the Brahmins; to the cow;\nMany-qualities-- extremely useful; gave-- donated;\nHaving reached there, they all bathed and, with the water of that pilgrimage site, satisfied the ancestors, the gods, and\nthe sages. They gave cows to Brahmins in royal donation.\n\nMeaning: Among the devotees of God, there are several categories, among which the accomplished and the accomplished are the main ones. Eternal.\nDevotees never fall below in the field of the material environment, even if sometimes God's mission\nTo fulfill it, why shouldn't they have to come to the physical level. Among the accomplished devotees,\nthey are chosen. Among the devotees, some are mixed and some are pure devotees.\nMixed devotees sometimes\ndisplay enthusiasm towards desire-driven actions and remain engaged in philosophical contemplation. Pure devotees are\nindependent of all mixtures and are completely absorbed in the service of God, wherever they may be.\nOr in any state. The pure devotees of God do not keep the service of God\nat the bottom of their feet to go to holy pilgrimage places. The song of Shrinrotam Das Thakur, a great devotee of the modern era,\nis, **going to pilgrimage sites is another infatuation of the mind, because the service to God done at any place\nis the ultimate culmination of spiritual accomplishment.'\"\n\nFor those devotees who are completely satisfied with the love and devotion of God, there is no need to go to various pilgrimage sites.\nBut those who are not so devoted have to go to pilgrimage sites and\nperform rituals and do the intended work.\nThe prince Prabhas of the Yadu dynasty, after going there,\nfulfilled all the duties to be performed in the pilgrimage site and offered his meritorious deeds to his ancestors and others.\n\nNormally, every human being is indebted