          "textEn": "97\nGold, silver, beds, and mats,\nAnd chariots, horses, and maidens, I also arrange in the circle. 27). Meaning of the word:\n\nHiranyam-- Gold; Rajatam-- Silver; Shayyam-- Spread; Vasansi-- Clothes; Ajin-- Leather for seats; Kambalan-- Blankets;\nYanam-- Horses; Rathan-- Chariots; Ibhan-- Elephants; Kanya-- Girls; Dharam-- Land; Vritti-kari-- For providing livelihood\nAlso- also,\n\nIn the donation to Brahmins, not only well-fed cows were given, but they were also given gold, silver, beds, clothes,\nLeather seats, blankets, horses, elephants, girls, and sufficient land for livelihood\nwere given. Meaning: All these donations were for those Brahmins whose lives were completely engaged in social welfare from both spiritual and material perspectives. The Brahmin-Gana were not providing their services to salaried servants,\nbut rather society was providing them with all the necessities.\nSome Brahmins,\nwhose marriages were not possible, were given daughters off. Therefore, there was no economic\nproblem in front of the Brahmins. Kshatriya kings and wealthy merchant people used to provide them with all the necessary items.\nAnd Brahmins were completely dedicated to the upliftment of society in return. Between different castes,\nthis was the only way of social cooperation. When the Brahmin class or caste, in which Brahmin qualities were not present,\nbeing nurtured by society, gradually became a means of livelihood, then they, falling, became Brahmabandhu, meaning ineligible\nBrahmins. Similarly, other members of society gradually fell below the social norms of progressive life,\nas it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, the caste system is created by God and is organized according to the merit of the work done towards society, not as a birthright as\nfalse claims are made in the current fallen society.\nHaving given food to the thieves, the Lord appeared.\nThe cowherds, the brave ones, and the warriors bowed their heads. 28>. Meaning of the word:\n\nAnn