          "textEn": "07\nIt depends on. This rule is expressed by the phrase \"more mind kachhu or hai karta ke man and\" (more mind something else is there). In ancient times, when the gods and Vasus performed Yagya, Uddhava, as a Vasu, expressed his desire to associate with God,\nwhich is extremely rare for the wise or those who are motivated by desire. Such\npeople do not know any practical things about becoming a companion of God. Only pure devotees\ncan know only by the grace of God that the personal association with God is the highest achievement of life. God gave assurance to\nUddhava that He would fulfill his wish. It seems that when God gave this information to Uddhava through a sign, then Maharishi Maitreya became aware of the importance of attaining the company of God in the end.\nHe is the best of the virtuous, the supreme.\nHe is my divine grace.\nWhom I have created in this world,\nI offer to him with a mind free from attachment. 92 Shabdartham\nSaha--He; TH: -Their; Sadho--He is a saint; Charamah--He is the ultimate; Bhavanam--From all your incarnations (in the form of Vasu); Asaditah--\nNow attained; Te- to you; Mat- mine; Anugraha- grace; Yat- in the form of; Yat--because; Mamu- to me; Nu-worlds-\nThe worlds of bound souls; Rahah- in solitude; Utsarjantam- renouncing; Dishtaya- by seeing; Dahashvan- that which you have seen; Vishad-\nAnuvritha- with unwavering devotion..\nOh saint, your present life is the last and supreme, because in this life you have received my\ngreatest grace, oh. Now, abandoning this universe of bound souls, you can go to my divine abode, Vaikuntha.\nYou can go. Because of your pure and unwavering devotion, your coming to me in this secluded place is a great blessing for you.\nMeaning: When a complete soul, having attained the state of liberation, is fully aware of the divine knowledge that can be attained,\nit is allowed to enter the spiritual sky, where the abode of Vaikuntha exists. God, in solitude, from the perspective of