          "textEn": "[0\nBlackness, that which is full of pride, the hermitage:\nThe wise man's mind is aroused by self-awareness. 16. Meaning of the word\n\nKarmani--actions; Anehasyam--not desiring; Bhavah--birth; Abhavasya--never born; Te--yours; Durga-ashrayah--fortress;\nTaking refuge in the fortress; Ath--thereafter; Ari-bhayat--from fear of the enemy; Palayanam--escape, flight; Kaal-atmanah--of the time; Yat--that; Pramada-ayuta--in the company of women; Ashramah--household life; Swa-atmanah--in one's own\nSoul; Rate:--One who meditates; Khyadhiti--is distracted; Dhih--intellect; Vidam--of the wise; Iha--in this world HL\nO Lord, even the intellect of the wise sages is disturbed when they see that you, while being free from all\ndesires, remain engaged in desire-driven actions; even being unborn, you take birth; being the controller of time, you flee from fear of enemies and take refuge in the fortress, and even while reveling in your soul, you, being afraid of many women, enjoy the pleasures of household life.\nMeaning: A pure devotee of God does not have much\nrelationship with philosophical contemplation of God's divine knowledge. Nor is it possible to have complete knowledge of God. Whatever little knowledge they have about God,\nthat is enough for them, because devotees are satisfied only by listening to and chanting the divine plays of God. This gives them all divine bliss. But some of the Lord's\nleelas seem mutually contradictory to these pure devotees. Therefore, Uddhav asked God about some mutually contradictory events of his\nleelas. It is described that God\ndoes not have to do anything himself, and in fact, it is so, because in the creation of the physical world and its\nupkeep, God has nothing to do. Then it seems contradictory to hear that God\nlifts the Govardhan mountain himself to protect his pure devotees.\nGod is the supreme Brahman, the ultimate truth, who\nappears like a human, but Uddhava had doubts whether he could perform many divine 