          "textEn": "77\nFor some time, they became sorrowful, but due to excessive pride in divine knowledge, they were able to\ncalm themselves through that knowledge. As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, due to long-term association with physical relationships,\nthe occurrence of grief due to the destruction of friends and relatives is not surprising at all, but man should learn the art of suppressing such grief through higher divine knowledge.\nThe beginning of the Krishna-related conversation between Uddhava and Vidura took place in the evening.\nAnd now, Vidura's knowledge increased even more with Uddhava's company. That great devotee, the Kauravas,\nDid not understand this main thing in the company of Krishna, due to their eagerness. 24). Meaning of the word\n\nSah-with Vidur; Tam-with Uddhava; Maha-great devotee of God; Vrajan-going; Kaurav-Rishabhah-in Kauravas\nThe best; Vrishambh-with faith; Abhyadhatta-made a request; Idam-this; Mukhyam-main; Krishna-of Lord Krishna;\nParigreh-in devotion to God.\n.\n\nWhen Uddhava, the chief and most trusted devotee of God, was about to leave, Vidur asked him with affection and\nwith faith. Note: Vidur was much older than Uddhava. In family relations, Uddhava was Krishna's contemporary brother.\nWhile Vidur was of the age of Krishna's father, Vasudeva. But Uddhava, despite being young, was very much advanced in devotion to God, that is why he is said to be the foremost among the devotees of God here. Vidur\nhad faith in this, therefore he addressed Uddhav by considering him of the same higher class. Between two devotees,\nthe custom of politeness is this way.\nVidur said,\nKnowledge is the supreme self-illuminating light.\nWhen the lord of yoga says,\nWho is worthy of speaking, that which is for Vishnu,\nThe servants, for their own servants, perform actions. 25. Meaning of the word\n\nVidur said-- Vidur said; Gyanam-- knowledge; Param-- divine; Swa-atma-- concerning the soul; Rahah-- mystery; Prakasham-- enlightenment;\n