          "textEn": "56\nThrough this, the entire physical world becomes possible. Meaning: The physical nature, called Maya, is the physical and capable cause of the universes, but\nIn the background, for all these functions, God is the form of consciousness. Just as consciousness in an individual body is the body,\nSimilarly, the supreme consciousness of God is the source of all\nForces in the physical nature. This is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (9.10) as follows--\n\nBy the Maya-adhyasita, the nature is produced, the moving and the unmoving.\n\nBy the cause, O son of Kunti, the world is transformed. *'God's hand is in the final overs of all the powers of physical nature. It is only as a result of this supreme cause that all the functions of physical nature appear well-organized and systematic,\nand all things grow regularly.\n''\nKalavruttya tu mayayam gunamayamadhokshajah |\nPurushenatmaabhutena viiryamadhattta viiryavan. 26). Shabdartham\nKaal--of time; Vrittya--by influence; Tu--but; Mayaayam--in Maya; Guna-mayyam--in qualities of nature; Rupam--in form; Adhoshshajah--Brahma; Purusena--by the incarnation of a Purusha; Atma-bhuten--that which is the essence of the self; Veeryam--the seed of living beings;\nAdhatta--established; Veeryavan--by the Supreme Being. In the form of his own divine incarnation, the supreme being establishes the seed in the three qualities of nature.\nAnd in this way, all beings are manifested by the influence of eternal time. Meaning: The offspring of any living being is produced when semen is established in the mother's womb by the father,\nand the creature that floats in the father's semen assumes the form of the mother. Similarly, the mother-like\nphysical nature cannot produce any living being from its physical element until itself\nGod does not conceive it with living beings. This is the secret of the origin of living beings.\nThis act of conception\nis accomplished by the first person incarnation, Karunaravashayi Vishnu. Only b