          "textEn": "]57\nThe Almighty God can conceive even with his eyes, therefore he is called Almighty. Each part of their divine body can perform the function of other parts. This is confirmed in the Brahma-\nSamhita (5.32)-- Agati yasya sakalecchadhriyatrimantti. In the Bhagavad Gita (14.3) also, the same\nprinciple is confirmed-- Maya yoniramahadrahm tasmin garbha dadhyasaham. When the great universal world manifests,\nthen the supply to living beings comes directly from God, they are not the product of material nature. In this way,\nNo scientific progress in physics can ever create any living being. The entire mystery of physical creation\nis this. Souls are different from matter, therefore, until they are like God,\nthey are not situated in spiritual life, they cannot be happy. The bewildered being, due to the forgetfulness of this original state of their life,\nwastes time in vain to become happy in this material world.\nThe complete Vedic process is to remind the living being of this essential nature of life. God provides a physical body to the enlightened soul for its so-called enjoyment, and if he is not conscious,\nand does not enter into spiritual consciousness, then God puts him back into the same unmanifest state in which he was at the beginning of creation. Here, God is called virile, because he\nconceives those countless beings in physical nature who have been bound since time immemorial.\nThen arose the great essence, unmanifested, unborn, and unmanifested.\nThe knower of the self, the self-existent, the universe, the inert, the unmanifested. 27). Meaning of the word\n\nTatah-- After that; Abhavat-- Born; Mahat-- Supreme; Tatvamu-- Essence; Avyaktat-- From the unmanifest; Kala-choditat-- From the time of time; Anthah-kriya-se; Vijnan-atma-- Pure essence; Atma-deha-stham-- situated in the physical soul; Vishwam-sampurnam-- The universe;\nVyanjant- while manifesting; Tamah-nudah-- Supreme light \\\n\nTatah-- After that, the supreme essence of the 