          "textEn": "62. Meaning: All physical creations are made from the subtle to the gross. The entire universe has developed in this way. The feeling of touch developed from the sky, which is a mixture of eternal time, external power, and the sight of God. This touch sensation developed into air in the sky. Similarly,\nAll other gross matter also evolved from subtle to gross--sound in the sky, touch in the air, form\nIn fire, taste in water, and smell in earth. Even though he is the one with the curved form, he is filled with the strength of the sky.\nHe who created the form, the essence, the light, and the eye of the world. 24). Shabdartham\nAnilah--Air; Api--also; Vikurvahah--having transformed; Nabhasah--Sky; Uru-balanvitah--Extremely powerful;\nSasarjah--Born; Roopah--Form; Tat-matram--Indian experience, Tanmatra; Jyotih--Light; Lokasya- of the world;\nLochanam- light for seeing.\n.\nThereafter, a very powerful wind, by interacting with the sky, created the form of sensory perception.\n(Tanmatra) and the experience of form was transformed into electricity, which is the light to see the world. Unmanifested, pervading the light, seen by the radiant sun.\nThe darkness, the ocean, the essence of time, and the union of the three. 35). Shabdartham\nAnilen-- by air; Anvitam-- while doing inner action; Jyotih-- lightning; Vikurvat-- transformed; Paravikshitam- seen by external\nBy sight; Adhatta-utyantha; Ambha-rasamayam- water mixed with taste; Kaal- eternal time; Maya-\nPart- and external energy; Yogatho- by mixture.\n.\nWhen the action of electricity occurred in the air, and Brahma cast his gaze upon it, at that time, eternal time,\nand from the mixture of external energy, water and taste originated.\nJyotishambhoornusansrishtam vikurvadrahmavikshitam.\nMahi gandhagunamadhadhakalamayamshayogatah. 36). Shabdartham\nJyotisha-- light; Ambha-- water; Anusansritham-- originated in this way; Vikurvat-- due to change of form; Brahma-- by Brahma;\nVikshitam-- seen; Mahi