          "textEn": "66\nis. In the Bhagavad Gita (16.19), the Lord has said--\n\nI am the destroyer of those who are wicked and cruel in this world.\n\nI am the destroyer of those who are devoid of mercy, who are lustful, and who are born of demonic lineages. \"Those who are jealous and wicked and vile, I keep them in the ocean of life in various demonic wombs.\nI keep putting them.\"Yamraj, like other controllers, are for those unwanted souls who\nare always engaged in disrupting the peace of God's kingdom. Because all these deities are the trusted servants of God,\ntherefore, they should never be despised.\nO God, utter!\nI bow to the lotus feet of the God.\nRemover of the suffering caused by sin,\nThey cast out the worldly sorrows. 39). Meaning of the word:\nDevah uchu- The gods said; Namam--We respectfully bow; Te--To you; Deva--Oh Lord; Pad-arvindam--Foot-lotus;\nPrapanna- surrendered; Tapa- suffering; Upashama- pacifying; Yat- root-keta- refuge of the lotus feet;\nYatayah- the assembly of sages; Anjasa- completely; Uru- great; Sansar- worldly sorrow; Bahi- outside; Utkshipanti- forcefully\nThrow. The gods said: O Lord, your lotus feet are like an umbrella for the surrendered, who\nprotect them from all the sufferings of the world. All the sages, under that shelter, all\nremove and throw away all physical sufferings. Therefore, we respectfully bow to your lotus feet.\nWe are. Meaning: There are many saints who are engaged in the effort to overcome rebirth and all other material sufferings.\nBut those who take refuge in the lotus feet of God, they\nWithout difficulty, can completely overcome all such sufferings. Other people who are engaged in various kinds of\ndivine works cannot do so. It's so difficult for them to do. They\ncan contemplate artificial methods to be liberated without taking refuge in the lotus feet of God,\nbut that is not possible. From such false liberation, man falls again into this material world"
