          "textEn": "67\nNo matter how much penance he has done. This is the opinion of those deities who are not only proficient in Vedic\nknowledge, but also seers of the past, present, and future. The opinions of the gods are important, because\nthe gods themselves are authorized to take charge of the work and business related to the world order. They\nremain appointed by God as His trusted servants. In the body, the living being,\nNot ashamed of being struck by the leaf.\nThey attain the Lord, the clear one,\nBy taking refuge in the knowledge of the self. 40>. Meaning of the word\n\nDhatah--father; Yat--why; Asminu--in this; Bhave--in the world; Ishah--God; Jivah--living being; Tapah--suffering; Trayena--three;\nAbhikhatah--always; Na--never; Sharam--in happiness; Atman--soul; Labante--obtain; Bhagavan--Oh God; Tava--yours;\nYour; Anghri-chhayaam--shadow of the feet; Sa-vidyaam--full of knowledge; or: Obtaining; Ashrayem--refuge.\nHey father, hey Lord, hey God, in this material world, beings can never attain any happiness\nbecause they remain overwhelmed by three types of sufferings. Therefore, they take refuge in those lotus feet of yours\nwhich are full of knowledge, and that is why we also take refuge in them. Meaning: The method of devotional service is neither emotional nor worldly. This is the path of truth,\nby which the living being can attain divine happiness to get rid of the three types of--bodily, divine, and material--sorrows. Any being bound by the physical world, whether it is a human, an animal, a deity, or a bird,\nhas to suffer spiritual (physical or mental), material (provided by living beings), and divine (divine)\nsufferings as a result of the fruits of their actions.\nHis happiness is to be free from the sufferings of a life bound by worldly affairs.\nNothing happens without hard struggle. But there is only one way to protect him, and that is to take refuge in the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead.\n\nThis argument that a man cannot be freed from material sufferings without acquiring proper knowledge is undoubtedly\ntrue. But the lotus feet of God are filled with divine knowledge, therefore, by accepting their lotus feet, that need is fulfilled. We will explain this in the first chapter"
