          "textEn": "[72\nIn the proximity of the body,\nI am not far from the obstacles.\nEven though I live far away,\nI worship that feet of the Lord. 44). Meaning of the word\n\nYat- since; Sa- in conjunction; Asti-- having become; Deh-- gross body; Gehe- in house; Mama- mine; Aham- I; Iti- thus; Udh- greatly, serious; Duragrahana- unwilling eagerness; Pumsam- of humans; Su- far; Dur- quite far;\nVasath- while residing; Api- although; Puriyam- in body; Bhajem- shall worship; Tat- therefore; Te- yours; Bhagavan- O Lord;\nPada- Anjam- lotus feet.Hey Lord, those who are bound by unwanted curiosity towards mortal bodies and relatives,\nand those who are bound by the thoughts of \"mine\" and \"I,\" they are unable to see your lotus feet,\neven though your lotus feet are situated in their own bodies.\nBut,\nLet us take refuge in your lotus feet.\n\nMeaning: The complete Vedic philosophy of life is that one should be freed from the physical bondage of gross and subtle bodies,\ndue to which man keeps living a painful, dishonorable life. This physical body then\nkeeps going until a person abandons the false notion of asserting dominion over physical nature\ndoes not become. This impulse to dominate the material world is my “”mystery”” and the CF. \"I am the all-\nsurvei of the world. I have many things and I am the owner of more and more things.\nIn matters of property and education, who can be better than me? I am Swami, and I am Ishar. My\nWho else is there?\"All these thoughts reflect the philosophy of \"I am everything\"\n. A person guided by such a way of life can never be freed from worldly bondage.\nBut if someone can agree to listen to only Krishna's stories, then even a person constantly rejected by the sufferings of the world can get rid of bondage. In this Kali Yuga, the process of listening to Krishna's stories is undesirable.\nTo get rid of family affection and to achieve permanent freedom in life, it is the most\ninfluential means. The Kali Yuga is overflowing with sinful deeds, and people are excessively engrossed in the virtues of this era.\nHowever, merely listening to and chanting the stories of Krishna is sure to bring a person back to\nGod's abode. Therefore, humans should be trained to listen to the only Krishna story in every way,\nso that they can get rid of all sufferings."
