          "textEn": "84\nChapter six\nCreation of the cosmic form\nSage said\nThus, considering them as the power of the self, he... The Lord moves swiftly in the still world. 9>. Meaning of the word\n\nRishi said--Maitreya Rishi said; Iti--Thus; Tasam--Their; Swa-shaktinam--By one's own power; Satinaam--Thus;\nStatic; Asametya-Without any combination; Sah-He (God); Prasupta-Idle; Lok-Tantranam-In the worldly systems;\nNishamya-Having heard; Gatim-Progress; Ishwarah-God..\n\nMaitreya Rishi said: Thus, God, due to the lack of combination of his powers like the great element,\nhe heard about the suspension of the progressive creative activities of the universe. Meaning: there is no lack of God’s creation. All powers remain there only\nIn a dormant state. But until their union happens by the will of God,\nno progress can be made. The stalled progressive work of creation can only be revived by the direction of God.\nThen, the goddess, with her knowledge of time, began to perform the Bibhachakramukha ritual.\nThe group of thirty-two elements was filled with the Yugapada. 2>. Meaning of the word\n\nKal-Sajjam- Kali, famous by that name; Tada- At that time; Devim- To the Goddess; Bibhrat- Destructive; Shaktim- Power;\nUrukramah- The most powerful; Traya- Twenty-three; Tatvanamu- Of the elements; Ganam- All of them; Yugapat- At the same time;\nAavishat- Entered..\n\nThen the supremely powerful God entered the twenty-third element, including his external power, the goddess Kali,\nbecause she is the one who combines various types of elements. Meaning: The number of elements of matter is twenty-three: complete physical energy, false ego, sound,\ntouch, form, taste, smell, earth, water, fire, air, sky, eye, ear, nose, tongue, skin, hand,\nfoot, anus (vagina), penis (clitoris), speech, and mind. All these remain interconnected due to the influence of time"
