          "textEn": "85\nAnd are disintegrated in chronology. Therefore, time is the power of God, and this power of God\nworks according to its own way, as per the instructions. This power is called Kali, and it is represented by the Kali, the destructive goddess,\nwho is generally worshiped by people influenced by Tamoguna in the physical world. In the Vedic hymn, this method is described as follows--Moolaprakritirvikrutiramahadashya:\nPrakritivikrutayaha sapta Neve] Vikarau na prakritin vikratiha purushaha. The power that acts as the form of physical nature through the combination of twenty-three elements is not the ultimate source of creation. God enters into the elements\nand transforms his power into Kali. ©. In all other Vedic scriptures, this\nis the accepted principle.\nIn the Brahma-Samhita (5.35), it is said--\n\nEven one of them, to create the universe,\n\nWhich power is there, which is the cause of the universe, which is within.\n\nBetween the universe and the atom,\n\nI worship the primeval being, Govinda. “I worship Lord Govinda, the first God. They enter into the material nature through their own self (Mahavishnu)\nand then into each universe (as the Garbhodakshayi Vishnu). They then (after the dissolution of the kshirodakashaya) enter into all the elements, including the atoms, of the material substance. Virat is countless in the form of universes and in both individual atoms.Similarly, it is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (10.42)--\n\nOr by many, or by one, or by the knower of all, O Arjuna!\n\nI am situated in this world, O king, by the self-existent, the unchanging. YT Arjun! There is no need for you to know about my countless powers,\nwhich work in various ways.\nI enter the physical creation in the form of my essence in all universes and all their elements. This is how the work of creation continues.'\"\nThe astonishing works of physical nature are due to Lord Krishna, therefore he is the ultimate cause or\nThe supreme FRE of all causes."
