          "textEn": "[87]\nIt remains. But when creation is awakened again, then God awakens it and puts it back into action. The soul\nis eternal, and through its actions, its awakened state of consciousness is naturally its life.\nWhile awake, it does not stop doing its work, and in this way, it performs actions according to its various desires. When its desires go to the divine service of God,\nits life becomes complete, and to attain the joy of a constantly awakened life, it\nis sent to Vaikuntha.\nThe thirty-third group of the gods, who are deluded by actions.\nInspired, he was born, with the self-born, the king of men. 4>. Shabdartham\nPrabuddha Jagrat; Karma - Karyakalaapah: by the will of Brahma; Ryaha - Vishatikaha: by the thirty-three main elements; Gana - Saman:\nPraanirupta: by inspiration; Ajanayat: revealed; Swabhimah: by oneself; Matraabhi: by the measure; Adhipurusham: the Supreme Being; Vishwaroopa: the cosmic form;\nWhen, by the will of the Supreme Being, the thirty-three main elements were activated, then the body of the cosmic form of God\nwas manifested. Meaning: The cosmic form or the universal form, which the non-differentialists greatly praise, is not the eternal form of God.\n\nIt is not the eternal form. This is revealed by God's supreme will after the elements of the material creation.\nIt is revealed. Lord Krishna showed Arjuna this cosmic or universal form to convince the non-differentialists\nthat they are the original God. Krishna had manifested a gigantic form.\nIt is not that\nKrishna appeared through the Virat form, therefore the eternal form that was manifested by the Virat form God in Vaikuntha is not\na form. It is the physical manifestation of God. For the curious, the archangels of the temple\nare just like that of God. But even though the immense and worshipped form of God is material, they are\ninseparable from their eternal form. Parena Vishta Swasmrityaya Vishvasrungana. Having eaten the other, one who is free from the worl