ibuting agricultural products, which includes transportation, banking,\netc. Industry is an artificial means of livelihood, and large-scale industries are\nespecially the root of all the problems of society. In the Bhagavad Gita also, the duties of the Vaishyas engaged in business\nGoraksha, agriculture, and trade are described. We have already explained that humans can safely depend on cows and agricultural land for their livelihood."
