          "textEn": "23\nMeaning: Some such foolish philosophers are there, who want to know God through philosophy and mental contemplation. When devotees who know God to some extent accept that\nthe glory of God is unimaginable or inconceivable, then the Koopamanduk philosophers criticize them with condemnation. This philosopher is like that barometer that tried to measure the calm ocean. They do not like to take the pain of meaningless mental contemplation by not taking advice from devotees like Adikavi Brahma.\nBrahmaji had done rigorous meditation for a thousand divine years; yet\nhe said that the glory of God is inconceivable. Therefore, what benefit can this foolish philosopher expect from his mental contemplation? It is said in the Brahma-Samhita that a mental thinker, in the sky of contemplation, with the speed of mind or air,\neven if he keeps flying for crores of years, he will still find it inconceivable.\nBut the devotees do not waste time in the futile search for the knowledge of Brahma, but rather they listen with humility to the glory of God from the authentic devotees. In this way, they experience the divine bliss of the process of listening and chanting. Devotees of God,\nor approve of the devotional works of great souls, and say ​​—\nSahatpanastu mamartha daivi prakritiashritah.\nBhajantyaananyamanaso jnatvabhutadimavyayam. Those who always engage in austerity, and those who are steadfast in their vows,\nand those who worship me with devotion, they are always engaged in austerity. (Bhagavad Gita 9. 13-14)\nThe pure devotees of God, the inner power of God, take refuge in the supreme nature, which is called\nLakshmi Devi, Sita Devi, Shrimati Radharani or Shrimati Rukimini Devi. In this way, they become real\nMahatmas. Mahatmas are not fond of mental contemplation, but they remain steadfastly engaged in devotion to God. The manifestation of devotion occurs through listening to the activities of God and\ninitiating the method of singing and chanting.\