          "textEn": "24\nIt is possible, so it is only through the means of devotion, not by any other method. While contemplating, why would a person waste the valuable time of his entire life, but it does not help in gaining entry into the abode of God. But the great souls do not show any interest in knowing God through mental contemplation, because they take pleasure in listening to the glorious activities of their devotees or demons through divine\ninteractions with God. Devotees,\nthe group, find joy in both of these and remain happy in this life and in the life to come. Therefore, the Lord is the illusion of Maya, and also the enchantress.\nHe who knows himself to be the self, knows no other. 39). Meaning of the word\n\nTherefore--therefore; Bhagwat--divine; Maya--powers; Mayinamu--to the magicians; Api--also; Mohini--the enchanting one; Yat--that;\nWhich; Swayam--by oneself; Cha--also; Atma-varma--self-dependent; Atma--self; Na--not; Veda--knows; Kim--what; Ut--\nTo say about the complete Supreme Being; Apara--of others;\n\nThe astonishing power of the Supreme Personality of Godhead is such that it enchants even magicians. This inherent power is unknown even to Atmaram Bhagwan, therefore, for others, it is certainly\nunknown. Meaning: Even though the foolish philosopher and the worldly disputants of science and mathematical calculations\nmay not believe in the incomprehensible power of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but sometimes they are confused by the wonderful magic of man and nature.\nSuch magicians and jugglers of the world are truly bewildered by the magic of the divine works of God,\nbut they try to reconcile their attachment by saying that all this is mythological imagination. But in the supremely powerful being, nothing\nis impossible or mythological. The most astonishing puzzle for worldly controversial people is this:\nThat on one hand, where they are engaged in calculating the length and width of the infinite power of the Supreme Being,\nAt 