्‌",
          "textEn": "25\nFruits contain thousands of small seeds, and within each seed, the power of another tree is hidden.\nAnd in this, in the form of cause and effect, the power of millions of such fruits is contained. Therefore, trees and seeds\nengage devotees in contemplation of the activities of God, while worldly quarrelsome\npeople waste their time in dry thoughts and desires, which is fruitless in this life and in the next life\nboth. Priding themselves on their thoughts, they never praise the simple hidden\nactivities of the banyan tree. Such poor thinkers are destined to remain trapped in material things. Those who, having not attained, do not turn their minds away.\nI bow to that God, the Lord of all. 40>. Meaning of the word:\n\nFrom whom; unattainable - not being able to measure; Nyavartant - stopping the effort; Vachah - word; Cha - also;\nManasah - from the mind; Saha - with; Aham cha - ego also; Anya - other; Ime - all these; Devah - the gods; Tasamai - to that;\nTo the Supreme Lord, the Lord, TH: - We have failed to know the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead. Therefore, we must respectfully bow down to them with discretion.\n\nMeaning:\n\nThe point is: The Kupamanduka assessor may raise the objection that if the words, mind, and\nthe controllers of ego are unknown to the gods, who are respectively Vedas, Brahma, Rudra, and Brihaspati, etc., then why should the devotees show so much interest in this unknown object? The answer to this is that the devotees\nreceive divine bliss in knowing the pastimes of God, which is certainly unknown to the non-devotees and\nmental thinkers.\nIf someone does not taste the divine bliss, then\nIt is natural that he will return from his contemplation and whimsical conclusion, because he will neither\nConsider them real nor blissful. Devotees can at least know that the supreme truth is complete\nLord Vishnu is the Supreme Being, as it is confirmed in the Vedic wisi-- Om awn: The supreme position is always\nSeen 