          "textEn": "229\nIt is done with the light of the sun and moon, which illuminates physical forms like trees and mountains.\nIs done. The ignorant one considers the reflection of the sun or moon as the real sun or moon, and pure non-dual vision arises from these very thoughts. In reality, the light of the sun and the moon is different from the sun and the moon themselves.\nHowever, there is always a relationship between them. The moonlight spread throughout the sky appears without form,\nBut the lunar world, in whatever form it is, is concrete, and the beings living in the lunar world are also concrete. In the rays of the moon, various physical objects appear less or more important on the Taj Mahal.\nThe moonlight (moonlight) in a deserted place looks more beautiful than that light. Although\nthe light of the moon remains the same everywhere, but by shining in different ways, it appears different.\nSimilarly, the light of God is equally distributed everywhere, but because it is perceived in different ways,\nit appears different. Therefore, the reflection of the moon on the water\nshould not be considered real, and the mistake of understanding the entire situation through Advaita philosophy\nshould not be made. The Moon's wobble (tilt) is also variable. When water remains still,\nthere is no vibration either. In a more stable, bound soul, there is less vibration, but due to physical\nrelationships, this quality of vibration remains present everywhere in varying degrees.\nSa vai nivruttidharmena vasudevanukampaya.\nBhagavaddhaktayogena tirodhatte shanairih. 12). Meaning of the word:\n\nSaha--He; Vai--He; Nivrutti- Virakti; Dharmena--By being attached; Vasudeva--Of the Lord; Anukampaya--With compassion; Bhagavat--In relation to the Lord; Bhakti-Yoga-ena--By connecting; Tirodhatta--Decreasing; Shanaih--In order; Iha--In this world.\n.\n\nBut that illusion of self-recognition can be gradually reduced through the method of devotional service to God, with detachmen