्रवण मात्र से मनुष्य कौ\nअसीम कष्टप्रद अवस्थाएँ शमित हो सकती दँ | अतएव उनके विषय में क्या कहा जाये, जिन्होंने\nभगवान्‌ के चरणकमलों की धूल की सुगंध की सेवा करने के लिए आकर्षण प्राप्त कर लिया\nहो?",
          "textEn": "23.\nWhen they are contaminated, their functions become impaired. To get rid of the disease of the senses,\nwe have to treat them, we don't have to stop them from working, as the non-differentialists\nsuggest. In the Bhagavad Gita (2.59), it is said that a person stops all physical work only when\nhe is satisfied by engaging in a superior task. Consciousness is naturally active, and it cannot be stopped from working\nby artificial means. Stopping a mischievous child artificially is not the real treatment. That\nchild should be put into some superior work so that he automatically stops creating trouble. Similarly,\nonly by engaging the disturbing activities of the senses in good deeds related to God\ncan they be stopped.\nWhen the eyes are busy seeing the beautiful form of God, the tongue is busy tasting the offering, the ears are busy hearing His glory, the hands are busy sweeping the temple of God, the feet are busy going to His shrines,\nThat is, when all the senses are engaged in various divine actions, only then can the divine senses be satisfied, and\nThey will be freed from worldly actions permanently. The Supreme Being, residing within the hearts of everyone,\nor the complete Supreme God, situated in the divine world beyond the material creation, is the seer of all our\ndeeds. Our actions should be so saturated that God bestows grace upon us\nAnd we engage in our divine service. Only then can the senses be completely satisfied, and physical attraction\nwill never be tormented again.\nThe one who removes all sufferings, the one who is praised by virtues, is Murari.\nWhat is the use of repeatedly serving the lotus-like one, which is the essence of the self? 14). Meaning of the word\n\nAshesh-- infinite; Sad- suffering; Shamam-- pacification; Vidhatta- capable of; Gun- translation-- divine name, form,\nQuality, play, associates and equipment etc.; Shravanam- listening and chanting; Murareah- of Murari (Shri Krishna); Kim-\nWhat more can be said; again --Then; Tat--of him; Charan-arvind--Charanakamalah; Parag-seva--Sugandhit Dhul Kau\nFor service; Rati-h-Attraction; Atma-lubdha-Those who have attained such self-achievement L\n\nBy merely chanting and listening to the divine names, forms, etc. of Lord Krishna, man\nCan be relieved of immense painful states. Therefore, what can be said about them, who\nHave attained attraction to serve the fragrance of the dust of the lotus feet of God\nHave?"
