          "textEn": "246\nThe honest guru wishes that his disciples know the method of performing the divine service of God, and\nthe disciples also know that they should learn from a person of proven form about the eternal relationship between God and the living being.\nThey should learn about this subject. To distribute this divine knowledge, a person should take time away from worldly activities with the light of Vedic knowledge.\nOn the strength of that light, one should take time away from worldly activities. This is the summary of all the questions of this shloka. For these reasons, these are not told by the sinless sages.\nWhere is the knowledge of oneself, and where is the devotion and detachment of men? 39). Meaning of the word:\n\nThe causes--The source of knowledge; Cha--also; Tasya--of such knowledge; Iha--in this world; Proktani--cut off; Anagha--without blemish;\nSuribhih--through devotees; Svatah--self-reliant; Gnanam--knowledge; Kutah--how; Pansam-of the living being; Bhaktiha--devotion; Vairagyam--detachment;\nDetachment; Eva-certainly; Va--also..\nWithout the help of such devotees,\nhow can a person attain the knowledge of devotion and detachment? Meaning: There are many inexperienced people who say that self-realization can happen without the help of a guru. They criticize the necessity of a guru, and by propagating this principle,\nthat a guru is not necessary, they try to take his place themselves. But,\nThe Shrimad Bhagavat does not accept this perspective. The great divine scholar Vyasadeva also needed a guru.\nAnd he, according to the orders of his guru Narad, composed this great book\nSrimad Bhagavat. Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu, who himself is Lord Krishna, accepted a guru. Even Lord Krishna made Sānipūnī Muni as his guru for attaining enlightenment. They were the gurus of all the acharyas and saints of the world.\nIn the Bhagavad Gita, Arjuna accepted Shri Krishna as his guru.\nAlthough there is no need for such a formal declaration. Therefore, in every way, there remains no doubt about the need to accept a guru. The only condition is that the guru is authentic.\nThat is, the guru should have come from a proper chain of mutual system. The great saints are learned, but they are never without sin or impurity. Anaghasuri is the one who"
