          "textEn": "249\nChapter 36\nBrahma's manifestation from the Garbhodakashayi Vishnu\nMaitreya said,\n\"He is worthy of being served, the ancient lineage,\nHe is the lord of the world, the supreme.\"\n\"In this world, he wears garlands of unbroken lines,\nAt every step, he is newly awakened.\" 9>. Meaning of the word:\nMaitreya said--Shri Maitreya Muni said; Satta-sevaniyaḥ--worthy of service; Bat--Oh, certainly; Puru-\nVansha--The lineage of King Puru; Yat--Because; Loka-pala:--the king; Bhagavat-pradhānaha--one who is chiefly devoted to God;\nBabhuvith--You were also born; Iha--in this; Ajit--invincible God; Kirti-malaam--a chain of divine deeds; Pade Pade--At every step; Nutanayasi--you become newer and newer; Abhikshnam--always;\nMaha-muni Metreya said to Vidura: The dynasty of King Puru is worthy of serving pure devotees,\nbecause all the heirs of that lineage are devoted to God.\nYou also\nare born in the same lineage, and it is surprising that through your efforts, the divine plays of God\nare becoming more and more new every moment.\nMeaning: The great sage Maitreya thanked Vidura and, giving the context of the fame of his lineage, praised him. The entire lineage was full of devotees of God, and because of this, it was glorified. Because they\nwere not attached to the formless, transcendental, or inner Supreme Being, but were directly connected to God, that is, the complete\nPurushottam, therefore they were worthy of serving God and his pure devotees. Because\nVidur was a descendant of the same lineage, it was natural that he engaged in extending the ever-new glory of God far and wide. Maitreya was delighted to have the glorious company of a person like Vidura. He\nConsidered the company of Vidur to be extremely desirable, because such company makes the dormant\ninterests of a person's devotional service quick.\nI am the remover of the sufferings of the poor and the happiness of the rich.\nI am the remover of the great sorrows of the great.\nI am the Bhagavata Purana"
