          "textEn": "250\nYada Yada Sakshadgavanrishibhyaha. 2>. Meaning of the word:\nSah-He; Aham-I; Nrnam-Of humans; Kshull-Very little; Sukhay-For happiness; Dukham-Sorrow; Mahat-Heavy;\nGatanam-Received; Viramay-For pacification; Tasya-His; Pravartaye-In the beginning; Bhagavatam-Shrimadbhagavatam; Puranam-Puran\nIn; Yat-That; Aah-Said; Sakshat-Directly; Bhagavan-God; Rishibhyah-From the sages..\nNow I begin with the Bhagavata Purana, which was directly said by God to the great sages\nfor the benefit of those who are trapped in excessive suffering for the sake of little pleasure.\nMeaning: Metreya Muni proposed to speak about Shriyadbhagavat, because its composition\nwas specifically done for the solution of all the problems of human society and it has been going on in the disciple-\ntradition. Only those who are fortunate can get the opportunity to listen to Shrimadbhagavat in the company of\npure devotees of God. ©. All beings under the magic of physical power\nare trapped in the bonds of many difficulties only for the sake of a little material pleasure. They are engaged in the karmas of desire,\nWithout knowing the confusions, they remain engaged in them. They, because of this false feeling that the body is the soul,\nattach themselves to numerous false attachments. They think that they are always connected to materialistic things, GHA. This false delusion of life is so strong that man\nremains subject to the external power of God, suffering birth after birth.\nIf he comes into contact with Bhagwat, the scripture,\nand the devotees who know Bhagwat, Bhagwat, then such a fortunate person\nis freed from the material bonds. Therefore, out of compassion for the suffering people of the world, Shrimatraya Muni is first\nproposing to speak about Shrimad Bhagwat. The one who is seated, the first of the gods,\nSuddenly, the god did not know the essence.\n'Vivitasvastatvamat: of others,\nThe chief of the princes, the sages, asked. 3. Meaning of the word\nAasinam--Seat