 को क्षमा कर दिया था। यज्ञ में पराशर सारे असुरो को नष्ट करने में",
          "textEn": "254\nAbsorbing the glories of the Lord. To the Guru who is present in the world,\nTo Parashara and Brihaspati. 8 ”. Meaning of the word:\nSankhyayanah - Maharishi Sankhyayan; Parahamsya - chief among all spiritualists; Vivakshamanah - while speaking; Bhagavat -\nVibhuti - the glory of God; Jagad - told; Sah - He; Asmat - mine; Gurave - to the Guru; Anvitaya - followed;\nParasharayah - to Parashara Muni; Atha Vrihaspatayah Cha - also to Brihaspati..\nSankayan Muni was prominent among the spiritualists, and when he was describing the glories of God in the words of Srimad Bhagavat, it happened that my Guru Parar and Brihaspati both\nheard him.\nI am the preacher, the compassionate one.\nThe sage Pulastya, the ancient one.\nI am that, I will tell you, child.\nWith faith, daily, I am devoted. 9>. Meaning of the word\nPravach-- said; Mahayam- HEH; Sah-he; Dayalah- kind; 3th-of-the-day; Uparyukta- the above; Muni- sage; Pulastya- from Pulastya Muni;\nPuranam- the first; Samastra- all; In the Puranas; Sah-he; Aham-I; Tav-from you; Etat-this; Kathayami- I say;\nVatsa-son; Shraddhalu- for the devotee; Nityam- always; Anuvratay- for the follower +\nAs it has been said before, Maharishi Parashara, upon being told by Maharishi Pulastya,\ntold me the foremost Purana (Bhagwat). Hey son, in the form in which I have heard of him, in the same form I will describe him to you, because you have always been my faithful followers. Meaning: Sage Pulastya is the father of all the Asuras.\nOnce, Parashar started performing a Yagya (a ritual sacrifice).\nIn which all the demons were to be burned and destroyed, because one of these demons had killed their father\nand swallowed him. Maharishi Vashistha Muni arrived at the Yagya and requested Parashar to\nstop this deadly act. In the community of sages, Parashar, due to his position and prestige,\ncould not refuse their request. When Parashar stopped the Yagya, then Asuras' father Pulastya praised him\nand gave him this blessing that in the future he would become a great speaker of Puranas\nwhich are complementary texts to the Vedas. Pulastya praised Parashar's work because Parashar had forgiven the demons\nwith his Brahmin power. In the Yajna, Parashara destroyed all the Asuras"
