          "textEn": "258\nIn that self, the Vedas, the creator,\nHe who is self-existent, whom they call the self, He became. 15). Meaning of the word\nTat--that; Lok--of the universe; Padam--the lotus; Sahah--He; U--certainly; Eva--in fact; Vishnu--Lord;\nPravivishat--entered; Sarva--all; Guna-Avabhasam--the abode of all qualities; Tasmin--in which; Swayam-self; Veda-\nMaya--authentic; Vidhata--the controller of the universe; Swayam-bhum-self-born; A - to whom; Sm-in the past;\nVadanti--they say; Sahah--He; Abhut-became; Eva-certainly; Eva-in fact; Veda-authentic; Vidhata-the controller; Swayam-self; Bhum-self-born; A - to whom; Sm-in the past;\nVadanti--they say; Sahah--He; Abhut-became; Eva-certainly; Eva-in fact; Veda- Within that universe-like lotus flower, Lord Vishnu himself entered in the form of the Supreme Soul.\nAnd when it was thus endowed with all the qualities of material nature, then the direct Vedic knowledge\nwas produced, which we call Swayambhuva (Brahma). Meaning: This lotus flower is the cosmic, universal form of the universe in the material world. At the time of destruction, this\nmerges into the belly of Lord Vishnu and appears at the time of creation.\nThis is Garbhodakashayi\nVishnu is the reason, who enters every universe. In this form, all the beings bound by physical nature\nremain the essence of their actions, and from this lotus flower, first of all, Brahma, that is,\nthe controller of the universe, is born. This first-born being has no physical father, although\nall the others have fathers, therefore he is called Swayasthu. At the time of destruction, he sleeps with Narayan.\nAnd when the second creation happens, he is born in the same way.\nFrom this description, we\nunderstand the gross, the cosmic form, the subtle, the golden womb, and the power of physical creation, Brahma--these three are understood.\nThen, with his four-faced, four-eyed one,\nhe who sees the world, situated,\nand who has opened his eyes in the sky,\nand who has four faces facing north,\nand who has four mouths. 16). Meaning of the word\nTasyam-in that; Sah-He; Cha-And; Ambhah-water; Ruha-in the ear; Karnikaya-in the lotus; Avasthitah-being situated;\nLokam-in the world; Apashyamanah-without being able to see; Parikraman-while circumambulating; Vyogni-in the sky; Vivrutt-eye; Vivrutta-eye;\nWhile moving; Chatvar-four; Labhe-obtained; Anudisham-in the directions; Mukhani-head..\nBrahma, who was born from a lotus flower, could not see the world, although he was situated in a treasure. Therefore, while circling the entire space and moving his eyes in all directions,\nhe attained four heads in the form of four directions."
