          "textEn": "267\nLike a vast mountain, God stands as a dwelling for all inert and conscious beings.\nStanding. They are friends with the serpent, because the infinite God is their friend. Just as there are thousands of golden\nwounds in the mountain, similarly, Lord Dikkh was seen with thousands of hoods with golden crowns of the infinite serpent. Just as a mountain is sometimes filled with jewels, similarly, his body was completely adorned with precious jewels. Just as sometimes a mountain remains submerged in sea water, similarly,\nGod sometimes remains submerged in the water of destruction.\nThe one who is pleasing to the mind, the one who is devoted to vows,\nThe one who is full of glory, the forest garland, Hari.\nThe sun, the moon, the fire, the wind, the sky, the ocean, the three directions,\nThe one who circumambulates, the one who is worthy of praise. 32 ॥ Meaning of the word\nNivitam--Surrounded in this way; Aamnaya--Vedic knowledge; Madhu--Vowel-like sweet sound in beauty; Swa-Kirti-Maya--Of one's own\nGlory; Van-Malaya--With a garland of flowers; Harim--To God; Surya--Sun; Indu--Moon; Vayu--Air; Agni--Fire;\nAgamam--Unreachable, inaccessible; Tridhaambhih--By the three worlds; Parikramat--While circumambulating; Pradhanya-kim--For the war;\nDurasadam--Difficult to reach.\nThus, looking at the mountain-like God, Brahma concluded that they are God\nHari himself. They saw that the garland of flowers lying on her chest was praising her with sweet songs of Vedic knowledge\nand was looking extremely beautiful. They were protected by the Sudarshan Chakra\nfor war, and they could not be hit by the sun, moon, air, fire, etc.\nTaryev Tannabhisarahsarojam\nAtmanambhah shwasanam viyachch. The visible God is the creator of the world.\nHe is beyond the world, yet He is seen by the departure of the world. 22). Meaning of the word\nTherefore, hence; indeed, certainly; his, her; navel, navel; lake, lake; lotus flower; self, self;\nwater of destruction; air of dr