          "textEn": "\nOoh! How unfortunate are the embodied beings that they are unable to know your form.\nThey are incapable. Hey Swami, you are the only knowable element, because nothing above you is supreme.\nEven if something appears superior to you, it is not absolutely complete. You are the creator of matter,\nexisting in the form of Brahman by manifesting the power. Meaning: The greatest ignorance of bound souls in the physical body is that they are not aware of the supreme cause of the vast universe. Different people have different opinions about the supreme cause, but none of them are true. The only supreme cause is Vishnu, but Lord Kou is the Mohini power that\ncomes in the way. God has put his wonderful physical power in manifesting numerous wonders in the physical world. Attracted by that same power, all bound souls, therefore, are unable to know that\nsupreme cause. Therefore, even the greatest scientists and philosophers cannot be considered amazing.\nThey seem wonderful, because they are toys in the hands of the enchanting power of God. Due to infatuation, ordinary people deny the existence of God, and accept the products of the enchanting power as the supreme.\n\nThe supreme cause, God, can only be known through His unintentional grace, which is pure like Brahma"
