          "textEn": "272\nIn the Samhita (5.33), such parts of God Govinda are described as follows--\n\nHTT TANTEI\n\nThe first being, the new youth. In the Vedas, rare, unattainable, and dear to the heart,\n\nI worship that first of all, Govinda. “8 I worship that original God, Govinda, who is non-dual and unbroken. Although they expand in many forms,\nthey are the original cause of all causes. Although they are the oldest person,\nBut remaining unaffected by old age, they always remain young. The Supreme Personality of Godhead cannot be known by bookish knowledge of the Vedas. To understand them, one has to go to the Bhagavad-bhakti.'\"\n\nThe only way to understand God's true form is either devotion to God or to such a devotee of God\nwhose heart is always filled with God.\nIt can be understood from the perfection of devotion that\nthe unique Brahmajyoti is only a partial form of the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, Lord Krishna, and in the material creation,\ntheir three expansions are their inherent qualities. In the spiritual sky of Brahmajyoti, even in the eons, there is no\nchange, and in Vaikuntha, there is no creative activity. The effect of time\nbecomes clear only from its absence. The rays of God's divine body or the infinite\nBrahmajyoti are not obstructed by the influence of material power.\nIn the physical world also, the original Kasha himself\nis God. He creates Brahma, who, receiving power from God, becomes Parvati Kashta.\n\nTadra idam bhuvanam angala angalaya\ndhyane sma no dashitam ta upasakanam.\nTasma namo bhagavaten anuvidhema tubhyam\nyo anahato narakabhagbhirasatprasandhaih. 4. Meaning of the word:\nTat--Lord Shri Krishna; Va--Or; Idam--This present form; Bhuvanamgala--All auspiciousness for all the universe;\nTEA--For all prosperity; Dhyan--In meditation; Sm--As if; Na--To us; Darshitam--Seen; Te--Yours;\nUpanishad--Of the devotees; Tasme--To them; Namah--My respectful obeisance; Bhagwate--To the Lord; Anuvideem--I offer;\nTubhyam--To you; Yah--He who; Anahatah--Without a heart; Narakabhagbhih--By those who go to hell; Asat--By the material\nStories +"
