हे |\n\nपरया शब्द अत्यन्त सार्थक है | पराभक्ति या ईश्वर का स्वत:स्फूर्त प्रेम भगवान्‌ से घनिष्ठ सम्बन्ध का",
          "textEn": "274\nTo showcase the special form of God is not worldly, even if the devotee has physical desires remaining;\nIt does not appear due to the influence of material power, as the nonspecific fools believe.\nSuch nonspecific fools, who consider the divine forms of God to be the product of the material world, are definitely\ngoing to hell. This is the fragrance of the lotus feet of your feet.\nThe ears perceive it with the apertures of the ears, the wind of the ears.\nThe devotee's feet are held in great reverence, and they are not satisfied.\nO Lord, from the lotus-like heart, the essence of the self. 500/-. Meaning of the word:\n\nYe-those people; Tu-but; Tvadiya-yours; Charan-Ambhuj-feet; Kosh-inside; Gandham-fragrance; Jihnanti-smell;\nare; Karna-vivah-through the path of the ears; Shruti-vat-taken by the air of the Vedic sound; Bhaktya-by devotion;\nGrihit-accepted; Paraya-divine; Cha-also; Tesham-for them; Na-never; Apaishi-\nseparate; Nath-Oh Lord; Hriday-like heart; Ambur-from lotus; Swa-own; Pumsam-of one's own devotees.\nOh Lord, those who, through the air, take the fragrance of your lotus feet, which are carried by the Vedic sound,\nthrough their ears, accept your devotional service. For them,\nyou are never separated from their heart-like lotus. Meaning: For the pure devotees of God, there is nothing beyond the lotus feet of God. And\nGod knows that such devotees do not need anything more than that. The word 'Tu' specifically establishes this\nfact. God also does not want to be separated from the hearts of those pure devotees. This is the divine relationship existing between a pure devotee and God. Because God does not want to be separated from the hearts of such pure devotees, therefore it is understood that he is more dear to them than to the non-differentialists. The relationship of a pure devotee with God develops because,\nbecause the devotional service to God is performed by the devotee on the real basis of Vedic evidence.\nLike this,\npure devotees are not worldly sentimental (emotional), but they are actually realistic, because their\nworks are supported by those Vedic authorities who have accepted the facts mentioned in the Vedic texts\nby listening.\n\nThe word 'Paryaya' is extremely meaningful. 'Parabhakti' or God's spontaneous love is a close relationship with God"
