          "textEn": "283\nNitya Das. Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu says that the living being is a perpetual servant of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Shri Krishna. Therefore, every living being has a special kind of eternal servitude relationship with God. This special\nattachment is awakened by the practice of devotion to God, and in this way, the devotee becomes eternally\nattached to the form of God, just as a person who is already eternally attached is. Of God,\nsuch attachment towards such a special form is called Siddhi. God, desiring the pure devotee,\nIn the eternal form, becomes seated in the lotus of the devotee's heart, and in this way, God is not separated from the devotee,\nAs has been confirmed in the previous verse. But God does not perform his SERA in front of any accidental or unauthorized\nworshiper. This is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (7.25)-- Naamah Prakashah:\nSarvasya Yogamayasamakritah.\nIn contrast, God, through his divine illusion, keeps himself hidden from those devotees or accidental devotees\nwho are engaged in serving their sense gratification. God is never visible to those six\ndevotees who worship the deities who bear the burden of the world's affairs. The conclusion that came out is that God can never be the enforcer of the orders of a devotee, but He is always ready to fulfill the desires of that pure\nunbound devotee, who is free from all kinds of material\ndefects.\nNot pleased by the pleasures of the world,\nNot attached to the pleasures of the gods, bound by the desires of others,\nNot easily accessible to the bestowal of all beings, the self-contented one,\nNot afflicted by the various worlds, the self-contented one. 92 Meaning of the word\nN--never; Ati--extreme; Prasidati-- is pleased; Tatha--as much as; Upachit-- with adornment; Prayogahi-- worshipful; Saaj-with; Aradhitah-- worshipped; Sur-ganaih-- by the gods; Hadi-bound-kapaih-- from all kinds of material desires\nWith the material; Yat-which; Sarva-all; Bhut-living; 