य रूप; महसा- महिमा के द्वारा; एव-- निश्चय ही; निपीत--विभेदित; भेद-- अन्तरः;\nमोहाय-- मोहमयी धारणा के हेतु; बोध--आत्म-ज्ञान; धिषणाय-- बुद्धि; नमः-- नमस्कार; परस्मै ब्रह्म को; विश्व-उद्धव--",
          "textEn": "286\nMeaning of the word\n\nPumsamu--of people; Atha--therefore; Vividh-karmabhi--by various actions; Adhvar-adhyaih--Vedic rituals\nBy performing; Dane--by donation; Cha--and; Ugra--extremely harsh; Tapasya--through penance; Paricharyaya--through divine service;\nCha--also; Aradhanam--worship; Bhagwat:--of God; Tava--yours; Sat-kriya-artha:--only to please you;\nDharma:--righteousness; Arpit:--offered --In this way, offered; done--at some time; dies--is destroyed; not--never; where--\nThere +.\n\nBut Vedic rituals, donations, rigorous penance, and divine service, such virtuous deeds, which people\nby offering you desirable fruits, to worship you and to satisfy you,\nare beneficial. Such are the works of charity, they do not go in vain. Meaning: The ultimate devotion that is accomplished through nine different spiritual practices--such as listening, chanting, remembering, worshiping, bowing--these do not always appeal to people with a flashy nature.\nThey are\nmore attracted to Vedic external rituals and other expensive displays of social religious showmanship.\nare. But according to Vedic commands, the law is that all the fruits of good deeds should be offered to God.\nShould be given. In the Bhagavad Gita (9.27), God demands that whatever a person does in daily tasks,\nthe fruits of all such worship, sacrifice, and charity should be offered solely to Him. This offering of the fruits of meritorious deeds to God\nis a sign of devotion to God, which has lasting importance, while\nthe enjoyment of those fruits for oneself is only momentary. Any work done for God\nis a permanent fund, and it accumulates as invisible merit for the gradual progress towards pure devotion to God. These unnoticed virtuous deeds will one day be rewarded by God's grace in the form of complete devotion.\nThey will be rewarded. Therefore, any virtuous deed done in the name of God is praised here for those\npeople who are not pure devotees.\nShashataswarupamahasaiiva nipitab