‌--अमरता; तम्‌--उसः; अजम्‌-- अजन्मा की; प्रपद्ये -में शरण लेता हूं \\.\n\nमैं उनके चरणकमलों की शरण ग्रहण करता हूँ जिनके अवतार, गुण तथा कर्म सांसारिक\nमामलों के रहस्यमय अनुकरण हैं। जो व्यक्ति इस जीवन को छोड़ते समय अनजाने में भी उनके",
          "textEn": "287\nVirat, the creation of the universe; state--nurturing; destruction--destruction; cause--for the sake of; play--from such plays; enjoyment--for enjoyment;\nThey--to you; salutations--salutations; this--this; I--I do; to God--to God..\n\nI salute that Supreme Brahman who, through the power of his inner self, remains in the eternal, distinct\nstate. Their undifferentiated, unique form of self-realization, which cannot be differentiated,\nis recognized through the intellect. I salute those who, through their divine plays,\nenjoy the creation, sustenance, and destruction of the vast universe. Meaning: God is always distinguished from beings through His inner power, although He\nis also understood in His formless form by the self-evident intellect. Therefore, the devotees of God,\nhonorfully bow to the unique form of God. The word Raas is important here.\nThe Raas dance is performed by Lord Krishna\nwith the Gopis in Vrindavan, and the Garbhodakshayi Vishnu also remains engaged in the enjoyment of Raas with his\nexternal power, by which he creates, nurtures, and destroys the entire material world. Indirectly, Brahmaji respectfully salutes that Lord Shri Krishna,\nwho is always engaged in Raasbhog with the Gopis, whose confirmation is in the Gopal Tapani Upanishad\nby the following words-- Parardhanti so'budhyata gopavesho se purushah Pristastadavirbhuvah.\n\nThe difference between God and the living being is clearly experienced when one has sufficient intelligence to understand their inner power, which is different from that outer power, by which they make the physical creation possible. Of the incarnations, qualities, actions, and deceptions,\nThese are spoken of by those who are not afraid of death.\nHaving removed the impurities of many births, having attained Him,\nI surrender to that immaculate, unborn one, who is beyond the endurance. 15). Meaning of the word\n\nYasya--Of whom; Avatar--Avatar; Guna--Divine quality; Karma--Deeds; Vidambanaan