          "textEn": "289\nYah--He; Vai--Certainly; Aham--I also; Girishah--Shiva also; Vibhu--Almighty; Swayam--Self (in Vishnu form);\nCha--And; Sthiti--Preservation; Uddhava--Creation; Pralaya--Destruction; Hetavah--Causal; Atmamulam--Self-established; Bhitva--Having; Bhedakar--Differentiating;\nTri-pat--Three-petaled; Vavru-de--Growing; Ekah--One; Uru--Many; Prahar-de--Shakti; Tasma--That; TH:-- Namaskar.\nBhagwate--To the Lord; Bhuvan-du-ma-ye--To the world-like tree;. This tree first emerged in the form of three trunks to the physical nature-Mujh, Shiv, and the all-powerful in your form, to distinguish for goodness, nurturing, and destruction.\nAnd from these three, many branches have emerged. Therefore, O Virat, the tree of the world,\nI bow to you. Meaning: The vast universe is broadly divided into three worlds--the higher, lower, and middle realms--\nand then, from the manifestation of the supreme original form, this vast universe spreads into fourteen realms.\nThe physical nature, which appears to be the cause of the vast universe, is merely the power of the cause or God. This is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (9.10)--Saya saradhya-pena prakruti: suyate sacha-racharam--\n\"Only under the control of God does the material nature appear to be the cause of all creation, preservation, and destruction.\"\"God, for nurturing, creation, and destruction, his expansion is respectively Vishnu, Brahma, and Shiva.\nHe manifests in these three forms. Among these three main agents of control of the three qualities of nature, Vishnu\nis omnipotent. Although they are instrumental in the maintenance of physical nature, they are not controlled by the laws of nature. The other two, Brahma and Shiva, although almost as powerful as Vishnu, are\nsubject to the physical power of God. The ideology of being controlled by many gods of many departments of physical nature\nis a dirty product of the mind of a foolish panentheist. God is now and they\nare the cause of all causes.\nJust as there are many departmental heads for government affairs, similarly, there are many presidents for the management of the universe's affairs. The non-differential ignorant do not believe in the self-arrangement of the objects as they are due to lack of knowledge.\nBut in this verse, it is clearly stated that every object is concrete, it is not formless or non-differential. In the introduction, we have already explained this matter, and this is confirmed in this verse. The description of the physical world-like tree is in the Bhagavad Gita as that Asvattha tree, whose roots\nare upwards. When we look at the reflection of a tree on the bank of a reservoir, we see similar trees"
