          "textEn": "290\nIt is a real experience. In the water, the reflection of the tree appears to hang down from its upright roots. Here, the creation-like tree that has been described is merely a reflection of truth, and this\nis the true Parabrahma, Vishnu. In the internal powerful expression of the Vaikuntha worlds, the real tree exists,\nand the reflected tree in physical nature is merely a reflection of this real tree. The theory of the non-experts\nthat Brahma is void of all diversity is false, because the reflected tree described in the Bhagavad Gita cannot exist without being a reflection of the real tree. The real tree\nremains situated in the eternal existence of spiritual nature, which is full of divine diversity and God\nVishnu is also the root of that tree. The root of both real and false trees is the same God, but\nthe false tree is merely a distorted reflection of the real tree.\nHere, Brahma, on his own behalf, and Shivji,\nare offering salutations to the real tree form of God. Those who are skilled and devoted to the worship of Vikramarna,\nWho are engaged in the worship of the Lord of the Universe,\nThose who are strong in their lives,\nMay they be quickly destroyed for the sake of seeing the blink of an eye, I bow to them. 17). Meaning of the word:\nLokah - common people; Vikarm - in thoughtless action; Nirahata - engaged; Kushale - in profitable work; Pramatta: -- Careless;\nKarmani-- in action; Ayam- this; Tvat- by you; Udite- announced; Bhavat- yours; Archane- in worship; Swayam- oneself; Yah- who; Tavat- until; Asya- of this; Balavan- very powerful; Iha- this; Jivit- of life; Sangharsh- struggle;\nSadyah- immediately; Chhinatti- cut into pieces; Animishaya- by the eternal time; Namah- salutations;\nAstu- let; Tasmai- for him \\.\nCommon people remain engaged in foolish actions. They do not involve themselves in the direct declared profitable activities for their guidance by you.\nAs long as their tendency to do foolish things\nremains strong, all their plans will be shattered in the struggle of life. Therefore, I salute those who are the embodiment of eternity. Meaning: people are doing useless things. They remain completely careless towards the truly beneficial work, which\nis devotion to God, and in a technical sense, is called Archana Vidhan.\nThe teaching of Archana Vidhan has been given by God himself in Narada Pancharatra, and their wise people"
