          "textEn": "296\nMeaning of the word:\n\nSah-- He; Ayam-- God; Samasta-Jagatam-- From all the universes; Suhat-Ekah-- The only friend and philosopher; Atma--\nSupreme soul; Sattvena-By the quality of goodness; Yat-- That; Mridayate-It creates happiness; Bhagavan-God; Bhaggan-By the six opulences;\nTena-By that; Ev-Certainly; Me-To me; Dasham-The power of self-examination, The inner sense; the absence of sense--that which gives; as--\nIn the manner; I--I; I will protect; as--like before; this--this universe; I bow--I surrender;\nDear--beloved; that--He;\nThe beloved--beloved; the one--He;\nThe one--He. May God be merciful to me. They are the only friends and souls of all living beings in this world, and\nThey nurture these Tal for the ultimate happiness of living beings through their six THATs. May they be merciful to me, so that I may be filled with the power of self-examination to create as I did before, Wah,\nbecause I too am one of those surrendered beings who are dear to God.\nMeaning: Lord Purushottam, that is, Shri Krishna, is the protector of all in both the divine and material worlds.\n<silence_gap> | He is the life and friend of all, because there is eternal, natural affection\nand love between beings and God. They are everyone's only friend and well-wisher, and they are one-of-a-kind. God, through his six divine\nglories, nurtures all beings everywhere, because of which they are called God or the complete Supreme Being.\nThey are called the Supreme Lord. Brahmaji prayed to receive God's grace so that he could be able to create the universe as before. Only by God's unconditional grace, he could create Marichi and Narad\nlike material and spiritual beings. Brahma prayed to God, because\nhe is very dear to the surrendered. The surrendered soul does not know anyone other than God\nTherefore, God is very affectionate towards him.\n\nEsha Prapannavardho Ramatmashaktya\nYadyaatkarishyati Grihitagunavatarah.\nIn that, even if one is born, with a mind free