          "textEn": "297\nOr are accomplished through Lakshmi. My only request to them is that in the creation of the physical world,\nthey should engage me in their service, and my only prayer is that I should not be physically affected by my actions,\nbecause in this way, I will be able to abandon the false prestige of being destroyed. Meaning: For the sake of creation, sustenance, and destruction, nature has taken three incarnations--Brahma, Vishnu,\nand Mahe Dharai. But in the form of Vishnu, in his inner power, the incarnation of God is the supreme power for all tasks. Brahma, who is only helpful in the qualities of creation, in the form of God's tools, his\ndesire to remain on his real position, expressed. Not to be proud of false prestige for being stubborn.\nTo be. This is the way to become dear to God and to receive His blessings.\nFoolish people want to take the credit for the entire creations made by themselves, but wise people know very well that without God's\nwill, not even a leaf can move. In this way, the credit for the wonderful creations should go to God.\nIt should be. Only through spiritual consciousness can a person free himself from the impurities of material contact,\nand attain the boon granted by God.\n\nNabhihadadiha satoambhasi yasya pumso\nVijnanashaktirahamasamanantashaktih.\nRoopam vicitramidasyam vivrunvanto me\nMa ririshisht nigamasya giranam visargah. 24). Meaning of the word\n\nNabhi-hadat--from the navel-shaped lake; Iha--in this kalpa; Satah--lying down; Ambhasi--in the water; Yasya-whose; Punasah--of the gods; Vijnan-completely of the universe; Shakti:--power; Aham-I; Asam-had been produced; Ananta-infinite; Iha:--of this; Ih-\nOf the powerful; Roopam-form; Vichitram-strange; Idam-this; Asya-his; Vivrunvat-while expressing; Me-\nTo me; ma--no; ri-rishis-lost; nigam-s-of-the-vedas; gi-gra-of-the-sounds; visarga--vibration..\n\nThe powers of God are countless. When they lie in the water of destruction, then from that navel-like lak