          "textEn": "298\nTends towards numerous physical activities, and if he is not able to protect himself from the impact of physical contact,\nhe may be ruined by spiritual power. In the physical creation, Brahma had to create all kinds of living beings, with which all their bodies would be in accordance with their physical\nconditions. Brahma wants that God should protect him, because his contact\nwas to be with many contaminated beings. A common Brahmin, in the company of many fallen souls,\ncan fall from his divine power. Brahma, as the supreme Brahmin, is afraid of such a downfall,\nTherefore, for protection, they pray to God. In the spiritual progress of life, this is a warning for everyone. Until someone is sufficiently protected by God, they can fall from their spiritual position. Therefore, for their safety and to continue their work,\nfor blessings, a person must constantly pray to God.\nShri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu also entrusted his\nreligious preaching work to his devotees and gave them assurance of protection from the impact of material contact. In the Vedas, the path of spiritual life has been described as sharp as the edge of a razor.\nIt has been said. Even a little carelessness can immediately cause hesitation and bloodshed, but the person who is\ncompletely surrendered and always prays to God for protection in completing the task entrusted to him,\ndoes not have any fear of falling into material impurity.\nOh, the one with the lotus-like face, the compassionate one, the one with the expanded form of the divine.\nWith a loving smile, he shakes the lotus-like eyes.\nArising for the victory over the universe, and not saddened.\nThe ancient one, who, with a smile, embraces the lotus-like face. 25. Meaning of the word\nSah--He (God); Asau--That; Adabhra--Infinite; Karunah--Kind; Bhagavan--God; Vivridh--Excessive; Prem--Love;\nSmiten--By smile; Nayan-Amburuham--To the lotus-like ones; Vijrumbh-Opening; Utthaya--For upliftment; Vishch-Vijayaya--Great\n