          "textEn": "307\nHow difficult the work was. But by the grace of God, Brahma was able to accomplish this more important task with such efficiency\nthat every person is amazed to see the miracle of the creator. Shri Bhagavan said:\nO, the one who is in the womb of the Vedas, who is asleep, who is the beginning of creation, who is the endeavor.\nThat which is caused by Me, that which is before me, that which you ask for. 29. Meaning of the word:\n\nShri-Bhagavan said—Bhagwan said; Ma--mother; Veda-garbh--one who reaches the depths of Vedic knowledge; Gaah—to sing; Tandrima—despair;\nHo—for creation; Udyamam—perseverance; Aavah—to put your hand; Tat—that (which you want); Maya-by me; Aadaptam—completed; Hi—certainly; Agre—before; Yat—that; Mam—from me; Prarthithate—you are asking; Bhavan—by you;\nThen the Supreme Personality of Godhead said, \"O Brahma, O one born from the Vedas, do not be disheartened nor be worried in creating the universe. What you are asking for, I have already given you.\nMeaning: Any man authorized by God or his authentic representative has already received the blessing.\nAnd similarly, the task entrusted to him as well. Undoubtedly, that person who has been entrusted with such\nresponsibility should always be aware of his inability and should expect God's grace for the successful completion of his duty. He should not be proud\nbecause he has been assigned any administrative work. He is fortunate, who has been given such a task\nand if he always remains steadfast in this feeling that I am subject to God's will, then\nhis success in the accomplishment of his work is certain. Arjun was assigned the task of fighting in the battlefield of Kurukshetra,\nand even before assigning him this task, God had already arranged his victory. But Arjun always remained conscious of the subordination of God, and in this responsibility,\nHe accepted them as his supreme guide.\nAny person who is proud of completing any responsible task,\nbut does not give credit to God, is certainly\nfalsely proud and cannot complete any task properly. Brahma and his footprints\nThe individuals of the disciple tradition who follow always succeed in attaining the divine love and devotion of God.\nThey are successful."
