          "textEn": "32\n\nThere is a very close relationship between the eyes and the sun, because without sunlight, the eyes cannot see.\nBut other parts of the body, because they are connected to the sun as a source of heat, take more advantage of the sun than the eyes. Without being endowed with affection towards the sun, the eyes cannot bear the sun's rays.\nOr, in other words, such eyes do not have the ability to understand the utility of the sun's rays. Similarly, an experiential philosopher, despite having theoretical knowledge of Brahman,\nis unable to utilize the grace of the Supreme Brahman because they lack affection. Therefore, many\nnihilistic philosophers, despite having theoretical knowledge of Brahman, remain subjugated to Maya forever,\nand they do not generate affection towards the external, nor is there any\npossibility of affection arising in them, because their method is flawed.\nA devotee of Suryadev, even being blind, can see Suryadev in his true form from this world, but one who is not a devotee of Surya cannot even bear the brightness of the sun. Similarly, through devotion, even if a person is not at the level of a wise person,\ndue to the development of pure love, one can have a vision of God within oneself. Man should try to develop devotion to God in all\nsituations, and by this, all complex problems\nwill be solved.\nSarvavedamayenedamatmanatmanayonina. People: Those who are as old as they are, are pleasing to me. 43. Meaning of the word\n\nSarva--All; Veda-mayena--under the complete knowledge of Vedas; Idam--This; Atmana--by the body; Atma--you; Atmayonina--by self-birth;\nDirectly born from God; Praja:--living beings; Srij--create; Yatha-Purvam--as before; Ya:--that; Cha--also; Mayi--in me;\nAnushera-te--are situated.\n.\n\nBy following my orders, you, like before, with your complete Vedic knowledge and\nthrough the cause-and-effect form, by obtaining from me, through your body, can create beings. Maitreya Ubacha\nTasma evam SEY Prad