          "textEn": "37\nHaving seen that, I contemplated that Pushkara, which is situated above.\nBy this, I thought that I had attained the worlds. 7>. Meaning of the word:\nTatvilokya--seeing that; Vyapti--extremely vast; Pushkaram--lotus; Yat--which; Adhisthitam-- established; Aneen--by this;\nFrom this; Lokan--all the worlds; Prak--before; Linaan--engaged in the first deluge; Kalpita Asmi--I will create; Iti--in this way;\nAchintayat--He thought..\nAfter that, he saw that the lotus on which he was seated was spread throughout the universe.\nAnd he thought about how all those worlds could be created, which were before this\nThey were absorbed in that lotus. Meaning: The seeds of all the universes were contained in that lotus on which Brahma was seated. God had already created all the worlds, and all beings had also taken birth in Brahma.\nThe physical world and all living beings were already produced by God in the form of seeds, and\nBrahma is to scatter these seeds throughout the universe. Therefore, the original creation is called Srishti, and later\nwhat was created by Brahma is called Visarga. The word then appeared, the divine action was uttered.\nThen it was seen, the threefold, the beautiful, the sevenfold. 8 ”. Meaning of the word.\nPada-kosham--in the lotus chakra; Tada--then; Aavishya--entering; Bhagavat--by God; Karma--in the activity;\nChoditah--encouraged; Ekam-ekah; Vyabhangshit-divided; Urudha-great segment; Tridha-three\nDivisions; Bhavyam-capable of creating further; Dvi-septadha-fourteen divisions. In this way, Brahmaji, engaged in the service of the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, entered the lotus-like vessel, and\nbecause it was spread throughout the entire universe, therefore he divided it into three divisions of the universe, and\nafter that, divided it into fourteen divisions.\nThe difference in the institution of this world is included.\nThe consequence of the cause of religion is the supreme. 9>. Shabdharam"
