          "textEn": "324\n\nThe power of ignorance of God is what makes the bound souls deluded. The physical nature is called ignorance,\nbut for the devotees engaged in devotion to God, this power becomes knowledge, that is, pure wisdom. This is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita. The power of God transforms from Mahamaya into Yogamaya,\nand appears before the devotee in its true form. Therefore, the material nature seems to act in three stages-- as the creation principle of the material world, as ignorance, and as knowledge. As it was uplifted in the previous verse, in the fourth creation, the power of knowledge also arises. Bound beings\nare not fundamentally foolish, but due to the influence of the ignorance of nature's work, they are made foolish, due to which they\nare unable to use knowledge in the right direction.\nThe bound soul forgets its relationship with God due to the influence of darkness, and it becomes overwhelmed by attachment,\nhatred, pride, ignorance, and false identification, which are the five types of attachments that create material bondage. The six types of Prakrita are Sarga, Vikruta, and others, listen to me.\nThe play of the radiant Lord is like the ocean of milk, which is difficult to cross. 18. Meaning of the word\n\nSixth-sixth; ima- all these; prakrutah- of the material energy; sargah- creation; vaikrutah- secondary creations by Brahma; api- also;\nme- I; munmse- listen; shrinu- hear; rajah- emanation; bhagavatam- of the supreme; leela- play;\niyam- this; hari- Lord; medhas- of the one with sharp intellect; me- of the one with;\nmeaning of the word:\n\nSixth-sixth; ima- all these; prakrutah- of the material energy; sargah- creation; vaikrutah- secondary creations by Brahma; api- also;\nmeaning of the word:\n\nSixth-sixth; ima- all these; prakrutah- of the material energy; sargah- creation; vaikrutah- secondary creations by Brahma; api- also;\nmeaning of the word. Now listen to me about those\ncreations made by Brahmaji, who are incarnat