          "textEn": "350\nDash-north-more:--ten times more thick; yatra-which; pravishta-entered; para-like-like atoms;\n'Lakshyate-(apparent weight of the universe) seems; antah-remained; cha-and; anye-in others; kotisha-many;\ncompounded; hi-because; and-of; egg-mass: -a huge combination of universes..\n\nThe layers of elements that hold the universes are ten times thicker than the previous one.\nAnd all the universes, when assembled together, appear like a huge combination of atoms. Meaning: The coverings of the universes (koshas) are also made of the elements of earth, water, fire, air, and sky.\nAnd compared to the previous covering, the SHAT is thicker. The first\ncovering of the universe is earth, and it is ten times thicker than the universe. If the universe is 4 billion miles in size, then\nthe size of the Earth's crust is four times ten, that is, 40 billion miles. The water cover is ten times thicker than the Earth's\ncover. And the covering of fire is ten times thicker than the covering of water.\nThe covering of air\nis ten times the covering of fire, and the covering of the sky is ten times that of fire. This\nUniverse appears like an atom within the coverings of matter, and the number of universes\nis not even known to those who can estimate the coverings of universes.\nTadahuraksharam Barham Sarvakaranakaranam.\nVishnurdham Parat Sakshatpurushasya Mahatmanah. 42). Meaning of the word\n\nTat-That; Aahu-It is said; Akshar-Undivided; Brahma-Supreme; Sarva-Causal-All causes; Karanam-Supreme cause;\nVishnu's abode-Vishnu's spiritual abode; Param-Supreme; Sakshat-Indeed; Purushasya-Of the incarnation of Purusha; Mahatmanah-Of the great soul.Therefore, Lord Krishna is called the cause of all causes. Thus, the spiritual abode of Vishnu\nis undoubtedly eternal, and it is also the abode of the origin of all manifestations, Mahavishnu.\nMeaning: Mahavishnu, who sleeps in Yoganidra in Karanarav, and through his breath,\nproduces countless universes, appears for a