          "textEn": "352\nChapter twelve\nThe creation of Kumaras and others\nMaitreya says,\nThus it is described: the knower of time, the supreme soul.\nThe glory is in the womb of the Vedas, as it is understood. 9>. Meaning of the word.\n\nMaitreya said-- Shri Maitreya said; Iti-- thus; Te- from you; Vivrita- described; Am: - Vidur; Kaal-\nAkhya- Nitya Kaal named; Paramatmanah- of the Supreme Soul; Mahima- Glory; Veda- Garbha- the abode of Vedas, Brahma; Ath- after this; Yatha- as this is; Astra-khet- produced; Nibodha- try to understand; Me- from me \\\n\nShri Maitreya said: Oh learned Vidur, until now I have explained to you the glory of the form of the complete Supreme Lord. Now you can hear from me about the creation of Brahma, the repository of all Vedic knowledge.\nThe darkness of ignorance, the darkness of delusion, and the darkness of the darkness, and the darkness of the darkness.\nGreat delusion and delusion, and the darkness of the darkness, and the darkness of the darkness. 2>. Meaning of the word\n\nSasarj--extended; Agre--first; Anand--bliss; Ath--then; Tamisram--the feeling of death; Ath--then; Tamisram--anger on despair; Adi--\nKrit--all these; Maha-Moham--ownership of enjoyable things; Cha--also; Moham--delusion; Cha--also; Tamah--darkness in self-knowledge\nDarkness; Cha--also; Ignorance--ignorance; Vrittayah--passions, tendencies..\n\nBrahma first created the illusion of self-deception, the feeling of death, anger after despair, the feeling of false ownership,\nand the illusionary physical perception or the forgetting of one's true form, like ignorance-filled\nphenomena.\n\nMeaning: Before the actual creation of living beings in various types of wombs, Brahma created those\nsituations under which living beings have to live in this physical world. Until a being forgets its true\nform, it is impossible for it to live in the physical states of life.\nTherefore, the first state of physical life is the forgetting of one's true nature. Upon forgetting one's true form, it is certain that man is terrified of death, although the pure soul is immortal and without birth. This false identification with physical nature is the cause of the false ownership of those objects that\nare provided by the system of superior control. Provided all the material resources to the living being"
