ा दुरुपयोग करने को अच्छा मानकर अविद्या में",
          "textEn": "353\nThey go so that he can live peacefully and fulfill the duties of self-realization in a bound life. But due to false identification, the bound soul becomes bound in the feeling of false ownership of God's property.\nIt becomes bound. From this verse, it is clear that Brahma himself is the creation of God, and the five types of ignorance of the material world, which bind the living beings, are the creations of Brahma. It is utterly\nridiculous to think that a living being is equal to the Supreme Being, while it can understand that the bound soul is under the control of Brahma's\nmagical wand. Patanjali also accepts that ignorance is of five types, which\nhas been mentioned here.\nThe seer, the sinful, the creation, and the self,\nBhagavad-dhāyanaputena, from the mind, then created. 3). Meaning of the word:\n\nHrutta--by seeing; Papyasim--full of sin; Srishti--to the creation; Na--not; Atmanam--self; Bahu--extremely; Amanyat--\nExperienced; Bhagavat--of God; Dhyan--meditation; Pooten--by him; Pure; Manasa--from the mind; Anyam--other; Tat--thereafter;\nTatpashchat..\n\nConsidering such a delusional creation as a sinful act, Brahmaji did not experience much joy in his work.\nTherefore, he purified himself through the meditation of God. Then,\nHe started the second phase of creation.\n\nMeaning: Although Brahmaji created various types of ignorances, he was not satisfied by completing such unappreciated\nwork. They had to do this work because most of the spiritual people\nwanted this.\nLord Krishna's statement in the Bhagavad Gita (15.15) is that He is present in everyone's heart\nand helps everyone in remembering or forgetting. Here, this question can be asked\nthat why does the all-compassionate God help one in remembering and forgets the other?\nIn reality, His grace is not manifested as partiality towards one and enmity towards the other. As a part of God, the living being is partially independent, because in it all the qualities of God are partially found. Anyone who has even a little freedom, due to ignorance, can misuse it. Now, the soul, considering misusing its freedom as good, in ignorance"
