          "textEn": "354\nIt seems to go away, so the all-compassionate God first tries to save him from the noose, but when\nthe soul becomes despondent as it falls towards hell, then God helps it to forget its real state. God helps the falling creature to fall to the lowest point, so that he can see whether he is happy or not due to the misuse of his freedom. In this world, almost all bound souls who are decaying are misusing their freedom, therefore, on them,\nfive types of ignorance are imposed. Brahmaji, as an obedient servant of God,\nproduces ignorances as necessities, but while doing so, he is not pleased,\nbecause it is natural that a devotee of God does not want to see anyone fall from their true position.\nHe wants. Those who do not care about the path of interview, God lets them live their evil tendencies to the fullest extent, and Brahma definitely becomes helpful in that.\nSanaka, Sanandam, Sanatanam, and Atmabho. Sanatkumaram cha muninishkriyanuvadhetasah. 4>. Meaning of the word:\n\nSanakam- Sanak; Cha-- also; Sanandam- Sanand; Cha-- also; Sanatanam- Sanatan; Ath-- After that; Atmabho- Swayambhu Brahma;\nSanat-Kumaram- Sanatkumara; Cha-- also; Munin- Muniganah; Nishkarion- freed from all desires; Urdhva-retas- those whose\nsemen flows upwards EL\n\nFirst of all, Brahma created four great sages whose names are Sanak, Sanand, Sanatan\nand Sanatkumar. They were all unwilling to accept materialistic activities,\nbecause due to their upwardness, they were extremely high. Meaning: Although Brahma, in the form of the need of those beings, as a principle of ignorance, created the universe,\nIn whose destiny, by the will of God, ignorance was evil, but they were not satisfied by doing such unappreciated work. Therefore, they created four principles of knowledge. These are Sankhya, Yoga, Vairagya and Tapa.\nSankhya is an experiential philosophy for the analytical study of physical states, to liberate the pure soul from the bondage of existence, to rise to the 