          "textEn": "449\nChapter Fifteen\nDescription of the kingdom of God\nMaitreya Ubacha\nPrajapatyam tu tattejah paratejahanam ditihi. Thousands of rain showers fall from the sun's heat. 9>. Meaning of the word:\n\nMaitreya said: The great sage Maitreya said; Prajapatim- of the great Prajapati; Tu- but; Tat- radiant; Para-\nAST: - others' prowess; Hanam- causing pain; Diti- Diti (Kashyapa's wife) did; Dadhar- held; Varshani- until; Shatam- one hundred; Shankamana- disturbing; Sur-arddhnat- causing agitation to the gods.\n\nShri Maitreya said: O Vidura, Diti, the wife of Maharishi Kashyapa, understood that in her womb\na son would be born, who would cause disturbance to the gods. Therefore, she continued to hold the radiant semen of Kashyap Muni\nfor a hundred years continuously, because it was causing pain to others. Meaning: Maharishi Shri Maitreya was discussing with Vidura the functions of all the gods, including Brahma.\nWhen Diti heard from her husband's mouth that the son she had conceived in her womb would\nbecome a cause of disturbance for the gods, she was not very pleased. Humans are of two types--\ndevotees and non-devotees. Non-devotees are called demons, and devotees are called gods. No wise\nman or devotee can tolerate the suffering given to devotees by an ungodly person. Therefore, the daughter of Diti\nwas hesitant to give birth. That is why she waited for a hundred years, so that at least for that period\nshe could save the gods from chaos.\nLoke tenahatalekle lokapala hataojasah.\nNyavedayanvischasrije dhvantavatikaram disham. 2>. Shabdartham.\n\n'Loke--in this universe; Ten--by the power of the conception of Diti; Aahat-- without being wounded; Aloke--light; Lokapala--guardian of the worlds;\nThe gods of different worlds; Hat-Ojasah-- whose radiance had faded; Nyavayadan-- inquired; Vishch-Srije-- from Brahma; Dhwantha-\nVyatikaram-- the expanse of darkness; Disham-- in all directions.\n.\n\nDue to Diti conceiving, the light of the sun and moon dimmed in all the worlds, and\nThe gods of various worlds, disturbed by that power, asked Brahma of the universe,\n“How is this expansion of darkness in all directions?”''"
