          "textEn": "45]\nYou are beyond all beings, beyond all beings, the knower of their essence. 4>. Meaning of the word:\n\nDeva-Deva--O Lord of the Gods; Jagat-dhatah--The one who holds the universe; Lokanath-Shikhamane--The crest jewel of other worlds; Paresham--Of the spiritual world; Aparesham--Of the material world; Tvam--You; Bhutanam--Of all living beings; Asi--Be; Bhav-vit--Knowing the sentiment, L\n\nO Lord of the Gods, O one who holds the universe, O knower of the sentiments of all the living beings in both the spiritual and material worlds. Meaning: Because Brahma is almost equal to God, that is why he is addressed here as Devdev,\nand because he is a minor TE of this universe, therefore he is called the one who holds the universe.\nIt is said. They are the head of all the gods, therefore they are called the crown jewel of the gods. To understand what is happening in both spiritual and material worlds is not difficult for them.\nIt is not difficult.\nThey know the heart of every person and every emotion. Therefore, they were requested to explain this\nevent, that why Diti's womb became the cause of such worry for the entire universe? Salutations to the one who is full of scientific valor. Salutations to the one who is the cause of the difference in qualities, to the unmanifest. 5>. Meaning of the word:\n\nNamah - Respectful salutation; Vijnan-Viryaay-- These are the primary sources of strength and scientific knowledge; Mayaya-- Through external energy; Idam--\nThis body of Brahma; Upayuhesh-- Having obtained; Grhit-- Accepting; Gunabhedaya-- Divided into qualities; Namah Te-- To you\nWhile saluting; Avyakta-- Unmanifest; Yonaye- Source L\n\nThese are the primary sources of strength and scientific knowledge, salutations to you. You have accepted the Rajoguna separate from God. You are generated from an unmanifest source by the power of the outer self. Namaste. Meaning: The Vedas are the knowledge of the beginning of all departments of knowledge, and this knowledge of the Vedas\nwas first established by God in the heart of Brahma.\nTherefore, Brahma, all the knowledge-filled with science,\nis lost from the beginning. They have originated directly from the divine body of that Garbhodakashayi Vishnu, who is this"
