          "textEn": "452\nNo creature in the physical universe can ever see, therefore they always remain unmanifest. Here, Brahma\nis said to be born from the unmanifest. They are incarnations of Rajoguna in that physical nature, which is the distinct external energy of God. This self-contemplation, by the power of the other, contemplates the self.\nIn the self, the universe is contained; the supreme is eternally complete. 6>. Meaning of the word:\n\nThese are the ones; you are the one; without being distracted; with devotion; they meditate; self-realization;\nThat which creates all beings; within oneself; connected; all worlds; supreme; truth;\nEffect; non-effect; the cause; the self; the origin.\n\nO Lord, all these worlds exist within you, and all beings are born from you. Therefore,\nyou are the cause of this universe, and whoever meditates on you with exclusive devotion,\nobtains devotion.\nOf those who are ripe in yoga, of those who are united in self-control.\nOf those who have attained your grace, there is no doubt of their downfall. 7>. Shabdartham\n\nTesham--Of them; Su-pakkam-yoganam--Those who are mature yogis; Jit--Conquered; Shwas--Breath; Indriya--Senses; Atmanam--Mind;\nLabdha- obtained; Yusht- Yours; Prasadanam-- Grace; Na- Not; Kutashchit- Nowhere; Parajayah- Defeat..\n\nThose who, by mastering the process of purification, control their mind and senses, and in this way,\nthose who become experienced and mature yogis, they do not face defeat in this world. This is because,\nin yoga, due to such accomplishment, they have attained your grace. Note: the purpose of the yogic practices is explained here. It is said that\na seasoned yogi, by controlling the breath process, gains complete control over the senses and the mind. Therefore, controlling the process of governance is not the ultimate goal of yoga. The real purpose of yoga practices is to control the mind and senses.\nAnyone who has gained such control should be considered an experienced adult yogi. Here it is indicated that the yogi who has control over the mind and senses\nremains blessed with the real boon of God, and he has no fear."
