          "textEn": "454. You, who are the cause of all beings, are the earth, and you are the one who is not born.\nWithout the eye of ignorance, you are not seen. 9>. Meaning of the word:\nSaha--He; Tvam--You; Vidhatasva--Make prosperous; Sham--Good fortune; Bhuman--Oh God; Tamasa--Through darkness; Luptah--\nAbsent; Karmanam- of regular tasks; Adashabhrah--Generous, without discrimination; Dayaya--By mercy; Drishtaya- by your sight;\nApannaan--We are surrendered; Arhasi- We are capable; Ikshitum- To see;\nThe gods praised Brahma: Please have a favorable gaze upon us, because we have attained a huge state\n; All our work has stopped because of darkness, oh!\nMeaning: Due to complete darkness throughout the universe, the regular functions and businesses of various realms stopped. Sometimes, in the northern and southern poles of this world, there is no division between day and night. In this way, when sunlight does not reach the various realms of this universe, there is no difference between day and night.\nThere is no difference. Esha Deva Ditergbham Ojah Kashyapamarpitam.\nThe all-pervading fire is increased by all that is pervaded. Gon\nMeaning of the word\nEshah- this; Deva- O Lord; Ditheh- of Diti; Garbha- womb; Ojah- virility; Kashyapam- of Kashyap; Arpitam- offered; Gaya; Dishah- directions; Timirayan- creating darkness; Sarvah- all; Vardhate- increases; Agnih- fire; Iva- like\nSadash; Edhasi- Eedhan..\nJust as fuel enhances fire, similarly, in the womb of Diti, from the semen of Kashyap,\nthe embryo that was produced has created complete darkness in the entire universe. Meaning: The darkness spread throughout the universe is said to have been created here by that embryo, which\nwas established in the womb of Diti from the semen of Kashyap. Maitreya said,\nSaying this, the mighty-armed one, the Lord, became visible.\nThen, with a loud voice, he embraced his own self. 11. Lexicon"
