          "textEn": "455\nMaitreya: Uvach--Maitreya said; Sah-Sahah--He; Prahasya--Laughing; Maha-Baho--Oh, with mighty arms (Vidura); Bhagavan--God;\nThe lord of all opulences; Shabd-Gohar--That which is understood by sound; Pratyach-Given; Atma-Bhu-Brahma;\nDevanu--To the gods; Prin-Given; Prasann-Given; Ruchiraya-Sweet; Gira-By words..\n\nSrimatraye said: Thus, Brahma, who is understood by divine sound,\nbeing pleased with the praises of the gods, tried to satisfy them.\n\nMeaning: Brahma understood Diti's misdeeds, therefore he laughed at the whole situation. They there\nresponded to the present gods in such words that they could understand. Brahmavaach\nManasa me suta yushmatpoorvajah sanakadayah.\nCheruvihayasaha lokalokeshu vigatasprhaha. 12>. Meaning of the word:\n\nBrahma said— Brahma said; Manasah— born from the mind; Me— mine; Sutah— son; Yushmat— compared to you; Purvajah— born earlier;\nSanak-Adayah— by Sanak etc.; Cheruh— a journey; Vihayasa— by air; Vihayas – in the sky; Lokan—\nUp to the physical and spiritual worlds; Lokesu— among the people; Vigata-sprihah— without any desire..\n\nBrahmaji said: The four sons born from my mind, Sanak, Sanatan, Sanandan, and Sanatkumar, are your\nancestors. Sometimes they travel without any special desire, through the physical and spiritual skies.\nThey travel. Meaning: when we talk about desire, our intention is linked to bodily sensual gratification. Sanak, Sanatan, Sanandan, and Sanatkumar, such saintly men have no material desires, but they sometimes\nsometimes travel throughout the entire universe to propagate devotion willingly. Then once again, the self of the Supreme Vaikuntha.\nYayurvakunthanilayam sarvalokanam sakritham. 13). Meaning of the word:\n\nThey-they; once--once; Bhagavatah--of the Lord; Vaikunthasya--of Lord Vishnu; Amal-Atmanah--all the material impurities;\nThey were freed; Yayuhu--entered; Vaikuntha-Nilayam--the abode called Vaikuntha; Sarva-Loka--by all the inhabitants of the material worlds;