          "textEn": "464\ncan, even then, they await to be kissed by God, so that their face and\nlook more beautiful. When Lakshmiji worships God with Tulsi leaves in her garden, then in the divine\nponds with pure water, her beautiful face is visible. Those who are attached to worldly pleasures, listen to this translation.\nThose who are engrossed in other worldly matters, are deluded by false stories.\nThose who have heard of the destruction of the kings, are struck by the darkness of their sorrows. 223. Meaning of the word\n\nYat- Vaikuntha; Na- never; Brajanti- arrive; Agh- destroyer of sins; Rachana- of creation;\nAnuvadat- than statement; Shunvanti- listen; Ye- those; Anya- others; Vishayah- subjects; Ku- bad words; Mati-\nGhnih- destroying intellect; Yah- who; Tu- but; SAT: - is heard; Hat- unfortunate; Nrithiha- by humans;\nAatt- seized; Saraah- life value; Tan- these persons; Kshipanti- are thrown; Asharaneshu- from all shelter\nWithout; in the darkest part of the world; halt--Oh!.\n\nIt is extremely regrettable that unfortunate people do not discuss the Vaikuntha realms, but rather\nengage in such topics that are not worth listening to and confuse the human intellect.\nThey do. Those who abandon the contexts of Vaikuntha, and engage in worldly matters,\nare thrown into the deepest darkness of ignorance. Meaning: The most unfortunate are the nihilists, who do not understand the pictorial diversity of the spiritual world. They are afraid to talk about the beauty of Vaikuntha Lokas, because they think that such\nvariety will surely be material. Such nihilists think that the spiritual world is completely void.\nOr in other words, there is no picture-variety there.\nThis mentality is here called 'Kooktha Matighniha'.\nThat is, '* 'fascinated intellect by inappropriate words' is said. Here, the unparalleled state of Shunyavada and the spiritual world\nis being condemned, because from these, man's intellect becomes fascinated. How can the non-absolutist and nihilist think about this world, which is full of variety, and then say that there is no variety in the spiritual world? It is said that this\nphysical world is a distorted reflection of the spiritual world, therefore, until there is diversity in the spiritual world,\nhow can there be momentary diversity in this physical world? This"
