          "textEn": "466\nHave obtained a better body than humans, yet all the gods, including Brahma, want to attain human life,\nbecause it is especially for that being who can attain divine knowledge and religious\nachievements. It is not possible to return to the divine abode in one lifetime, but at least in human\nlife, understanding the life goal, one should start Krishna consciousness. It is said that\nhuman life is a great blessing, because to cross the ocean of ignorance, this is the most suitable boat. A spiritual guru is considered the most capable captain (navigator) of that boat, and the information received from the scriptures\nis a favorable wind to float on the ocean of ignorance. The person who does not take advantage of all these facilities in this life commits suicide. Therefore, the person who, after coming into human life,\ndoes not start Krishna consciousness, he, being controlled by Maya, loses his life. Brahmaji thus\nexpresses sorrow over the state of mankind.\nThose who are always engaged in the pursuit of the best of milk-producing animals,\nare not desirable by Yama, nor are they pleasing.\nBhuturmithah Suyashasah Kathananuraga-\nVaikalyabashyakalaya Pulakikritaangah. 25. Meaning of the word:\nYat- Vaikuntha; Cha- Tatha; Vrajanti- go; Animisham- of the gods; Rishabh- head; Anuvruttya- following the footprints;\nAnuvartanam- following; Dur- far; Yamah- Yama; Hi- certainly; Upari- above; Nah- to us; Spruhadya- desirable;\nShilah- virtue; Bhartuh- of the Lord; Fren- for each other; Suyashasah- fame; Kathana- narration; Vichar- deliberation; Vaaratha- conversation;\nDwara- through; Anurag- attachment; Vaikalya- emotion, joy; Bashpakalaya- tear; TG: -\nBody.In a state of bliss, those individuals whose physical characteristics change and who, upon hearing the glory of God,\nstart taking deep breaths and become overwhelmed, they\ngo to the abode of God, even if they do not care even a little about meditation and other rituals.\nThe abode of God 