          "textEn": "483\nThat which is attained, that which is resisted, that which is related to the self,\nThat which is seen by the eyes, that which is related to the self, that which is the fortune of self-absorption.\nOf the swan and the bumblebee, the wind of Shiva, the playful,\nThe moon, the sun, the lotus, the water of the sky. 38. Meaning of the word:\n\nTam- them; Tu- but; Aagatam- having come; Pratihata- taken away; Opikam- equipment; Swa- of one's own; Pum- of a woman; Te- by them; Maha- great; Muni- sage; Achakshat- seen; Aksha- subject; Swa- Samadhi-\nBhagyam- fortune; Bhavam- emotion; Samadhi- by which one attains union with the divine; Vibhagam- separation; Vyajanayo: -whisk; Swa- of one's own; Pum- of a woman; Tam- of a woman; Kesar- saffron; Shikar- deer;\nAmbum- of water; Vrinda- lotus; Shashi- moon; Kesar- pearls; Shikar- deer;\nAmbum- of water; Vrinda- lotus; Shashi- moon; Kesar- saffron; Shikar- deer;\nAmbum-.\n\nSanak and other sages saw that Lord Vishnu, who in his emotional meditation, was previously visible only within their hearts,\nNow he is appearing in a tangible form before their eyes.\nWhen they came forward with their companions, including umbrellas and brooms, with all their equipment, then the hairs of the broom were slowly moving, as if there were two white swans, and with the favorable wind, the pearl garlands hanging from the umbrella\nwere also moving, as if drops of nectar were dripping from a full moon, or as if the snow was melting from a gust of wind. Meaning: In this verse, the word 'achakshatakshavishayam' has come. God does not appear to the ordinary people,\nBut now he was becoming visible to the eyes of TUR. Another important word is Samadhi Bhagam. Those\nmeditators who are very fortunate, they can see the form of Lord Vishnu within their hearts through the method of yoga. But seeing them in person is a different matter. This is only possible for pure devotees.\nIt is possible. Therefore, when Kumaras saw that God was coming with his companions, who were carrying umbrellas and\nwhisks, they were astonished that they were directly seeing God.\nBrahma-\nIt is said in the Samhita that the devotees who are always in love with God, within their limits, always see Lord\nShyamasundar. But when they mature, then the same God appears directly before them. Ordinary people do not see God, but when someone can understand the importance of God's holy name,\nand by starting with the tongue through chanting and the taste of Prasad, and by engaging oneself in devotion to God,\nGod himself appears in it gradually. In this way, the devotee constantly sees God in his heart, and in a more mature state, he directly sees that same God"
