          "textEn": "49]\nIt is a very deplorable thing that many illegal so-called yogis come to Western countries and people\ntake undesirable advantage of people's inclination towards yoga practice. Such illegal yogis publicly\neven dare to declare that even while being addicted to alcohol and wine,\none can practice meditation.\n\nFive thousand years ago, Lord Krishna praised yoga practice for Arjuna, but Arjuna\nclearly expressed his inability to follow the strict rules of the yoga method. A person should be very practical in every field of work, and he should not waste his precious time in the name of yoga, in the practice of useless\nyoga asanas. The real yoga is to find the four-armed Supreme Being within your heart and to constantly see Him in meditation. Such continuous\nmeditation is called Samadhi, and the goal of this meditation is the four-armed Narayan with a decorated body.\nAs described in this chapter of Shrimad Bhagwat.\n\nGod is omnipresent, and His authority over every object applies. God, in whatever form He is present everywhere, is called the Supreme Soul. The meaning of 'Atma' is individual.\nThe meaning of 'Atma' and 'Parmatma' is individual Supreme Soul. The soul and the supreme soul are both individual beings. The soul\nand the supreme soul, this is the only difference, that the soul remains present only in a particular body, while"
