          "textEn": "492\nGod is present everywhere. In this context, the sun's wr is very good. Any individual\nlives in a certain place, but the sun, even though it is an individual entity, remains above the head of every person. It is explained in the Bhagavad Gita. Therefore, although all beings,\nincluding God, have similar qualities, the Supreme Being is different from the individual soul due to the power of His expansion-\nfilled power. God or the Supreme Soul can expand in millions of forms,\nbut the individual soul cannot do so. By being situated in everyone's heart, the Supreme Being can observe everyone's actions--whether\nthey are past, present, or future. In the Upanishads, the Supreme Being is described as being present with the individual soul as a friend and witness. As a friend, God is eager to attain his friend, the individual soul, and to take him back to the abode of God.\nAs a witness, they are the givers of all boons, and they\ngive the fruit of their deeds to each individual soul. God provides all those facilities to every individual soul,\nwhich he wants to enjoy in this material world. Suffering is the result of the desire of the living being to show dominance over the material world. But God, to his friend, the individual soul, who is also his son, renounces all other tasks and commands him to go to his\nshelter for a life of eternal bliss and knowledge. This is the last teaching of the Bhagavad Gita, which is very authentic and the most read on all types of yoga. In this way, the last word of the Bhagavad Gita is Yoga.\nIt is the last word in the attainment of Yoga. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that the person who always remains absorbed in Krishna consciousness is the supreme\nYogi. What is Krishnabhavanamrith? Just as an individual soul remains present in all his body through his consciousness,\nin the same way, the Supreme Soul remains present in the entire creation through supreme consciousness.\nThis is superconsciousness.\nThe power of the individual soul, whose consciousness is limited, is imitated. ©. I can understand that\nwhat is happening in my limited body, but I cannot experience what is happening in another's body.\nWhat is happening. I am present in my entire body through my consciousness, but my consciousness is not present in the body of others. But the Supreme Being being present everywhere and within all, of every person's body"
