 स्वतः नियंत्रित हो जाती हैं । कृत्रिम साधनों से\nइन्द्रियों के कार्यो को नहीं रोका जा सकता, किन्तु यदि कोई इन्द्रियों को भगवान्‌ की सेवा में लगाकर",
          "textEn": "494\nEven 1000 years ago, it was very difficult, otherwise Arjun would not have rejected Krishna's proposal to adopt this system. This Kali Yuga is called a fallen era. In this era, people are generally short-lived,\nand they are very slow in understanding self-realization or spiritual life. They are usually unfortunate.\nTherefore, if someone has even a slight interest in self-realization, they can be misled by many conspiracies. The only way to attain the complete state of Yoga is to follow the principles of the Bhagavad Gita, which was practiced by Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu. This yoga practice\nis the simplest and the highest accomplishment. Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu demonstrated this Krishna Bhava Namrata Yoga system\nIn practical form, by merely chanting the holy name of Krishna, as it is prescribed in Vedanta,\nShrimad Bhagavat, Bhagavad Gita, and many important Puranas.\nIndians follow this yoga method in the highest number, and it is gradually spreading to many cities of the United\nState. This is very simple and practical for this era, especially for those who are serious about success in yoga. In this era, no other method can be successful.\nThe method of meditation was possible in the golden age or the age of truth, because the people of that era lived for millions of years. The person who wants success in practical yoga practice is advised to\nchant Hare Krishna, Hare Krishna, Krishna Krishna, Hare Hare; Hare Rama, Hare Rama, Rama Rama, Hare Hare, and\nthen he will start to feel himself that he is progressing. In the Bhagavad Gita, this practice of Krishna consciousness is called Rajavidya. Those who have adopted this most sublime method of devotion and those who practice devotion in the divine love of Krishna\ncan prove its blissful and simple richness.\nSanak,\nSanatan, Sanandan, and Sanatkumar, all four sages, were also attracted to the form of God and to the lotus feet of him,\nto the dust and divine fragrance, as has been stated in verse 43.\n\nFor yoga, control of the senses is necessary, and Bhakti Yoga or Krishna Bhava Namrata is the method of purifying the senses. When the senses are purified they become self-controlled. From artificial means,\nthe functions of the senses cannot be stopped, but if someone puts the senses in the service of God"
