्‌ द्वारा भक्त कौ तुष्टि हेतु सतत्‌ प्रकट कौ जाती है | भक्त परम सत्य को शून्यता या निर्विशेषता में\nनहीं देखना चाहता। एक अर्थ में, परम दिव्य विविधता केवल भक्तों के निमित्त होती है, अन्यों के लिए\nनहीं, क्योकि दिव्य विविधता का यह स्पष्ट रूप एकमात्र भगवत्कृपा से ही समझा जा सकता है,\nमानसिक चिन्तन या आरोही विधि से नहीं। कहा जाता है कि जब मनुष्य को भगवान्‌ की किंचित्मात्र",
          "textEn": "497\nTam--to him; Tvam--to you; Vidam--we know; Bhagavan--Oh God; Parmu--Supreme; Atma-tatvamu--the essence of the self; Sattatena--by that;\nBy your virtuous form; Samprati--now; Ratim--love; Rachayantam--creating; Egham--of all of them; Yat--that;\nWhich; Tete--yours; Anutapam--mercy; Viditai:--understood; Hadah--unwavering; Bhakti-yogai:--through devotion; Udagranthaya:----Free from attachment,\nFree from material bondage; Hadi--in the heart; Viduh--understood; Munayah--the group of sages; Viragah--not having interest in material life;\nWe know that you are the ultimate truth, that is, God, who manifests His divine form in the pure quality of truth. Your divine, eternal form is understood only by your grace,\nthrough unwavering devotion, by those sages whose hearts have been purified through devotion.\nhave been cleansed.\nMeaning: The supreme truth can be explained in three forms: the formless Brahman, the indwelling Supreme Soul, and the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead.\nHere, it is accepted that in understanding the supreme truth, the ultimate word is 'He'. Although the four princes were taught by their great scholar father, Brahma,\nthey could not understand the Supreme Brahman in its true form. They could only understand the Supreme Brahman when they\nsaw God directly with their own eyes. In other words, if someone sees or understands God, So, the other two forms of Parabrahma, namely, Nirvishesh Brahma and the inner-dwelling Supreme Soul form-- also automatically become understandable. Therefore, the Kumaras reaffirm, \"you are the supreme truth\".\"The non-differentialist can argue\nthat since God was so beautifully decorated, therefore he was not Parabrahma. But here,\nit has been confirmed that all the diversity (variety) of the supreme state is made of pure essence.\nIn the physical world, any quality--Satva, Rajo, or Tamo--remains tainted. Even in the physical world,\neven the Satva Guna is not free from the touch of Rajo and Tamo Gunas. But in the divine world, only the Satoguna\nremains present, in which there is not even a trace of Rajo or Tamoguna. Therefore, the form of God and\ntheir various pastimes and materials are all pure virtues. Such diversity in the quality of goodness\nis constantly manifested by God for the satisfaction of the devotee. The devotee does not want to see the ultimate truth in emptiness or non-differentiation. In a sense, the supreme divine diversity is only for the sake of devotees, not for others.\nNo, because this clear form of divine diversity can only be understood through the grace of God,\nnot through mental contemplation or ascending method. It is said that when a human being is even a little bit of God"
