्म\nसे तदाकार होना है। भक्तगण ऐसी मुक्ति की परवाह नहीं करते, क्योकि वे वास्तव में बुद्धिमान होते\nहैं। न ही वे अन्य चार प्रकार कौ मुक्तियों में से किसी की भी कामना करते हैं--ये हैं भगवान्‌ के ही",
          "textEn": "498\nIf grace is obtained, then he can understand God; otherwise, without His grace, a man\nEven after contemplating for thousands of years, he will not be able to understand what the true Parabrahma is. This\ngrace is then experienced by the devotee when he is completely free from sin. That is why it is said\nthat when all the impurities are eradicated and the devotee is completely detached from material attachments,\nonly then can he attain this grace of God. Even after considering the end, they are pleased with that grace.\nWhat fear is caused by the unjustly ordained fear, O foolish one?\nYou are the one who is pleasing to the ears of the stories.\nYou are the one who is skilled in singing and is famous for pilgrimages. 48. Meaning of the word\n\nNa- no; Atyantikam- ultimate liberation; Viganayanti- care; Api- also; Te- they; Prasadam- boon; Kim- what; U- what is said;\nAnyat- other material happiness; Arpit- given; Bhayam- fear; Bhruvah- of the eyebrows; Unnavi: --From lifting; satisfied; these-those\nDevotee; Ank-your Lord; Tvat-yours; Ankhri-Lotus feet; Sharanah-taken refuge; Bhavat-yours; Kathayah-stories; Kirtanya-worthy of Kirtan; Tirtham-pure; Yashasah-fame; Kushalah-skillful; Atyantapatu-extremely skilled; Ras-knower-knower of taste\nThose individuals who are extremely skilled and most intelligent in understanding things in their true form\nare engaged in listening to the auspicious deeds of God and the stories of his pastimes, which\nare worthy of Kirtan and listening. Such a person does not care about the supreme material boon, that is, liberation,\nnor about the material pleasures of heaven, so there is nothing to say.\nMeaning: The divine bliss that is experienced by a devotee of God, that is different from the material pleasures experienced by the ignorant. In the physical world, the weak remain engaged in the four principles of Varo,\nwhich are called Dharma, Artha, Kama, and Moksha. Generally, they adopt a religious life to attain a physical boon, the purpose of which is to satisfy the senses. When they, through this method, become frustrated or deluded in fulfilling the maximum\nsensory enjoyment, then they want to become one with the supreme element,\nwhich is freedom from their thoughts. Liberation is of five types, of which the least important is Sayujya or becoming one with Brahma.\nIt is to be like that. Devotees do not care about such liberation, because they are truly intelligent.\nThey are. They do not desire any of the other four types of liberation--they are only of God"
        },
        {
          "pageNumber": 1897,
          "text": "499\nलोक में निवास करना (सालोक्य), संगी के रूप में भगवान्‌ के साथ साथ रहना (सामीप्य), उनके\nजैसा ही ऐश्वर्य पाना (सार्षटि) तथा वैसा ही शारीरिक रूप प्राप्त करना। (सारूप्य) वे तो एकमात्र\nभगवान्‌ कौ तथा उनके शुभ कार्यों की महिमा का गुणगान करना चाहते हैं। शुद्ध भक्ति तो श्रवणं\nकर्तनम्‌ हे | भगवान्‌ की महिमा के श्रवण तथा कीर्तन में दिव्य आनन्द लेने वाले शुद्ध भक्त किसी\nप्रकार की मुक्ति की परवाह नहीं करते | यदि उन्हें पाँचों मुक्तियाँ भी प्रदान की जोय वे उन्हें अस्वीकार\nकर देते हैं जैसाकि भागवत के तृतीय स्कन्ध में बतलाया गया हे । भौतिकतावादी लोग स्वर्गलोक में\nस्वर्गिक सुख के इन्द्रिय-भोग कौ आकांक्षा करते हैं, किन्तु भक्तगण ऐसे भौतिक आनन्द का तुरन्त\nतिरस्कार कर देते हैँ । भक्त इन्द्र के पद तक कौ परवाह नहीं करता। भक्त जानता है कि कोई भी\nआनन्दप्रद भौतिक पद कभी न कभी विनष्ट हो जायेगा । यदि वह इन्द्र, चन्द्र या किसी अन्य देवता के\nपद तक पहुँच भी जाता है, तो एक अवस्था ऐसी आयेगी जब वह विनष्ट हो जायेगा । भक्त कभी भी\nऐसे क्षणिक आनन्द में रुचि नहीं दिखाता | वेदिक शास्त्रों से यह समझा जाता है कि कभी न कभी ब्रह्मा\nतथा इन्द्र तक नीचे गिरते हैं, किन्तु दिव्य भगवद्धाम से भक्त कभी नीचे नहीं गिरता। जीवन कौ इस\nदिव्य अवस्था कौ, जिसमें मनुष्य भगवान्‌ कौ लीलाओं को सुनने में दिव्य आनन्द का अनुभव करता\nहै, श्री चैतन्य महाप्रभु ने भी संस्तुति की है । जब श्री चैतन्य महाप्रभु रामानन्द राय से बातें कर रहे थे\nतो आध्यात्मिक साक्षात्कार के विषय में रामानन्द ने तरह तरह के सुझाव रखे थे, किन्तु श्री चैतन्य\nमहाप्रभु ने इस एक सुझाव के अतिरिक्त सबों को निरस्त कर दिया था कि मनुष्य को शुद्ध भक्तों की\nसंगति में भगवान्‌ की महिमाओं का श्रवण करना चाहिए | वह सबों को स्वीकार्य है, विशेष रूप से इस\nयुग H | मनुष्य को चाहिए कि शुद्ध भक्तों से भगवान्‌ के कार्यकलापोँ के विषय में सुनने में अपने को\nलगाये | मानव जाति के लिए यह सर्वोच्च वरदान माना जाता हे ।\n\nकामं भवः स्ववृजिनैर्निरयेषु नः स्ता-\nच्चेतोऽलिवद्यदि नु ते पदयो रमेत |\nवाचश्च नस्तुलसिवद्यदि ASST:\nपूर्येत ते गुणगणैर्यदि कर्णरन्धः ॥ ४९॥\nशब्दार्थं",
          "textEn": "499\nTo reside in the world (Saalokya), to live with God as a companion (Saamiya), to have the same opulence as them, and to attain the same physical form. (Sarupya) They are the only ones\nwho want to sing the praises of God and the glory of his auspicious deeds. Pure devotion is listening.\nPerforming is this. Pure devotees who take divine joy in listening to and chanting the glory of God,\ndo not care about any kind of liberation. If they are given even five liberties, they reject them, as it is said in the third chapter of the Bhagavata, O. Materialistic people in heaven\ndesire sensual pleasures of heavenly bliss, but devotees immediately\nreject such material pleasure. The devotee does not care about the position of Indra. The devotee knows that any\nblissful material position will be destroyed sometime. If he reaches the position of Indra, Chandra, or any other deity,\nthen a state will come when he will be destroyed.\nDevotees never\nshow interest in such momentary bliss. It is understood from Vedic scriptures that Brahma\nand Indra sometimes fall down, but a devotee never falls down from the divine abode. Of life, this\ndivine state, in which man experiences divine bliss in listening to the divine plays of God,\nShri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu has also praised. When Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu was talking to Ramananda Raya,\nRamananda made various suggestions regarding spiritual realization, but Shri Chaitanya\nMahaprabhu rejected all of them except one, that a person should listen to the glories of God in the company of pure devotees. That is acceptable to everyone, especially in this\nera H. Man should listen to the works of God from pure devotees and\nfeel engaged. This is considered the supreme boon for mankind.\nWork, existence, and the world are all different from the self.\nIf the mind were to be attached to the body,\nIf the speech were to be attached to the ears,\nIf the qualities were to be fully attained,\nIf the ears were to be the holes of the ears. 49). Shabdharam"
