          "textEn": "507\n\nGenerally, people blame the master of a servant for the wrong deeds done by him.\nJust as white leprosy spots on any part of the body make the entire skin impure. Meaning: Therefore, a Vaishnava should be perfectly qualified. As it is said in Bhagwat, whoever\nbecomes a Vaishnav, all the virtues of the deity come into him. In Chaitanya-charitamrita, twenty-six qualities\nare mentioned. A devotee should always see that with progress in Krishna consciousness,\nthere should be an increase in his Vaishnava qualities. A devotee should remain without fault, because any crime committed by a devotee is a stain on God. It is the duty of a devotee to always be aware in his behavior with others, especially\nwith other devotees of God, in his behavior.\nYesyamrutamalayashahshravanavagahah\nSadyaha punati jagadashapachatavikunthaha\nSoaham bhavadbhya-daavagdhasutirthakeerthi-\nChhandam swabahumapi vaha pratikoolvruttim. 6>. Meaning of the word\n\nYasya- of whom; Amrut-- immortal; Amal-- without blemish; TIT: - fame, glory; Shravan-- hearing; Avagahah-- entering;\nHe: - immediately; Punati-- purifies; Jagat- universe; Achash- from the dog-eater; Vikunthah- without a face; @: -\nThat person; Aham- I am; Bhavadbhyah- from you; Avagahah- entering; Su- pilgrimage; Tirtha- the best place of pilgrimage; Kirti: - fame;\nChhindyam- will cut; Swa- arm; Api- also; Vah- towards you; Pratikula- in an adverse manner; Vrittim- acting like an enemy..\n\nIn the entire world, any person, even a Chandal who cooks and eats dog meat,\nand lives by eating it, also becomes immediately pure if he listens with his ears to the praise of my name, fame, and other virtues\nand bathes in the nectar.\nNow you people have definitely\ninterviewed me, therefore I will not hesitate to cut off my own arm and separate it,\nif its behavior seems unfavorable to you. Meaning: If the members of human society accept Krishna consciousness, then its real\npurification can happen. This is clearly mentioned in all Vedic literature. Whoever sincerely\nreceives the nectar of Krishna consciousness, even without being elevated in HEATER, becomes pure. Of a devotee,\nthe selection can be made from any class of human society, although it is not expected that\nall the people of all the parts of the society are of good behavior. As in this verse and in the Bhagavad Gita"
