          "textEn": "50\nBecause; of a Brahmin; from a Brahmin; from the mouth; from the mouth;--While performing; Anughasam--Kaur; Tushtasya--Tushta; Mayi-Mer\nFor; Avahitah—Offering; Nija--Own; Kamam--Work; Pakah—Through fruits,\nIn the sacrificial fire, which is one of my own mouths, in the offerings made by the sacrificer Om,\nI do not get as much taste as I get from those dishes soaked in ghee, which are offered in the mouths of those Brahmins\nWho have offered me the fruits of their deeds, and who are always satisfied by my blessings. Meaning: A devotee or a Vaishnava does not accept any item without offering it to God. Because\na Vaishnavan offers all his fruits of action to God, therefore he does not\nenjoy any food item that has not been offered to God before.\nGod also offers all the food items to himself,\nand tastes them by giving them to the mouths of Vaishnavas. It is clear from this verse that God\neats through the fire of Yagya and the mouth of the Brahmin. Therefore, to satisfy God, many things are offered in the Yagya,\nsuch as food, ghee, etc. God accepts the offerings of Brahmins and devotees. It is said elsewhere that whatever is offered to Brahmins and Vaishnavas for food,\nGod also accepts it, but here it is said that he accepts the offerings of Brahmins and\nVaishnavas with more taste. Its best example\nis found in the behavior of Udraiit Prabhu with Haridas Thakur.\nAlthough Haridas was born in a Muslim family,\nAfter the Advaita Prabhu completed the holy fire festival, he offered the first plate of Prasad to him.\nHaridas Thakur told him that since I was born in a Muslim family, why are you giving the first plate to a Muslim instead of a high Brahmin? Haridas,\nout of his humility, scorned calling himself a Muslim, but because he was an experienced devotee,\nAdvaita Prabhu considered him a true Brahmin. Udwet Prabhu said that by offering the first plate to Haridas Thakur,\nthey are receiving the reward of feeding one lakh Brahmins. The conclusion is that if\none can feed one Brahmin or Vaishnav, it is better than performing millions of yagyas. That is why\nin this era, it has been prescribed that chanting the holy name of Harni, that is, God, and\npleasing the Vaishnavas is the only means to uplift a person to spiritual life."
