          "textEn": "578\nIf someone does not become Krishna conscious by firmly performing their regular religious duties,\nthen all his efforts in following so-called religious principles are merely a waste of time. Here, the sages also confirm this statement that it is not the gods, but the Supreme Being who are the ultimate goal of all religious principles. There are many foolish advertisers who say that even the worship of gods is the ultimate\nmethod of reaching the goal, but it has not been accepted in the authentic statements of Shrimad Bhagavat and Bhagavad Gita. The Bhagavad Gita says that the person who worships a particular deity\ncan reach the abode of that deity, but the man who worships the Supreme Lord can\nenter Vaikuntha. Some advertisers say that no matter what one does, in the end\nhe will reach the abode of the Lord, but this is not valid. God is eternal, and God's servant is eternal.\nAnd God's abode is also eternal.\nAll of these are called Sanatan or Shaswat here. Therefore, the fruit of devotion is not as temporary as the attainment of heaven by worshiping deities.\nThe sages wanted to emphasize that although God, by his selfless grace, this\nsays that he worships Brahmins and Vaishnavas, but in reality, God is not only worshiped by Brahmins and\nVaishnavas, but also by deities. Those who are free from death by your grace.\nO Yogi, you are the one who is pleased by whom others are pleased. 99. Meaning of the word\n\nThey cross over--cross over; He--because; Anjasa--easily; Death--birth and death; Nivrittah--having abandoned all material desires; Yat--your; Anugrahatah--by grace; Yoginah--yogis; Sahah--He; Parameshwarah--God; Bhavan--you; Kim--what; Swit-never\nIt is not possible; Anugrahite--can be granted; Yat--what; Parai:--by others; \\\n\nBy the grace of God, the yogis and all the spiritual people, having abandoned all material desires\nThey overcome ignorance. Therefore, it is not possible for any God to bestow grace upon them. Meaning: