          "textEn": "520\nWhose search is for gods, Brahmins, Vaishnavas, and other wells, they are always engaged in the service of the lotus feet of God. The conclusion is that no one can be a benefactor of God. In reality, every person is a servant of God's servant. You, who are constantly engaged in various actions,\nare beyond comparison, the delight of the supreme devotees.\nYou are the meritorious one who has performed the act of bathing the feet of the Brahmins.\nOh, beloved of Shri, what a vessel for offering to the gods! 29). Meaning of the word\n\nYah- who; Tam- to Lakshmi; Vivikt- without; Charitaih- devotion; Anuvartamanam- while serving; Na- not;\nAtyadriyat- extremely; Anurakt- attached; Param- supreme; Bhagwat- devotees; Prasangah- while serving;: - Supreme; Tvam- you; Dwija- Brahmin;\nKim- what; Agah- what you have attained; Bhag- all opulence or all virtues; Bhajanah- abode; Tvam- you\nOh Lord, you are very attentive to the deeds of your pure devotees, yet you\nare never attentive to those Lakshmijis who are constantly engaged in your divine loving devotion. Therefore, how can you be purified by the dust of the path on which Brahmins walk, and on your\nchest, how can you become glorified or fortunate by the Srivatsa symbol? Meaning: It is said in the Brahma-Samhita that God is always served by millions of Lakshmi's in his Vaikuntha world,\nbut with the feeling of being detached from all desires, they are not attached to any of them. God has six qualities--Infinite wealth, infinite fame, infinite strength, infinite\nbeauty, infinite knowledge, and infinite sacrifice. All the gods and other beings worship Lakshmiji to receive her grace.\nYet, God does not remain attached to that Lakshmiji, because to get his divine\nservice done, he can create countless Lakshmis.\nSometimes, Lakshmiji is jealous of those Tulsi\nbuds that are offered on the lotus feet of God, because those buds remain still there\nand do not move, whereas Lakshmiji, even while residing on their chest, sometimes goes to please those other\ndevotees who pray to receive her grace. Lakshmiji\nsometimes has to go to satisfy her countless devotees, but Tulsi buds never leave their place,\ntherefore, they prefer serving Tulsi more than serving Lakshmiji"
