          "textEn": "524\nSecurity should be provided. Special protection should be provided to Brahmins and Vaishnavas in all classes of humans.\nShould be given. They should be worshipped. When they are protected, it is like worshiping God.\nIs. This is not really safety. It is a duty. A person should offer all kinds of wealth and gentle words to Brahmins and Vaishnavas and worship them. If someone has no means to offer anything,\nthen at least use sweet words to pacify them. God himself showed such behavior towards the Kumaras.\n\nIf those who lead do not initiate this system, then human civilization will be destroyed. Whenever there is no protection and specific behavior for the devotees of God, who are highly intelligent in spiritual life, then the entire society is destroyed.\nThe word 'nadkshyati' indicates that\nsuch a civilization is destroyed and gets destroyed. ©. The type of civilization that is suggested\nis called 3999, which means 'highway of gods'.\" It is expected from the gods\nthat they are completely stable in devotion or in Krishna consciousness. This is the auspicious path, which should be protected. If the great men or leaders of society do not give special respect to Brahmins and Vaishnavas,\nand do not give them not only sweet words but also all facilities, then the progress of human civilization\nwill be destroyed. God himself wanted to give its teaching, therefore he praised the Kumaras\nso much.\nLike a thunderbolt, he is desired by the treasure of virtues.\nHe protects and nourishes the people with his own powers.\nTherefore, the lord of the three worlds,\nHe is radiant, and he is the delight of those who are subdued. 24). Meaning of the word\n\nTat--that which is auspicious; Tev--by you; Anabhishtam--not desired; Iva--like; Sattva-nidheh--all\nThe abode of goodness; Vidhitsah--desirous of doing; Kshemam--welfare; Jana-na--for the common people; Nija-shaktibhih--by one's own powers; Udadhrutah--destroyed; Arehah--the opposing element; Na