          "textEn": "30\nThus, the demon Hiranyaksha and Lord Hari, with the desire to win each other,\nbecame angry and struck each other with their respective huge maces. Meaning: Haryaksh is another name for Hiranyaksha. They are eager, with their bodies and hands\nDripping with blood, their eyes wide open.\nThey walk on strange paths, awake and alive\nLike a frog in a dry place. 99. Meaning of the words\nTayoah--both of them; Spudhoah--both competitors; Tigmoah--pointed; Gadaah--with maces; Ahatah--injured;\nAngkhayoh--their bodies; Kshata-astvaah--blood flowing from wounds; Praanah--life; Vivruddah--increased; Manshoah--anger;\nVicitrah--of various kinds; Margah--walking; Charatoah--doing; Jigishaya--with the desire to win; Vyabhat-k\nSeemed similar; Ilayam-for the cow (or earth); Iva-like; Shushpinoh-of two pairs; Mridhaah-\nFistfight.\n.\nThere was a fierce competition between the two warriors, both had sharp\npunches on their bodies from each other's pointed\nmaces, and with the smell of flowing blood from their bodies, they\nwere becoming increasingly angry. With the eagerness to win, they were making various moves.\nAnd this encounter seemed to them just like two strong bulls\nfighting for a cow. Meaning: here the earth is called Ila. The Earth was previously called Ilavrita-varsha.\nBut when Maharaj Parikshit ruled over the Earth, it was called Bharatvarsha.\nIn reality, Bharatvarsha is the name of the entire world, but over time, Bharatvarsha has come to be known as Bharat (India). Just as some time ago, India was divided into Pakistan and Hindustan,\nin the same way, the Earth was previously called Ilavrita-varsha, but as time passed,\nit was divided into the borders of many nations. Of the demon, of the limb of the sacrifice, Maya-\nHolding the greatness of the Varaha, the demon."
