          "textEn": "96\nChapter 31\nManu-Kardama Conversation\nVidura said\nSvayambhuva's mind was controlled by the Supreme Soul.\nWhy should the king tell the story of the people being in bed? 1>. Meaning of the word\n\nVidur said-- Vidur said; Swayambhuva's- of Swayambhuva; Cha-- and; Manoah-- of Manu; Vanshaah-- lineage; Param--\nMost; Sammatah-- respected; Kathatyam-- please tell; Bhagavan-- O venerable sage; Yatra- in which; Maitunen- by intercourse; Edhire- increased; Prajah- progeny..\n\nVidur said - The lineage of Swayambhuva Manu is highly respected. Oh venerable\nSage, my request to you is that you describe this lineage whose progeny\ngrew through intercourse. Meaning: To produce good children, one must adopt a controlled worldly life.\nIn reality, Vidur was not interested in listening to the history of such individuals who are living a worldly life. He wanted to know about the lineage of Swayambhuva Manu, because in this dynasty,\nmany devotee kings have been there, who had taken care of their subjects with self-knowledge and with utmost\ncare. Therefore, by listening to the history of their activities, man can become more enlightened.\nIn this context, an important word, 'Pram-Samat', has come, which indicates\nthat the progeny of Swayambhuva Manu and his sons was acceptable to great officials. In other\nwords, to produce ideal offspring, the acceptance of worldly life is given by all the sages and\nauthorities of Vedic religious texts. Priyatratottanapadaau Sutau Swayambhuvaasya Vaai.\nAs the Dharma is, so are the seven continents. 2>. Meaning of the word\n\nPriyatrat- Maharaj Priyavrata; Utthanapadaau - and Maharaj Utthanapada; Sutau - two sons; Swayambhuva's - of Swayambhuva Manu;\nVai - without doubt; Yatha - according to; Dharmam - religious rule; Jugupatu - ruled; Sapta-Dvipa-vatim - seven islands\nof; Mahim - Earth, on the world."
