          "textEn": "99\n\nOh sage, please tell me how Brahma's sons Daksha and Ruchi, after obtaining the other two daughters of Swayambhuva Manu\nas wives, produced offspring? Meaning: Those great men who contributed to the increase of offspring at the beginning of creation are called Prajapati.\nBrahma is also called Prajapati, similarly, some of his later sons also. Swayambhuva.\nManu is also Prajapati, and similarly, Brahma's second son is Daksha. Of the self-existent Manu, two daughters\nwere--Aakuti and Prasuti. Prajapati Ruchi married Akuti, and Daksha married Prasuti.\nThey got married.\nThese pairs and their descendants produced many descendants to settle the entire universe.\nVidur's question was, \"How did they produce generations in the beginning?\" 2\n\nMaitreya said,\n\"The Lord created the people, Kardama, from Brahma.\"\n\"Saraswati, with penance, endured thousands of times.\" 6>. Meaning of the word\n\nMaitreya said--Maitreya Muni said; Prajaah--children; Sruj--to do; Iti--in this way; Bhagavan--venerable;\nHEH:—Kardama Muni; Brahmana--by Lord Brahma; Uditah--ordered; Saraswatyam--on the banks of the Saraswati River;\nTapah--penance; Tape-practiced; Sahasranamah--thousands; Samah--years; Kausa--ten;\n\nThe great sage Maitreya replied--Having received the order from Lord Brahma to produce children in the worlds,\nthe venerable Kardama Muni performed penance for ten thousand years on the banks of the Saraswati River. Meaning: Here it is revealed that before attaining Siddhi, Kardam Muni meditated in yoga for ten\nthousand years.\nSimilarly, we come to know that Valmiki Muni\nalso practiced yoga and meditation for sixty thousand years before attaining Siddhi. Therefore,\nOnly those can successfully complete yoga practice whose life is quite long, such as one\nlakh years. In the same situation, one can achieve perfection in yoga, otherwise, real perfection\nis difficult to attain. Following the rules, controlling the senses, and doing various postures 