          "textEn": "08\nThis is the mind, the destroyer of the self-existent,\nThe ocean of existence, the ocean of the ocean. Those who worship desirelessness,\nEven those who are free from lustful desires. 14). Meaning of the word\n\nThis--the person; Mayaya-by the power of deception; Te-yours; Hata-corrupt; Medhasah-whose intellect; Tvat-yours;\nPad-Arvindam-the lotus feet; Bhav-of the world; Sindhu-ocean; Potam-boat to cross; Upaste-worshiping;\nare; Kam-for the sake of desires; Tesham-their; Rasi-give; Isha-Oh God; Kaman-desire; Niraye-in hell; Api-also; Ye-those who desire; Syu-can be attained..\nYour lotus feet are equivalent to a true boat to cross the ocean of worldly ignorance. Only ignorant men, controlled by Maya, worship these feet.\nThey do so for the sake of the petty and momentary pleasures of the senses, the attainment of which, even a person rotting in hell,\ncan also do.\nEven then, O God, you are so merciful that even on them,\nyou bestow your grace.\n\nMeaning: As it is said in the seventh chapter of the Bhagavad Gita, there are two categories of devotees\n--first, those who desire material pleasures, and second, those who, besides serving God, think of nothing else. Material pleasures can be obtained even by cookers and pigs whose lives are extremely\nhellish. The pig also eats, sleeps, and fully enjoys sexual intercourse, and this world\nremains extremely pleased with such hellish pleasures. The modern Yogi preaches that since\nman has senses, therefore he should also fully utilize them like dogs and cats\nand also practice yoga. Here, Kardam Muni has condemned it. They say that such material pleasures are for dogs and cats who live a hellish life.\nFor them.\nGod is so merciful that if the so-called yogis become satisfied with these material pleasures,\nthey allow them to attain all those material pleasures according to their wishes, but they\ncannot attain the state of perfection like Kardam Muni. The reality is that the hellish and demonic people do not even know what Siddhi is"
