          "textEn": "]0\nMeaning: Although Kardam Muni criticizes such people who go to God for material gains,\nbut they expressed their physical inability and\ndesire before God, saying, ** Although I know that I should not ask for any material thing from you,\nbut still, my wish is to marry a virtuous maiden.\"Here, the word 'samanvayam' (coordination) is very important. In ancient times, boys and\ngirls of similar nature were married; boys and girls of similar nature were thus tied with threads\nso that they would be happy. It would not have been more than twenty-five years, and possibly\neven today, in India, the parents of girls and boys used to show their horoscopes\nto find out if their mental combinations could be real or not. Thoughts like these\nare important. Nowadays, marriages are happening without much thought, and as a result, immediately after marriage,\nthere is divorce and separation.\nIn earlier times, husband and wife lived a happy life for life.\nBut nowadays, it has become very difficult. They wanted a wife of equal character, because a wife is necessary to help in spiritual and worldly progress. It is said that a wife fulfills all desires related to dharma, wealth, and desire. The one who gets a good wife,\nis considered very fortunate. According to astrology, a fortunate man is considered\none who has ultimate wealth, good sons, or a superior wife. Among these three, the one who has a best wife is the most fortunate. Before marriage, the choice of a woman should be based on equal character,\nnot on the so-called physical beauty or gestures for the sake of sensual pleasure.\nNo. In the twelfth verse of Bhagwat, it is said that in Kali Yuga, based on worldly life,\nmarriages will happen, and as soon as there is any deficiency in worldly life, the question of divorce will arise.\nKardam Muni could have received this boon from Uma, because it is said in the scriptures that"
