          "textEn": "[6\nInnumerable leaves are attached. It is eternally revolving in the axis of the universe. One, self-existent, through desire,\nSecond, through the self-controlled, through the self-controlled.\nHe who creates, you are the creator, you are the sustainer.\nAs the sun and moon, by their own power. 99. Meaning of the word\nEkah-- one; Swayam-- by oneself; San-- having become; Jagatah-- the universe; Sisrukshaya-- with the desire to create;\nAdvitiyaya-- unique; Atman-- in oneself; Adhi-- while being in control; Yogamayaya-- through Yogamaya; Srujasi-- you create; Adah-- that universe; Pasi-- you fill; Punah-- again; Grasishyase-- you end; Yathah-- as\nthe way; Oorna-nabhih-- spider; Bhagavan--¢ God; Swa-shaktibhih-- by one's own power.. Hey Shri Bhagwan, with the desire to create these\nuniverses, you create them, nurture them, and then\ndestroy them with your powers. These powers are under your other power, Yogmaya.\nJust as a spider weaves a web with its power and then swallows it again.\nMeaning: From these two words of this verse, the principle of the Nirvisheshvadis (those who believe that everything is God) is that every object is God.\nIt becomes nullified. Here, Kardama Muni says, \"O Lord! You are alone, but\nyour powers are diverse.\"The example of a spider is also very important. The spider is an individual\nliving being, and it weaves a web with its power and plays on it, and when it wants\nit ends the web and ends the game. When a web is woven from the spider's saliva,\nthen the spider does not become without qualities. Similarly, the creation or manifestation of physical or spiritual power,\ndoes not make the doer without attributes. This prayer tells that God is sensitive and\nlistens to the prayers of devotees and fulfills them. Therefore, they are the embodiment of Sachchidananda. I desire the position of the lord of the universe,\nWhich I have not attained through my own power, even though it is subtle like a ghost.\nFor your grace, even though it is through my own power"
