          "textEn": "G7\nLasattulasya Bhagavanvilakshithah. 20>. Meaning of the word\n\nNa- not; Etat- this; Bat- without doubt; Adhishadh-- O God; Padam- physical world; Tav- yours; Ipsitam-\ndesire; Yat- which; Mayaya- from your external power; Na- for us; Tanuse- appearing; Bhut- subtle;\nand subtle element; Anugrahaya- to bestow grace; Astu- be; Api- also; Yarhi- when; Mayaya- your\nWithout cause; Lasat- grand; Tulsi- from the garland of basil leaves; Bhagwan Shri Bhagavan; Vilakshitah- seen\nThat Lord, Even without desire, you manifest this creation of gross and subtle elements\nfor our sensory gratification. May we receive your unconditional grace, because\nyou, adorned with a garland of basil leaves in your eternal form, have appeared before us. Meaning: Here, it is clearly mentioned that the creation of the physical world is by God's own will,\nnot by His external power, because the souls want to enjoy it.\nThis world is not made for those who do not desire the pleasure of sensual gratification,\nwho are constantly engaged in divine love and devotion, and who are always absorbed in Krishna consciousness. For them, the spiritual world is constantly present, which they can experience. Shrimad\nIt is said elsewhere in the Bhagwat that for those who have taken refuge in the lotus feet of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, this world is meaningless. Because this world is full of crisis at every step,\ntherefore, it is not for the sake of devotees, but for those souls who, at their own risk,\nwant to keep material power under control.\nShri Krishna is so merciful that for those who desire sensual pleasures,\nHe has created a separate world for them, which they can enjoy according to their wishes; yet,\nHe appears in his virtuous form. God willingly creates this material world,\nbut either He incarnates Himself or sends one of His trusted sons,\nor a servant, or a reliable author like Ved Vyas, to give teachings. They\ngive themselves as sermons in the form of discourses of Bhagavad Gita. Along with creation, this preaching work also\ncontinues, so that the rotting, misguided souls in this world, reaching the abode of God"
