          "textEn": "[8]\nTake refuge in them. Therefore, the final teaching of the Bhagavad Gita is, abandon all the artificial tasks of this world and come to my refuge. I will save you from all sinful fruits of actions.\nI will take.That which is beyond your experience, for the sake of action,\nThat which is governed by its own self, the world,\nI bow to the one who is worthy of salutation, the one whose lotus feet,\nThe lotus-like one, is the destroyer of desires. 21). Meaning of the word\n\nTam--that; Tvam--you; Anubhutiya-- through experience; Uparat-- neglected; Kriya- Sakam Karmo ka Sukh; Artham--\nFrom whom; Swamayaya-- by one's own power; Vartita-- brought; Loka-Tanram-- the material world; Namami-- I salute; Abhikshna-- continuously; Namaniya-- venerable; Pada-Sarojam-- lotus feet; Alupiyasi-- the poor; Kama-- desires;\nAkankshas-- aspirations; Varsham- while doing..\n\nI constantly offer my respectful salutations at your lotus feet, whose refuge\nit is better to take, because you are the one who showers all blessings on the poor\nHmm.\nYou have expanded these physical realms with your own power, so that all\nsouls can attain detachment from desire-driven actions through your experience. Meaning: Every person who desires physical happiness, liberation, or divine love and devotion to God,\nshould offer salutations to God, because God is the one who gives every human being\nthe desired fruits. In the Bhagavad Gita, God has emphatically said--Yatha mam\nPrapadyante, those who want to enjoy successfully in this world, God gives them the boon of enjoyment,\nThose who want to be free from the bonds of this world, He grants them liberation, and those who\nwant to remain fully engaged in Krishna consciousness, God grants them the boon of devotion. For material\npleasure, He has praised performing many sacrifices in the Vedas, and by the benefit of those commands,\neither in higher realms or by living in a prosperous family, one can attain material bliss.\nThese methods are mentioned in Vedas and people can adopt them. From this physical world,\npeople who want salvation can also benefit in the same way."
