          "textEn": "39\nGatiranyatha--That is, in this Kali Yuga, besides chanting the holy name of God, there is no other\noption, and no other option, and no other option. A celibate should wake up early in the morning\nand should quickly get up and chant the name of God in a stable manner. Of that sage,\nIt seemed from his appearance that he had performed rigorous penance, and this is\nalso the characteristic of observing celibacy. If someone lives differently, then the work-related signs visible in their face and body will make it clear. The word Vidyotsanam indicates that his body showed the characteristics of a celibate. This is the biggest proof of doing rigorous penance in yoga. A drunkard, a smoker, or an addictive person is never suitable for yoga practice.\nNot suitable. Generally, yogis appear very weak because they do not live in a comfortable situation, but Kardam Muni was not weak, because he had a direct\nvision of the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead.\nHere, 'Sigdhapaṇavalokanat' means that they had the good fortune to have a direct vision of God. They looked healthy, because they had directly drunk the nectar-filled words emanating from the lotus-\nlips of God. Similarly, the one who listens to the divine sound of \"Hare Krishna\" of God's holy\nname, his health improves. We have actually\nseen that many celibate and householder, who are associated with the International Krishna Bhava Anand Sangh, their\nhealth has improved and radiance has come to their faces. The celibate who is engaged in spiritual progress\nit is necessary for him to look very healthy and radiant. A sage\nAnd the comparison of a gem without carving is also very appropriate. Even if the gem that came out of the mine\nis without polish, but no one can stop its aura. Similarly, even though\nKardam Muni did not wear good clothes and his body was not properly clean,\nbut overall, his appearance was like a gem.\nAthotjamupayatam nrdevam pranata purah. By the sight of the other, according to the desire. 48."
