          "textEn": "52.\nBy following the principles, a common person cannot attain the supreme state of spiritual attainment.\nCannot. He will have to take refuge in an authentic guru and work with faith and devotion under his guidance. Only then will he be able to achieve perfection, there is no doubt about it. I have shown you the excellent grace.\nWith the open ears, the sixteen types of sight, and the divine. 7>. Meaning of the word:\n\nBy seeing, fortunately; by you, by you; instructed:--taught; I am--I; given:--provided; and--and;\nGrace:--grace; great:--great; opened:--open; ear:--through the holes of the ears; accepted:--accepted;\nfag--by fate; pure:--pure; word:--word\n\nFortunately, I have received instruction from you, and in this way, you have bestowed great grace upon me. I thank God that I am opening my ears and listening to your\npure words.\nMeaning: Srila Rupa Goswami has instructed in his book Bhaktirasayat-Chindhu that how\nan authentic guru should be accepted and how one should behave with him. First,\nthe interested person should search for an authentic guru, and then with great eagerness,\nshould receive instruction and act accordingly. It is a two-way (mutual) service. A true guru or saintly person is always eager to uplift those who come to them.\nThey remain. Because every person is controlled by the illusion of Maya and keeps forgetting his main duty, Krishna-\ndevotion, therefore, saints want every person to become a saint. It is the duty of every saintly man to awaken Krishna devotion in every ignorant common man. Manu said, because he received teachings from Kardama Muni, therefore he became fulfilled.\nHaving received the message from the ears, he is considering himself fortunate. Here is a special mention\nthat a person should listen to the message by opening his ears from an authentic guru. But how to obtain it?\nHow to do it? Humans should receive divine messages through their ears. The meaning of the word 'karnarandhra'"
