          "textEn": "53\nis through the ear holes.\"The grace of the Guru is not obtained from any other part of the body,\nbut is obtained only from the ears. But it does not mean that the guru takes some money\nand in return gives some mantra in the ear, by whose meditation one can attain perfection in six months and become God\ncan go. Such a perception from the ear is fake. The reality is that an authentic guru\nknows what kind of person a human is and how he can act in Krishna-Bhava-Anmrita,\ntherefore, he preaches to him in the same way. He does not secretly in his ear, but rather\nHe preaches in front of everyone, saying, \"You are suitable for such and such work in devotion to Krishna.\" You can work like this.\"Any person can be asked to do Krishna devotion in the room of Shrivigraha,\nthen the second to do literary editing work, the third to give sermons,\nand any other to manage the kitchen can be asked.\nThere are different departments to work in Krishna devotion, and the guru, knowing the ability of a particular person, gives him this\ntype of education so that he can become complete. It is clearly stated in the Bhagavad Gita that a person, according to their ability, by serving, attains the highest accomplishment in spiritual life, which\nJust as Arjuna served Krishna with his military skills. Arjun, like a soldier,\nBy offering his services, could become complete. Similarly, any artist, under the guidance of their guru,\ncan achieve success while doing artistic work. If a person is interested in literature,\nthen he can serve God by composing articles or poems under the guidance of a guru.\nHe can. A person should receive a message from their guru regarding acting according to their ability,\nbecause the guru is skilled in giving such advice.\nThe entire system becomes complete through the combination of the teachings of the Guru and the faithful adherence by the disciple.\nSrila Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur explains this verse from the Bhagavad Gita--'Vyavasayatmika\nBuddhi:--'He who desires spiritual progress should receive orders from his Guru\nthat what is his special task? ©. He should complete the special teaching with faith"
