          "textEn": "54\nShould do and should consider that as one's own. The disciple's only duty is that\nhe should faithfully follow the teachings received from his guru. Only through this will he achieve success. Man\nshould be careful in receiving the message of the Guru through his ears and should perform it with reverence. This will help him to live his life successfully. O Lord, my heart is distressed by the affection for your well-being.\nYou are worthy of hearing it, O sage, please listen to it with compassion. 8>. Meaning of the word\n\nSah- Aapah; Bhavan- Aapah; Duhitru- Sneha- Aapah; Pariklishit- Atmanah- Kshubdha- Manah; Mama- Mine; Shrotum- To listen; Arhasi- Be pleased; Dinasya- Muncha- To the poor; Shravitam- To the prayer; Kripya- Kindly; Mune- Oh sage..\n\nOh sage, please listen to the humble prayer of me, because my mind is extremely agitated by the affection of my daughter.\nMeaning: When a disciple, after receiving a message from his guru, fulfills it with devotion,\nthen he has the right to ask his guru for any kind of grace. Generally, a pure devotee of God or a pure disciple of an authentic guru does not ask for any grace from God or\nthe guru, but if ever there is a need to receive some kind of grace from the guru,\nuntil he completely pleases them, he cannot ask for it. Swayambhuva Manu, due to the affection of his daughter, wanted to express the matter of his mind,\nthat what work he wanted to get done. Beloved, I desire my own son, who is the best of all.\nHe desires a husband, who is virtuous and full of good qualities. 9>. Meaning of the word\n\nPriyatvrat-uttanpadodhah - Priyatvat tatha uttanapad kau; Swasya-- sister; Iyam-- this; Duhita-- daughter; Mama- mine;\nAnvichchati-- is searching; Patim- husband or groom; Yuktam- suitable; Vayah- character, virtues, etc. - from age, character, virtues\netc.\n. He, in terms of age, character, virtues, etc., his own"
