          "textEn": "55\n\nIn search of a suitable husband. Meaning: The character of Devahuti, the young daughter of Swyambhuva Manu, was excellent and she was also worthy,\nTherefore, she was in search of a husband according to her age, character, and qualities. Manu introduced his daughter\nto Priyavrata and Uttanapada, these two great kings, as their sister.\nThe purpose was to assure the sage that the maiden was from a high family. She is their daughter, and also\nShe is the sister of the Kshatriyas, she is not from the lower class. Therefore, Manu, considering Kardam suitable,\nwanted to hand over his daughter to him. It is clear that although Devahuti was an adult in age and qualities,\nshe did not go there to choose her own husband. She expressed her desire for a suitable husband according to her age, character, and qualities, and the father, out of affection, took upon himself the burden of finding such a husband for her.\nWhen you, with your character, knowledge, and form,\nHaving spoken, I have made this determination. 90 Meaning of the word\n\nWhen--When; Tu- but; Bhavatah yours; Sheel- excellent character; Shrut- knowledge; Roop- beautiful form, appearance; Vayah-\nyouth; Gunan- qualities; Ashrunot- heard; Naradat- from Narada Muni; Egha- by Devahuti; Tvayi- in you; Aasit- was\ngone; Krit- determined; Dh- resolve..\n\nSince she has heard from Narad Muni about your excellent character, knowledge, beauty, age (Ayu), and other\nqualities, she has since then fixed her mind on herself. Meaning: Devahuti had neither seen Kardam Muni himself, nor had he any personal experience about his character or qualities,\nbecause there was no social gathering from which\nhe could have obtained such information. But he had heard about Kardam Muni from Narad Muni. It's better to get personal information from an official. She had heard from Narada Muni that Kardam Muni was worthy of being her husband.\nTherefore, she had decided in her mind\nthat she would marry only him. H