          "textEn": "59\nThe sage said,\nI am not the first to desire a marriage with you, my own daughter.\nThe word meaning is:\n\nThe sage said,\nThe best of the virtuous, Kardama; he said; I am not; the desire is; I am not;\nNot bound by any other promise; and; and; your; daughter; both of us;\nAppropriate; this; first; marital; and;\nAppropriate; this; first; the first;\nThe marriage; the marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and;\nThe marriage; and.\n\nThe great sage replied - Undoubtedly, I am desirous of marriage, and your daughter has neither\nmarried anyone, nor has she given her word to anyone else. Therefore, according to the Vedic method,\nwe both can get married. Meaning: Before accepting the daughter of Swyambhuva Manu, in front of Kardama Muni,\nthere were many things to consider. Firstly, Devahuti had decided to marry him. She did not want to make any other man her husband.\nThis was the biggest\nconsiderable thing, because when a woman, at the very first glance, offers her heart to a man,\nit is difficult to take it back. This is the psychology of Siyo ©. Also,\nbefore this, she was not married; she was a weaver. From all these things, Kardam Muni\naccepted him. Therefore, he said, \"Yes, according to the religious rules of marriage, I\naccept your daughter.\"\" Marriage has many forms. The best marriage is one in which, after calling the suitable groom, the bride is adorned with JG and ornaments, and according to the father's ability,\na dowry is given, and the bride is offered. There are other types of marriage as well, such as Gandharva.\nMarriage and love marriage. These are also considered marriage. If a girl forcefully goes to Hari and\nlater accepts her as wife, then that is also considered marriage.\nBut Kardam Muni\nAccepted the best system of marriage, because the girl's father wanted and that girl\nwas also worthy off. He had not loved anyone else. From all these things, Kardam Muni\nbecame agreeable to accepting the daughter of Swayambhuva Manu."
