          "textEn": "8]\nChapter twenty-three.\nThe sorrow of Devahuti.\nMaitreya said,\nBeing pleased with the departed ancestors, the virtuous one attained the desired husband.\nAlways wandering with love, she became like Bhavani, the Lord. 1>. Meaning of the word\n\nMaitreya said--Maitreya said; Pitrabhyam--by the parents; Prasthite--on arrival; Sadhvi--chaste;\nPatim--of her husband; Iṅgit-kovid--knowing the sentiments; Nityam--constant; Paryacharat-seva kau--for service;\nPritiya--lovingly; Bhavani--Goddess Parvati; Iva--like; Bhavam-Shivji's; Prabhum-one's own master..\n\nMaitreya said - upon the departure of her parents, Devahuti, the devoted wife who understood her husband's wishes,\nbegan to serve her husband daily with love, just as Bhavani serves her husband Shankar Ji.\n\nMeaning: The example given specifically by Bhavani is important.\nThe meaning of Bhavani is\nBhav, meaning Shiva's wife. Himalaya Raja's daughter, Bhavani or Parvati, chose Shiva\nas her husband, who appears like a mendicant. Even though she was a princess, she endured many hardships to\nget Shiva. Those who had no home and who sat under a tree\nand spent all their time in meditation. Although Bhavani was a very great king's daughter,\noff, but she used to serve Shiva like a nun. Similarly, Devahuti, the emperor,\nwas the daughter of Swayambhuva Manu, yet she chose Kardamuni as her husband. She\nServed them with great love and knew how to please them. Therefore, here she is\ncalled a 'Sadhvi,' which means, 'A devoted wife or a virtuous woman.' This rare\nexample is the ideal of Vedic civilization.\nEvery woman should be like Devahuti or Bhavani, superior and\ndevout. Even today, in Hindu society, unmarried girls are told to worship Shankar Ji\nto get a husband like them. Shiva is the best among the devotees,\nnot from the point of view of lust, but because he is the best among the devotees, he is the ideal husband. Among the Vaishnavas,\nlike Shumbha-- Shumbha or Shiva is the ideal Vaishnava. They constantly meditate on Lord Rama"
