          "textEn": "230\nIn him, there is a tendency to deceive others, and his senses are incomplete. But if someone\nfollows the Guru's command through tradition, then he conquers these vices\nand takes them. Therefore, the knowledge obtained from an honest guru is not a fraud. Brahmaji was well aware\nthat Kardam Muni was literally following his commands, and in this way, he was giving his guru\nreal respect. The meaning of respecting the Guru is to literally follow his orders. For the sake of serving, the sons should be like this.\nThey should be respected and honored with the words of the Guru. 13). Meaning of the word.\n\nEtavati--up to this extent; Eva--exactly; Shushrusha--service; Kayam--should do; Pitari--of father; Putrakaih--by sons;\nBy the sons; Badham--accepting, 'Jo aagna anumanyet--one should obey the order; Gaurvena--respectfully; Gurouh--of the guru; To:-- order..\nThe son should obey his\nfather or guru's orders with respect, * saying 'the command'.\n\nMeaning: In this verse, two words are very important, one is 'Pitari' and the other is 'Guruh'. A son or disciple should accept the words of his father or guru without hesitation. Say \"yes\" to whatever the Father or Master says without argument. There should not be any such opportunity\nwhen a disciple or son says, 'This is not appropriate, I cannot do it.''\"\nIf he says this, then he has fallen. The father and the guru have equal status, because\nthe guru is the second father. People of the upper class are called 'dvija'--born twice--when the topic of birth\narises, it is necessary to have a father. The first birth happens because of the real father,\nbut the second birth is only possible through the Guru. Sometimes father and guru can be the same person,\nthen sometimes different different. In every situation, one should immediately obey the command of the father or guru.\nWhile doing so, one should follow it.\nOne should not reason. This is the true service of the Guru and\nfather. Vishwanath Chakrabarti Thakur has said that the Guru's command is for the disciples"
