          "textEn": "23\nFor life and soul are equivalent. Just as a human cannot separate the soul from the body,\nin the same way, a disciple cannot remove the Guru's command from his life. If a disciple follows this\nway of the Guru's teaching, then he will surely become accomplished. In the Upanishads, this\nis confirmed--those who have faith in Shri Bhagwan and their Guru, they automatically receive Vedic education. Even if someone is uneducated in terms of physical vision, but if he has faith in the Guru along with\nthe complete Supreme God, then the knowledge of scriptures immediately manifests before him.\nBHT duhitarah satyastava vatsa sumadhyamah.\nSargametam prabhavaih svairbrihayishyantyanekaadha. 14>. Meaning of the word:\nImāha - these; Duhitaraha - daughters; Satyaha - virtuous; Tava - yours; Vatsa-- this son; Su-madhyamaha - Tanvangi, slender waist; Vali-vali; Sargam-creation; Etam-this; Prabhavaiha-by influence; Svaih-spontaneously; Vrnhachisyanti-they will increase; Aneka-dhaha-many; Vrahmaji praised the nine daughters of Kardam Muni by saying this- your\nAll Tanvangi daughters are undoubtedly virtuous. I believe that they will, in many ways, through their lineage, enhance this creation. Meaning: In the beginning of creation, Brahmaji was worried about the increase in population, and\n\nWhen he saw that Kardam Muni had already had nine beautiful daughters, he hoped\nthat many descendants would be born from these daughters, who would take on the task of creating the universe. Therefore, they were happy to see them. The word su midhyama means, \"The best daughter of a beautiful woman\".\n\"\nIf a woman's waist is slim, then she is considered very beautiful. All the daughters of Kardam Muni were just as beautiful. Therefore, according to the conduct and taste of the best of sages,\nthe self-born should be given a body, and that which is praised in the world. 15). Shabdharam"
