          "textEn": "238\nHe who was driven away by the hundred-fold curse,\nAnd who was given to his own son by the curse,\nAnd then the world was destroyed. 21). Meaning of the word:\nGaten-- after leaving; Shatadhrutau-- Lord Brahma; Kshatrah-hey Vidur; Kardamah-hey Kardam Muni; Tena-- by him;\nChoditah-being ordered; Yatha-uditam-according to being cut; Swa-duhituh-his daughter; Pradaat-being given; Vishch-srijam-being created; Tatah-thereafter lL\nOh Vidur Brahmaji, Kardam Mani gave his nine daughters to the nine sages according to the orders given by Brahma\nAccording to which, he gave them to the nine sages, who made the people of this world wise. Marichaye kalam pradadanamthaatraye. With faith, in the mind, he offered the sacred fire. 22). Pulahay gati yuktam kratave cha kriyam satim.\n\nViprishbhankrto-drahansamalalayat. 24). Meaning of the word:\nAtharvane- Atharva to whom; Adadaat- Provided; Shantim- Peace; Yaya- By which; Yagya- Yagya; Vitanyate- Is done; Vipra- The foremost among the Brahmins; Krit- Uddhrahan- Married; Sa- Daran- His wives\nAlong with; Samalalayat- Taken care of.. Due to peace, the Yagya seems to be well completed. In this way, he married all of them off to leading Brahmins, and along with wives,\nhe started taking care of all of them."
