          "textEn": "239\nThose sages who were engaged in their respective tasks, having completed their duties,\nAnd having attained their respective abodes, they returned to their respective hermitages. 25. Meaning of the word\nTatha--Tava; Te-Ve; Rishayaha-Rishiganaha; Kshatrah-Hey Vidur; Krita-Daaraaha-In this way married; Nimanya-Vida-Having taken;\nTam-From Kardama; Pratishtha-Went away; Nandim-To Prasannata; Apanna-Received; Swam-Self; Swam-Self; Ashram-\nManandam-Ashram. Hey Vidur, in this way, after getting married, the sages bid farewell to Kardam, and they\nWith joy, went to their respective hermitages. Sava-tiranam triyugama-ajnaya vibudharshabham.\nVivikta upasadhyam pranamya samabhasitam. 26). Meaning of the word\nSah-- Kardam Muni; Cha-- Tatha; Avatirnam-- Took incarnation; Tri-yugam-- To Vishnu; Agnaya-- Understanding; Vibudha-\nRishabham- The head of the gods; Vivikte-- In a secluded place; Upasadhyam- Going near; Pranamya-- Having bowed;\nSamabhashat- Spoke.\n.\nWhen Kardam Muni understood that the chief of all the gods, the complete Purushottam Bhagwan,\nVishnu has incarnated, then he went to a secluded place and, bowing to them, spoke in this way. Note: Lord Vishnu is called Treta Yuga. They appear in three eras--Satya, Treta, and Dwapara--\nbut do not appear in Kali Yuga, but it is understood from the praises of Prahlada Maharaj that they appear in Kali Yuga in the guise of a devotee. Bhagavan Chaitanya is the only devotee. But he never revealed this distinction that Krishna appeared as a devotee, then\neven then, Roop Goswami recognized him, because God does not hide himself from a pure devotee. When Roop Goswami first greeted Lord Chaitanya, he recognized him.\nThey had recognized him then. They knew that Lord Chaitanya himself was Shri Krishna, therefore they bowed to him in these words,\n“I pray to Shri Krishna who has now appeared as Lord Chaitanya\nare.\n'' This is also confirmed by the praises of Prahlad Maharaj, that in Kali Yuga, they appear directly\nrather than as devotees. That is why Vishnu is called Triyuga. Triyuga kau ek"
