          "textEn": "243\nare, but the devotee not only has a complete understanding of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, but also attains His direct\nassociation. You yourself are the nectar of words, having come to my house. Chikirsha-bhagavan-gyana-bhaktanam manavardhanah. 30>. Meaning of the word\n\nSvayam- of oneself; Vakyam- word; Ritam- truth; Kartum- to make; Avatirnah- descended; Asi- have become;\nMe Grihe- in my house; Chikirshuh- desirous of expansion; Bhagavan- Shri Bhagavan- knowledge; Bhaktanam- of devotees;\nMaan- respect, honor, reverence; Vardhanah- increaser. Kardam Muni said - O my beloved Lord, who always bestows human-like qualities upon your devotees,\nYou have descended into my house\nto fulfill your words and to spread true knowledge. Meaning: When Lord appeared before Kardam Muni after his yoga practice,\nhe promised that he would become their son. Therefore, only to fulfill his promise, he\ndescended as the son of Kardam Muni.\nAnother reason for their appearance was [Taig rar\nKnowledge, to distribute knowledge. Therefore, they are called Bhaktanam Manavardhanah, meaning they increase the honor of the devotees. By distributing Sankhya, they will increase the devotees, therefore Sankhya philosophy\nis not a dry knowledge. Sankhya Darshan is the philosophy of Bhakti Yoga. If it was not for the devotion of Sankhya,\nhow would the honor of the devotees have increased? Devotees do not have interest in knowledge, therefore Kapil\nThe Sankhya propounded by the sage is for the purpose of making man egoistic in his devotion. True knowledge\nand true liberation is to go to the refuge of Shri Bhagwan and be engaged in his devotional service. You are the form of the formless, O Lord. That is, they are pleased with their own forms. 31st. Lexicon"
