          "textEn": "25]\nIn this era, for self-realization, this method of Kirtan (chanting) is the best, therefore, God\nChaitanya preached this for the welfare of all humanity. TAH, in this world, for those who are desirous of liberation,\nFor the sake of contemplation, for the sake of understanding the essence of the elements. 26). Meaning of the word:\n\nThis - this; mine - mine; birth - birth; in this - in this; desiring liberation - the supreme saints who desire liberation;\nFrom the wicked; from unnecessary material desires; for discussion - to discuss; of the principles - of the truths;\nFor agreement - extremely agreeable; self-realization - self-realization. In this world, my manifestation has been especially to propound the Sankhya philosophy.\nIt has happened. This philosophy is supremely united for self-realization by those individuals who\nwant freedom from the bondage of unnecessary material desires. Meaning: here the word 'durashayat' is very meaningful. Dur means misery or sorrow. Ashayat.\n\"We mortals have taken refuge in the physical body, which is full of suffering and\nsorrows. Foolish people do not understand this situation, and this ignorance, attachment, or illusion is called a stick. Human society should understand seriously that the body itself\nis the root of all unhappy life. It is said that modern civilization is progressing in scientific knowledge,\nbut what is this scientific knowledge? It depends only on physical pleasure (comfort),\nit does not have the knowledge that no matter how much pleasure one keeps the body, it is perishable.\nIt is said in the Bhagavad Gita, ¶— Antavanta ima dehah--the destruction of these bodies is certain. Nityasyukta: Sharirinah: It is the sense of the living soul or spark within the body. That\nThe soul is immortal, but the body is not immortal.\nTo perform work, we need a body; without\na body, without senses, no activity comes. But people do not have the desire to know\nwhether the body can be immortal. In reality, they desire an immortal body\nso that they can enjoy sensual pleasures, but these pleasures are not immortal. Therefore, the lack of such a thing\nis bothersome to them, which they can constantly enjoy, but they do not know how to obtain it"
