          "textEn": "259\nIt is necessary, rather, he should be completely dependent on God for his food and shelter. He should go for a walk. Silence Silence means \"Be quiet.\"Until a man is silent (without speaking), he is not able to fully think about the divine plays (of God). It does not mean that because of being foolish\nand being unable to speak, a vow of silence is taken. Rather, a person has to remain silent,\nso that people cannot bother him. Chanakya Pandit has said that as long as a cunning person\ndoes not speak, he appears very intelligent. Speaking itself is the real test. The so-called silence of the Nirgunia 'Swami'\nindicates that he has nothing to say. He only wants to beg. But Kardama Muni did not maintain such silence. They remained silent to get rid of irrelevant talks. When a man, being serious, does not talk nonsense, then he is called a sage. Maharaj Ambarisha had presented a good example--Whenever he spoke, he\nspoke about the divine plays.\nIt is mandatory to remain silent to avoid nonsense,\nand to put the power of speaking into the divine plays of God. In this way, one can make their life\nsuccessful by chanting and listening to God. The meaning of Vratam\nis to make a resolution, as it is said in the Bhagavad Gita--Amanitvam Adagbhitvam--Without caring for one's\nrespect and without being proud of one's position. Non-violence means not to become violent. There are eighteen ways to attain knowledge and accomplishment, and Kardam Muni, through vows,\naccepted the principles of self-realization. The mind is used in the Brahman, which is the ultimate truth.\nIt shines with qualities, and is manifested by the devotion of one. 43). Meaning of the word\n\nManah-- mind; Brahmani-- the Supreme Brahman; Yunchanah-- while stabilizing; Yat-- that; Tat-- that; Sat-- that; Asat-- that; Karya-- work; Karana-- cause;\nParam-- past, beyond; Guna-avabhase-- one who reveals the three Gunas; Vigune-- beyond the physical Gunas; Eka-\nBhaktya-with devotion