          "textEn": "26]\nHe who remains engaged in devotion to God is like an undisturbed ocean in the waves.\nThe same example is given in the Bhagavad Gita as well- man should become like the ocean. In the ocean, millions of rivers come together, thousands of tons of water turn into vapor and form clouds, yet\nthe ocean remains unchanged. May nature continue to do its work, but if someone is fixed in devotion to the lotus feet of God, then he does not get disturbed, he becomes introverted. He does not see the external nature; he sees the self-nature of his power,\nHe remains engaged in the service of God with a calm attitude. In this way, he attains self-realization.\nSuch a supreme devotee never gets entangled with others, because he sees everyone from the seat (step) of self-knowledge.\nHe sees himself and others in their true form.\nVasudeva, the divine, is in all beings, in their inner selves.\nHaving attained the self through devotion to others, one is liberated from bondage. 45). Meaning of the word\n\nVasudeva-- to Vasudeva; Bhagwati-- Shri Bhagavan; Sarvajna- Sarvajnata; Pratyaksha-- in the self, stable within every being; Parmatma-- Supreme Soul; Parena-- divine; Bhakti-bhava-- with devotion; Labdha-Atma-- absorbed; Mukta-Bandhanah-- from worldly bondage.\nETL.\nThus, they were freed from the bondage of life and became absorbed in the divine service of Shri Bhagavan Vasudeva, the all-knowing Supreme Soul, residing within every individual. Meaning: When someone engages in divine devotion to God, they realize that they are\na constant servant of the Supreme Lord Vasudeva. Self-realization does not mean that God and\nindividual souls are equal in every way because they are both souls. Of the individual soul,\nthere is a possibility of being bound, but the supreme soul is never bound.\nWhen the bound soul\nrealizes that it is subject to the Supreme Soul, then this state of his is called Langhatya\nself-realization or liberation from bondage, that is, liberation from material impurities. Material\nImagination remains until he considers himself equal to God. This\nstate is the final web of Maya. Maya always affects the living being. If sufficient"
