          "textEn": "270\n\nOh Lord, you are the only means to get out of this dense darkness of ignorance,\nbecause you are my divine eye, which I have obtained after many births by your grace. Meaning: This verse is very instructive because it describes the relationship between a guru and a disciple.\nThe disciple or a bound soul is placed in this greatest realm of ignorance, as a result,\nhe faces the world of sensual pleasure. To attain freedom by breaking free from this bondage\nis extremely difficult, but if someone is so fortunate that he gets the company of a guru like Kapil Muni or\ntheir representative, then by their grace, he can be freed from the mud of ignorance. Therefore, the worship of the guru is done by the guru, who, from the light of knowledge, uplifts the disciple from the mud of ignorance. The word 'Pargam' is extremely important.\nThe boatman has come for him, who can take the disciple across. On this side is bound life.\nAnd on that side, (is) unbound life. The guru, through the knowledge of the guru, opens the eyes of the disciple and takes him across.\nHe goes. We all suffer because of ignorance. By the Guru's teachings, the darkness of ignorance\nis dispelled, and the disciple becomes capable of moving towards independence. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that\nA man takes refuge in Shri Bhagavan after many births. Similarly, if someone gets an authentic guru after many\nbirths, and he takes refuge in such an authentic\nrepresentative of Krishna, then he can attain the shore of light.\nYa Aadyo Bhagavan Pumsami Shvro Vai Bhavankele.\nLokasya Tamasandhasya Chakshuh Surya Ivuditah. 9>. Meaning of the word:\n\nYah--He; Aadya--First; Bhagavan--Lord; Pumsam--Of all living beings; Ishwarah--Lord; Vai--In reality; Bhavan--Yours; Kil--Indeed; Lokasya--Of the world; Tamasa--From the darkness of ignorance; Andhasya--Of the blind; Chakshushah--Of the eye\nEye; sun; like; similar; risen; sunrise..\nYou are Shri Bhagwan, the origin and supreme God of all living beings. You, to remove the darkness of ignorance from the universe, to expand the rays of the sun"
