          "textEn": "27]\n\nHave risen. Meaning: Kapil Muni is considered to be the incarnation of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, Krishna. Here,\nthe word 'Aadya' means, ** the origin of all living beings** and 'Gam Ishwarah' means 'the God of living beings'\n(Swami).\"Kapil Muni is the direct descendant of Krishna, who is the sun of spiritual knowledge. In the same way that the sun removes the darkness of the universe,\nwhen the light of God descends, it immediately dispels the darkness of Maya. We have eyes, but without the light of the sun,\nthe eyes have no importance. Similarly, without the light of God or without the divine grace of the Guru, he cannot see things in the same form.\nNow, O God, you are the one who is deluded by my own self.\nWhoever has believed in me as mine, in this very moment, you have joined him. 10>. Meaning of the word:\n\nAth--Now; Me--mine; Dev--Oh God; Sam-Moham--delusion, illusion; Apakrushtamu--to be destroyed; Tvam-you; Ah-I; Mam-mine; Iti-in this way; Iti-in this way;\nEtasmind-in this; Yojitah-attached; Tvaya-by you;\nPlease be pleased now and remove my great delusion. Due to ego, I remained busy in your\nillusion and I recognized myself as body form and as a result of physical\nrelationships. Meaning: The ego of self-intellect in your body and the claim to connect the things of your collection with this body is called Maya. In the fifteenth chapter of the Bhagavad Gita, the Lord says,\n\"I am present in everyone's heart, and the memory and forgetfulness of all is in me.\"\n\"\nDevahuti said that considering oneself as the body and attachment to physical objects is also\nunder the direction of God, so does this mean that God discriminates by putting one in devotion and\nthe other in sensual gratification? If that happens, then God will be from somewhere else, this\nwill be inconsistent, but in reality it is not so. As soon as a being forgets its true\nnatural servitude towards God and wants to enjoy through sega"
