          "textEn": "272\nis, then he is imprisoned by Maya. This bondage is a false identity with attachment to the body and physical\nobjects by Maya. These are the works of Maya, and since\nMaya is also an agent of God, therefore, indirectly, this is the work of God. God's peace be. If someone wants to forget them and enjoy the pleasures of this material world, then they get its\ncomplete freedom not directly, but through their material power (Maya). Because this physical power is the power of God, therefore, God is the one who provides the facility to obliterate directly. Therefore, Devahuti said, \"In the pleasure of Indra, my\ndistraction was because of you. Now, free me from this bondage.\"\nBy the grace of God, man is permitted to enjoy this material world, but\nwhen he becomes disheartened by being bored of material pleasures and when he sincerely surrenders at the feet of God,\nthen God, being merciful, frees him from bondage.\nTherefore, in the Bhagavad Gita, Shri Krishna says, \"First come into my refuge, then I will\ntake your responsibility and I will free you from the fruits of all sinful deeds.\"\" Sinful deeds\nare acts that we commit in a state of forgetting our relationship with God. In this world, the actions considered sacred for material pleasures are also sinful. For example, sometimes a person donates to a stormy person with the view that in return\nhe will get four times more money. Charity given for the purpose of gain is Rajasic charity. Here, whatever\naction is performed, it is done by being subject to the qualities of material nature, as a result,\napart from serving God, all actions are sinful.\nDue to sinful deeds, we remain fascinated by material attachments.\nI am this body.\"I think of the body as self and physical possessions\n'mine'. Devahuti prayed to Lord Kapil to free her from false identities and the bonds of false possessions."
