          "textEn": "277\nHe can say that he is not disturbed by happiness, but he does not know that after enjoying the so-called\nhappiness, sorrow will come. This is the law of the physical world. Lord Kapil says\nthat the yoga method is the science of the soul. Man practices yoga to achieve the completeness of spiritual position. It does not raise the question of physical pleasure or pain. This is divine. Ultimately, Lord Kapil will explain how this is divine, but here, an initial\nintroduction is given. I will now explain that which is said by Yama, the ancient one.\nFor the sake of the sages and those who listen, I will describe the perfection of all yoga. 14). Meaning of the word\n\nTam imam- that; te- to you; pravakshyami- I will tell; yam- who; avocham- I had told; pura- before;\nAnaghe- O venerable mother; Rishinam- to the sages; Shrotu- eager to listen; Yogam- Yoga method;\nSarva- all kinds of; Naipunam- useful and practical L\n\nOh most sacred mother, now I will explain to you that ancient yoga method, which I\nFirst, explain to the great sages. This is useful and practical in every way. Note: God does not create a new yoga method. Sometimes this claim\nis made that a certain person has become an incarnation of God and is establishing a new\nmoral aspect of the ultimate truth. But here we see that although Kapil Muni himself\nis God and is able to create new principles (arguments) for his mother, still\nhe says, \"I will explain that ancient yoga method which I once explained to the sages,\nbecause they were eager to hear about it.\"\"When we have the best method already available in our Vedic\nscriptures, then what is the need to create a new method and to mislead the people? 2 In today's era, rejecting the standard method\nand presenting a newly invented corrupt method in the name of yoga has become a fashion."
