          "textEn": "283\nLet's do it so that he can see the real eternal form of God within the divine light.\nUntil a man attains the divine form of God, there is no question of devotion. It is mandatory for devotional service that there should be a receiver of devotion,\nand a devotee who does devotion. The realisation of God is the culmination of devotion. The knowledge of the radiant rays of God's body is not the final stage of Brahm Siddhi. Neither\nThe vision of the Supreme Being, the form of the Supreme Soul, is complete, because God is the all-conscious divine\nSupreme Soul. He who realizes God, also sees other forms--such as the Supreme Being form and\nthe Brahman form--and complete realization is the attainment of Brahman.\nThose who know the secret of the snake, the self, and the enemy,\nThat alone is accomplished by the virtuous, and is not covered by the darkness of liberation. 20>. Meaning of the word:\n\nPrasankham- attachment; Ajaram- strong; Pasham-- bondage; Atmanah-- of the self; Kavayah-- learned men; Viduh-- knowers; Sahah- He; Sahah- He; Sadhushu-- in the devotees; Krutah- used; Moksha- door; Apavrutam- open..\n\nEvery learned person knows very well that worldly attachment is the biggest bondage of the soul. But if that same attachment is towards the self-realized devotees, then\nthe door to salvation opens. Meaning: Here it is clearly stated that attachment to an object is bondage.\nIn life, it is the cause of bondage, but if this same attachment is towards someone else,\nthe door to salvation opens. Attachment cannot be killed; it only needs to be\ntransferred. Attachment to physical objects is called physical consciousness, and attachment to Krishna or his devotee is called Krishnachetana (devotion, emotional liberation).\nTherefore, consciousness is the medium of attachment's\nexpression. Here, there is a clear mention that when we purify our physical consciousness\nand transform it into Krishna consciousness, we attain salvation. Despite 