          "textEn": "284\nIn the soul, there is a natural inclination to be attached to something or the other. We see\nthat if someone has no object of attachment, if they have no children, then they\ntransfer their attachment to dogs and cats. This indicates that\nthe inclination towards attachment cannot be stopped; it should be used for superior work. Our bondage continues because of our attachment to material objects, but\nif this attachment is directed towards God or his devotee, then it becomes the source of salvation\nand goes away. Here, the recommendation is given that attachment should be transferred to the self-realized devotees or saints.\nIt should be given. But who is a saint? A saint is not an ordinary person who wears saffron robes\nor keeps a long beard. In the Bhagavad Gita, it is said that a saint is one who, without\nhesitation, remains engaged in devotion.\nEven if he does not strictly follow the rules of devotion,\nbut if he has unwavering faith in the Supreme Personality of Godhead, then he is considered a saint. Sadhurev santvyah. Sadhu is a staunch follower of Bhakti. Here, it is recommended\nthat one who wants to realize Brahman or is desirous of spiritual perfection should\nattach themselves to a saint or devotee. This has also been affirmed by Bhagavan Chaitanya. Love is only with a saint.\nAll accomplishments can be attained through the momentary association of a saint. The word Mahatma is synonymous with saint. It is said that Mahatma is the secret to liberation through service.\nThe path is--Dwaramahurvimukteh. Great service is the doorway to liberation. Those who serve the great are served by the great. (Bhagwatam)\n5.5.2) Serving materialists has the opposite effect. If someone serves a person who is a materialist or engrossed in sensual pleasures, then by association with such a person,\nthe door to hell opens. This is the principle that has been confirmed here.\nAttachment towards devotees.\nAttachment towards the service of God, 