          "textEn": "288\nThose who are under the shelter of the divine, those who are absorbed in stories, listen and tell.\nThey are burning with various penances, not being absorbed in their minds. 23). Meaning of the word:\n\nMatt-ashrayah - about me; Kathah - stories; Mrustah - delightful; Shrunvanti - listen; Kathayanti - sing;\nCha - and; Tapanti - endure; Vividhah - various kinds of; Tapah - physical suffering; Na - not; Etan - them;\nMat-gat - attached to me; Chetasah - one's own thoughts..\n\nConstantly engaged in the chanting and listening of my, that is, the complete, supreme being, God,\nthe saints do not suffer any kind of physical hardship, because they are immersed in the thoughts of my pastimes and\nactivities. Meaning: In this world, various kinds of sufferings, physical and mental, are caused by other beings\nand are obtained from natural products. But a saint is not disturbed by such painful\nsituations, because his mind is always filled with the nectar of Krishna consciousness,\ntherefore, he does not want to discuss anything other than the activities of God.\nKing Ambarisha spoke nothing but described the divine plays of the Lord. Vachansi Vaikrishtagunanukarne ( Bhagavat 9.4.18) | They used their speech only for\nSinging the glory of Shri Bhagavan. The saints are always eager to listen about the activities of God or his devotees. Because they are filled with devotion to Krishna,\ntherefore, they are oblivious of material sufferings. Because of forgetting the activities of the ordinary bound soul, they are always full of worries and material sufferings. On the other hand,\nbecause the devotees are always engaged in the stories of God, therefore they forget the sufferings of the world\nand remain. Those who are virtuous, those who are free from all associations.\nWEE, those who pray, are the destroyers of sins. 24). Lexicon"
