          "textEn": "289\nThey are--they are; Sadhavi--devotees; Sadhvi--she; Sarva--all; Sang--with attachment; Vivarjita--free; Sadah--\nAttachment; Teshu--to them; Ath--therefore; Tete--by you; Prartha--should be searched; Sank-dosh--bad effects of material attachment\nOf; Hara--those who destroy; Hi--indeed; Tete--they..\nO Mother, O virtuous lady, these are the qualities of a great devotee, who is free from all attachments. You should associate with such holy men, because such association is the destroyer of all the bad influences of material attachment. Meaning: Here, Kapil Muni is advising his mother Devahuti that if she wants to be free from material attachment, then she should increase her attachment towards the saints, that is, towards all the devotees who are completely attached. Bhagavad Gita (15.5) says that\nWho is the authority to go to Bhagavad Gama? Nirmansoha jitasangdoshaah. This is a sign of that person\nwho is completely free from the pride of material possessions.\nEven if someone is very\nwealthy, prosperous, or prestigious, but if he wants to return to the spiritual-kingdom, that is,\nto his home, the abode of God, then he must give up the pride of his material opulence,\nbecause this is a false situation. Here, the word 'moh' (attachment) used indicates a false notion, indicating that someone is rich or\npoor. In this world, this concept that someone is extremely wealthy or poor, or\nin relation to material things, someone is false, because this body itself is false or REM ©.\nThe pure being who wants to be free from this material bondage must first be freed from the three qualities of nature\nthrough association. Currently, our consciousness, due to the coordination of the three qualities of nature,\nhas become polluted. Consequently, this very principle has been stated in the Bhagavad Gita. It is said--\nJitasankadhoanah- meaning, a human being should be free from the defect of association with the three qualities of nature.\nShould be.\nIn Shrimad Bhagwat also, this is confirmed here--A pure devotee who wants to bring himself to the abode of God,\nHe becomes free even from the contact of the three qualities of nature. We should find such\ncompany of devotees. For this reason, we have initiated the SIFT Krishna Bhawanamrit Sangha.\nWe have started it. To generate a specific type of education or consciousness (awakening) in human society"
