          "textEn": "295\nHow can I practice and develop myself so that I can immediately and easily receive the service of your lotus feet? Meaning: It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that no one can be prevented from serving God. Even if she is a woman or a worker or a merchant, if she keeps herself engaged in the devotion of God,\nthen she attains the supreme state and goes back to the abode of God. The determination of supreme devotion for various types of devotees is accomplished by the grace of the Guru. Yo yogo bhagavadgano nirvatanatmamswato yoditah.\nKidashah kati ATG yatastatvavabodhanam. 29). Meaning of the word:\n\nYah--He who; Yoga--Yoga method; Bhagavat-Baanah--Targeted to God; Nirvana--Self;\nTvaya--By you; Uditah--Said; Keedashah--What kind of; Kati--How much; Cha--And; Akhanni--Branches;\nYatah-From which; Tatva--Of truth; Avabodhanam--Knowledge;\nAs you have explained, the purpose of the yoga method is to attain the supreme being, the perfect Lord\nTo do or for the complete destruction of worldly existence (Maya), then please tell me\nthe nature of that yoga method. How many ways can that transcendental yoga be understood in its true form? Meaning: There are many types of yoga methods whose goal is to know the different states of the ultimate truth.\nis to know. The goal of Gnanayoga is the formless Brahmateja, and the goal of Hathayoga is the residing being\nGod, while the goal of Bhaktiyoga, which is accomplished through nine different methods such as listening, chanting, etc.,\nis the complete realization of God. There are also different ways of self-realization. But,\nDevahuti mentions the specialty of Bhakti Yoga, which God had already explained. The various limbs of Bhakti Yoga are--listening, chanting, remembering, bowing, worshiping, serving, obeying.\n(Dasya), making friends with them (Sakhya), and ultimately offering everything in the service of God.\n(Atma Nivedana). The word Nirvanaatman in this verse is of utmost importance. Bhakti vidhi"
