          "textEn": "307\nremains, such a pure devotee never wants to be one with me. Such a\ndevotee who remains steadfast and always praises my pastimes and activities,\npraises. Meaning: Five types of liberation are mentioned in the scriptures. One of these is to merge into the Supreme Soul by\nidentifying with God or renouncing one's own personality. It is called Ekatmata. Such a liberation is never accepted by a devotee. There are four other types of liberation--\nTo go to Vaikuntha, to associate with God, to attain the opulence of God, and to attain the form of God.\nAs Kapil Muni will tell, the devotee does not desire any of these five types of liberation.\nHe considers the thought of becoming one with God to be hellish and hates it.\nShri Prabodhananda Saraswati, the supreme devotee of Lord Chaitanya, has said -- \"Kaivalyam Narakayate\" meaning\nThe pleasure of being one with God, which the illusionists desire, is considered hellish.\nThis oneness is not for pure devotees. There are many so-called devotees who think that in a bound state we worship God,\nbut in the end, he is not a man. They say that since God is formless,\ntherefore, to carry out the work, we can give a concrete form to the formless God,\nbut as soon as one is liberated, worship ceases. This principle is held by the Mayavadi philosophy. In reality, the non-differentiated Supreme Being is not in the self, but in their physical light, the light of Brahman,\nthey are absorbed. Although this external light is not different from their body, but pure devotees do not accept this\nkind of oneness (identity), because devotees want to be absorbed in greater bliss than the so-called joy of being one with God.\nThe greatest joy\nIs to serve God. Devotees constantly think about how to serve God.\nHow can one go? Even with the biggest obstacles in the world, they keep gathering such resources\nSo that God can be served."
