          "textEn": "303\nSrimad Bhagavatam and other Puranas mention them. The Mayavadi philosophers denounce them by telling stories,\nbut in reality, these are great and venerable subjects, and are delicious to the devotees. This is the only difference between a Mayavadi and a devotee. They behold me with their eyes, filled with delight.\nWith their faces serene, with beautiful eyes.\nWith their forms divine, with their boons,\nThey speak with a voice that is pleasing to hear. 35). Meaning of the word\n\nThey see; they are; mine; beautiful; mother; saints; cheerful;\nFace-face-face; Arun-like the morning sun; eyes; forms-forms-divine-divine; giver-\ngiver-giver; with me; word-word; desirable-desirable; they say L\nO mother, my devotees always observe the radiant form of my cheerful\nface-face-face-face-face. They see my various divine friendly forms\nWant to see and also want to have a favorable conversation with me.\n\nMeaning: Mayavadi and atheistic people consider the forms of their Shrivighras kept in the temple of God as idols, but devotees do not worship idols. They worship God\ndirectly as an incarnation of the Arva. From Archana, one gets the sense of that form, which\nwe can worship in the present circumstances. In fact, in the present state, it is not possible to see God in their\nspiritual form, because our eyes and senses cannot imagine the spiritual form.\nTo the extent that we cannot even see the spiritual form of the soul,\nwe cannot see it. When a human dies, we cannot see how the spiritual form leaves the body.\nHow does it renounce the body? It is the fault of our senses. For the sake of being able to see with our senses,\nGod takes on a suitable form, which is called Arva-Vigraha. Sometimes Arca-Vigraha\nis called Arca-Avatar, which is not different from God.\nJust as the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead\ntakes many incarnations, in the same way, He accepts the forms of substances like soil, wood, metal, and gems.\nHe accepts."
