          "textEn": "305\nTa- from those forms; Darshaniya- worth seeing; Avayavi- with limbs; Udara- generous; Vilasa- plays; Haas- laugh;\nMuskara; Chitvan- to contemplate; Vaama- charming; Sukta- with pleasing words; Hata- deluded; Atmanah- the self; Hata-\nDeluded; Prana- senses; Cha- and; Bhakti- devotion; Ufa- unwillingly; Anichita- not wishing; Me- mine; Gatimu- abode;\nAnvim- subtle; TIF- attained..\n\nSeeing the smiling and attractive form of God, and hearing his very enchanting\nwords, the pure devotee loses all his other consciousness. His senses\nbecome free from all other functions and become absorbed in devotion. Thus, unwillingly,\nhe spontaneously becomes HUTS. Note: There are three classes of devotees--the superior, the middle, and the inferior. Devotees up to the lowest class\nbecome liberated. This verse states that even without knowledge, by seeing the decoration of the idol in the temple, the devotee, absorbed in its meditation, loses all other consciousness.\nIn this way, by stabilizing oneself in Krishna consciousness and engaging the senses in the service of God,\nman unknowingly becomes liberated. This is also confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita. Only\nby performing unmixed devotion approved by the Shakhas, a man becomes equal to Brahma. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita:\nBrahmabhooyaya Kalpate. This means that the soul is Brahman in its original state,\nbecause it is a part of the Supreme Brahman. But by forgetting this true nature of oneself, that one is an eternal servant of God, one becomes deluded by Maya. The forgetfulness of one's true natural\nstate is Maya. Otherwise, it is eternally Brahman. When a person is taught to be aware of their situation, then understanding\nseems that he is a servant of God.\n'Brahma' is the sign of the state of self-realization. Here,\neven the lowest-ranking devotee who does not have the knowledge of the ultimate truth and who only\ndevoutly bows to God, contemplates on him, sees him in the temple,\nand brings flowers and fruits to offer in the idol, he too, unknowingly, becomes liberated. Devotees: That is, with utmost devotion, the devotees respect the idol and\noffer materials. The idols of Radha-Krishna, Lakshmi-Narayana and Sita-Rama for the devotees"
