          "textEn": "337\nThis group or the main womb is described as Mahadrahya; it is the source of birth and\nnurturing of all living beings. The five great elements are the earth, water, fire, air, and space.\nTheir subtle elements are taste, smell, touch, and sound. 12. Meaning of the word:\nMaha-bhutani-- gross elements; Pancha-- five; Eva-- exactly; Bhoo- earth; Apah- water; Agnih-- fire; Marut--\nVayu; TH:— sky; Tat-matrani-- subtle elements; Cha- thus; Tavanti- in this manner; Gandha-adini-- fragrance etc.\n(Taste, color, touch, and sound); Mata- are considered; Me- by me.\nThe names of the five gross elements are earth, water, fire, air, and space (zero). The subtle elements are also five--Gandha (smell), Swadha (taste), Ranga (colour), Spashta (touch) and Shabda (sound) 8 Shabda).\nIndriyani dasha, Shrotam, Tvagadagrasana, Nasika.\nVakkarau, Charanau, Medam, Payudasam, Dasham, Uchyate 23.\nShabdartham.\nIndriyani--Indriyas; Dasha--Dashah; Shrotam--Shrotendriya; Tvak--Sits; Haku--Drishti Indriya; Rasan--Swadhishtha;\nIndriya; Nasikah--Gandha Indriya; Vak--Vaani Indriya; Karau--Two Hands; Charanau--Walking Indriya (Feet);\nMedam--Reproductive organ; Payudasam--Drishti Indriya; Dasham--Dasham; Uchyate--Is called..\nThe number of sensory organs and motor organs combined is ten. These are--the auditory sense,\nthe gustatory sense, the tactile sense, the visual sense, the olfactory sense, the motor sense, the senses of action, the locomotor, reproductive, and excretory senses.\nMind, intellect, and consciousness, all are interconnected.\nIt is divided into four parts: in terms of distinctions, in terms of characteristics. 14>. Shabdartham (Meaning of word)\nManah (Mind)-- Mind; Buddhih (Intellect)-- Intellect; Ahankarah (Ego)-- Ego; Chittam (Consciousness)-- Consciousness; Iti (Thus)-- In this way; Antarah (Inner)-- Internal;\nSubtle senses; Chatuh-dha (Four types)-- Four types; Lakshyate (Are seen)-- Seen; Bhedah (Difference)-- Difference; Vrittya (By actions)