          "textEn": "338\n\nMeaning: Four internal or subtle fa, which are described here, are defined by their various\ncharacteristics. When pure consciousness becomes contaminated by physical impurities and\nthe body-consciousness becomes dominant, it is said that a person is subjugated by ego. Consciousness is the soul's\naction, therefore the soul remains behind consciousness. Consciousness contaminated by physical impurities, ego\nis called. Therefore, the number of Brahmins is countless.\nI have described the assembly, which is the twenty-five times of time. 95 Meaning of the word\n\nEtawan--so much; Eva--this; Sankhyaath--counted; Brahmanah--of Brahma; Sa-gunasya--endowed with physical qualities;\nHa-Nisanshadha; Sannivesha--arrangement; Maya- by me; Proktah- said; Yah-who; Kaalah-time; Pancha-\nVimshakah-twenty-fifth.. The element that combines all of these is time,\nwhich is counted as the twenty-fifth element.\nMeaning: According to the Vedic statement, there is no existence beyond Brahman-- Sarva khalvidam Brahma (Chandogya Upanishad 3.14.1). The Vishnu Purana also states that whatever we see\nThat is the power of the Supreme Brahman:--Every object is the power of the expansion of the Supreme Brahman. When Brahma\nis mixed with the qualities of Sato, Rajo, and Tamo, then there is physical expansion, which\nsometimes is called Sagun Brahma, in which these twenty-five elements reside. In the formless Brahman, there is no physical\nimpurity, or in the spiritual world (Vaikuntha), the three qualities of Sattva, Rajo, and Tamo--these three qualities\ndo not remain. Where the formless Brahman is present, the pure Sattva is found. According to Sankhya philosophy,\nin Saguna Brahma, twenty-five elements are included, in which time (past, present, and future) is also\nthere. The effect of pride is known to the one who knows time. The one who is deluded by ego, the nature of the doer is revealed. 96. Lexicon"
