          "textEn": "365\nThose who know the meaning of the special qualities of the Yoga, know its touch. 47). Shabdarman\nNabha-guna visheshah-- the specific quality of the sky (sound); arthah-- subject; yasya- whose; tat- that; shrotram- of the ear;\nShravanendriya; uchyate- is called; vayo-guna visheshah- the specific quality of the air (sound); arthah- subject; yasya- whose; tat- that; sparshanam- the sense of touch (skin); viduh- know;.\nThat sense whose object is the word, the auditory sense, and whose object is touch, that\nis called the skin sense. Meaning: The word is one of the qualities of sky and its subject is hearing. Similarly,\nTouch is a quality of air, and its subject is the sensation of touch.\nHe whose eyes are called the eye of sharpness,\nHe whose taste is called the taste of ambhoguna (the quality of enjoyment).\nHe whose nose is called the nose,\nHe whose land is called the land of ghaṇa (the quality of smell). 48>. Shabdartham\nTejah-guna-visheshah-- the special quality of fire (form); Arthah-- subject; Yasya-whose; Tat-that; Chakshuh-eye,\neye; Uchyate-is said; Abhbhah-guna-visheshah-- the special quality of water (taste); Arthah-subject; Yasya-whose; Tat-that; Rasanam-the sense of taste, the sense of taste, the tongue; Viduh-is known; Bhumih-guna-visheshah-the special quality of land (smell); Arthah-subject; Yasya-whose; Sah-that; Pranah-the sense of smell; Uchyate-is said..\nThat sense whose object is a special quality of fire, that is fsa. The sense whose object is the special taste of water is called the rasendriya (taste organ). The sense whose object is the unique quality of the earth, that is called the olfactory sense.\nDharma is seen in the connection of the other.\nTherefore, the special emotions are seen in the greatness. 49). Meaning of the word:\nOf another--of the cause; Hashyate--is seen; Dharmah--quality; Hi--indeed; Aparasmin--in the work; Samanvayat--from coordination;\nFrom coordination or arrangement; Atah--therefore; V