          "textEn": "366\nMeaning: The word is the cause of the sky, the sky is of air, air is of fire, fire is of water, and\nwater is the cause of the earth. In the sky, there is only sound; in the air, sound and touch; in fire, sound, touch, and form; in water, sound, touch, form, and taste; and in the earth, sound, touch, form,\ntaste, and smell also remain. Consequently, the earth is the abode of all the qualities of other elements. Earth\nis the essence of all elements. In the earth, all five qualities of elements are found; in water, four; in fire, three; in air, two; and in the sky, only one quality -word-- is found.\nWhen these are not present, then the great and the seven are not found. The one who is endowed with the quality of time, has come to the world. 50>. Meaning of words\n\nThese; unthinkable; together; when; great; etc.; great element, ego, and five gross elements; seven;\nTogether, seven; in reality; time; action; qualities and of the three qualities; together;\nWorld-origin; creation; entered.\n.\n\nWhen all these elements were not combined, then the original cause of creation, Shri Bhagavan, along with time, action,\nand qualities, along with his entire physical power (Mahat Tattva) consisting of seven divisions,\nentered into the universe. Meaning: After mentioning the origin of the causes, Kapildev is saying about the origin of the work. When all the reasons were not combined, then the complete Supreme Personality of Godhead, in his\nGarbhodakshayi Vishnu form, entered within each universe. Along with them, there were seven\nbasic elements--five physical elements, the total power (mahatattva), and ego--also present. This entry of Shri Bhagwan is in the atoms of the physical world. This is confirmed by the Brahma-\nSamhita (5.35)--Andantarastha-parasanuththa-chayantarastam. They are not only within the universe,\nbut also within the atoms. They are within the heart of every living being. The one who holds the womb.\nLord Vishnu has entered int