          "textEn": "43\nAnd wants to open a school. This is all delusion (maya), because from such material activities,\nhe cannot benefit anyone. If he wants to benefit his fellow believers,\nhe should awaken his dormant Krishna consciousness. The state of being endowed with Krishna consciousness, the state of being enlightened,\nis the state, which means pure consciousness. And the nature of the known truth is in the mind.\nHe who is united does not perform any action for the sake of the self. 26). Meaning of the word\n\nEvam--in this way; Vidit-tatvasya--of the knower of the ultimate truth; Prakriti--nature; Mayi--on me; Manasam--to the mind; Yunjitah--by stabilizing; Na- not; Apakurute--can cause loss; Atma-aarambhasya--in the self, bliss\nTo the one who brings; Krichit--never. The influence of nature cannot harm any enlightened person, even if he\nis busy in physical activities, because he knows the ultimate truth, the truth\nand his mind remains stable in God.\nMeaning: Lord Kapila says that the devotee whose mind always remains fixed on the lotus feet of the Lord,\nis called Atmarama or Vitat-Tatva. The meaning of Atmarama is, one who *“' rejoices in himself '' or “who enjoys in the spiritual environment”\n.\"From a physical point of view, the meaning of 'Atma' is body or mind, but here it is for such a person\nwho whose mind remains steady in the lotus feet of God, he is Atyaram,\nwhose meaning is \"who remains engaged in spiritual activities in the context of the Supreme Being.\"\nThe Supreme Being is God, and the individual soul is the living being. When they mutually exchange service and blessings,\nthe soul is said to be in the state of Atmarama. Any person who\nknows the truth in its true form can attain the state of SERA. The truth is that God is the enjoyer, and all beings are instruments of His service and enjoyment.\nHe who knows this truth\nand tries to put all his resources into the service of God, he all\nescapes from the fruits of material actions and the effects of the qualities of nature."
