          "textEn": "49\nChapter Adusa\nFor the practice of devotion, Kapila's order\nShri Bhagavan said\nI will tell the characteristics of yoga to the king's son. By the mind, by the right means, one goes to the path of truth. 1. Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Bhagavan said-- God said; Yogasya- of the yoga method; Lakshanam- description; Vakshye- I will tell; Sabijasya-\nAuthentic; Nrip-self-born-- O princess; Manah- mind; Yena- by which; Eva- certainly; Vidhina- by practice;\nPrasannam- pleased; Yati- attains; Sat- patham- the path of ultimate truth \\.\n\nGod said: O mother, O princess, now I will tell you the method of yoga\nwhose purpose is to concentrate the mind. By practicing this method, a person, being happy,\nmoves towards the path of the ultimate truth.\n\nMeaning: In this chapter, the yoga method told by Lord Kapildev is authentic and\nideal, therefore these commands should be followed with utmost care.\nFirst of all,\nGod says that through the practice of yoga, a man can progress towards understanding the ultimate truth, that is, the supreme being, God.\nHey. In the previous chapter, it has been clearly stated that the desired goal of yoga is not to attain any astonishing yogic power. A person should not be attracted to such yogic power, but rather, one should gradually attain the realization of the path to understanding God. This is also confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita, in which in the last verse of the sixth chapter,\nit is said that the greatest Yogi is one who constantly thinks about Krishna in his inner self,\nor who is full of Krishna consciousness. It is mentioned here that by following the method of yoga, a person can remain cheerful. Lord Kapil, who is a great authority on yoga, here presents a description of the yoga method,\nwhich is called Ashtanga-Yoga, which includes eight different practices. These are-- Yama, Niyama,\nAsana, Pranayama, Pratyahara, Dharana, Dhyana, and Samadhi.\nFrom all these stages of practice,\na person has to realize Lord Vishnu, which is the goal of all yoga. Such"
