          "textEn": "420\nThere are so-called yoga methods in which the mind is to be focused on the void or the formless,\nbut in authentic yoga practice, this is not recognized, as Kapildev explains. Even Patanjali states that the goal of all yoga is Vishnu. Therefore, Ashtanga Yoga\nis a part of the Vaishnava method, because its ultimate goal is the realization of Vishnu. The success of yoga\nis not in attaining the power of yoga, which has been condemned in the previous chapter,\nbut is to be free from all titles and the circumstances of natural state. Of yoga practice,\nThis is the ultimate achievement.\nFollowing one's own duty and abandoning one's own duty due to the power of dharma.\nBeing content with what is obtained by divine grace, one should contemplate the self. 2>. Meaning of the word:\n\nSwa-dharma-acharanam--Acting according to one's duty; Shaktya--By one's own power; Vidharmat--Duty against the scriptures;\nCha--And; Nivartanam--Avoiding; Daivat--By God's grace; Labdhen--From what is obtained; Santhosha--Satisfaction;\nSvaa-vit-Swaroop-Siddha--Of a self-realized being; Charan--Of the feet; Archanam--Worship. A person should perform their duties to the best of their ability and avoid doing those actions\nthat they are not supposed to do. One should be content with whatever one receives through the grace of God,\nand one should worship the lotus feet of the Guru. Meaning: In this verse, there are many important words that can be explained in detail,\nbut we will only explain some of the important aspects of each. The final statement is\nAtmavicharvranaarnivinim.\nThe meaning of Atyavit is a self-realized being or a genuine TE. Until\na person does not remain self-realized and does not know his relationship with God, he\ncannot become a pious guru. Here, this recommendation has gone that by searching for an authentic guru,\none should go to his refuge (Archanam), because by inquiring from him and worshiping him,\none can learn spiritual tasks, O.\n\nThe first recommendation is WHER) Until we have taken this body,\nfor us, some actions have gone to recommendation, O. Such actions are categorized into four social classes"
