          "textEn": "457\nIt is applied in action, but in divine state, these material qualities do not disturb the mind of the devotee.\nThey are not found. A devotee has no worries except for the desires of God. This is the ultimate state of perfection, which is called Nirvana or Nirvana Mukti. In this state, the mind\nbecomes completely free from material desires. Yathaarchih. Archi: Archi means flame, flame. When the lamp breaks or the oil runs out, then\nthe flame of the lamp goes out. But according to scientific knowledge, the flame does not go out, it remains preserved. This is the preservation of power. Similarly, when the mind stops functioning at the physical level,\nit remains protected in the actions of God. Here, the explanation of the imagination of the obstruction of the karma of the minds of the Mayavadi thinkers has been given. The meaning of mental function being obstructed is\nthe blocking of actions caused by the influence of the three qualities of nature.\nEven with the ultimate mind, by the cessation of the mind,\nIn that, the happiness and sorrow are situated.\nEven without the cause, what is the sorrow of the doer?\nThe self-determined, the self-existent, the end of the self. 36). Meaning of the word\n\nSah-- Yogi; Api-- in addition to this; Etaya-- from this; Charamaya-- the ultimate; Manasah-- of the mind; Nivrittiya- by stopping (the end) of the karmic result; Tasmin- in that; Mahimni- the ultimate glory; Avasitah- established; Sukha-dukha-bahaye- with happiness and sorrow; Bahyah- outside; Hetutvam- the cause; Api- without doubt; Asti- the fruit of ignorance; Kartari- in the ego; Dukhayo- of sorrow; Yat- that; Swa-self; Vidhatta- is indicated; Avasthit- existing; Par-other; Atma- of the self; Kashah- the supreme truth \\. Thus, the mind, situated in the highest divine state, being free from all the fruits of action,\nbecomes established in its own glory, O, which is beyond all material knowledge of happiness and sorrow. At that time, the 