          "textEn": "460\nThe activity considers the situation. Note: the following questions may be raised. As long as the free soul remains in contact with the body,\nwhy don't the physical functions affect it? Does he not become tainted by the actions and fruits of physical activities? In response to such questions, it is said in this verse\nthat God takes upon himself the burden of the physical body of the liberated soul. This organism\ndoes not function due to the life force; it functions as a reaction (result) of past deeds. An electric fan, even after being turned off, keeps spinning for some time.\nIt keeps spinning. This motion is not due to electric current, but is in the continuity of past motion;\nSimilarly, although a free being appears to act like a normal person, his\nactions must be considered in the continuity of past actions.\nIn a dream, a person can see himself expanded in many bodies,\nbut upon waking, he can understand that all these bodies were false. Similarly, although the body of a liberated being has secondary fruits--such as children, wife, home, etc.,\nhe does not recognize these physical expansions himself. He knows that these\nare all the products of material dreams. The gross body is made up of gross elements, and the subtle body\nmind, intellect, It is made of ego and impure consciousness. If a man considers the subtle body of dreams\nto be false and does not identify himself with that body, then certainly an enlightened\nperson should not identify himself even with the subtle body. Just as an enlightened\nperson sees in a dream that he has no connection with the functions of the body, similarly, the liberated soul\nhas no connection with the functions of the present body. In other words, since he is aware of his\nnatural state, therefore he never accepts the body-consciousness.\nAs a son, as wealth, as a mortal, it appears. The self-realized, the unborn, the embodied, the supreme. 39). Shabdharam"
