          "textEn": "473\noff | God is always merciful to the sinners of this world, therefore, to save them,\nHe either incarnates Himself or sends His faithful servants. Because they\nare constantly kind to them, therefore if any of their devotees is also compassionate towards all of them,\nit rises, then they are very pleased with the devotees. It is clearly stated in the Bhagavad Gita that those who\ntry to uplift the fallen souls by giving the conclusion of the Bhagavad Gita, that you should fully surrender to God,\nthey are very dear to God. Therefore, when God\nsaw that his mother is very merciful towards fallen souls, then he became pleased, and he became\nextremely merciful towards them. Shri Bhagavan said:\nDevotion is of many kinds, and is considered precious.\nThrough the path of one's own nature, the feelings of men are diverse. 7/. Meaning of the word:\n\nShri-Bhagavan said-- Bhagavan replied; Bhakti-Yoga-- Bhakti; Bahu-vidha-- of many kinds; Margaish-- by paths;\nBhamini-- O best of women; Bhavyate-- is manifested; Swabhavah-- nature; Guna-gunaah-- qualities; Margena-- according to the path; Pumsam-- of men;\nSadhakas-- of seekers; Bhavah-- is manifested; Vibhidyate-- is divided..\n\nLord Kapil replied: O beautiful one, according to the various qualities of a seeker,\nthere are many paths of devotion.\n\nMeaning: Being absorbed in Krishna consciousness, pure devotion is only one, because in pure devotion, the devotee\ndoes not ask God to fulfill any request. But generally people do devotion with this\npurpose. As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, those who are not pure, they worship with four\ntypes of purposes. Someone, suffering from physical circumstances,\nbecomes a devotee of God and goes to God to remove his suffering.\nThe person who lacks wealth, they reach God and plead to improve their financial situation. Other people who have no suffering or need financial assistance,\nthey live in search of knowledge to know the ultimate truth. They also"
