          "textEn": "479\nThey do not understand the one who is near, the one who is similar, and the one who is one with the self.\nThey do not understand what is given without my service. 13). Shabdartham\n\nSaalokya-- residing in the same world; Saati-- having equal opulence; SaamiPya-- being close; Saaroopya-- having the same\nPhysical form; Ekatvam- identification; Api-- also; Ut-- up to; Diyamanam- being given; Na-- not; Grihantanti- accepting; Vina- without; Mat- mine; Sevanam- devotion; Janaah- pure devotee\n\nPure devotees do not accept any kind of salokya, saashta, saamiPya, or ekatva\nMoksha, even if it is being given by God. Meaning: Lord Chaitanya teaches us how to do devotion to God with spontaneous\nlove. In the Ashtakam, he prays to God as Lord CT! I\nI do not want any property from you, nor do I want a beautiful wife, nor many followers.\nI want.\nI only want this much from you that, throughout my life, I remain a pure devotee of your lotus feet.\nI will remain.\"There is similarity in the hymns of Lord Chaitanya and the statements of Shrimad Bhagavatam. Chaitanya\nMahaprabhu prays ' ' birth-after-birth ' ' which indicates that a pure devotee does not want birth and\ndeath to end. Yogis and voluntary philosophers want to end the process of birth and death, but a pure devotee wants to remain in this material world and do devotion. Here is a clear mention that a pure devotee does not desire oneness with God.\nAs the non-essentialist, the mind-controlled, and the meditator keep desiring. ©. Being one with God\ndoes not occur to a pure devotee even in a dream. Sometimes, with the intention of serving God,\nhe accepts going to Vaikuntha, but he does not even bring the thought of being absorbed in external radiance in his mind,\nbecause he considers it even worse than hell.\nSuch oneness, that is,\nTo be absorbed in the divine light is called 'acy', but the happiness attained from liberation is for the pure devotee\nNarakay hey. A devotee is so eager to serve God that he does not care about the five types of salvation. If someone is engaged in pure love devotion to God,\nthen it is believed that he has already attained the five types of salvation."
