          "textEn": "497\nAn order has been given, those who are only engaged in their assigned work. People of different castes, such as--\nBrahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaishyas, and Shudra caste people, and different ashrams, such as Brahmacharya, Grihastha,\nVanaprastha, and Sanyas, have some specific duties. A person should worship the idol of God until he\nstarts experiencing the presence of God in every living being. In other words, that man should be content in fulfilling his duties correctly. He should experience the relationship between himself and other beings with God. If he does not understand this much, then it should be understood that even if he\nis managing his work properly, but he is doing labor in vain. The word swa-karma-krit in this verse is of utmost importance. Self-action means such a\nperson who completes his assigned tasks.\nIt is not that one who becomes a devotee of God,\nor who worships, should stop their prescribed duties. No one should become lazy under the pretext of devotion. He must perform the prescribed rites of devotion according to the prescribed actions. Self-action-\nKritt says that a person should do their assigned work without negligence. Atmanashcha parasyapi yah karotyantarodaram. His different end, death, knows fear, the unbreakable. RE II\n\nMeaning of the word\n\nAtmanah--of the self, one's own; cha--and; parasya--of another; api--also; yah--whoever; karoti--keeps discrimination;\nIn between the inner and outer; Udaram--of the body; Tasya--of that; Bhinna-dashah--difference show; Mrityu--in the form of death; Vidadhe\nI create; Bhayam-fear; Ulbanam-great..\n\nWhoever, due to differences in perspective between themselves and other beings, even slightly\ndiscriminates, for them, I create a great fear like the blazing fire of death.\nMeaning: There are many physical differences among all kinds of living beings, but a devotee\nshould not discriminate between one living being and another on this basis. The perspective of a devotee 