          "textEn": "509\nIt goes. Here is the confirmation of this-- Purusha: Purusham Brajet--By understanding the divine nature of God and His\nactivities, the living being comes to God. The formless, divine, and time-defying is what is called. Among the great and the lesser, there is a difference. 37). Meaning of the word.\n\nForm-difference--of the changes of forms; Aapadhānam--cause:; Divyam--divine; Kālah--time, period; Iti--thus;\nAbhidhīyate--known; Bhutānam--of living beings; Māhān--of greatness; Aadinam--of the beginning; Yatah--from whom; Bhitna-dasham--from which;\nFrom a different perspective; Bhayam-fear; Ur..\n\nThe time that creates various physical transformations is another form of God.\nThe person who does not know that time and God are one and the same, remains\nfrightened by time. Meaning: Everyone is afraid of the activities of time, but one who knows that\ntime is another form of God, is not afraid of the influence of time at all. The form is uniquely important.  The influence of time, I don't know how many forms change.\nFor example, when a child is born, its form is small, but over time, that same\nform changes into a large form - first in the body of a child, and then in the body of a young man.\nIt changes. Similarly, every object changes by time or by God's indirect control.\nIt keeps changing. Generally, we do not see a difference in the body of an infant, a child, or a young man,\nbecause we know that this is the effect of time. The person who does not know\nthat how time acts, for him time is the cause of fear. Entering into the inner self, the beings, the beings are the supreme refuge.\nThat Vishnu, the supreme sacrifice, that time, the Lord, is dissolving the ages. 38. Meaning of the word:\n\nYah- who; Antah- inside; Pravishya- entering; Bhutani- to the living beings; Bhuta- by the living beings; Ati- destroyer;\nAkhila- of all; Ashrayah- support; Sah- he; Vishnu- Vishnu; Aakhyah- named; Adhiyajna- the enjoyer of all sacrifices; Asa