          "textEn": "52]\n\nEven though he is always burning with worry, such a fool never fulfills\nhopes, he does all kinds of evil deeds, so that he can support his so-called\nfamily and society. Meaning: It is said that in today's time, when Kali Yuga is so strong that every\nperson, accepting the false offerings of the family of Maya, remains full of worries. In such a situation, running a\ngreat empire is not as difficult as running a small family. Our family is Maya-generated, it is a distorted reflection of the family of Krishna. In Krishna's world, there are family, friends, society, father, mother, everything, but they are eternal. Here, as our bodies\nchange, our family relationships change. Sometimes we are in the family of humans,\nthen sometimes in the family of gods, and sometimes in the family of dogs and cats. Family, society,\nand friendship are momentary, therefore they are called false.\nIt is said that as long as we remain bound by this\nfalse, transient, temporary society and family, we remain surrounded by worries.\nThe materialists do not know that in this world, family, society, and friendship are merely shadows\nand they get attached to them. It is natural that their hearts always burn, but\neven after all the inconveniences, they work to maintain such false families,\nbecause they have no idea of real family association with Krishna. Aashakṣiptatmendriyas: of women and men, both, and also of those who are not. May they live in the created world, for the sake of the children. 8>. Meaning of the word:\n\nAbsorbed- enchanted; self-hearted- senses; senses; of women- women; untrue- false; and also;\nBy me- by me; in solitude- in a secluded place; created- displayed; conversation- from conversation; of children- of children;\nWith sweet- with sweet words..\n\nHe gives his heart and senses to that woman, who falsely enchants him with illusion.\nHe comes into solitude with her, caresses and converses, and remains captivated by the sweet-sweet words of his little\nlittle children."
