          "textEn": "549\nThey are, therefore, the child and the worm are really brothers. We are eager to establish brotherhood among humans,\nbut we should consider even insects as our brothers, other creatures, then\nthe matter is different. Therefore, we should be concerned about all living beings. Nathaman Rishirbhit: Saptavadhih Kritanjalih. He who is praised, is offered speech by the one who is disturbed. 11. Meaning of the word\n\nNathmanah-- one who begs; Rishi-- a sage; Bhitah-- one who is afraid; Saptavadhih-- one bound by seven coverings; Krita--\nAnjalih-- hands folded in prayer; Stuvit prayers; Tam-- to God; Viklavaya-- in distress; Vacha-- by words;\nYena-- by which; Udare-- in the womb; Arpitah-- one who is offered; em.\n\nIn this frightened state, the soul, bound by seven coverings of physical organs, hands\nfolded in prayer, begs God, who has brought it to this state.\nMeaning: It is said that when a woman has to go through labor pains, she takes a vow\nthat she will not conceive again and will not suffer such pain again. Similarly, when someone has an operation in the hospital, the patient takes a vow that now she\nwill not do such a thing that makes her sick and she has to undergo an operation again. Or when\na person is in trouble, then he pledges that he will not make such a mistake again\nthat would lead to a crisis. Similarly, when a being attains a hellish state, he prays to God\nthat he will not commit sinful deeds again, so that he does not go into the mother's womb and fall into the cycle of birth and death. Inside the womb, the being is frightened by being reborn in a hellish state.\nBut when he comes out of the womb, when he becomes fully young and healthy, he forgets everything and repeatedly commits the same sins for which he was kept in this\nterrible situation.\nJanatruvacha\nTasyaopasannamavitum jagadichchayaatt-\nNanatanorbhuvi chalacharanarvindam."
