          "textEn": "556\nWants to be satisfied or who wants to claim authority over nature, God provides him the opportunity of forgetting his service\nand the so-called happiness of material activities. In this way, when someone becomes frustrated in trying to control this nature and wants to be free from worldly bondage,\nthen God gives them this knowledge from within that they should seek refuge in Him, only then\nwill they be liberated. This knowledge can be given only by God or his representative. In Bhagavan Chaitanya Chaitanya Charitamrita, Rupa Goswami is advised that the soul wanders through births and rebirths\nand continues to suffer the hardships of the world. But when someone is very eager to be freed from worldly bondage,\nthey receive light from the Guru and Krishna. This means that Krishna, as the Supreme Being, is situated in the heart of every living being, and when a being is truly\ncurious, He commands them to take refuge in their representative, authentic guru.\nHe does.\nBy being guided from within by the Guru and by showing the path from outside, a person attains the path of devotion to Krishna,\nwhich is the path to be freed from worldly bondage. Therefore, until one receives God's blessings, one cannot be situated in one's true position. Until he receives light through supreme knowledge, he has to endure hard torments for life's struggle in this\nworld. Therefore, the grace of the supreme being, the Guru,\nbecomes manifest. Bound souls have to receive direct orders from the Guru, and in this way,\ngradually they begin to progress on the path of devotion to Krishna. The seed of devotion to Krishna is sown in the heart of the bound soul,\nand when a person listens to the Guru's teachings, this seed bears fruit,\nand life becomes blessed. Having digested the body, the fire of the stomach,\nWithout urine and feces, the body is burnt and heated.\nHaving desired to be seen, counting my meals"
