          "textEn": "558\nFor doing. He uses that intellect for the benefit of the public, to preach devotion to Krishna,\ntherefore he is generous. He who is in this state, the tenth lord,\nIs seized by the sun, by the wind, and by the rain.\nHe alone is pleased by his own actions, O Lord of the humble.\nWhat name will he do without, without sin? 18. Meaning of the word\n\nYen--by whom (by God); Edashim--such; Gatim--state; Asau--that person (I); Dash-masyah--of ten months;\nDash-mas'ah--of ten months; Ish--O Lord; Sangrahitah--being accepted; Puru-dayen--Extremely merciful; Bhavah-shen--\nUnparalleled; Svan-own; Ev-alone; Tushyatu- may he be pleased; Kriten-by one's action; Sah-him; Of the poor;\nWith folded hands; Asya-of God; Kuryat-can; Karyat-can be done..\n\nOh God, by the grace of your well-wishers, I have gained consciousness, although I am only ten\nmonths old.\nGratitude for this unintentional grace of God, a friend to sinners,\nWhat else do I have besides joining my hands and praying to express it? Meaning: As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, that situated within the body with the soul,\nthe Supreme Soul is the giver of intellect and forgetfulness. When God sees that the bound soul is eager to be freed from the bonds of Maya,\nHe bestows wisdom from within as the Supreme Being and from outside in the form of a guru,\nor takes the incarnation of God himself and gives sermons, such as the Bhagavad Gita. God always keeps looking for such an opportunity that the fallen souls are taken to the abode of God.\nTake. We should be fadagh with God because they want to make us happy forever.\nWe do not have enough resources to repay God for his goodness,\nTherefore, we can only experience gratitude and pray to him with folded hands\nWe can. Some atheists may express doubt about this prayer for the unborn child\nthat how can the child make such a beautiful prayer in his mother's womb? But by the grace of God, everything is possible. Outwardly, the child is kept in such a terrible condition,\nBut internally, he is the same, and God is there. By the divine power of God, everything"
