          "textEn": "560\nThe meaning of the word 'Dam-Shariari' is that we have such a body, in which we can control the senses and the mind. All the complexity of physical life is from uncontrolled mind and uncontrolled\nsenses. Man should express gratitude to God that he got such a beautiful\nhuman body and he should use it correctly. The difference between animals and humans\nis that animals cannot control themselves, they do not have a sense of restraint.\nWhereas humans have a sense of restraint and self-control. If a human being is not able to demonstrate this\ncontrol, then he is like an animal. By controlling the senses or\nthrough the method of yoga, a person can understand himself, the Supreme Being, the world, and the mutual relationships between all of these. Control of the senses is the key. Otherwise, we are like animals. Here, the self-realization is explained by the control of the senses. Man should strive to see beyond the God and also see his (her) own soul.\nTo consider oneself as God\nis not self-realization. Here it is clearly stated that God is eternal or ancient,\nand they have no other reason. The soul is born as a part of God. Brahma-\nIt is confirmed in the Samhita--Anadiradigovinda:--The Supreme Personality of Godhead is without cause. They are unborn. But the soul is produced from them. It is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita that all beings--both living beings and God--are unborn, but it should be known that the supreme cause of the part is God.\nIs. Therefore, the Brahma Samhita says that every object originated from God (Skaranakaranam).\nThe Vedanta Sutra also confirms this-- Janmadyasya Yatah--the ultimate truth is the root cause of everyone's birth. In the Bhagavad Gita also, Krishna's statement is-- Aham Sarvasya Prabhavah-- I am the source of every object, in which Brahma, Shiva, and other living beings are included. It is self-realization. A man should know that he is subject to God, he should not consider himself supremely independent.\nShould understand.\nOtherwise, why would he be kept in a confined life?"
