          "textEn": "575\n\nPraja-patih-- Brahmaji; Swam-- his; Duhitaram-- to the daughter; Drishta- seeing; Tat-rupa- from his beauty;\nDharshitah- enchanted; Rohit- as a deer; Sah- he; Anvadhavat- ran; Rishish- as a deer;\nHata- without; Trapah- Lala..\n\nBrahma, upon seeing his daughter, became enchanted by her beauty, and when she assumed the form of a deer,\nhe began to chase her shamelessly in the form of a deer. Meaning: Brahma's fascination with his daughter's form, and Lord's fascination with the enchanting form--these burning examples teach us that even gods like Brahma and Shiva\nare fascinated by the beauty of the beautiful, so what is the status of an ordinary mortal? Therefore, everyone is advised to meet their own daughter, their mother, or their sister\nwithout any hesitation, because the senses are so strong that a person becomes\nand the senses do not see the relationship of a daughter, mother, or sister.\nTherefore, in the service of Madan-Mohan,\nby engaging in devotion, it would be best to practice subduing the senses. God\nKrishna's name is Madanmohan, because he can control Kamdev or lust.\nOnly by serving Madanmohan, unrestrained commands of Madan can be imposed, otherwise\nAll efforts to control the senses will fail. In the sixth, seventh, and eighth creations, the one who is unbroken and steadfast.\nThe sage, Narayana, is in the essence of the Yogi, by my illusion. 37). Meaning of the word\n\nTat- by Brahman; Srisht- created; Srishteshu-- from all created beings; Kah- who; Nu- without doubt; Akhandit- undivided; Vipath- without obstacles;\nHaving happened; Dhih- one with intellect; Puman- man; Rishim- sage; Narayanam- Narayana; Rithe- besides; Yosit-\nMaiya- as a woman; Iha- here; Mayaya- through Maya..\n\nAmong all the beings created by Brahma, that is, humans, gods, and animals, there is no one other than Rishi Narayan\nwho is indifferent to the attraction of the female form of Maya.\nMeaning: The original beings themselves are Brahma, f