          "textEn": "576\nIn the world, from Brahma to an ant--all beings are attracted to worldly life. This is the basic principle of this physical world. Being fascinated by Brahma by one's daughter is burning.\nIt is an example that no one can escape from lust towards a woman. Therefore, the most\nsurprising creation of Maya is, which keeps the bound soul in bondage. Balam me pashya mayayah stri mayyayo jayino disham. Or, with the karoti padakranthabharuvijambe. 38. Shabdartham (Meaning of the word)\n\nBalam (Strength)-- Power; Me- mine; Pashya- see; Mayaah- of Maya; Stri- in the form of a woman; Jayinah- the victor;\nDishnyaam- of all directions; Ya- that; Karoti- does; Pada- the one who roars; Bhruvi- of her eyebrows\nKi; Jumbeena- with speed; Kevalam- only L\n\nTry to understand the immense power of my subtle female form, which is only\nWith the movement of her eyebrows, she keeps even the greatest of the world's conquerors in her fist.\nMeaning: In the history of the world, there are many examples where a great conqueror has been captivated by the beauty of a FASTA. There is a need to study the hypnotic power of man and his\nattraction to that power. After all, this\nWhose loss was it produced from? According to the Vedanta Sutra, we know that every object is from God.\nIt is born. It is said in that-- Janmadyasya yatah, which means that God or the Supreme Being,\nBrahma or the ultimate truth is the source from which every object originates. In the spiritual world,\neven such a woman's enchanting power and man's falling prey to such attraction, God\nmust be found in and they must be manifested in the divine plays of God.\n\nGod is the Supreme Being, that is, the Supreme Man. Just as a normal man has a desire to be attracted to a woman,\nthe same intensity is found in God as well. They too are captivated by the beautiful form of a woman.\nThe question is, if they are fascinated by such a kiss, then will they be attracted to a physical woman? That's not possible. The people of this world are also women"
