          "textEn": "579\nHe who is slow to anger, who is created by the Lord of Gods,\nI desire to see that death, which is covered by grass like a well. 40 Il\nMeaning of the word\nYa-who; Upayati- comes near; Shanaih- slowly; Maya- of Maya; Yoshit- woman; Dev- by God;\nVinirmita- produced; Tam- that; Ikshet- should be; Atmanah- of the soul; Mrityum- death; Trunai- with grass;\nKuppam- well; Iva- like; Avrutam- covered;\nThe woman born by God is of the nature of Maya, and whoever accepts the services of such Maya\nand associates with it, he should understand very well that this is like a blind well covered with grass,\nthe path to his death. Meaning: Sometimes, a useless well is covered with grass, therefore if\na traveler unknowingly passes by that path, he falls into that well, and his death\nis certain. Similarly, when someone accepts the service of a woman, then association begins,\nbecause God has created woman for the service of man.\nHis service\nBy accepting, a man gets bound in the noose. If he is so intelligent that he considers a woman the gateway to hell,\nthen he can be liberated and associate with her. This is forbidden for him,\nfor those who aspire to rise to divine status. Until fifty years ago, such association was forbidden in Hindu society. A wife could not meet her husband during the day, oft | Even\nThe householders had separate residential houses. For the women in the inner quarters of residential houses,\nthere used to be, and outside rooms for men. The service performed by Khi may seem alluring,\nbut while accepting such service, a person should be cautious, because it is clearly\nsaid that Khi is the gateway to death or is self-forgetfulness. That obstructs the path of spiritual enlightenment.\nOr, it is considered the husband, deluded by me, the mother of the bull.\nWomanhood, SHEE: attained, the father of wealth and home. 49). Lexicon"
