          "textEn": "582\nThey become absorbed in Krishna consciousness and their union remains excellent. Therefore, there is a commendation of Srila Rupa Goswami:\n\nOf the detached one [Tee Iga: |\n\nThat detachment which is united with Krishna's association is called dispassion. (Bhaktirasamutthasindhu 1.2.255)\n\nWomen and men should serve Krishna while living together as householders. If in this service, children, wife, husband, all get involved, then all these physical or material ailments\nwill be resolved. Because consciousness is pure and Krishna is the medium, therefore there is no possibility of downfall.\n\nHaving become the living being, he renounces the world.\nHe performs his actions without interruption. 43. Meaning of the word:\n\nDue to the body; Jiva-bhutena--pervaded by the soul; Lokat-from one world; Lokam-to another world;\nAnuvrajant-wandering; Bhujnchanah-experiencing; Ev-thus; Karmani-desire-driven actions; Karoti-does;\nAviratam-continuously; Puman-living being;\n\nDue to the special type of body, the materialistic living being, according to his actions,\nkeeps wandering from one world to another.\nSimilarly, he engages himself in desire-driven actions,\nand constantly experiences the fruits. Meaning: When a living being is confined within the body, it is called a 'jeevbhut,' and when\nit is free from the body, it is called 'brahmabhut.' ©. After one birth, in the next birth, the body\nchanging, the living being not only keeps wandering in different wombs, but also keeps going from one world to another. Lord Chaitanya says that from desire-driven actions, See, the souls\nkeep wandering in the entire universe, and if, fortunately or due to some virtuous deed, they\ncome into contact with an authentic guru, then by the grace of Krishna, they receive the seed of devotion. If any being, upon finding this seed, sows it in its heart and in the form of listening and chanting"
