          "textEn": "607\nCan do. Here, Lord Kapila gave this very sermon to his mother. In this verse,\nBy the refuge of that quality, devotion to the feet is also important. Its meaning is that devotion to Krishna is complete,\nto do is a divine deed, it is not a material deed. This is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita--\nThose who are engaged in devotion to Brahmabhutaya Kalpate, they immediately attain the divine abode.\n\nFor a human being, the only means to attain the ultimate perfection of life is to fully\ndevote oneself to Krishna consciousness. Lord Kapila gave this teaching to his mother here. Therefore, devotion is free from the influences of all qualities, that is, is ‘Nirguna’. Although devotion\nseems to be a material task to accomplish, it is never 'sagun' (with attributes), meaning it is not contaminated by material\nqualities. Tadugunashraya means that the divine qualities of Lord Krishna are so great\nthat man does not need to pay attention to other tasks.\nTo the devotees,\ntheir behavior is so praiseworthy that they do not have to turn their minds towards any other worship.\nIt is said that a demon named Putana came to kill Krishna by poisoning him,\nbut Krishna was so pleased that he breastfed her and gave her the position of his own mother. Therefore, the devotees pray that when Putana, who came with the desire to kill Krishna,\ncould attain such a high position, then what is the benefit of worshiping anyone other than Krishna? Religious works are of two types--one for material development and the other\nfor spiritual development. By taking refuge in the lotus feet of Krishna--both material and\nspiritual--one attains both kinds of prosperity.\nThen why go to any other gods?\nWhy? Vasudeva, the Lord, has applied the Bhakti Yoga.\nHe creates detachment, knowledge, and the unseen vision. 23). Meaning of the word:\n\nVasudeva - towards Krishna; Bhagavati - God; Bhakti-Yoga - devotion; Prayojita - done; Janayati - gives birth; Utayanna - immediately;