          "textEn": "64\nIt goes, it is the expansion of my power.\" Every object is dependent on them, but it does not mean that they are every object. The senses perceive objects as they are, such as the sound of a drum, the perception of a drum, the sight of a beautiful woman, or the taste of delicious things made of milk through the tongue--all of these\nare obtained from different senses, and consequently, they are understood in different ways. Therefore,\nthe knowledge of the senses is divided into several categories, although all things are one in the form of God's power. Similarly, the powers of fire are heat and light, and through these two powers,\nfire can manifest in many forms. The Mayavadi thinkers declare this diversity as untrue,\nbut the Vaishnava thinkers do not believe so. They consider them inseparable from God, because\nfrom them, the various powers of God are displayed.\nVaishnava philosophers do not accept this philosophy that God is true and this creation\nis false (untrue) (Brahma Satya Jagansithya). Although this example is given that all\nshining objects are not gold, but it does not mean that shining\nobjects are untrue. For example, CP appears to be Sunahli. Its golden color is due to the perception of the eyes,\nbut it does not mean that CP is false. Similarly, God,\nBy looking at the form of Krishna, no one can know what he actually is, but its\nmeaning is not that he is untrue. The form of Krishna is known based on the form described in the scriptures such as Brahma Samhita. Ishwarah Paramah Krishnah Sachchvidanandavigrahah-- Lord Krishna\nWhose spiritual body is eternal and blissful <silence_gap> | Due to our incomplete understanding, we cannot understand the form of God\nWe need to gain knowledge about them. That is why here\nJnanam ekam is said.\nThe Bhagavad Gita confirms that those who, upon seeing Krishna,\nconsider him an ordinary person are fools. They do not know the infinite knowledge, power, and authority of God. The physical sensory-imagination leads to the conclusion that God is formless. Due to such a thought, the bound soul, being controlled by Maya, remained in ignorance"
