ै\nउसी तरह परमात्मा भी है । इस प्रकार परमात्मा तथा आत्मा में साम्य होने पर भी आत्मा की",
          "textEn": "676\nAs the great form, the fivefold, the self-existent,\nThe elevenfold is his support, the world is his. 29). Meaning of the word\n\nAs-- in the manner; Mahan- great- nature; Aham- form- false, ego- three-fold-- the three qualities of nature; Pancha-\nVidh- five-fold; Swar- individual consciousness; Ekadash- twelve-fold-- eleven senses; Tasya- of the living being; Vapu-\nbody; Andam- universe; Jagat- world; Yatah- from which..\n\nI have created ego, the three Gunas, the five Tattvas, individual consciousness,\neleven senses and the body. Similarly, the entire universe appeared from me, God. Meaning: God is described as Mahat-phad, which means that\nthe entire physical power, which is called Mahat-tattva, is lying at his lotus feet. The visible world\nis the origin or the entire power Mahat-tva ©. From Mahat-tattva, other twenty-four divisions were created, which are as follows--Eleven senses (including the mind), five subjects, five elements, consciousness, intellect, and ego.\nBecause God is the cause of the great element, therefore, in a way, every object is emanated from God.\nTherefore, there is no difference between God and the visible world. But along with that, the visible\nworld is different from God. The word 'swarat' is very important here. This means\n‘Ta | God is independent and the soul is also independent. Even then, there is no similarity in these two types of\nfreedom, because the living being is somewhat independent, and God is completely\nindependent. Just as every living being has a physical body, which is made up of five elements and senses,\nin the same way, this universe is the supreme, self-independent, immense body of God. The body is perishable.\nSimilarly, the entire universe, which is the body of God, is also perishable, and these two types of bodies\nare made of the eternal element. Therefore, this difference should be understood with intelligence.\nEvery person knows\nthat his body is born from a divine spark, similarly, the immense body is born from the Supreme Soul or\nthe supreme spark. Just as every body is born from the soul, similarly this\ncosmic body is born from the Supreme Soul. Just as every soul is endowed with consciousness,\nso is the Supreme Soul. In this way, even though there is equality between the Supreme Being and the individual soul, the individual soul"
