          "textEn": "62\nLearned to do. Therefore, to have a vision of Krishna, a person has to learn to transcend even the bliss of Brahman. Because the mind is the center of all senses and their functions, Krishna is\ncalled the master of the senses or *Hashikesh*. Its method is to fix the mind on Krishna or Hashikesh,\nas Maharaj Ambarisha did (Sa Vai Manah Krishnapadaravindayo:). Devotion\nis the fundamental principle of all methods. Without devotion, neither knowledge-yoga nor Ashtanga-yoga can be successful.\nAnd without reaching Krishna, there is no ultimate goal of the principles of self-realization.\nThere is no ultimate goal. By action, by offering, by penance, by self-study, and by sacrifice.\nAnd by self-control, and by study, and by action. 34). Yoga is also by various devotion.\nHe who is engaged in righteousness, fearlessness, and inaction. 35). By the knowledge of the self, by detachment, and with firmness,\nHe is obtained by the Lord, both with attributes and without attributes, by one's own accord. 36. Shabdartham\n\nKriyaya--from desire-driven action; Kratubhimah--from the deeds; Daanibhih--from donations; Tapah--penance; Swadhyay--study of Vedic literature; Maranaih: --And through the yoga of knowledge; self-indriya-jayen--by controlling the mind and senses; api--also;\nSanyasen--through renunciation; cha--and; karmanam--of actions; yogena--by yoga; vividha-angdhen--with various\ndivisions; bhakti-yogena--through devotion; cha- and; eva-certainly; hi-indeed; dharmena- by righteousness;\nubhay-chihen--with both characteristics; yah-who; pravritti- attachment; nivritti-man- detachment; atma-tatva- the essence of the self;\natmap-sakshatkar's science; avabodhena- through knowledge; vairagyena- through detachment; harden- firmly; cha- and; Eyate--experience; Bhagwan--God; Ebhih--from these; S-Gunah--in the material world; Nir-Gunah--beyond qualities; Swah-Hak--own\nL, who looks at his legal status,\n\nBy performing desirable actions and sacrifices, by giving donations, by doing penance, by studying various scriptures, by knowledge, by controlling the mind, by restraining the senses, by accepting renunciation,\nAnd by performing the duties of one's ashram, by accomplishing the various methods of yoga,\nBy devotion, and by manifesting the devotion-yoga endowed with the characteristics of attachment and detachment, By knowing the science of self-realization and awakening a strong sense of detachment,\na person who is very skilled in understanding the various methods of self-realization, in that form,\nrealizes God as he is in the physical world and in spirituality"
