          "textEn": "63\nDevahuti said:\nEven so, lying down in the inner ocean,\nYou are the self-existent one with the senses, the senses, and the self.\nYou poured out the stream of qualities, the complete seed,\nYourself, the one who is born from the lotus-like mouth. 2>. Meaning of the word\n\nDevahuti said--Devahuti said; Athapi- also; Ajah- Brahma Ji; Antar- in the water; Shayanam- lying down; Bhut- physical element; Indriya- senses; Artham- subject; Atma- mind; Mayam- pervaded; Ag: - body; Te- this; Sat- manifested; Ashesh- all; Bijam- seed; Dadhyau- meditated; Swayam- self; Yat- of whom; Jathar- from the stomach; Abaj- lotus-flower; Jaathah- born; Yatah- from whom; Jathar- from the stomach; Ajah- of whom; Bajah- from the lotus-flower; Jaathah- born; Jaathah- born; Jaathah- from whom; Jathar- from the stomach; Ajah- of whom; Bijam- seed; Dadhyau- meditated; Swayam- self; Yatah- from whom; Jathar- from the stomach;.\n\nDevahuti said: Brahmaji is called unborn, because he is born from the lotus-flower that emerges from your womb,\nand you keep sleeping on the ocean floor at the bottom of the universe.\nHmm. But even Brahmaji only focused on the origin source of infinite universes. Meaning: Brahma is also called Aja, because Aja means unborn.\nWhenever we think about someone's\nbirth, they must have a mother and a father, because\nthey will take birth from them. But Brahma, being the first creature in this universe,\nwas directly born from the body of that Lord, who is the Garbhodakshayi Vishnu, that is, Vishnu who sleeps in the ocean on the surface of the universe.\nDevahuti wanted to tell God that when Brahma\nwants to see Vishnu, he also has to meditate on you. He said,\n“You are the seed of the entire creation. Although Brahma has originated directly from you, still\neven when they meditate for years, they are not able to have a direct vision of you. Your body\nlies within the vast watery mass on the plane of the universe, therefore you are called Garbhodakshayi Vishnu.In this verse, there is also an explanation of the cosmic form of the Lord.\nThis body is divine and\nuntouchable from matter (inertness). Since this world has originated from their body, therefore their\nbody was also present before creation. The conclusion is that Vishnu's divine body is material"
