          "textEn": "632\nNot made of elements. Vishnu's body, along with all other living beings, is the source of God's power-\nthe physical nature is also the origin. Devahuti said, \"You are the root of the world and all that has arisen,\nYou are the basis of power, therefore, by explaining Sankhya philosophy in this way, you are freeing me from the noose of Maya,\nSo it is not surprising.\" But taking your birth from my womb\nis certainly surprising, because even after the origin of the entire creation, you have, by grace,\ntaken birth as my son. This is the most astonishing. Your body is the origin of the entire universe.\nYet, you took a body from the womb of a woman like me. This is what seems extremely surprising to me. He is the cause of the universe, He is the cause of the qualities.\nThe beginning of creation is not like that.\nThe power of the self is infinite. 3). Meaning of the word:\nSah-- that man; Eva-- certainly; Vishvasya-- of the universe; Bhavan-- you; Vidhattate- they do; Gunapravhena- by the flow of qualities; Vibhakt-- divided; Viraha- your powers; Sarga- etc.- creation etc.; Aneehah- inactive;\nAvitatha- meaningful; Abhisandhih- determination; Atma-Ishwara- lord of all living beings; Atakya- unimaginable;\nSahasra- thousands; Shakti- endowed with powers;.\nOh God, although you do not have to do anything personally, but you have distributed your\npowers in the interactions of the qualities of nature, by the power of which\nthe origin, maintenance, and destruction of the visible world takes place. Oh God, you are firm in resolve and\nyou are the God of all beings. You created this world for them, and although you are one,\nyour powers work in many ways. This is unimaginable for us.\nMeaning: In this verse, Devahuti has said that even though the ultimate truth does not have to do anything on its own,\nthere are various powers of theirs. Its confirmation is also there in the Upanishads. From them,\nNeither is anyone greater, nor is anyone equal