          "textEn": "634\nShet Sma Mayashishuruddaprapanah. 4>. Meaning:\nHe is the same man; Tvam is you; Yel is born; Me jatarena is from my stomach; Nath is Lord; Katham is how;\nNu is then; Yasya is whose; Udarena is in the stomach; Etat is this; Aasit is was; Vishvam is the universe; Yuga-ante is at the end of the era; Kya is what;\nAnya is someone else; Sate sma is sleeping; Maya is unimaginable powers; Shishu is a child; Adri is thumb; Paanah is sucking;\n\nYou have taken birth from my stomach in the form of Shri Bhagavan. Oh Lord, how was it possible for that God\nin whose belly this entire visible world is situated? Its answer will be that it is possible, because at the end of the kalpa, you lie down on a\nleaf of a banyan tree and like a small child, suck the toe of your lotus feet\nHey. Meaning: At the time of destruction, God sometimes appears as an infant, who\nlies on a banyan leaf floating on the destructive water.\nTherefore, Devahuti says, *'It is not as surprising for you to lie in the womb of a common woman as it is.' You can lie on a banyan\nleaf, and like a baby crow, you keep floating in the floodwaters. Since this is more\nnot surprising, therefore you can lie in my stomach. You teach that those who\nare desirous of children in this world and those who want to enjoy the happiness of a family with children by getting married, they can get a child just like God, and the most\nthe surprising thing is that God himself sucks his thumb.Because all the sages and devotees dedicate all their power and all their activities to the service of the lotus feet of God, therefore, in the toe of his lotus feet, there must be\nsome divine bliss.\nGod sucks his thumb to taste that nectar,\nwhose desire the devotees always have. Sometimes even God himself is surprised that\nhow much divine bliss is contained within him, therefore, with the intention of tasting his power,\nsometimes he takes his taste. Lord Chaitanya is directly Krishna, but he appears as a devotee