          "textEn": "635\nThose who know can taste the sweet essence.\nYou are the master of the body, the remover of sins,\nAnd the cause of the manifested and the unmanifested. As the incarnations are, so are the Shukra and others.\nThus, for the attainment of the path of the self. 500/-. Meaning of the word\n\nTvam-- You; Deh-- this body; Tanhrah-- has assumed; Prashamay-- to reduce; Papmanam-- of sins;\nNidesh-bhājam-- of the teaching of devotion; Cha-- and; Vibho-- O Lord; Vibhutaye- for expansion; Yatha- as;\nAvatarah- incarnation; Tav- yours; Sukar-adayah- pig and other forms; Tatha- in the same way; Ayam- this Kapila\nincarnation; Api- certainly; Atma-path- the path of self-realization; Avagdhaye- to show..\n\nOh God, you have taken this body to reduce the sinful deeds of the fallen and to increase their devotion and knowledge of liberation. Because these sinful souls are dependent on your instructions,\ntherefore, you voluntarily incarnate in the form of a boar and other forms. In this\nway, you have appeared to distribute divine knowledge to your dependent ones.\nNote: The previous verses described the general divine attributes of God. Now, the description of the specific purpose of the Lord's\nis being done. They, through their various powers,\nprovide diverse types of bodies to those beings who are bound by the desire to dominate nature,\nbut over time, they become so fallen that they need guidance. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that whenever there are errors in the realization of the true objective in this world, then God appears in the form of an incarnation. In the form of Kapil, the form of God directs the fallen and enriches them with knowledge and devotion, so that they can go to the abode of God. There are many incarnations of God--such as Varaha,\nMatsya, Kachhap and Nrusimha. Kapildev is also an incarnation of God. Here it is accepted\nthat on this earth, the manifestation of Lord Kapildev was to provide divine knowledge to the misguided bound