          "textEn": "643\nMeaning of the word\n\nMaitreya: Ubach--Maitreya said; Iditah--being praised; Bhagavan--Bhagavan; Evam--Thus; Kapila--\nAkhyah--being named Kapila; Parah--Supreme; Pumanh--Man; Vachah--By words; Aviklavaya--seriously; Iti--Thus;\nAh--Gave the reply; Matrumu--To his mother; Matru-vatsalah--Affectionate to one's mother.\n\nThus, pleased by the words of his mother, the affectionate Lord Kapila\ngave the answer seriously. Meaning: For God is omnipotent, therefore, his display of love for his mother was complete. Hearing his mother's words, he replied with great respect, seriousness, and\ndecency. Kapil said,\nBy the path, by the mother, by the well-watered one, I am.\nAasthiten paran kashtamachiradavarotshyasi. 90 Meaning of the word\n\nKapil said--Bhagwan Kapil said; Margena--by the path; Aneen--this; Matah--Oh Mother; Te--for you;\nSu-sevyen- to be accomplished with simplicity, easy; Uditen--the teaching was given; Me--by me; Aasthiten- done\nGaya; Param- supreme; Kashtam- the goal; Achirat- quickly; Avarotshyasi--you will attain L\n\nBhagwan said: Oh Mother, the path of self-realization that I have taught you\nis extremely easy. You can follow this without difficulty, or\nBy doing this, you can be liberated quickly in this very body (birth). Meaning: Devotion is so complete that by following the rules and regulations and by fulfilling them in the guidance of the Guru, one can be freed from the clutches of Maya even in this body. In other yoga methods or jnanayoga, a person never becomes certain whether he will attain Siddhi\nstate or not.\nBut in doing devotion, if someone has unwavering faith in the orders of an authentic guru,\nand follows the rituals, then his salvation is possible only in this body. Srila Rupa Goswami has confirmed this in Bhakti-Rasayat-Chindhu - Iha Yasya\nHare-Dasya-Chahe, wherever he is situated, if his goal is to serve God according to the instructions of the Guru, then he is liberated, that is, even in his physical