          "textEn": "659\n\nBecause of always being absorbed in the thoughts of God, he did not even remember that\nhis hair has fallen out and his clothes have become disheveled, O.\n\nMeaning: In this verse, the word 'Daivaguptamu' is very important. Its meaning is *'Protected by God.'\"Once, after taking refuge in God, He alone takes care of the devotee's body,\nand no worries remain for its protection. In the second chapter of Shrimad Bhagwat,\nit is said that a completely surrendered person does not care about the\nmaintenance of his body. God takes care of countless types of beings, therefore,\none who is engaged in their service cannot remain unprotected. Therefore, it is natural that Devahuti\ndid not have any sense of her own body, her protection was being done by the Supreme Being.\nAnd having gone through the path of the Kapilaka, the supreme...\nHaving attained the self, the Brahman, and the liberation from the self, the Lord... 30>. Meaning of the word\n\nEvam-- in this way; Sa-- he (Devahuti); Kapila-- by Kapila; Uktena-- told; Margena-- from behind; Achiratah--\nQuickly; Param-- supreme; Atmanam-- to the soul; Sel- Brahman; Nirvana- the end of life; Bhagavantam- to the Lord;\nAvap-- attained; Ha-- certainly..\n\nHey Vidur, Devahuti, following the rules told by Kapila, quickly became free from worldly\nbondage and attained the Supreme Being, the form of God, without difficulty.\n\nMeaning: In this context, three words have been used to describe the attainment of Devahuti--\nAtmanam, Brahmanirvanam, and Bhagavantam--which explain the sequential method of searching for the ultimate truth,\nwhich is called Bhagavantam. Lord resides in Vaikuntha, which is different from Vaikuntha Loka. The meaning of Nirvana is the pacification of the sufferings of the world. When someone goes to Vaikuntha, they become free from all the sufferings\nspontaneously. It is the Brahmam-nirvana.\nAccording to Vedic scriptures, Nirvana means\nthe end of physical life. Atmanam means the realization of the Supreme Soul within the heart.\nUltimately, the ultimate accomplishment is the realization of God. It should be understood that Devahuti entered that\nworld which Kapil calls \"Vaikuntha\". The number of Vaikuntha worlds is infinite, in which"
