          "textEn": "8\nDakshaay Brahmaputraaya Prasutim Bhagwanmanu. Prayachitah sargastrilokyam vitato mahan. 19. Meaning of the word:\nDaksha, the son of Prajapati, the son of Brahma; Prasuti, the mother; Bhagavan-Mahapurusha; Manu, the self-existent Manu;\nPrayachit, given; Yat-kritah, by whom; Sargah, creation; Trilokyam, in the three worlds; Vitatah, extending;\nDone; Mahan, exceedingly great;\nSwayambhuva Manu gave his daughter named Prasuti to Daksha, the son of Brahma, who was one of the Prajapatis. Descendants of Daksha are spread across the three worlds.\nThese are the nine Brahmarshis' sons, as said.\nI will now explain the birth and upbringing of them. 12). Meaning of the word:\nYah--who; Kardam-sutah--daughters of Kardam; Proktah--mentioned; Nav--nine; Brahma-rishi--those with spiritual knowledge; Rishiyah--of the sages; Patnayah--wives; Tasam--their; Prasuti-prasutam--generations of sons and grandsons; Prachyamanam--being described;\nNibodh--try to understand; Me--from me..\nI have already told you about the nine daughters of Kardam Muni, that they nine\nwere handed over to different sages. Now I will describe the descendants of these nine maidens. Listen to me about them.\nMeaning: It has been told in the third Skandha that how Devahuti got nine daughters\nand later how they were handed over to sages like Marichi, Atri, Vasistha. Wife, Marichestu, art, well, Kardama's daughter.\nKashyapa, the full moon, and the one who is filled with the world. 13. Meaning of the word\nWife--Wife; Marichiha- from the sage named Marichi; Tu- also; Kala-- from the name Kala; Sushuve- gave birth; Kardama-self-born;\nKardama Muni's daughter; Kashyapam- from the name Kyap; Parnimanam- also from the name Purnima; Yayo- from whom; Apuritamu- filled;\nGone, spread everywhere; Jagat- world \\.\nKardama Muni's daughter Kala was married to Marichi, from whom two children were born whose names were\nKashyap and Purnima. Their children failed in all the world."
