          "textEn": "\nBut from before, their heart was attracted to these gods, therefore, in this way, they regained consciousness\nand with folded hands, they began to praise the chief presiding deities of the universe with sweet words. Atri Muni said: O Brahma, O Vishnu, and O Shiva, you have accepted the three qualities of material nature\nand have divided yourself into three bodies, just as you have been doing in every kalpa\nfor the creation, sustenance, and destruction of the perishable world. I respectfully greet all three of you.\nI offer my salutations, and I want to know which of you I called in my prayer.\nWho was it? Meaning: Atri Muni had invoked Jagadishra, that is, the lord of the universe. If God existed before creation, how could he be its master (God)? If someone constructs a building,\nit indicates that they are already present before that building construction. Therefore, the HFT God of the universe must be transcendental.\nBut it is known that Vishnu is the head of Sattva Guna, Brahma\nof Rajoguna, and Shiva is the head of Tamoguna. Therefore, Atri Muni said, \"That Jagdishwar (Lord of the Universe) is definitely\nsomeone from within himself.\" But you three have appeared together, therefore I am unable to recognize that\nwhom I had invoked. Please tell me who among you is really Jagadishshar?''\nActually, Atri Muni had doubts about the natural state of Lord Vishnu, but his firm belief was that the Lord of the Universe could not be a creature born of Maya. Their question that they whom"
