          "textEn": "[7]\nThe call indicated that they were doubtful about the legal status of Bhagwan Kau. Therefore,\nThey prayed to the three, *' Please tell me who is the divine lord of the world?\"Actually, their\nbelief was that all cannot be God, but only one of these three can be Jagadishwar.\nIs. Oh Lord, the one who is in the various forms,\nHe who is thought of as the cause of procreation, how can we know Him?\nThose who have come here, even from afar,\nOh Lord, I am greatly astonished. 28>. Meaning of the word\n\nEkah- Ekah; Maya- by me; Iha- here; Bhagavan- Supreme Being; Vividh- many; Wer: -by means of; Chitti- in the mind;\nKritah- having fixed in mind; Prajanayan- for the origin of offspring; Katham- why; Nu- but; Yuyam- all of you; Atra- here;\nAtra- here; Agatah- having arrived; Tanu- body; Manasah- mind; Api- even though; Duraat- from afar; Bhitu- by; Krupa- by\ngiving; Prasidat- being pleased with; Mahan- very; Iha- here; Vismayah- doubt; Me- mine.\nI had invoked the same son with the desire for a son, just like the supreme Purushottama Bhagwan.\nAnd I had contemplated the same. Although they are beyond human mental imagination, but\nYou three are present here. Please tell me how you came here, because I\nam extremely fascinated by it. Meaning: Atri Muni had complete faith that Shri Bhagwan is the Lord of the Universe, therefore he prayed to one\nGod. Therefore, they were wondering how the three appeared. Maitreya said,\nHaving heard his words, the three wise kings.\nRepeatedly, with a thousand signs of speech, laughing, they spoke to him, O Lord. 29>. Meaning of the word.\n\nMaitreya said— Rishi Bhetreya said; Iti— thus; Tasya— his; Vachah— words; Shrutva- having heard; Trayah- those three; Vinudh- deities; Rishabhah- chief; Pratyahu- answered; Shlakshnaya- polite; Vacha- speech; Prahasya- smiling; Tam- to him;\nRishim- Rishi; Prabho- O mighty one.\n.\n\nMaitreya Maha-Muni said: Hearing Atri Muni speaking in this way, the three great gods\nsmiled and in a soft voice, they replied in this way."
