e word used for 'pratichakshanaya'\nmeans 'they are forms (of what)' declaring the glory of Shri Bhagavan, who has manifested in the form of Nar-Narayan,\nand who is the root of all forms of material nature. He who is situated, who removes the obstacles, the creator,\nHe is not to be compared to the gods by his truthfulness, that essence.\nBy the compassion of the destroyer of the nine enemies, by the sight of"
