          "textEn": "36\nHow did Shiva destroy the glory of the gods through his uncivilized behavior? By Daksha,\nthe words spoken against Lord Shiva can also be understood in a better context in another way. For example, Daksha said that he is Yashoshna, which means, \"'Destroying name and fame.\"\nBut it can also be interpreted that he was so famous that others'\nfame was destroyed by his fame. Daksh also used another word, Nirfatrap, which can be used in two senses. One meaning is '* the dwarf' and the other meaning is '* the protector of the helpless'.\"Generally, Shiva is known by the name of Bhootnath, that is, the lord of the beings of the lower order. Bharat means,\n“' Inferior creatures.\" They go to the refuge of Lord Shiva because they are merciful to all and\n quickly pleased. That is why he is called Ashutosh.\nFor such humans, who cannot reach other gods or\nVishnu, Shiva is the one who gives refuge. Therefore, the word 'Nirfatra' can be taken in this sense. I have attained discipleship from him, whose daughter is ahead of me.\nLike Savitri from the mouth of the Brahmin, like a virtuous woman. 99. Meaning of the word\nEshah--This (of Shiva); Me--mine; Shishyatam--being a disciple; Praptah--accepted; Yat--because; Me dhutuh-of my daughter;\nAgrahit-accepted; Panih-hand; Vipra-Agni-of Brahmins and fire; Mukhatah-in front; Savitriyah-Gayatri; Iva-like this;\nSadashah-like; Sadhuvat-like a virtuous man..\nHe has already accepted my subordination by marrying my daughter before me in front of fire and Brahmins.\nHe has accepted it. He has married my daughter, similar to Gayatri, and has called himself\nA true man. Meaning: Daksha's statement that Shiva created a pretense of a virtuous man, indicates that Shiva was not honest\nbecause even after becoming Daksha's son-in-law, he was not showing respect towards him.\nHaving taken, the deer-eyed one, the monkey-faced one.\nIn response to the rising, the argument, or the uncalled-for action. 12). Lexicon"
