          "textEn": "39\nThey accept the burden of those who are attached, but Shivji is so merciful that he takes the burden of all those people\nwho are Tamoguni and whose conduct is even lower than animals. Therefore, Shiva is specially called auspicious. Therefore, to the one who is free from delusion and untruth, to the one who is free from impurity, I give two things.\nI have given the virtuous woman to the Supreme Soul. 16). Meaning of the word.\n\nTo him; to the master of the spirits; destroyed; devoid of all cleanliness; Durade- full of defects; heart; Datta- was given; Bat- aho; by me; Sadhvi- a virtuous woman; Chodite- upon being requested; by the supreme guru (Brahma)..\n\nAt Brahmaji's request, I had given my virtuous daughter to him, although she is devoid of all kinds of purity, and her heart is filled with disorders. Meaning: It is the duty of parents to marry their daughter into a family that is clean,\npious, wealthy, and socially well-positioned, etc., in accordance with their lineage.\nDaksha regretted\nthat he had given his daughter to such a person at the behest of his father Brahma, who was\ndisgusting according to his calculation. He was so angry that he was not even accepting that\nthe request for marriage was made by his father. On the contrary, he called Brahma the Supreme Being.\nThat is, he called Jagadguru, because out of anger, he was not accepting Brahma as his father. In other words, he accused Brahma of being ignorant because he advised to give his beautiful daughter\nto an ineligible person. In anger, a man forgets everything, therefore,\nDaksha, in a fit of rage, not only blamed Shiva but also criticized his own father, Brahmaji,\nbecause it was on his foolish advice that he married Shiva's daughter.\n\nMaitreya said,\n\"He who is angry and arrogant towards the mountain,\nDaksha, touching it, angrily proceeded to curse him.\" 17). Lexicon"
