          "textEn": "40\nMaitreya said--Maitreya said; Vinindya, after scolding; Evam--Thus; Sah--He (Daksha); Girisham--Shiva; Apritim--\nARTE; Avasthitam--Staying; Daksha--Daksha; Ath--Now; Apa:--Water; Upasprushya--Having washed hands and face; Kuddha--Enraged;\nKruddha--Angry; Shaptumu--To curse; Prachamra--Started..\n\nMaitreya Muni further said: Seeing Shiva situated against him in this way, Daksha performed Achamana with water\nand began to curse with the following words. He is the one who is born from the gods, Indra, Pandra, and others.\nHe is not to be shared with the gods, the assembly of gods. 98 Meaning of the word\n\nAyam- this; Tu- but; Deva-yajne-- in the sacrifice of the gods; Indra-Upendra-Adishi-- Indra, Upendra, and others including; Bhavah--\nShiva; Sah-- with; Bhagam-- a part; T— not; Labhataam-- should be obtained; Devaih-- from the gods; Deva-gan-Adhamah--\nAmong all the gods, the lowest Shiva\nShould not receive the share of the sacrifice.\nMeaning: Because of this curse, Shiva was deprived of participating in the Vedic sacrifices and the offerings. In this\ncontext, there is a commentary by Srivishwanath Chakraborty that due to this curse of Daksha, Lord Shiva remained safe from the temptation of supporting other materialistic\ngods. Shivji is the greatest devotee of Shri Bhagwan, and this does not suit him\nthat he should sit and stand with materialistic people like gods. Thus, Daksha's\ncurse proved to be a boon because, due to this, Shiva, along with other gods, who were\nextremely materialistic, neither eating nor sitting up, US. Before us, Gaurkishor Das\nBabaji Maharaj has presented a practical example. They used to sit near the toilet and chant 'Hare Krishna'.\nThey used to chant. Because many people would come and interfere with his Hare Krishna chanting, he would sit near the toilet only to avoid their company, because then materialistic people would not like to go near due to dirt and stench.\nBut they were such great men that they became the guru of Om Vishnupad\nSrimad Bhakti Siddhanta Saraswati Goswami Maharaj. The conclusion was that Shiva deliberately\npracticed such behavior that materialistic people should not be hindered in their devotion."
