th eyes closed, practicing self-control, Lolakshim, with eight earrings.\nHer husband, the lord of the earth, spoke out of eagerness. 7/. Meaning of the word\n\nTat- Tav; Upashrutya- by listening; Nabhasi- in the sky; Khe- Charanam- by the path of the sky; Prajalpataam-\nSalutation; Sati- Sati; Dakshayani-- Daksha's daughter; Devi-- Shiva's wife; Pitru- Yagya-Maha-Utsavam-- A great yagya performed by one's father; Vrajanti- were going; Sarvath- all; Digbhyah- from the directions; Upadeva- Var-wife-of-the-Gods;\nA beautiful feat; Vimana-yana- flying in their respective Vimanas; Sa-pshthah- with their respective husbands; Nishka-kanthi- wearing a beautiful necklace; Su-vasas- adorned with beautiful clothes; Drutta- seeing; Swa-nilaya-abhyase- near one's home; Lol-akshi- with flickering eyes; Mishra-kundalaah--Beautiful ear ornaments; Patim--Her husband; Bhut-patim--Of the ghosts; Swami--Lord; Devam--God; Otsukyat--With eagerness; Abhyabhashata--She spoke.\n\nDaksha's daughter, virtuous Sati, while going through the sky, spoke to the inhabitants of heaven, mutually"
