          "textEn": "6\nLeft--O dear Shiva; They--Yours; If--If; Meaning--Desire; Ami--This; Vibhuda--The gods; Brajanti--Are going; Hi--\nBecause..\n\nSati said: Oh beloved Shiva, at this time your demon ancestors are performing a great yagya (sacrificial ritual), and all the\ngods are going there, invited. If you say so, we will also come along. Meaning: Sati knew about the tension going on between her husband and father, yet Sati\nsaid to her husband that since a Yagya (ritual) is happening at her father's house and so many deities are going into it,\ntherefore she also wants to go. But she could not express her wish directly,\nTherefore, she said to her husband that if they were willing to go, she too could go with them.\nMeaning that she expressed her wish very humbly before her husband.\n\nThen, with her brothers, she will go to her husband's house.\nI am also desirous of that,\nto help her husband in his household chores. 9>. Meaning of the word\n\nTasmin--in that Yagya (sacrificial fire); Bhaginyah-sisters; Mamah-mine; Bharatribhih-with their respective husbands; Swakaih-from their side; Dhuvam-\nCertainly; Gamishyanti-will go; Suhit-desirous; Aham-me; Cha-and; Tasmin-in that;\nIn that festival; Bhavat-with you (of Shiva); Abhikam-desire; Saha-with; Upanitam-offered; Parivaham-traveling;\nAarohanam-ascending; Arhat-accepting; Upahitam-offered; Parivaham-traveling;\nBahuvrihi-with; Bharatibhih-with their respective husbands; Swakaih-from their side; Dhuvam-\nCertainly; Gamishyanti-will go; Suhit-desirous; Aham-me; Cha-and I think that all my sisters, with the desire to meet their relatives, along with their respective\nhusbands, must have come to this great Yagya. I too, with the ornaments given by my father,\nby adorning myself, am eager to participate in that festival with you.\nMeaning: It is the nature of women that they, adorned with ornaments and clothes, want to go with their husbands to social festivals, there they meet their dear friends and relatives, and\nin this way, they enjoy life. This is not a peculiarity, because the foundation of material happiness\nis Fert. Therefore, the word 'stri' (woman) is used in Sanskrit, which means 'ae' which expands the field of material\npleasures and enjoyments.\"In the physical world, attraction occurs between a woman and a man. This is the system of life imprisonment. It attracts the right man and in this way"
