          "textEn": "74. It is also said that, out of courtesy, as soon as a Vaishnav is seen, one should immediately offer a salutation.\nThis indicates that the Supreme Being resides within him. Vaishnav considers the body as Vishnu's\ntemple. Because Shivji had already bowed to the Supreme Being in Krishna consciousness, therefore Daksha\nwho was considering himself in body form, had already offered his salutations. His body\ndid not need to be offered salutations, because it is not specified in any Vedic order.\nIt is not. That which is pure in essence, spoken by Vasudeva,\nIs there, there, covered by the man.\nIn that truth, the Lord, Vasudeva,\nis worshiped by me with oblation. 23). Meaning of the word\n\nSattvam-- consciousness; Vishuddham-- pure; Vasudeva-- Vasudeva; Shabditam-- known by name; Yat- because; Iyate- appears;\nTat- there; Puman- supreme being; Apavrithah- without any covering; Sattve- in consciousness; Cha- and; Tasmin- in that;\nBhagavan- God; Vasudevah- Vasudeva; Hi- because; Adhokshajah- divine; Me- by me; Namas- with salutations; Vidhiyate- is worshiped;\nPujit- worshiped. I always offer my salutations to Lord Vasudeva in pure Krishna consciousness. \nThis is always pure consciousness, in which, without any kind of\ndisturbance, one experiences Shri Bhagavan, who is known by the name Vasudeva. Meaning: the soul is naturally pure. Asadhko hyayam purushah. It is said in the Vedas that\nthe soul is always pure and untouched by material attachments.\nTo recognize the body with the soul\nIs due to ignorance. As soon as someone is completely filled with Krishna consciousness, then it should be understood\nThat he has attained the pure original natural state. This state is called pure-essence. Because\nThis pure essence is under the direct control of the inner power, therefore in this state all worldly tasks stop\n. For example, when iron is placed in fire, it gets hot, and when it turns red,\nit becomes iron and acts like fire. Similarly, when electricity flows through copper,\nit does not act like copper; it acts like electricity."
