          "textEn": "75\n\nIt is also confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita (14.26) that whoever worships God without any mixture, he immediately\nobtains the state of pure Brahman. He who serves with unbroken devotion,\n\nHe who is beyond qualities, is called the Brahman. Therefore, as it is said in this verse, pure essence is a divine state, which is technically called Vasudeva.\nVasudeva is also the name of a man, from whom Krishna manifested. This verse explains that the pure\nstate is called Vasudeva, because in that state, Lord Vasudeva is experienced without any distance.\nThey go. Therefore, to perform unconditional devotion, one should follow the rules of devotion without any desire for material gain through desireful actions or mental imaginations. In pure devotion, a person, without any reason or without any obstruction, considering his duty to God,\ncontinues to serve only. This pure essence or Vasudeva is called, because in this state, in the heart of the devotee,\nthe Supreme Personality of Godhead, Krishna, arises.\nSrila Jeeva Goswami, in his Bhagavat-sambandh, has described this\nVasudeva or pure essence as extremely enchanting. They say that before the name of the Guru,\nAshtottara-sta (108) is added, which indicates that he is in a pure state or Vasudeva Ka\ndivine state. The word Vasudeva is also used in other ways. For example, the meaning of Vasudeva is\nalso omnipresent. The Sun is also known as Vasudeva-Sankarshana. Even if Vasudeva is not used in various senses,\nbut the meaning of Vasudeva is omnipresent or omnipotent God. In the Bhagavad Gita (7.19) also,\nit is said-- Vasudeva: sarvam, iti. The real experience is to understand Lord Vasudeva and to go to his\nshelter. Vasudeva is the ground of Being, on which shines the Luminous Vasudeva of the Lord. When a human\nis free from the impurities of material nature and is situated in pure Krishna consciousness or Vasudeva, that is, in the state of Vasudeva,\nthen there is an understanding of Lord Vasudeva.\nThis is called Kaivalya Pad, which means\n“Pure consciousness.\"Knowledge is Sattvic, liberation / When a person attains pure divine knowledge, then he\nis situated on the state of liberation. Therefore, the meaning of Vasudeva also includes liberation, whose behavior is ordinary"
