          "textEn": "97\nLeave it and go away, or else close your ears so that you don't hear those insulting words. If\nhe is a Kshatriya, then he has so much power that he can punish any person, therefore a Kshatriya\nshould immediately cut off the tongue of a critic and kill him. But as far as Vaishyas and Shudras\nare concerned, they should immediately give up their lives. Sati resolved to give up her body,\nbecause she considered herself one of the Shrautas and Vaishyas. As it is said in Bhagavad Gita (9.32)\nKhio Vaishyastatha Shadrah. The Khans, the labourers and the merchant class are of the same level. Because this recommendation\nhas gone that upon hearing the insult of a great man like Shiva, the Shudras and Vaishyas should give their lives\ntherefore Sati decided to give her life. I will not bear this body of bones.\nI will not bear the throat of a parrot.\nOf the destruction of delusion, the purification of the darkness,\nAnd the upliftment of the afflicted, is seen. 18. Meaning of the word:\nTherefore, so; Tava-- from you; Utthyanam-- obtained; Idam-- this; Kalevaram-- body; Nadharishye-- will not hold; Shiti-\nKantha-Garhinah-- one who insults Shiva; Jagdhasya- eaten; Mohat- by mistake; Hi-because; Vishuddhim- purification;\nAndhasah- of food; Jugupsitasah- disgusted; Urahanam- vomiting, Ka; Prachakshate- is declared..\nTherefore, I will not hold this unworthy body, which I have received from you, for any longer, because you have condemned Shiva. If someone consumes poisonous food,\nthen the best treatment is to induce vomiting.\nMeaning: Since Sati was the representative of the external power of God, it was in her power that\nshe could destroy many universes, including many Dakshas, but to save her husband from this\nblame, that she made her wife Sati the medium to kill Daksha,\nbecause she herself could not do so from being in a lower position, Sati decided to give up her body. Not following the Vedas, the intellect"
