          "textEn": "07\nShe wanted to transfer into the body so that she could have pure association with Lord Shiva.\nIn fact, it is clear that in the next life, she will be born as the daughter of the Himalayas, Parvati, and then\nshe will again accept Shiva as her husband. The relationship between Sati and Shiva is eternal, to the extent that\neven after changing bodies, their relationship does not break. Then, the one who is the lord of his own house, the lotus-like one,\nThe world-teacher contemplates, and no other.\nHe saw the body, the impure one,\nImmediately ignited the fire of Samadhi. 27). Meaning of the word:\n\nTatah-- there; Swa-bhartuh-- of one's own husband; Charan-ambhuja-asavam-- on the nectar of the lotus feet; Jagat-gurouh-- the guru of the universe; Chintayati-- contemplating; Na- not; Cha- and; Aparam-other ( besides her husband); Dadarsha-seen; Deha-the body; Hata-kalmashah-destroyed by sin; Sati-Sati; Sadyah-immediately; Prajajwalah-burned; Samadhi-Ja-by the fire that arises from meditation\n\nSati focused all her attention on the sacred lotus feet of her husband, the world teacher Shiva.\nIn this way, she was purified from all sins. She, by meditating on the fiery elements, was ignited.\nShe gave up her body in the fire. Meaning: Sati immediately meditated on the lotus feet of her husband Shiva, who is one of the three deities who govern the physical world. They received so much joy from meditating on the lotus feet\nthat they forgot all their bodily relations. This joy was certainly material, because\nthey had renounced their body with the intention of attaining another physical body. But from this example,\nwe can estimate the joy of a devotee, which he attains by focusing his mind on the lotus feet of Lord Vishnu or Krishna. Only by meditating on the lotus feet of God, one attains such divine bliss that a person can forget everything except the divine form of God. This is the perfection of Yoga-Samadhi. In this verse, it is said that with such meditation, Sati became completely\nfree from sins.\nWhat was that stain? This impurity, as the body-consciousness obtained from Daksha,\nBut in Samadhi, he forgot all this. The meaning is that when man in this physical world all"
