          "textEn": "5\nWhen Sati gave up her body, Narada informed Shiva about it. Narada always takes such\nimportant information. When Shiva heard that his virtuous wife had died, he\nNaturally became extremely angry. They also came to know that Bhrigu Muni, through the recitation of Yajurveda mantras,\ncreated the Ribhus, and these gods drove away all their attendants who were present at the Yagya-\nsite. Therefore, he wanted to take revenge for this insult and decided that Daksha's\nmurder should be done, because he was the cause of Sati's death.\nAngry, with a well-formed, strong jaw, and a cunning-\nWith matted hair, with a sharp, pointed face.\nRudra, having made a sound, suddenly arose and laughed,\nA deep sound, pouring out on the earth. 2>. Meaning:\nKruddha - angry; Su-dashta-Oshth-Putah - clenching the lips with the teeth; Sahah - he (Shiva); Dhahu-Jati-H - wearing matted locks on the body; Kiye; Jatam - a hair; Tadit-Bijali Kaau - lightning; Vahi-Agni ki; Sata-Jwala, Lapat - flame, blaze; Ugra-Bhishan - terrible; Rochish-Prajwalitah - blazing;\nUtsarga-Noch Karna - having done; Sudra-Shiva; Sahasa-Turant; Uthitah-became rocky; Hasan-laughing; Gambhir-deep; Nadah-sound;\nVisarjna-Noch Karna - having thrown; Tam-that; Bhuvi-on the earth;.\nIn this way, due to being extremely angry, Shiva, while chewing his lips with his teeth, immediately\nsnapped a hair from the matted hair of his head, which started burning like lightning or fire. They\nLaughing like a madman, immediately stood up and threw that bunch of grass on the ground.\nThen, with a huge body, touching the earth,\nWith a thousand arms, a thousand heads, and a sun-like face,\nWith a fierce-faced, blazing, fire-like head,\nWith a skull garland, various weapons, and a youthful form. 3. Shabdarman\nTatah--At that time; Atikayah--one with a voluptuous body (Veerabhadra); Tanuva--with one's body; Spooshn--touching;\nDivam--sky; Sahasra--thousand; Bahuha--arms; Ghanar-Rukh- one with a dark complexion; T