          "textEn": "[6\nLooked like a lit fire. She had thousands of arms, which were equipped with weapons, and\nshe was wearing a garland of skulls. What should I do, O Lord, to those who praise me?\nO Lord of the gods, with folded hands.\nKnow me to be skilled in sacrifices,\nO foremost among the wicked, you are the best among the wicked.4>. Meaning of the word:\nTam-that (to Veerabhadra); Kim-what; Karomi-shall; Iti-in this way; Gruntam-in asking; Aah-given order;\nBandh-with folded hands; Bhagavan-Lord of all; Bhut-Lord of beings; Daksham-to Daksha;\nSa-with the Yagya (sacrificial fire); Jahi-hit; Mat-of all my council; Tvam-you; Agrani-leader; Rudra-Oh Rudra;\nBhat-hey, skilled in war; Anshakah-born of the body; Me-my LL\nWhen that gigantic demon asked with folded hands, \"Hey Lord. What should I do.\"Bhutnath Rupa\nShiva directly ordered, \"Because you are born from my body, you have become the leader of all my councilors,\ntherefore, go to the Yagya (site) and kill Daksha along with his soldiers.\n''\nMeaning: From here on, the competition between Brahma Teja and Shiva Teja begins. Bhrigu Muni created the Ribhu Devas from the radiance of Brahma,\nwho drove away the soldiers of Shiva from the sacrificial place. When Shiva heard that\ntheir soldiers had been driven away, he created a long-duration, black demon named Veerabhadra to take revenge. Sometimes the Satvik and Tamovic qualities compete. This is the custom of this world. Even if someone is virtuous, the possibility is that they also have a part of Rajoguna or Tamoguna.\nIt remains mixed in them. This is the law of material nature. Although in the spiritual world, pure self is the fundamental\nelement (principle), in this world, the pure essence of truth is difficult to grasp. In this way, in various physical\nqualities, the struggle for life continues. This conflict between Shiva and Bhrigu Muni regarding Prajapati Daksha\nis a burning example of competition among the various qualities of nature. Having commanded and angered, with many others,\nHe circumambulated the God of Gods, the all-pervading one.\nMenetadatmanamsadharaansa"
