          "textEn": "77\nMahiyasan tat sahah sahishnum. 5>. Shabdarman\nSH: — Giving orders; evam--in this way; kupiten--angry; manyuna--by Shiva (who is in anger); saah-He (Veerabhadra);\nDeva-Devam-that which is worshiped by the gods; parichareyate-is circumambulated; vibhum-of Shiva; meene-was considered; tada-At that time;\nAtmanam-self; asadg-the power of Shiva, which cannot be opposed; mahiyaasam-extremely powerful; ka; tata-Oh Vidura; saah-power; sadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; saadhinshn-capable of enduring; sa.\nMaitreya further explained: O Vidura, that dark man was the direct anger of God, and Shivji\nwas eager to follow the orders. Thus, considering himself capable of facing any opposing force, he circumambulated Lord Shiva.\nAnviyamanaha s tu Rudraparshade-\nBhrusham naddhirvyanadtsubhairavam.\nUdyamya shulam jagadantakam\nSamparadravadhonbhushanadhishih. 6>. Shabdarman\nAnvayimanah-- walking behind; Sah-- he (Veerabhadra); Tu-- but; Rudraparshadah-- by the soldiers of Shiva; Bhusham-- making a noise; Nadadhah-- roaring; Vyanadit-- of sound; Su-Bhairavam-- extremely terrifying; Udyamya- having taken; Shulam- trident; Jagat-\nAntak- death; Antakam- while killing; Sampradravat- having rushed towards; Ghoshana- roaring; Bhushan- ornamented; Angrahyah- having earrings on their feet..\nWhile making a terrible roar, many other soldiers of Shiva also joined that terrifying demon. He was holding a huge trident, which was so terrible that it was capable of even killing death, and there were bangles in his feet, which seemed to be roaring.\nThus, the Yajamana, the members,\nHaving seen the Kakubhyudiya Renu,\nWhy is that? How is this adorned one?\nThe twice-born, the twice-born, and the milk-drinking ones,\nDrink the milk. 7/. Meaning:\nAth--At that time; Ritvijah--priests; Yajamanah--the chief person who performs the Yajna (sacrifice); Sadasyah--the members gathered at the Yajna site;\nAll men; Kakubhi Udiyam--in the northern direction; Prasamikya--seeing; YUH--dust; Tamah--darkness; Kim--what; Etat--this;\nThis; Kutah--from whom; Etat--this; Rajah--dust; Abhuut--having come; Iti--thus; Dvijah--the Brahmins; Dvijapalyah--the wives of the Brahmins; Cha--and; Dadhyuh--started thinking;\nMeaning:\nThey began to contemplate. At that time, all the people gathered in the Yanna place-- priests, chief patrons, Brahmins, and their\nwives-- began to wonder where this darkness was coming from. Later, they understood"
