          "textEn": "8\nThat it was a dust storm and they all became very anxious. There is no wind, nor fire, nor thunderbolt for the demons.\nThe ancient Bharati lives on the staff of the serpent. Why is this world destroyed by the darkness of time?\nWhat is the destruction of the world now? 8/. Meaning of the word\nVata:--winds; not vanti- not flowing; na--not; hi--because; santi- possible; dasyavah- robbers; prachin- ancient; barhi- king; jeevati- alive; ha- even now; ugra- punishment; danda- severe punishment; ga- village; na- not going; idam- this; kutah- from; rajah- dust; lokah- world; adhuna- now; kim- what; pralayay- for destruction;\nfor; kalpate- comes, understood..\nWhile estimating the source of the storm, he said: Neither strong winds are blowing,\nnor are the cows going, nor is it possible that this dusty storm has been raised by robbers, because\neven now, the mighty king Barhi is alive to punish them.\nSo then, this dusty storm,\nWhere is it coming from? Is the world going to be destroyed? Meaning: In this verse, especially the ancient Barhi is important. The king of that region\nwas known as Barhi, although he was old, but he was a very powerful ruler. In this way,\nthere is no possibility of the attack of thieves and robbers. Indirectly, it is said here that\nwhen the ruler is not powerful, then thieves, robbers, unwanted people, remain in the state. When in the name of justice, thieves are given freedom, then such looters and unwanted people spread unrest in the state. The dust raised by Shivaji's soldiers and followers is presenting a scene of the apocalypse.\noff | When this creation is about to be destroyed, Shiva alone accomplishes this task. Therefore, by them,\nThe created state is like the time of destruction of the visible world.\nThe mixed women are anxious-minded.\nThe ripening of the barren is like that of a barren woman.\nThose who are born, the sons, the king.\nThe daughter, the virtuous woman, he said. 9>. Lexicon"
