          "textEn": "29\nBe guilty towards the lotus feet. Even then, if you go to them without any hesitation,\nand surrender to them and fall at their lotus feet, then they will be very pleased. Note: Shiva is also referred to as Asutosh. Ashu means \"big hurry\" and Tosha means \"to be happy\".' 'The gods were advised to go to Shiva and ask for forgiveness, and since\nShiva is about to be pleased soon, his work will surely be done. Brahmaji knew the mind of Shiva\nvery well and he believed that the offending deities at his lotus feet would go there\nand be freed from their sins by surrendering without hesitation. Aashasana Jivitamadhvarasya\nLokah sapalah kupitena na yasmin.\nTamasu Devam Priyaya Vihinam\nKshamapayadhwam Hadi Viddham Duruktah. 6>. Meaning of the word:\nAshasana:--intending to ask; Jivitam--for a period of time; Adhvarasya--of the Yagya; Lokah--all the worlds; Sa-palah--with oneself;\nKupit- when angry; Na- not; Yasmin- in which; Tam- that; Ashu- immediately; Devam- from Shiva; Priyaya- to one's beloved; Viheenamu- without; Kshamapayadhvam- forgive me; Hadi- in his heart; Viddham- extremely sorrowful; Duruktayah- harsh words;\nFrom the words..\nBrahma also told them that Shivji is so powerful that all the worlds\nand their chief guardians can be destroyed immediately by his wrath.\nHe also said that especially\nRecently, due to the death of his beloved, he is very sad and is extremely saddened by Daksha's harsh words.\nIn such a situation, Brahma suggested to him that it would be beneficial for him that\nhe immediately went to him and asked for forgiveness.\nNeither am I a Yagya, nor am I a Yuyamanya.\nThese are the body-born sages, the essence of them.\nThey know the proof of strength and valor.\nWhoseself-will is the method to be determined. 7>. Meaning of the word:\nNa- not; Aham-- I; Na-- not; Yagya-- T=; Na- not; Cha- also; Yuyam-- all of you; Anye- others; Ye- that; Deha- body; Bhajah- to worship; Munayah- sages; Cha- also; Tatvam- truth; Vi