          "textEn": "30\nWa--or; yasyasya--of Shiva; atmatantrasya--of self-reliant Shiva; kah--what; upayam--means; vidhitsheti--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; vidhitasya--to find out; v.\n\nBrahma said that neither he himself, nor Indra, nor all the members present in the Yagya place, nor\nall the sages can know how powerful Shiva is. In such a state, who will be there\nwho dares to commit sin at the lotus feet of them? Meaning: When Brahma advised the gods to go to Shiva and ask for forgiveness, this\nsuggestion was given that how should this matter be presented before them and how should they be pleased?\nShould it be done? Brahma also explained that no living being, even he himself and all the gods,\ndoes not know the method of pleasing Shiva. But he said, \"It is known that they can be pleased immediately,\ntherefore we should try to please them by falling at their lotus feet. 8,\n\nIn reality, a subordinate should always seek refuge in God. This is the teaching of the Bhagavad Gita.\nGod tells everyone to renounce all kinds of ostentatious positions and to come to His refuge.\nFor that, he says. By this, the living being is freed from all the bonds of sin. Similarly, here Brahma suggested that they go to Shivji and take refuge in his lotus feet, because of their\nextremely compassionate nature and being pleased with simplicity, the work will be done. He who is united with the gods, the best of the gods,\nAnd with the fathers, the best of the fathers. Yayau Swadhishnayannilayam Puradvishah\nKailasamadripavaram priyam prabhoh nen\nShabdartham\n\n|: — He (Brahma)