          "textEn": "37\n\nIt happens.\n\nAnother important thing is that Lord Govinda is called Tirthapada. Tirtha means,\n“A holy place’ and Eda means, “The lotus feet of God”.\" People go to holy places to get rid of their\nsins. The meaning is that those who are devoted to the lotus feet of Lord Krishna\nbecome pure by themselves. The lotus feet of God are called Tirthapada,\nbecause under their protection, hundreds and thousands of saintly men sanctify pilgrimage sites. The great Acharya of the Gaudiya Vaishnava sect, Srila Narottamdas Thakur, says that we do not need to go to various pilgrimage sites.\nUndoubtedly, the journey from one place to another is painful, but\none who is wise can take refuge in the lotus feet of Govinda, by which he becomes automatically pure as a result of his pilgrimage.\nWhoever is steadfast in the service of the lotus feet of Govind,\nis a pilgrim; he does not need to travel to pilgrimage sites, because by being engaged in the service of the lotus feet of God, he can reap all the benefits of such a journey. Such a pure devotee\nwho has unwavering faith in the lotus feet of God, wherever he decides to live in any part of the world,\nit becomes a pilgrimage site. ©. Tirthikurvant Tirthanis (Bhagwat 1.13.10) | Such places become pure\ndue to the presence of devotees, if God or his pure devotee resides in any place,\nthen it automatically transforms into a pilgrimage site. In other words, such a pure devotee who is a hundred percent\nintent on serving God, can live in any part of the world, and that place\nquickly becomes a holy place, where he can serve God according to His will.\nYayastatsnavabhrashtanavakunkumapijaram |\nVitrushopi pibantyambhah payayanto gaja gajih. 26). Meaning of the word.\n\nBuby Par Jor myname Sh Sakhi,\nGaji:--Hathinis.After bathing in water by the beautiful women of heaven, the kumkum of their bodies"
