          "textEn": "75.\nMurdhanyam Dhrutanjaliputa Upatasthuradhokshajam. 23 ज़a. Meaning of the word\n\nTatu-tejasa--with the shining radiance of their body; Hat-rucha--with a dull glow; Sanna-jihla--with a silent tongue; Sa-sadhvasah--\nfrightened by their fear; Murghwa--with the head; Dhrita-ankhali-putaah--with hands on the head; Upatasthah--prayed; Adhokshajam--\nAdhokshaja of God..\n\nWith the intensity of Narayan's physical radiance, the radiance of all others faded, and everyone's\nspeech stopped. Frightened by surprise and respect, everyone placed their hands on their heads\nand became ready to praise Lord Adhokshaja.\nThose who are always with him, whose minds are always with him.\nAs they please, they praise the form of grace. 24). Meaning of the word\n\nApi--even now; Arvak--beyond mental activities; Yasya-whose; Mahi-fame; Tu-but); Atmabhu-\nAdayah-by Brahma and others; Yathamati-as per their own ability; Gruntanti-sm-praised; Krita-anugraha-by their\nAnugraha-revealed; Vigraham-divine form \\.\n\nAlthough even gods like Brahma were unable to estimate the infinite glory of God,\nthey could all see his divine form by the grace of God. Therefore, they can respectfully praise each other according to their respective\ncapabilities.\n\nMeaning: God is eternally infinite, and it is difficult even for a man like Brahma to describe His glories. It is said that the direct incarnations of God are infinite faces, and they\nFrom each face, from infinite time, they have been trying to describe the glory of God, yet\nThe description of their glories could not be completed.\nIt is not possible for an ordinary man to understand the infinite glory of God,\nto attain or to describe it, but according to their own strength, people can praise Him.\nSo they can do it. This power increases with the spirit of service. Sevonukhe hi jihva ka arth hai ki jibh se\nBhagwan kau seva praramb hoti hai. This is indicative of Kirtan, from Hare Krishna Kirtan, serving God.\nThe beginning can be done.\nThe second function of the tongue is to taste and accept the offerings of God.\nIs. We should start serving the infinite with our tongue, and we should be skilled in chanting and accepting the Prasad of God.\nThe meaning of accepting the Prasad of God is to control all the senses"
