          "textEn": "79. Rudra said,\nYour boon is for the sake of fulfilling all desires.\nEven by the sages, with devotion and respect, it is worthy of being accepted. If the created mind is not bound by the unmanifested world,\nHe who chants does not count the supreme truth by the grace of the Supreme. 29). Meaning of the word\n\nRudra said--Shiva said; Tav--yours; Var--great; Akhrau-- precious lotus feet; Ashisha-- by wish;\nIha- in this world; Akhil- for fulfillment of all; Hi api- certainly; Munibhishah- by the sages; Asaktahi- free; Adrena- with respect;\nApaviddham- impure deeds; Japati- says; Nagaye- do not know the value; Tat- that; Tvat- by your grace; Par- by your grace;\nKrupah- by your grace..\n\nShivaji said: O God, my mind and my consciousness constantly remain fixed on your venerable lotus feet,\nwhich, being the source of the fulfillment of all boons and desires, are worshiped by all liberated\ngreat sages because your lotus feet alone are worthy of worship.\nIn your lotus feet,\nKeeping the mind steady, I do not deviate from those people who, by saying this, criticize me,\nThat my deeds are not pure. I do not care about their accusations, and I, in the same way,\nout of compassion, forgive them, just as you show compassion towards all living beings. Meaning: Here, Shivji expresses remorse for being angry and destroying Daksha's Yagya (sacrificial ritual) work.\nKing Daksha had insulted him in many ways, due to which, being angry, he completely ruined his\nYagya celebration. Later, upon their being pleased, all the Yagya (sacrificial) work was completed again. Therefore, they expressed regret for their actions. Now they say that because their mind\nremains stable at the lotus feet of God, therefore they are not disturbed even a bit by those ordinary critics who criticize their conduct.\nIt should be understood from this statement of Shiva that when\nas long as a man lives on the physical level, he remains influenced by the three qualities of nature,\nbut as soon as he starts doing Krishna devotion, these physical activities do not affect him. Therefore, a human being should always remain steadfast in the nectar of Krishna consciousness and remain engaged in the divine love of God"
