िए वध किया गया था।\nपशु की बलि होते और उसको पुनः तरुण होते देखना एक मनोहारी दश्य होना था, किन्तु अब वैसा",
          "textEn": "84\n* Your octagonal form is as good as your quadrilateral form.\"There is no doubt in this.\nO beloved,\nThis sacrifice was created for your Yagya (sacrificial fire),\nBy the destructive Pashupati (Lord Shiva), from the first Daksha Kopa (Kopa).\nThat which is not, is not, the ashes of the corpse, the fire, the lord of Yagya, the lotus-faced one, the state, purify it. 33). Meaning of the word\n\nPalyah uchu:-- The wives of the Yagya-karta said; Yagya:-- Yagya; Ayam:-- This; Tava:-- Yours; Yajnaya:-- for the purpose of worship; Kena:-- by Brahma; Srishta:-- organized; Vidhwasta:-- destroyed; Pashupatinah:-- by Shiva; Adya:-- today; Daksha:-- from anger;\nTamah:-- This; Nah:-- ours; Tvam:-- you; Shavah:-- corpse; Aabhah:-- like; Shantam:-- peaceful; Medham:-- peaceful sacrifice; Yagya:--\nAtman:-- O lord of the Yagya; Nalin:-- lotus; Rucha:-- beautiful; Hasha:-- with the sight of your eyes; Punihi:-- purify.\n.\nThe wives of the sacrificers said: O Lord, that sacrifice was arranged according to Brahma's orders,\nbut unfortunately, being enraged by Daksha, Shiva destroyed the entire scene, and\ndue to their anger, the animals brought for the purpose of the sacrifice are lying lifeless. Therefore, all the preparations for the Yagya\nhave become useless. Now, by the gaze of your lotus-like eyes, may the purity of this Yagya place be restored again. Meaning: In the Yagya (sacrificial fire), animals were sacrificed to give new life to them; there,\nthe purpose of bringing the animals was this. In the Yagya, the sacrifice of animals and giving it new life\nwere proofs of mantra chanting power.\nUnfortunately, when Shiva destroyed Daksha's Yagya, some animals\nwere also killed (one was killed to be sacrificed at Daksha's head). Their bodies were scattered\nand the sacrificial site became a cremation ground. As a result, the real purpose of the Yagya was lost.\n\nSince such Yagyas are performed with the aim of Lord Vishnu, therefore the Yaji's wives\nprayed to Vishnu that they should cast a glance at the sacrificial site through unintentional grace so that the\nprogram of the Yagya could be started. In summary, let's not unnecessarily kill animals. They were used for testing the power of mantras,\nand they had to regain youth through the power of the mantra. Their killing was not necessary, as Daksha was killed by Shiva for putting an animal head on his head. The sacrifice of the animal and seeing it again young, was a captivating sight, but now it is not like that"
