          "textEn": "88\nHis dead body is decorated. In this way, after decorating with ornaments, a funeral procession is taken out.\nIt goes. In this way, the decoration of the corpse has no real meaning, because the soul has already\npassed away. Similarly, without Krishna consciousness, no kingdom, no social\nprestige, or progress in material civilization is like a decorated corpse. Daksha's wife's name was Prasuti, and\nshe was the daughter of Swayambhuva Manu. Her sister Devahuti married Kardama Muni, and they were Lord Kapil\nDev's mother off. Thus, Prasuti was the aunt of Lord Vishnu, often. She was showing affection to Lord Vishnu\nout of kindness; since she was his aunt, she was especially seeking special grace from him. This\nverse also has the special feature that it praises Vishnu along with Lakshmi. Wherever\nVishnu's worship is done, there naturally Lakshmi ji's grace remains. Lord Vishnu is\ncalled nectar or divine.\nBrahma and Shiva, along with all the gods, were created after the creation, but\nVishnu was also present before the creation. Therefore, they are called Amrit. Vaishnavas worship Vishnu with his\ninner power. Daksha's wife, the midwife, prayed to God to make the priests Vaishnavas,\nso that they would not remain merely performers of sacrifices for the fruits of desire.\n\nLokapala Uchu:\nDrihah kim no hagbhirasadagrahai: Tvam\nPratyagdashta dashyate yena vishwam.\nMaya hayesha bhavadiya hi bhuman: Yastvam shashtah panchabhir bhasi bhutaih. 37). Meaning of the word\nLok-palaah-- administrators of different worlds; Ouchchu-- said; Dashtah-- seen; Kim-- what; Nah-- by us; Dagbhih-- from the senses;\nIndriyasah-- by the senses; Asat-grahaih-- those who reveal the world; Tvam- you; Pratyaksha-seer-- inner witness; Dashyate- is seen; Yena- by which; Vishcham-universe; Maya- the material world; Hi-because; Esha-this; Bhavadiya-yours; Hi-certainly;\nEarth--O Lord of the Universe; Yah--because; Tvam--you; Shashthah--sixth; Daal--five; Panchabhih-