rial world, due to which their origin, state, and\nMay destruction happen. They themselves are not subject to external power, they are directly without material qualities\nThey are free from various manifestations and are far from false illusion and delusion. Meaning: This verse describes two situations. One is the origin, state, and\ndestruction of the physical world, and the other is God's own state. In the abode of God, that is, in his kingdom"
