          "textEn": "209\nAnd Dakshayani, having been killed, Sati, in the past.\nFrom the birth of Himavat, in the field, we heard that. 58. Meaning of the word\n\nEvam--in this way; Dakshayani--Daksha's daughter; Hittva- having abandoned; Sati- Sati; Purva- Kalevaram- her previous body;\nJajne- born; Himavatah- of the Himalayas; Kshetre- in the field; Menayam- in Menayam; Iti- thus; Shushrum- I have heard\nIt is..\nMaitreya said: I have heard that after abandoning the body obtained from Daksha, Dakshayani (daughter of Daksha) took birth in the Himalayan kingdom. She was born as the daughter of Mena. I have heard this from\nauthentic sources. Meaning: Menaka also called Menaka is the wife of King of Himalayas.\nYou alone are the cause, again and again, the one who is greatly enriched, O consort of the Mother.\nThe power that is inseparable, in one's own way, is like a sleeping man. 59>. Meaning of the word\n\nTam-us (Shiva) to; Ev-certainly; Dayitam-beloved; Bhuyah-again; Agg-accepted; Patim-in the form of husband;\nAmbika- Ambika or Sati; Ananya-devoted; Ek-agatim-one goal; Shakti-(stative and external),\nFemale powers; Supta-inactive; Iva-like; Pirusham-man (Shiva as the representative of God) +\n\nAmbika (Durga), who was called Dakshayani (Sati), again accepted Shiva as her husband, Just as the various powers of God work at the time of the new creation. Meaning: The Supreme Power is heard in various forms. - According to this Vedic mantra, Lord Kau has many powers. Power is a force and God is a man. The duty of a chi is to serve under the male. As the Bhagavad-gita says, all souls are the manifestations of the one God.\nTherefore, all\nliving beings have the duty to serve this Supreme Being. In this physical world, Durga is the symbol of both internal and external powers, and Shiva is the symbol of the supreme being. Shiva and Ambika or\nDurga's relationship is eternal. Sati, besides Shiva, cannot accept another as her husband. Further,\nJust as Shiva married Durga or Himalaya's daughter, Himavati, and Kartikeya\nwas born, it is a long story in itself."
