          "textEn": "22\nDid not produce offspring. This narrative was about the descendants of Brahma, who was born from Manu's daughter, Prasuti. The daughter of Prasuti was Dakshayani or Sati, about whom the story of Daksha Yagna was told. Maitreya is now\ntalking about the lineage of Brahma's sons. Among the many sons of Brahma, Sanakadi were celibate.\nAnd Narad did not marry, therefore, there is no question of describing the history of their descendants. The wife of the illusionary dharma is the earth, and the illusion is the enemy.\nThe union of the two is in the unborn, without birth. 2). Meaning of the word:\n\nMrisha--Mrisha; Adharmasya--of Adharma; Barya--Woman; Aasit--was; Dambhamu--False Pride; Mayam--Deceit; Cha--And; Shatru-Han--The destroyer of enemies; Asut--Did; Mithunam--Marriage; Tat-That; Tu-But; Niruti-Niruti; Jagruhe-Accepted;\nKarita--Accepted; Aprajah-Without offspring L\n\nBrahma's other son was Adharmasya, whose wife's name was Mrisha. By their coincidence, two demons were born.\nWhose names were Dambh, meaning deceiver, and Maya, meaning thug.\nThese two were taken away by an Asura named Nirriti,\nbecause he had no children. Meaning: Here it is known that Brahma had a son named Adharma, who married his sister\nMrisha. This is the beginning of the subjective life between brother and sister. In human society, such an unnatural combination is possible only where there is unrighteousness. It is revealed that in the beginning of creation,\nBrahma not only produced virtuous sons like Sanak, Sanatan, and Narad, but also produced demonic offspring named Nirruti,\nAdharma, Dambh, and Mrisha. In the beginning, Brahma created every object. It is said about Narad that his previous life was pure and his company was good.\nTherefore, he was born as Narad. Other sons also were born according to their ability and background. The law of Karma continues for lifetimes, and when a new creation happens, then the same Karma\nreturns with the living souls.\nThese all, according to their respective actions, with various abilities,\nwere born, although their original father is Brahma, who is the embodiment of the qualities of God.\nToyah samabhavallobho nikrutishcha mahamate."
