          "textEn": "223\nWith exclusive devotion, being absorbed in one's own duty,\nHaving established the mind, worship the Supreme Being. 22). Meaning of the word\n\nTam--that; Ev--also; Vatsa--my son; Ashray-- take refuge; Bhritya-vatsalam-- of God, who is very merciful to his devotees; Mumukshubhimahi- those who desire liberation, they also; Mrigya-- going in search; Pad-abja-- lotus feet;\nPadhitim-- system; Ananya-bhave-- in solitary emotion; Nija-dharma-bhavite-- in one's original natural state; Manasi-- to the mind;\nAvasthapya-keeping; Bhajasva - keep on worshipping; Purusham- the Supreme Being..\n\nMy son, you too should seek refuge in God, because He is very merciful to His devotees. Those who desire liberation from the cycle of birth and death always take refuge in the lotus feet of God with devotion. Having done your assigned work, being pure, in your heart,\nestablish God and remain absorbed in his service without being disturbed even for a moment.\nMeaning: The method of Bhakti Yoga that Suniti told her son is an ideal method of attaining God-realization. Every person, while performing their natural, emotional work, along with that, can keep God residing in their heart. God himself gave this same teaching to Arjuna in the Bhagavad Gita,\n\"Keep fighting and keep me in your mind.\"\"In Krishna consciousness, every\ndevout person who desires perfection should have this ideal. In this context, Queen Suniti gave advice to her son,\nthat God is called Bhrutiyaatshal, that is, he is very merciful to his devotees. She said, \"You\nhaving been humiliated by your mother-in-law, you have come to me crying, but I cannot do good to you.\nBut Krishna is so merciful to his devotees that if you go to him, his affection and\nhis gentle behavior will be greater than that of millions of mothers like me.\" When someone else is unable to alleviate someone's\nsorrow, then only Shri Krishna helps the devotee.\nSuniti also emphasized on this\nthat the action of reaching G