महालक्ष्मी जी",
          "textEn": "224\nDid not advise to do, only told them to go to the refuge of God, so that accomplishment is attained\nAs soon as a person enshrines God in his heart, every work becomes easy and success\nis achieved. Otherwise, then, with the sight of the lotus-like feet,\nI hunt the sorrowful deer, every single one.\nHe who is hunted by the hand, holding the foot,\nAnd the other deer, while being hunted. 23). Meaning of the word\n\nNot other, not others; Tatha - therefore; Pada-palash-lochanat - from the lotus-eyed Lord; Dukha-chidam - reducing the sufferings of others;\nTey-yours; Mrigayami- I am in search; Kanchana - someone else; Yah-who; Mugyate- is firm; Hasta-held-\nPadaya- with lotus in hand; Shriya- Goddess of wealth; Ith-from others; Ank-my son; Vimrugyamana- worshipped..\n\nOh dear Dhruva, besides the God with eyes like lotus petals, I don't see anyone\nwho can alleviate your sorrows.\nMany gods like Brahma are eager to please Lakshmi Devi,\nbut Lakshmi herself, holding a lotus flower in her hand, is always ready to serve God. Meaning: Suniti points out that the blessings received from God and other Gods are not the same. Foolish people say that whichever deity you worship, you will get the same result, but\nthe fact is not so. It is also said in the Bhagavad Gita that the boons received from the gods are momentary and\nare for the ignorant. In other words, since all the gods are bound by the physicality of the living being,\ntherefore, even though they are seated in high positions, their boons cannot be permanent. Permanent boon.\nIt is spiritual, because the soul is eternal. In the Bhagavad Gita, it is also said that those whose minds\nare struck, they only worship the gods. Therefore, Suniti said to her son that instead of becoming a recipient of the gods'\ngrace, he should go to God to reduce his suffering.\nGod controls material opulence through his various powers, especially the goddess of wealth. Therefore, those who are in search of opulence, they want to become worthy of the grace of the goddess of wealth. Here,\neven the great gods worship the goddess of wealth, but the goddess of wealth, Mahalakshmi ji"
