          "textEn": "232\nIt is. When we fall into suffering, we should understand that the fruit of our sinful deeds is decreasing.\nIs. If we, instead of being attached to the happiness and sorrow derived from sin and virtuous deeds, want to overcome this ignorance,\nthen we should accept God's will, no matter what the situation may be,\nwe should accept it. In this way, if we take refuge in God, then we can escape from the clutches of this material world. The one who is more virtuous is overcome by the one who is less virtuous.\nFriendship is destroyed by equal ones, and is overcome by the one who is superior. 34). Meaning of the word:\n\nGreater than a virtuous man--more worthy; pleased--experiencing; experiencing--experiencing; compassionate--kind; lesser than a virtuous man--less worthy; equal to a virtuous man--equal; desiring--desiring; suffering--suffering;\nBecomes overwhelmed--becomes overwhelmed.\n\nEvery person should behave in such a way that: if he is more worthy than himself\nIf you meet a person, you should be very happy, if you meet someone less capable than yourself,\nyou should be kind to them, and if you meet people of equal ability, you should be friendly with them. In this way, the three types of heat of this material world never affect a human being.\nThey are unable to do so. Meaning: Generally, upon finding someone more capable than oneself, we start envying them,\nUpon meeting someone less capable than oneself, we make fun of them, and upon finding someone equal to oneself,\nwe become proud of our actions. This is the reason for all physical suffering. Therefore,\nNarad Muni preached that a devotee should act with restraint. Instead of hating someone more capable than yourself, one should welcome them with joy. Instead of bringing pain to a less capable person, one should be compassionate towards them so that they can rise to a proper level.\nAnd when meeting someone with similar qualities,\none should not express pride in their actions in