uru.\nThe supreme guru is Shri Krishna, who\nis called Chaitya Guru, which means the Supreme Soul, who resides in the heart of every being. As it is said in the Bhagavad Gita, the Supreme Soul helps from within and sends a guru who helps from outside. The Guru is the Chaitya Guru, meaning that the external manifestation of the Supreme Being residing in the heart of each being."
