          "textEn": "248.\nSmayamanam--The laughter of the Lord; Abhidhyayet--Meditate on Him; Sa-anuraga-avalokanam--With utmost affection towards the devotees; Nivethena--In this way, regularly; Ek-bhuthena--With utmost care; Manasa--With mind-only-mind; Var-da-r-bharam--Meditate on the bestower of boons..\n\nGod always keeps smiling, and the devotee should always keep seeing Him in this form.\nBecause He casts a merciful gaze upon the devotees. In this way, the meditator should\nkeep gazing towards the God who gives all boons. Meaning: In this context, the word 'niyaten' is very meaningful, because it indicates that the aforementioned\nshould be meditated upon only by a definite method.\nA person should not adopt any new method of meditation on Shri Bhagwan,\nbut rather follow authentic scriptures and great men. By this method, a person can continue to practice concentrating his mind\non God until he becomes so stable that he remains in Samadhi and constantly thinks about the form of God. Used here\nThe meaning of the word Ekashuten, ** very carefully and with attention, is '' . If someone remains focused on the physical form of God,\nthen he does not fall into misfortune.\nTE Bhagwato Rupam Subhadram Dhyayato Manah. That which is accomplished through practice, does not cease. 52). Meaning of the word:\n\n'Evam--in this way; Bhagavatah--of the Lord; Rupam--form; Su-bhadram--extremely auspicious; Dhyayatah--while meditating;\nManah--mind; Nirvrittya--free from all material impurities; Paraya--divine; Turmoo--quickly; Sampanna--becoming prosperous; Na--never; Nivartate--comes down.\n.\n\nOne who, while concentrating his mind in the eternally auspicious form of God, meditates in this way,\nquickly gets rid of all material impurities and does not return downwards (to the mortal world) from the state of meditation of God. Meaning: Stillness of attention is called Samadhi as illustrated here. In the love and devotion of God,\nA person who is constantly engaged cannot be distracted from his meditation. In the temple, for the worship of the deity, in the Pancharatra Bhakti method, the worship that is described, in that, the devotee constantly contemplates God,\nthis is Samadhi. He who practices in this way, from the service of God"
