          "textEn": "265\nOnly for that, food should be taken, not for luxury. Dhruva Maharaj was an Acharya, but by doing penance, he\nwanted to teach us how devotion can be done. We should understand the process of devotion to Dhruva Maharaj\nin a good way. How much suffering they endured, this will be told in the next verses.\nWe must always remember that becoming an authentic devotee of God is not an easy task, but\nin this era, it has become easy with the grace of Lord Chaitanya. But if we cannot even follow the generous\norders of Chaitanya Mahaprabhu, then how can we hope to perform the regular duties of devotion?\nHow can we be able to do it? In this era, it is difficult to follow the penance of Dhuv Maharaj, but the rules should be followed. We should not violate the procedures prescribed by the gurus because they\ntell them to be simple for the bound soul.\nAs far as our ISKCON movement is concerned, we only\nsay that man should follow four prohibitive rules, chant sixteen malas, and without putting the tongue\nin taste, accept only the one offering given to God. It does not mean that if\nwe fast, then God should also fast. Offer the best possible offering to God, but our\npurpose should not be to satisfy our own taste. As far as possible, consume simple food,\nSo that the body can be sustained for devotion. It is our duty to always remember that we are insignificant compared to Dhruva Maharaj. It is absolutely impossible for us to do what they did for self-realization because\nwe are incapable of doing such service.\nBut for this era, Chaitanya Mahaprabhu has given us all kinds of exemptions.\nTherefore, let us remember that the fulfillment of our purpose cannot be achieved by not performing our duties for the sake of devotion.\nOur ultimate duty is to follow the footsteps of Dhruva Maharaj, because\nhe was a very firm devotee. We too should take a vow to complete our tasks to do devotion in this life.\nWe should not wait for another life to complete this