          "textEn": "27]\nIf you read the character of the Maharaj, then understanding it will not be difficult at all. Oh God, I call upon you.\nI do not know any other way to relieve the distress of the Lord's life.\nOh Lord of all beings and the entire creation,\nI seek liberation from this suffering.\nHaving attained you, we are your refuge. 81. Meaning of the word:\n\nDevah uchu- The gods said; Na- No; Evam- Thus; Vidamah- We understand; Bhagavan- O Lord; Prana-\nRodham- The breath that is constricted; Char- Walking; Acharasya- Of the unmoving; Akhil- Universal; Satva- Existence; Dhamnah- Abode;\nVidhehi- By showing kindness; Tat- Therefore; Na- Our; Vrijinaat- From the difficulty; Vimoksha- Deliverance; Praptah-\nHaving come near; Vayam- We all; Tvam- To you; Sharanam- Refuge; Sharanyam- Entitled to refuge.\n\nThe gods said: Oh God, you are the refuge of all inert and conscious souls. We\nfeel that all beings are suffocating, and their breathing has been obstructed. We've never had such an experience.\nYou are the ultimate refuge of all the refugees, therefore we have come to you.\nPlease save us from this crisis.\n\nMeaning: As a result of the devotion to God, the gods were also experiencing the effect of Dhuv Maharaj,\nwho had never experienced such a thing before. Yd Maharaj's breath was held\nUpon his death, the breath of all the worlds was stopped. If it is not God's will, then the physical beings cannot breathe,\nwhile the divine souls can breathe. Physical beings are the result of the external power of God,\nwhile divine souls are of the internal power. The gods, the controllers of both types of beings,\nwere brought to God to find out why their breaths were being blocked. In this world, for the solution of all kinds of problems, God is the ultimate goal. In the spiritual world, there are no problems,\nbut the physical world is full of problems.\nBecause God is the master of both worlds,\ntherefore, when problems arise, it is better to approach Him. Those who are devotees, in this world,\nhave no problems. Vi Purnayukhayate (Chaitanya Charitamrita) - Devotees are free from all problems\nbecause they are completely surrendered to God. For a devotee, every object in this world is extremely joyful,\nbecause he knows how to use it for divine devotion to God."
