          "textEn": "274\n(Nine\nGd Maharaj's return home\nMaitreya said\nThen, in fear of eagerness, he hurried\nKritavanamaha: Prayayustrishvipam.\nThousand-headed, then Garutmana\nMadhurvanam Bhrityadidrishtaya Gatah. 1>. Meaning of the word:\nMaitreya said—Maitreya Muni said; Te—the deities; Evam—in this way; Uttsannabhayaah— free from all kinds of fear;\nUrukrame—to Lord, whose actions are divine; Krita-avanamaah— saluted; Prayayuhu— they returned; Tri-\nVishtapam—to their respective abodes; Sahasra-shirsha api— even the one with a thousand heads; Tatah—from there; Garutmatata-\nHaving mounted Garuda; Madhouh vanam—Madhuvan; Bhritya- Dasah—Servant; Dihakshaya—with the desire to see; Gatah—went..\nMaharishi Metreya said to Vidur: When God reassured the gods in this way again,\nthey were freed from all kinds of fear, and they all bowed to him and went to their respective\ndivine abodes. Tan Bhagwan, who is the direct incarnation of Sahasrashirsha, mounted on Garuda,\nwent to Madhuvan to see his servant Dhruva.\nMeaning: The word Sahasrarsha is used for Vishnu in the Garbhodakashaya form. Although God\nappeared as Kshirodakshayi Vishnu, but here he is described as Garbhodakshayi Sahasrashirsham Vishnu\nbecause he is inseparable from Garbhodakshayi Vishnu. Srila Sanatan Goswami in his\nBhagavatayuta has described this form of Vishnu as a Pishnigarbha incarnation. They created the Dhuvlok's creation for Dhuv Maharaj to live in. The intense yoga-vipakativriya (result of yoga practice)\nAppeared in the lotus of the feet, like a flash of lightning.\nIt disappeared, and then, with a hundred thousand signs,\nIt was seen outside, remaining in its state. 2). Shabdartham\nSaha-- Dhuv Maharaj; Vai- also; Dhiya- with attention; Yoga- Vipaka- intensely; Hat- of the heart; Pada-\nKoshe- on the lotus; Sphuritam- manifested; Tadit- like lightning; Tirohitam- disappeared; Sahasam- suddenly;\nEva- also; Upalaschya- seeing; Bahi- situated outside; Tat- in that posture; Dadarsha- saw