          "textEn": "287\nOne, the supreme Lord, by the power of His own self-power,\nWith the qualities of illusion and other qualities, the great beginning and the endless.\nThe Supreme Being, who is beyond creation, in His unmanifest qualities,\nAnd in the manifested qualities, He shines forth. 7/. Meaning of the word\n\nOne-- one; you-- certainly; Bhagavan-- O Lord; this-- this material world; by self-power-- by one's own power;\nBy Maya-- by name of Maya; 36-- extremely powerful; by qualities-- endowed with the qualities of nature; great-- greatness; etc.- etc.; unbounded-- infinite; created-- having created; again entering-- entering again; the Supreme Being-- the Supreme Soul; that-- of Maya; unreal-- unreal; in every way-- in every way; like-- as if; in wood, in pieces; like fire-- like fire; appearing-- appearing..\n\nOh Lord, you are the best, but you appear in the spiritual and material worlds in different ways due to your various\npowers. You, with your external power,\nby generating all the power of the physical world, later in the physical world, as God,\nyou enter.\nYou are the supreme being and create various kinds of creation from transient qualities, which\nis such that fire, entering into various shaped pieces of wood, shines in various forms\nand burns. Meaning: Dhuv Maharaj realized that God works through his various powers, he\ndoes not become zero or without attributes, and thus becomes omnipresent. A Mayavadi thinker thinks that\nGod is pervading the entire visible world, therefore he has no form. But by the realization of Vedic knowledge,\nby knowing, here Dhruva says, '' You are pervading the entire visible world through your power.\"\" This\npower is truly transcendental, but because it is temporarily functional in the physical world, it is called Maya. In other words, besides the devotees, for everyone else, the power of God is the external power.\nIs. King Dhruva understood this fact well. And also understood that Shakti and\nShaktimaan 