          "textEn": "290\nOn the head, his conch FAT, so the real knowledge manifested from within and Dhruva Maharaj could understand the divine form of God. Here, Dhruva Maharaj admits that he was not only ignorant,\nbut also a child in age. If God had not blessed them, then for the innocent child,\nit would not have been possible to recognize the supreme form of God. Having consumed all this in the stomach,\nI am engaged in the battle of the gods,\nWhose ocean of gold is the lotus-like womb,\nI bow to that God. 94. Meaning of the word\n\nAt the end of the cycle--At the end of the cycle; Etat--This universe; Akhilam--All; Jathrena--Within the stomach; Grihan-Lekhin-like; Shet-like--\nLying down; Puman-like--Like a human; Swa-Hak-like--Looking at oneself; Anant-like--Like an infinite being; Sakha-like--With; Tat-like--Like that;\nAngke--In his lap; Yat-like--Whose; Nabhi-like--From the navel; Sindhu-like--Like the ocean; Ruha-like--Like the sky; Lok-like--Like the world;\nOf lotus-like feet; womb--flower cluster; divine--Lord Brahma; Bhagavate--to the Lord; Pranata--bowing; Asmi--I;\nTo him..\n\nOh Lord, at the end of each kalpa, Lord Vishnu, who is in the Garbhodakashayi form, appears in the universe.\nHe encompasses every object that appears in the universe within his stomach. He lies down in the lap of Sheshnag.\nA golden lotus-pusya emerges from a stem from his navel, and Brahmaji is born on this lotus-flower. I can understand that you are God. Therefore, I respectfully\ngreet you. Meaning: The knowledge of God that Dhuv Maharaj had was perfect. It is said in the Vedas -- In whom one knows,\nAll this is known, by the divine unselfish grace of the Lord, the knowledge attained is so complete that the devotees\nBy that knowledge, the Lord becomes acquainted with various creations. In front of Dhruva Maharaj, the one with the milky ocean,\nVishnu was present.\nThey could also understand the other two forms of God, Garbhodakshayi Vishnu and Karanodakshayi (Maha).\nV