          "textEn": "29\n\nI worship Govinda, the supreme being. At the end of each kalpa, when all the worlds dissolve, then every object enters the Garbhodakashayi\nVishnu's body, who lies in the lap of Sheshnag, another form of God. Those who are not devotees cannot understand anything about the various forms of Vishnu and their situations towards creation. Sometimes atheists argue, \"How can a lotus-bearing Vishnu's navel\ncome out by bursting?\".\"They treat all the sayings of the scriptures as stories. Due to their inexperience in the subject of the ultimate truth and their hesitation in accepting evidence, they\nbecome increasingly atheistic; they are unable to understand God.\nBut a devotee like Dhuv Maharaj\nKeeps knowing the various forms of God and their positions by the grace of God. It is said that on whom\nEven a little bit of God's grace happens, he can understand their glory, other people keep contemplating on the ultimate truth\nBut they are not able to understand God. In other words, until a human\ndoes not come into contact with a devotee, until then he cannot understand the divine form or the spiritual world and its divine\nactivities. You are eternally free, pure, and enlightened soul.\nThe one who is the original man, the lord of the gods.\nThat which is situated in the unbroken state, with one's own vision,\nThe seer is situated, without any other desire. Eye\nMeaning of the word\n\nTvam- Tumah Nitya- Shashwatah Mukta- Mukta; Parishuddha- Vishuddha; Vibuddha- With knowledge; Atma- Supreme soul; Kut- Stha-\nWithout change; Adi- Original; Purusha- Man; Bhagavan- Complete with six opulences, Bhagavan; Tri- Adhisha- Master of the three qualities;\nYat- From where; Buddhi- of intellectual work; Avasthitim- of all states; Akhanditaya- unbroken, complete; Swa- of self; Drishti- by sight; Drashtaa- seer; Sthitau- of being; Brahmaanda- of universe; Adhimakhah- the enjoyer of all sacrifices; Vyatiriktaah- distinct, separate; Prakaar se- of type; Asae- t