          "textEn": "298\nA devotee is such that even when wealth is present, he will not be distracted by divine love. This example proves that a very worthy devotee can have devotion to God along with the convenience of material pleasures. But this was a special condition. Where the auspicious, steadfast, and unshakeable moon is established,\nWhere the planets and astrologers are not disturbed,\nWhere the moon, like a wheel, is situated, beyond the abode of the gods. 20>. Dharmo Agni: Kashyapah, Shukro Munayah, these forest dwellers.\nThey wander, performing the southern rituals, they rejoice, these stars. 29>. Meaning of the word:\n\nNa-- not; Anyeah-- by others; Adhisthitam-- established; Bhadra-- my good child; Yat-- which; Bhrajishnu- radiant; Dhuv-\nKshiti- place named Dhvalaoka; Yatra- where; Graha- planet; Riksha- constellation; Taranam- like stars; Jyotisham- from constellation;\nChakram- wheel; Aahitam- is done; Medhyam- around the central rod; Go- oxen; Chakra- herd; Vat- like\nSthānu-- steady; Parastānu-- beyond; Kalpa-- a day of Brahma; Vasanām-- of the dwelling places; Dharmā-- Dharma; Agnih-- Fire; Kashyapa: Kashyapa; Shukra: Shukra; Munayah-- of the group of sages; Ye- all; Van-o-Van-o-Van-o-Van-o-Van-o-Van-o-Van-o-Van-o; Charanti-- walking;\nare; Dakshin-kṛtya-- facing to the right; Bhramantah-- circumambulating; Yat-that-that-that-that-that-that-that; Graha-that-that-that-that-that; Sātaraka-that-that-that-that-that;.\n\nGod further said: O Dhruva, I will grant you the radiant planet named Dhruva, which\nwill remain in existence even after the destruction at the end of the eon. Until now, no one has ruled that planet.\nAnd it is surrounded by the entire solar system, planets, and constellations. In the sky, all the planets\ncircumambulate this planet, just as all the oxen circle around a central AE to grind grain.\nReligion, fire, Kashyap and Shukra, like the sages,\nAll the stars settled by keeping YEA to their right and orbiting it, which remains in the same way even after others\nbecome extinct. Meaning: Although the year existed even before Dhruva Maharaj obtained authority,\nBut it had no presiding deity. This Dhruvaloka, which is our Shravatara, is the center of all other stars and\nthe solar system, because all those constellations and the solar system circumambulate Dhruvaloka in the same way as a bull revolves around an intermediate pillar to grind grain. Dhruva desired the best planet (world). And his wish was like that of a child, yet God fulfilled it"
