          "textEn": "299. A small child can ask his father for such a thing, which he has not yet given to anyone.\nWhether it is a river, but even then, the father, out of love, gives him that thing. Similarly, this unique Dhruvaloka\nwas attained by Maharaj Dhruva. The characteristic of this planet is that even after the apocalypse, even in the apocalypse that occurs during Brahma's\nnight, it will remain. The destruction is of two types--one is of Brahma's\nnight and the other is at the end of Brahma's life. At the end of Brahma's life, some chosen\nmen go to the abode of God. Dhuv Maharaj is one of them. God assured Dhruva that he\nwill remain alive even after partial destruction. In this way, upon the complete destruction, they will go directly to Vaikuntha. In this context, Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur's commentary is that Dhruvaloka is like Sretapad, Mathura, and\nDwarka, a world.\nThey are the eternal abodes of God (asm\nparamam) as described in the Bhagavad-gita (asm\nparamam) and the Vedas (8% tad vishnoh WHE pardas sarvashah). Parastat Kalpa-\nThe meaning of the words Vasinam is, \"After the dissolution, beyond the inhabited planets,\" which indicates Vaikunthloka.\nIn other words, God assured Dhuv Maharaj that he would be sent to Vaikunthloka. Having given the forest to his father, he is under the protection of Dharma.\nHe protects sixteen million enemies, and is unafraid. 22). Meaning of the word:\n\nAfter departure; but; Vanam-- forest; Pitra-- by your father; Datta-- by giving; Gam-- the whole world;\nDharma-sanshrayah-- with righteousness; Shat-- thirty-six; Varsh-- year, year; Sahastramu-- one thousand; Rakshita-- you will rule; Avyahata--\nWithout destruction; Indriya-- the power of the senses.\n.\n\nWhen your father gives you the rule of his kingdom and departs for the forest, then you\nwill rule over the entire world for thirty-six thousand years continuously, and all your senses will remain as powerful as they are today. You will never grow old. Meaning: In Satyayuga, people lived for about one lakh years. In those days, it was absolutely possible for Dhuv Maharaj to rule for thirty-six thousand years. In your mind, in the absence of the best, in the destruction of the hunt, your mind is distracted."
