          "textEn": "300\nThey search the forest, the mother enters the fire. 23). Meaning of the word\n\nTvat- your; Bhratari-- brother; Uttame-- best; Nashte-- upon being killed; Mrigayayam-- in hunting; Tu-- your; Tat-manah-- extremely; Shokakul- sorrowful; Anvesanti- searching; Vanam- in the forest; Mata- mother; Daav- fire- in the fire of the forest; Sa- that;\nPraveshyanti- will enter; Praveshyati- will enter..\n\nGod further said: In the near future, your brother will go hunting in the best forest.\nAnd when he is engrossed in hunting, he will be killed. Your wife, Suruchi, will go to the forest in search of her son,\nmad with grief over his death, but there she will be killed by the fire. Meaning: Dhuv Maharaj had come to the forest to search for Lord Kau, and in his mind, the feeling of revenge from his own mother-in-law\nto take revenge off. The mother-in-law had insulted Dhruva, who was no ordinary person,\nbut rather a great Vaishnava. An offense committed against the lotus feet of a Vaishnava is the biggest in the world.\nIt is the biggest offense.\nBecause of insulting Dhruva Maharaj, Suruchi will be mad with the grief of her son's death\nand will enter the fire of desire, which will end her life. Its special\nmention was made by God from Dhuv, because he was eager to take revenge on his mother-in-law. From this, we\nshould take this lesson that even by mistake, we should not insult any Vaishnav. We should not only\ninsult any Vaishnava or anyone without reason. When Suruchi\ninsulted Dhruva Maharaj, he was a small child. Undoubtedly, he did not know that Dhruva\nwas a well-known Vaishnav, therefore he unknowingly committed a crime. When someone unknowingly serves a\nVaishnav, even then, its fruit is good. Shri Bhagwan Vaishnav's special bias\ndoes. By pleasing or displeasing Vaishnav, God's pleasure and displeasure are affected.\nSrila Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur has said in his Guru Ka Ashtapadi prayer-- Yasya Prasadad Bhagwat\nPrasadah-- God is pleased when a pure Vaishnava form of the Guru is pleased by a human, but if he\noffends the Guru, who knows what will happen to him. Ishta Maa Yagyahridayam Yajnahaih Pushkaladakshinah |"
