          "textEn": "302\nUparishtaḥṣibhyastvam yato navaartate gatūna. 25. Meaning of the word\n\nTatha--thereafter; Ganta Asi--you will go; Mat-Sthanam-to my abode; Sarva-Loka-by all the worlds; Namah-Kritam-being saluted; Uparitah-above; Rishibhyah-than the realms of the sages; Tvam-you; Yatah-from where; Na-never; Aavartate-will return; Gatah-having gone there.\n\nBhagwan further said:\n\nLord said further:\n\nYou will return from there.\n\nMeaning of the word:\n\nTatha--thereafter; Ganta Asi--you will go; Mat-Sthanam-to my abode; Sarva-Loka-by all the worlds; Namah-Kritam-being saluted; Uparitah-above; Rishibhyah-than the realms of the sages; Tvam-you; Yatah-from where; Na-never; Aavartate-will return; G Hey Dhruva, in this body, after your physical life, you will go to my realm,\nwhich is always venerable by the inhabitants of all other realms. This is situated above the realms of the Sapta-Rishis,\nand after going there, you will never have to return to this physical world again. Meaning: In this verse, the word 'Navati' is extremely important. God says, *'You will not come again in this material\nworld, because you will reach my abode, that is, my abode.'Therefore, in this\nphysical world, Dharubaloka is the abode of Lord Vishnu. Above it is the Kshirsagar, inside which is the Shwetadvipa.\nIt is also clearly indicated that this world is situated above the seven realms of the sages, and since this is\nVishnu's abode, therefore it is worshiped by all other realms. Here, the question can be raised as to what will happen to this Dhruvaloka at the time of the apocalypse? The answer is simple. Like other Vaikuntha worlds, he remains in the Dhruvaloka. In this context, Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur's commentary is that the word 'nivartate' itself is indicative of\nthat this world is eternal. Maitreya Ubacha\nThus, having spoken, the Lord, turning towards the right, said this to the self:\nSeeing the child, the abode of the self, the Garuda flag. RE Il\nMeaning of the word\n\nMaitreya said--Maitreya Rishi further said; Thus--in this way; Ardhitaḥ--being honored and worshiped; Saha--God; Bhagavan--\nGod; Atidishya--by giving; Atmanah--your own; Padam--dwelling place; Balasya--while the child; Pashyatah--was watching;\nDhama--their abode; Swam--yours, private; Agat-they returned; Garuda-Dhwaja-God Vishnu whose flag has the symbol of Garuda\nin it.\n.\n\nMaitreya Muni said: After being worshiped and honored by the boy Dhruva Maharaj, and giving him his abode, Lord Vishnu, riding on the back of Garuda, Dhruva, while watching, went to his abode.\nHe went."
