          "textEn": "308\nIn the world, they wanted to achieve a position greater than Brahma and assert their dominance. Therefore, as described elsewhere,\nwhen Dhruva Maharaj sat down to compare his resolve and the reward he had finally obtained upon the appearance of God,\nhe realized that he had asked for only a few pieces of broken glass, but\nin return, he received many diamonds. As soon as he saw God before him, he immediately\nrealized how much he had\nasked for a higher position than Brahmaji, even greater than God. When Dhruva Maharaj, after seeing God himself, became situated at the feet of Vasudeva, then all his\nmaterial impurities were removed. In this way, they were embarrassed about what their demand was and what they received. They were displeased by the fact that although they had left their father's kingdom and gone to Madhuvan, and they had received a guru like Narad\nMuni, they were still thinking of taking revenge on their mother-in-law, and in this\nworld, they wanted to take a respected position.\nThis was the reason that even after receiving all the desired boons from God, they were broken. When Dhuv Maharaj actually saw God in front of him, he had neither the feeling of taking revenge on his mother, nor the desire to rule this material world, but\nGod is so merciful that he understood that Dhruva Maharaj has this desire. In front of Dhruva Maharaj,\nWhile speaking, God used the word Vedaham, because when Dhutra Maharaj made a demand for material gains,\nHe knew everything because he was present in their hearts. Whatever a person thinks,\nGod always knows it. In the Bhagavad Gita also, its confirmation has been done in this way-- Vedaham\nGAA |\n\nGod fulfilled all the wishes of Dhruva Maharaj. Towards his brother-in-law and step-brother,\nTheir vengeful mentality was fulfilled; the desire to attain a position superior to his great-grandfather was also fulfilled.\nAnd along with that, his eternal position was determined in the realm of the 