          "textEn": "309\nWhat will he do after receiving? 2 Therefore, he gave Dhruva the opportunity to perform many sacrifices without aging for thirty-six thousand years and to become the most famous king of this world and rule.\nHe provided an opportunity and thus, after all material pleasures, sent Dhruva to the spiritual world,\nwhich includes yore. Ya uvacha\nSamadhina naik bhavena yatpadam\nViduh sanandadayah urdhwaretasah. In the month of Masi, with six months of nudity,\nHaving set out in the shade, he departed. 30>. Meaning of the word.\n\nShruvah Ubacha--Shadruva Maharaj said; Samadhina--in Samadhi through yoga practice; Na--never; Ekabhave--from one birth;\nYat--that; Padam--foot, position; Vidu:--understood; Sanand-Aadih - Sanandan etc. four celibates; Urdhva-retasah--uninterrupted; Brahmachari; in months; Aham--I; Shadibhah-six; Amushya-their; Padayoh-of the lotus feet; Chhayaam-shade, shelter;\nSaran-refuge; Upetya-having attained; Apagatah-fell; Preta-separated; Mati-mind; other than God, my mind is situated on other objects.\n.\n\nDhruva Maharaj thought to himself-- to remain situated in the shadow of the lotus feet of God,\nto try is not an easy task, because even great celibates like Sanandan etc.,\nwho practiced Ashtanga Yoga in Samadhi, only after many births have attained the refuge of the lotus feet of God. I have already achieved the same result in six months, yet I, God,\nbecause of thinking differently, I have fallen from my position. Meaning: In this verse, Dhruva Maharaj himself explains the reason for his sadness. First of all, they\nRepent that it is not easy to have a direct vision of God. Even great saints,\nmen, such as Sanandan, etc., all four celibate-Sanandan, Sanak, Sanatan, and Sanatkumar--many\nhaving practiced yoga for many births, staying in Samadhi, were able to have a direct vision of God. But,\nAs far as the question of Dhruva Maharaj is concerned, he attained the realization of God through devotion for six months.\nTherefore, they hoped that as soon as they met God, they would immediately take them to their abode. They\nAlso clearly understood that God has given them the boon to rule the world for thirty-six thousand years\nbecause they were initially under the control of physical power and took revenge on their mother"
