rishna consciousness, Vaishnava philosophy forbids the devotee from all kinds of material\ndesires. A Vaishnava devotee should always be free from other desires, that is, from the fruits of desireful actions,\nfrom material desires or from philosophical contemplation. In reality, to Dhruva Maharaj"
