          "textEn": "32\nIt is controlled. Bhruva Maharaj came to the conclusion that these gods, being jealous of his devotion,\nopposed him and corrupted his intellect, so that even though he was a disciple of the supreme Vaishnava Narada Muni,\nhe could not accept Narada's correct teachings. Now, Dhruva Maharaj was deeply remorseful that\nwhy he neglected those teachings. Narada Muni had said to him, ^\"Why do you care about the insult or praise done by your mother-in-law?\"\"He had said to Dhuv Maharaj that, gE is only a child, therefore what do you have to do with such insult or praise?\"--But Dhuv Maharaj was\ntired of receiving the blessings given by God, so Narad advised that they should go home for now\nand try to worship when they grow up.\nBhruva Maharaj was feeling sorry\nthat why he rejected the teachings of Narad Muni and why he was determined to get revenge on Bhagwan from any perishable object\nthat is, from the mother-in-law and to get a boon to take control of his father's kingdom. Dhruva Maharaj regretted that he did not seriously consider the teachings of his guru;\nTherefore, his consciousness was corrupted. Even then, God is so merciful that, due to devotion, he\ngave Dhuvra the ultimate Vaishnava-Lakshya. Depending on divine illusion, like a dormant one, different from others.\nHe who performs penance in the second, without the fear of his own and others. 33. Shabdartham (Meaning of the word)\n\nDaivim-- of God; Mayam-- illusion; Upashrita-- having taken refuge; Prasutah-- sleeping; Ib-- directly; Bhinna-- different;\nDak-- one with a different vision; Tapye-- I have repented; Dvitiye-- in illusion; Api-- even though; Asatti-- momentary; Bhratru-- brother;\nBhratruvya- enemy; Hat-- within the heart; Ruja-- from repentance.\n.\n\nDhruva Maharaj began to repent that I was under the control of Maya; being unaware of reality,\nI slept in her lap. Because of the dualistic perspective, I considered my brother an enemy.\nAnd falsely, thinking this, I