          "textEn": "33\nThey keep doing, but all of them are momentary and false. Similarly, although we appear to be awake (conscious) in physical life,\ndue to the lack of knowledge about the soul and the Supreme Soul,\nwe create many friends and enemies through imagination. Srila Krishna Das Kaviraj Goswami says that in this\nphysical world or physical consciousness, good and bad are both the same. The difference between good and bad is only\nour mental speculation. The reality is that all souls are either descendants of God or\nare the consequences (byproducts) of His Few power. Due to being contaminated by the qualities of nature, we\nconsider one spiritual spark different from another. This is also another type of dream-vision. It is said in the Bhagavad Gita that those who are truly learned do not discriminate between a learned Brahmin, an elephant, a dog, and\na Chandal.\nThey do not see the person as an external body, but see the person as the soul.\nThrough higher knowledge, man comes to know that this body is nothing but the combination of five elements. From this perspective also, the structure of the human and the divine body is similar. From a spiritual perspective, we\nare all spiritual beings, parts of God. Whether from a physical point of view or from a spiritual point of view, we are all one, but being inspired by Maya, we make friends and enemies, therefore Dhruva Maharaj said\nThat--Daivi Sayamupashrayitva-The cause of their attachment to Maya is off.\nMayaitatprarthitam vritya chikitseva gatayushi\nPrasadadyajagadatmanam tapasadushprasadanam.\nBhavachchidamayeham bhavam bhagyavarjitah. 34). Meaning of the word\n\nMaya--by me; Etat--this; Prarthitam--prayed for; Vyartham--in vain; Chikitsa-treatment; Iva-like; Gata--finished; Ayushi--for whose age; Prasadya--to satisfy; Jagat-atmanam-the soul of the universe; Tapasa-\nFrom penance; Dushprasadam--that which is difficult to please; Bhavachhidam--that which is capable of cutting the chain of birth 