re this good and evil originates. 37). Meaning of the word:\nAkarnya- having heard; Atma-jam- one's own son; Aayantam- coming; Samparetya- after death; Yatha- as; Aagatam- having come;\nVapastha- having returned; Raja- King Uttanapada; Na- not; Shradhade- having believed; Bhadramu- welfare; Abhadrasya- of inauspicious;\nKutah- from where; Mama- mine."
