          "textEn": "347\nAll illusion is immediately removed in the same way as when self-knowledge is attained, all material sufferings\nand happiness are destroyed. Meaning: Krishna is like the sun and Maya is like darkness. Darkness means the absence of light.\nAnd Maya means the absence of Krishna consciousness. Krishna-consciousness and illusion are always close together. As soon as Krishna consciousness is awakened, all the material sufferings and pleasures caused by Maya are removed. Maya Meta Tantri Taranti Mahamantra Ka Nirantar Jaap Maya ki Shakti se hamare sada door rakhte hai.\nWith that weapon, the bow, and the arrows,\nWearing golden armbands, adorned with peacock feathers,\nWith their natures, they are like the wind, like the Bhimarvas and Shikhandis. 3). Meaning of the word\nTasya--When Dhruva; Arsha--The weapon given by Narayana Rishi; Dhanushi--On his bow; Prayujyantah--He raised; Suvarna--\nPungkaha--Golden fruits; Kalahansa-Vasasah--Like the wings of a swan; Vinishrutah--They emerged; Aavivishu--Entered;\nPravishthah--Entered; Dvishat-balam--The enemy's soldiers; Yathah--As; Vanam--In the forest; Bhimaravaahah--They made a terrible sound; Shikhandinah--\nMore\nWhen Dhruva Maharaja, as soon as he raised the weapon created by Narayana Rishi on his bow, From that,\ngolden fruits and feathered arrows began to emerge, similar to the UE of a swan. They make a 'phukar' sound.\nHaving done so, they began to enter the enemy soldiers in the same way that peacocks enter the forest making a 'keka' sound.\nThose who are in the fortresses, with their mouths open,\nFrom there, the virtuous people are disturbed.\nThey are driven away, and the angry ones are armed.\nThey are like a parrot, a lion, and a serpent. 4>. Meaning of the word\nTaih--by them; Tigma-dhara-i--with a sharp edge; Pradhane--in the battlefield; Shili-mukhaih--arrows; Itha-tatah--here and there; Punya-\nJanaah--yakshas; Upadhrutah--been greatly agitated; Tam--towards Dhuv Maharaj; Abhyadhavan-