से कुछ समय के लिए क्रुद्ध होना उनका\nकर्तव्य था। उनका भाई उत्तम निर्दोष था, तो भी किसी यक्ष ने उसका वध कर दिया था। राजा होने के\nनाते ध्रुव महाराज का कर्तव्य था कि अपराधी का वध जैसे को तैसा करते। ध्रुव राजा थे, चुनौती",
          "textEn": "373\nTvam--you; Pratyakshatmani--to the self; Tada--that time; Bhagavati--to the God; Anante--to the infinite; Anandamatre--of bliss alone;\nSamasta--all; Aanandatmak--the abode of bliss; Upapanna--being associated with; Samasta--all; Shaktayah--of powers; Bhaktima--devotion; Vidhaaya--by doing; Param--supreme; Shanakaih--immediately; Avidya-Maya ki--of ignorance and illusion; Granthim--nest; Vibhetasi--you will destroy; Mama--mine; Aham--I;\nThus, this is how; Proridham--steadfastly; Sudaddu-like;\nSamasta--all; Aanandatmak--the abode of bliss; Upapanna--being associated with; Samasta--all; Shaktayah--of powers; Bhaktima--devotion; V.\n\nIn this way, by attaining one's natural state and serving the all-powerful abode of all bliss,\nand the Supreme Being situated in every soul and in the Supreme Soul, you will immediately forget the illusionary sense of 'mine' and\n'mine'.\n\nMeaning: Dhuv Maharaj was already a liberated man, because in the state of five years, he had already had a vision of God. Even after being liberated, they were afflicted by the illusion of Maya at this time, because they were seeing their\nbrother Uttam with bodily-minded intellect. The entire physical world is functioning based on \"me\" and \"mine\".\nThis is the basic reason for the attraction towards the physical world. If a person is attracted by 'I' and 'mine'\nfrom the illusion of attachment, then he will remain in this world on various respected or hateful positions\nwill remain. By the grace of God, Manu and the sages reminded Dhuv Maharaj that he should not remain in this 'I-mine'\nmaterial consciousness. Only through devotion to God can this attachment to him be easily removed.\nControl your anger, fear, and pride, and choose the supreme good. Shruten bhooyasaa raajannagaden yathamayam. 39). Meaning of the word\n\nSanyachya-- Stop for a moment; Rosham-- Anger; Bhadram-- Well-being; Te-- Yours; Pratipam-- Enemy; Shreyasam-- Of all goodness;\nParam-- Leading; Shruthena-- By hearing; Bhuyasa-- Constantly; Rajan-- O King; Agadan-- By treatment; Yatha-- As; Aamayam--\nDisease. Hey Rajan, think about what I just said. This raga will work like medicine on the body. Stop your anger, because in the path of self-realization, anger is the biggest enemy. I wish you all the best.\nYou follow my teachings. Meaning: Dhuvo Maharaj was a liberated soul and was never angry with anyone. But being a ruler,\nin the name of maintaining peace and order in the kingdom, to be angry for some time was their\nduty. His brother Uttam was innocent, yet he was killed by a Yaksha. Being a king,\nit was the duty of Dhruva Maharaj to kill the criminal as he pleased. Dhruva was the king, the challenge"
