e being Krishna is the center point, and we are all parts of Him, just like\nhands and feet are parts of the whole body. When we realize that we are eternally connected to God,\nthis difference cannot remain. This example should be understood here as being used--hands-hand and feet-feet, but when both of them are engaged in the service of the entire body, then"
